window.SUPREME_MAGUS_CHAPTERS=(window.SUPREME_MAGUS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4401,"title":"Chapter 4401 Sacrificial Pawns (Part 1)","paragraphs":["The Breaker infused more of his bloodline ability into the Break Annihilation and squeezed all the mana reserves he had left. He consumed as much energy as the undead Ranger, but Orulm was much stronger than Acala to start with.","Restoring his undead vessel so many times had consumed a lot of the life force stored in Acala’s blood core, leaving him little to fuel the Rising Sun. On top of that, he lacked the Firstlight armor that was still in Dawn’s possession.","\"You forget something, monster.\" Acala replied. \"I’m the Horseman of Dawn, and I came here with my steed!\"","Only then did Orulm remember about the mage tower. Only then did he raise his eyes to the sky and notice the white crystal horse that was almost invisible as it stood facing the sun.","Sunrise had left Dawn right after she had dealt with Bathos, and now infused all of its power into the undead Ranger instead of splitting it between Horseman and host. The mage tower kept its distance so as not to offer an easy target to the Breaker, and released red beams of world energy through its eyes.","Blood and mana seeped into Acala, restoring his blood core to its full power as if he were using Invigoration. At the same time, the Blade Spell became a Tower Blade Spell, increasing its power one hundredfold.","Acala roared as the Rising Sun grew in size and pierced through the Break Annihilation. He also altered the angle of the spell so that it would turn upward and blast the Eldritch high in the sky where it wouldn’t hurt Batara’s innocent people.","Orulm watched the Tower Blade Spell repairing itself faster than he could destroy it. He watched it come closer and knew that the time he had left on Mogar amounted to a handful of seconds.","The Skinwalker-Eldritch consumed all the Break energy he had left as he conjured the emergency Chaos Gate stored in the Maw of Bytra. The artifacts Forgemastered by the Fourth Ruler of the Flames were linked just like their hybrid masters.","Abthot’s black pillar resonated with Orulm’s core along with her Maw, providing him with the dimensional coordinates to her position. The Break energy bought Orulm just the time for the Chaos Gate to open, but not what he needed to cross it.","He let the Rising Sun push him into the dimensional corridor and follow him on the other side, dispelling the Gate the moment he crossed over.","\"Fuck.\" Orulm said from the left corner of his mouth since the right side of his head was gone, and with it, most of his body. \"Fuck!\"","Tendrils of his flesh plunged into the ground, draining the life it contained and the world energy coming from the mana geyser below.","\"I could have won! I should have!\" He snarled in outrage as his body regenerated at a speed visible to the naked eye. \"I’m supposed to be the most powerful Eldritch on Mogar. Stronger even than the gods-damned Suneater.","\"Yet I lost to a measly Vampire! I lost because I played with my food like a stupid toddler and choked on it.\"","\"Lucky you.\" Abthot shrugged. \"At least you have an excuse. Pathetic, but still an excuse. I did my best, yet I got destroyed. Nothing I did took Dawn by surprise. No matter what I tried, she had a counter ready.\"","\"If it’s of any consolation, the human Vampire was the same.\" The Breaker snarled. \"He was immune to my Skinwalker abilities and shrugged off my Break energy. He was... a perfect counter to my winning moves.\"","The rage disappeared from Orulm’s voice as he replayed his fight with the undead Ranger.","\"What?\" Abthot asked, surprised by the Breaker’s uncharacteristic contemplative mood.","\"Don’t you find everything that happened today weird?\" Orulm asked. \"Dawn cut ties with her Court a long time ago, yet there she was, fighting for them. She didn’t just direct the undead assault on the Blood Minotaurs. She led them into battle.\"","\"You are right, this is weird.\" The elf-ogre hybrid pondered. \"Dawn took center stage while she was supposed to be hiding from the Dead King and revealed several of her hidden cards.","\"I would understand it if it were a matter of survival or to locate the Dead King, but this was a waste of her time. Losing Batara barely puts a dent in the Organization’s assets, and if we send Tezka, we’ll reclaim it in a second.","\"Also, to rebuild the Undead Courts’ influence, Dawn needs to conquer many more cities and expose her presence to the Dead King. Why is she taking so many risks for something that is of no importance to her?\"","\"You’re asking the wrong questions.\" Orulm’s gaze steeled, and his eyes flared with black and crimson mana. \"I’m more interested in knowing how Dawn and her lapdog seemed to know our abilities so well.","\"Sure, we fought together against the World Tree, but back then we played a secondary role. Dawn spent all the time on the front lines, and there’s no way she glanced more than once at us.\"","\"Order and Chaos, you are right!\" Abthot took her communication amulet out of her pocket dimension and called Xenagrosh.","\"You’re alive.\" She said with a half-smile that expressed amusement and surprise in equal measure. \"You cost me a pretty coin, but congratulations nonetheless.\"","Horror and outrage froze the elf-ogre hybrid, but only for one second.","\"We are coming back to the base and expect to find you there when we arrive.\" Abthot snarled in fury.","\"Where am I supposed to go?\" Xenagrosh shrugged. \"I have lots of paperwork left, and I can use a few extra hands. Feel free to join me at your earliest convenience.\"","Rage didn’t cloud the hybrids’ minds, so they took a roundabout route back to Essagor and followed protocol by the book to avoid being followed.","The moment they stepped inside the Master’s secret lab, loud applause welcomed them.","\"Thank the gods you made it, Abby!\" Bytra threw her arms at the elf’s neck, forcing her to squash her anger like a bug.","No matter how much she might hate the Master, the Organization, or Xenagrosh, no one dared anger the Fourth Ruler of the Flames. She was the kindest and warmest of their kind on top of being one of the best Forgemasters on Mogar.","\"Thanks, Bytra.\" Abthot turned to look at Orulm, afraid he would lash out without a care for the consequences.","Instead, she found him silent and eerily calm like a man resigned to his destiny.","\"I knew you runts would have survived.\" Tezka smirked. \"The gods hate me too much to bless me with your death.\"","\"Did you send us into a trap?\" Orulm ignored the Suneater and moved to stand before the Shadow Dragon.","\"No. If I wanted to kill you, I would have done it myself, or asked the Master or Tezka to do it. It wasn’t a trap.\" Xenagrosh replied.","\"Frey is still scared of you, boy.\" Tezka released a black golden aura so strong that all the Eldritches but Zoreth and Bytra fell to their knees. \"If you weren’t useful to the Master’s plans, I’d have killed you a long time ago.\""]},{"number":4402,"title":"Chapter 4402 Sacrificial Pawns (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Xenagrosh doesn’t need to ask me to do anything. You only have to give me a reason, boy. It doesn’t need to be a good one.\"","\"What was it, then?\" Orulm nodded to the Suneater, aware that his position in the Organization had always been precarious.","\"A test that you passed.\" The Shadow Dragon said. \"We didn’t inform Baba Yaga of your identity or abilities. We only told her we would send two hybrids to Batara.\"","\"Since when getting your ass kicked is a passing grade?\" Abthot reeled at the revelation. \"Also, what do you mean, inform? Was this some kind of joint operation?\"","\"You’re smarter than you look and way smarter than you act, Abthot.\" The heel of the Grimbark Staff thumping on the ground accompanied the Master’s steps. \"Maybe there is still hope for you.","\"Keep up like this, and there will also be a place for you in my Organization once our project is complete.\"","\"Do you mind explaining to us what everyone else already knows, Master?\" Orulm asked, his tone devoid of both mockery and respect.","\"I expected you to have figured it out by now, but sure.\" Vastor nodded. \"We need to pull back part of our forces stationed in Garlen for the time being.","\"Thanks to the cooperation between Jiera’s natives, the three great countries’ colonizing efforts, the elves, and the people of Zelex, at the current rate it won’t take more than two years to bring the continent under control.","\"Once that happens, our mining operations will be discovered, and even if we are allowed to continue them, the Awakened Councils of both continents will ask us questions I don’t want to answer.","\"For this reason, I have agreed to let the Undead Courts reconquer the less profitable branches of the black market. It gives me plausible deniability to redeploy my forces without raising suspicions and the Undead Courts the funds they need to fight Meln.\"","A wave of his hand activated the arrays of the room and conjured the holograms of several data charts.","\"As you can see, allocating more workforce to our mines in Jiera will earn us in days resources that the underworld of cities like Batara takes months to gather. In a couple of years, the main crystal and metal veins will peter out, but by then we should have accumulated everything we need.","\"Finding new veins and digging deep enough to reach them won’t be our problem. The Awakened Councils might have suspicions, but if we do our job properly, they’ll have no evidence leading them back to us.\"","\"Why do we care about the Undead Courts, and what about our fellow Abominations? What about Gukah and Karto?\" Bathos asked.","\"We don’t.\" The Master replied, his voice turning as cold and sharp as a blade. \"I’m using the Undead Courts to justify our reduced activities on Garlen and give the Dead King one more enemy he has to look out for.","\"The Eclipsed Lands, the Undead Courts, and the Organization are allied to find and kill Meln Narchat once and for all. I’m giving them something I don’t need and plunging another thorn in Narchat’s side. Two birds with one stone.","\"As for Gukah and Karto, this was a test for them too.\" Vastor grunted. \"They were tasked with protecting the Organization’s assets and failed. Instead of stupidly trying to fight Dawn on their own, they should have retreated and called for backup.","\"Had they warned you of the nature of your enemy, maybe you would have won, and they would still be alive. Instead, Gukah and Karto threw their lives away out of sheer arrogance and almost cost you yours.","\"They should have known that I don’t care about money or treasures. They are just a means to an end. You, my chosen, are the only assets worth protecting. As long as you are by my side, there is nothing I can’t do.","\"Gukah and Karto failed us. They deserved to die. Moreover, the loss of those two imbeciles will give credibility to our ruse. Everyone will overestimate the Undead Courts’ power and underestimate ours, diverting attention from us.\"","\"You keep saying ’us,’ yet you had no qualms about using Abthot and me like sacrificial pawns in your game.\" Orulm said with the same tone he would use to discuss the weather.","\"Indeed, but I did it for a good reason.\" The Master replied. \"Orulm, you are too dependent on your Break ability. You rely on it so much that you have no other noteworthy skill aside from the spells you learned from me after joining the Organization, have you?\"","The Breaker raised his hands in apology and nodded for Vastor to continue.","\"Your arrogance is also a big problem. I watched the fight from start to finish. Zepho Acala was weaker than you, yet he beat you because he did a much better job at hiding his skills.","\"Everyone knows your name, Orulm, which also means everyone knows what you can do and how to defend from your Break energy. Unless you develop new techniques and spells, this will just be the first of many defeats.","\"Your Eldritch ability is amazing, but it’s not omnipotent, and it does nothing if it doesn’t hit its target. As you are, the moment you run out of Break energy you are weaker than Bytra, and she’s not even a fighter.\"","Orulm gritted his teeth and swallowed a harsh retort. He could refute none of the Master’s words, only find empty excuses.","\"Abthot, I know that it’s a painful page of your past that you’d rather forget, but you need to work on recovering your elven powers. With just Chaos and your Ogre side, you are no better than a Dryad Eldritch. You are one of my hybrids. Act like one.\"","She stiffened for a bit, but said nothing.","\"If you are done whining, let’s all get back to work. We have a lot to do before this day ends.\"","***","Eclipsed Lands, city of Lightkeep at the same time.","It took Dawn a single Steps to return to Vladion’s Mansion, where Baba Yaga was waiting for her.","\"I have only one question.\" Acala said after they dismounted from Sunrise and split into two separate beings again. \"Why didn’t you tell me I was facing Orulm the Breaker? I never met him before, but you did.","\"I slumbered while you fought together against the World Tree, so you had seen his hybrid appearance already. He could have killed me. He could have killed us.\" There was pain in his voice, but no accusation.","\"I did it because I trust you, Zepho.\" Dawn took his hands into hers while looking him in the eyes. \"I never doubted you would find a way to protect us. Never. Also, I wanted to give you a victory that was your own.","\"You didn’t rely on my memories, experiences, or tactics to beat the legendary Breaker, Zepho. You did it only thanks to the efforts you put into your training and the sacrifices you made to become a Vampire.","\"Even if in the future we are forced to fight on two different battlefronts, now you know there is no enemy you can’t take on. Orulm is one of the few beings on Mogar who might kill even Mother, Zepho, and you kicked his ass with half our equipment.\""]},{"number":4403,"title":"Chapter 4403 Trial Run (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"I see.\" Acala didn’t like being kept in the dark, but he could see from their partial mind fusion that Dawn was sincere.","She just wanted the undead Ranger to trust himself at least half as much as she did. She had put her life in his hands, knowing that he would rise to the occasion.","\"Only one question?\" Nyka echoed. \"I have lots of them. Starting with why Dawn took action if the Master had already agreed to leave Batara and what the point of revealing her and Acala’s new abilities was.\"","\"It’s all part of my plan, child.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"Dawn agreed to act as bait for the same reason the Master agreed to set up a stage for us. Without the conflict, Dawn moving alone would have made Meln suspicious.","\"He would have wondered what gave her the confidence to leave my side after what happened to Dusk and might have sensed the trap. Remember that he’s a coward, child. He never starts a fight unless he’s sure to win.","\"Now, instead, he has seen Dawn and Zepho having each their own body. Zepho has revealed to the entire world his transformation into a Vampire who has no weak points, can endure sunlight, and can use all elements.","\"It’s thanks to Zepho that Dawn now has a perfect justification to both rejoin the Undead Courts and travel across Mogar away from me. She has displayed a power so great that it allowed her to take on two of the Master’s Eldritch-hybrids at the same time.","\"She has double the strength any of my Horsemen had ever had and a core superior to the bright violet. Unless Meln discovers the secret of the white core, he will never be on her level.","\"Moreover, Zepho becoming a Vampire is a taunt Meln won’t be able to ignore. He and Zepho have the same undead blood coursing through their veins and are bonded to a Horseman, yet their standing is completely different.","\"Zepho is the recognized king of the same Undead Courts that betrayed Meln and sold him to Thrud. He has proven to be a great warrior even without Dawn, and she has complete trust in him.","\"All things that the Dead King’s inferiority complex makes impossible for him to ignore.","\"He will feel overshadowed by Zepho, which will only exacerbate the envy Night has always harbored towards Dawn. With a bit of luck, they will fall into our trap without even noticing.","\"Giving the Undead Courts a foothold on Garlen again is just the icing on the cake. Meln has sworn revenge against them as well, and now that they have resurfaced, he won’t be able to ignore them for long.","\"Not after they will publicly swear their allegiance to the Horseman of Dawn.\" The Mother smiled. \"I wouldn’t be surprised if Meln and Night were throwing a tantrum right now.\"","***","Jiera continent, ruined city of Tle’ket, at the same time.","Baba Yaga was right about the maelstrom of violent emotions that was ravaging Night’s heart. Envy, rage, and betrayal fought for dominance like lions tussling as they fell down a steep cliff.","No matter which one won, they would all die the moment they reached the ground below.","\"That bitch!\" Night snarled. \"That fucking mama’s girl did it. After failing for millennia to achieve Manifestation like the rest of us mortals, she had to succeed now just to spite me and lick Mother’s boots!","\"The only silver lining is that Dawn’s little stunt made her so arrogant that she fell for the Undead Courts’ flattery. They’ll betray her just like they betrayed us, and when they do, we’ll be the ones laughing!\"","Night didn’t care about the Undead Courts. She considered them a failed project, and her host being the king of the Upyrs was enough to satisfy her ego. What truly angered her was Acala defeating the Breaker and Dawn’s technique to tap into her tower’s powers from a distance.","The Black Night doubted that Orpal would have survived the encounter with Orulm, with or without her help. Any wounds the Vurdalak would suffer would be permanent, just like the damage on her crystal or steed.","’That dumb bitch can now hide her tower and prowess whenever she wants.’ Night thought. ’The worst part, however, is that knowing it does me no good. I can’t replicate Dawn’s technique, not even with Dusk’s crystal.’","As for Orpal, he threw his head back and burst into a bitter laughter. He sounded so much more deranged than usual that even his most loyal Upyrs brought their hands to the hilts of their weapons, afraid he had lost his mind for good.","\"Nicely played, Acala.\" He said with a wide, joyless smile. \"You think yourself so much better than me, yet you are nothing but a fine gift ready to be unwrapped.\"","\"What do you mean?\" Night asked.","\"I admit that I’d never fight someone like Orulm. Too much danger for no return.\" The Dead King clicked his tongue. \"Yet I wouldn’t hesitate to take Dawn on even now. We knew about her Morning Star spell.","\"It gives her the mass of a Divine Beast, but so what? We are a Divine Beast, and we also have Life Maelstrom. It’s more than enough to bridge the gap in our cores even if we fought one-on-one, something we won’t do.","\"We’ll take her down with our army of Upyrs during the day, when her little undead servants need to take their beauty sleep. Doom Tide will strip her of the Light Mastery she’s so proud of, and Origin Flames will burn her host to cinders.","\"We’ll drag your sister away from that old hag of your mother and feed on Dawn as we did for Dusk. This time, however, we won’t fail to absorb her mind. With the three Horsemen’s crystals fused into one, Light Mastery, and the secret of Manifestation, we’ll be invincible.","\"Imagine us using Morning Star to double our mass. Imagine our power never waning, no matter the time of day. Imagine what would happen if Sunrise and Moonlight fuse as well and grant us the might of two mage towers!\"","Night pictured all those things, and she loved what she saw.","\"Mother will be so sad when we kill her favorite daughter.\" She said with a voice filled with mock compassion. \"Remind me to pull Mother’s lips up into a smile after we rip her head off her neck and hang it on a wall.\"","***","Jiera continent, Maneka Region, inside the Black Throne, a few hours later.","After nothing more had happened for a while, the Dead King had ordered everyone to resume their usual duties. Jorl had discussed with Orpal the best strategies for capturing Dawn, learning much about what the Horseman could do.","He had been careful in wording his questions, so that Night had often ended up revealing part of her own abilities to explain how those of her sister worked.","Once the Dead King had dismissed him, the Storm Griffon had left the fortress of Tle’ket at the first opportunity, rushing to inform the Black Throne of the latest developments and share his worries with the cursed tower."]},{"number":4404,"title":"Chapter 4404 Trial Run (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I’m telling you, it works.\" Jorl paced around the throne in a frenzy. \"Orpal’s plan can work. He has everything he needs to succeed. His tower evens out Dawn’s, his mass eclipses Acala, and Life Maelstrom more than makes up for the gap in their mana cores.","\"Once you factor in that Orpal is going to gang up on Dawn and exploit Dusk’s abilities to neutralize her best cards, you can see that unless Dawn has a few more cards up her sleeve or Baba Yaga comes to her rescue, she has little chance of victory.\"","\"If none at all.\" The Black Throne’s raspy voice sounded smug. \"Yes, the Dead King came up with a good plan. One that for once isn’t based on boastful words and wishful thinking. I agree with your assessment.","\"There are several unknown variables, but unless this is Baba Yaga’s scheme, Orpal can pull it off. He can absorb Night’s last sibling and become one of the most powerful beings on Mogar despite his many faults.\"","\"That’s great news.\" Jorl sneered. \"We should throw him a party. Maybe you could swear your allegiance to him while we are at it. He can use a third tower to conquer Garlen a bit faster and still have time to have his nails done.\"","\"Foolish apprentice, you’ve misunderstood my words.\" The cursed tower laughed at the idea of submitting to an inferior intellect. \"I wasn’t praising the Dead King, nor was I admitting defeat. Far from it.","\"I’m simply amused by fate’s uncanny sense of humor.\"","\"What’s so amusing about this?\" The Storm Griffon stopped pacing, staring at the twisted chair-shaped corpse that gave the Black Throne its name in spite. \"Once Orpal gets his hands on that kind of power, he’ll be beyond our reach.","\"Our alliance will become pointless. I’ll have to cross my fingers and wish for a Guardian to kill him, and you’ll have to hide for the gods know how long.\"","\"* If * Orpal gets his hands on that kind of power, you mean.\" The cursed tower’s laugh sounded like a raspy fit of cough. \"Think about it, apprentice. Everything he’s planned for himself, we can do better.","\"My tower has many enchantments, whereas his crystal paperweight has none. You have his same Life Maelstrom and the strength of a Griffon. Akhton has Origin Flames and Mana Body.","\"If any of your followers has access to Doom Tide, what’s the difference between Orpal and us? Why shouldn’t we make our move before he does and reap the benefits?\"","’He is right.’ Jorl thought. ’I can put together a team the likes Orpal can only dream about. I only lack the Doom Tide, but that’s not important for me. I also know Light Mastery and would lose as much as Dawn if we removed the world energy.’","\"What benefits?\" He actually said. \"The only thing I’d obtain by capturing Dawn is keeping her out of Orpal’s clutches. You, instead, could study her just like you would Night and discover the secret of the Horsemen’s regenerative powers.","\"At that point, you wouldn’t need me any longer, and I’d be left holding the bag. Thanks, but no thanks. There is no loyalty between us, only shared interests. If I do this, Orpal will discover my betrayal, and without your help, I would have no way to defend myself.\"","\"I won’t be his slave, but I won’t be yours either. Our deal is about mutual benefit, and there isn’t anything for me in kidnapping Dawn.\"","\"A fair, but incomplete assessment of our situation, apprentice.\" A pristine white cut opened in the Black Throne’s headrest as the corpse smiled. \"I’d indeed learn the secret of Dawn’s regeneration, but you’d also have the Healer you need to treat the Vurdalak’s corruption.\"","At those words, Jorl frowned in focus.","\"That’s not all. Once I can finally mend my broken body and Forgemaster my tower’s combat form, killing Orpal will be much easier. I’m not going to abandon you, apprentice.","\"Our game has gone too far, and I’m having too much fun to call it quits. After millennia of boredom, things have gotten so exciting that I can feel blood rushing through the dried husk of my body!\"","\"I’m sure that in some cultures that’s a compelling argument.\" The Storm Griffon scoffed. \"Too bad I’m from Garlen. In my homeland, we call speeches like yours a convenient pile of bullshit.\"","\"I love that you don’t trust me, apprentice, just like I appreciate your confidence in talking back to me like that.\" The Black Throne replied. \"If only you were a bit smarter, I would consider you almost on my level.","\"Let me put it this way. Right now, we have no feasible plan to take the Dead King down with your current forces, correct?\" He asked, and Jorl nodded for him to continue. \"Yet capturing Dawn is a different story.","\"Orpal already shared with you all the information about her we need, and we have the means to overpower her. Consider this a trial run. If we win, we’ll increase our power and test our abilities against a lesser version of Night.","\"Even if Dawn still has a few tricks up her sleeve, we can still beat her and use what we learn to understand the full scope of Night’s abilities. If we fail, however, all is lost. There is no way we can take Night prisoner if we can’t even defeat Dawn.","\"Last, but not least, what’s the alternative? Sit on our thumbs and wait for Orpal to make his move? I can always go into hiding until someone kills him, but what about you, apprentice? Your family and Verhen want you dead.","\"Even if you desert the Dead King and run away, there’s no place on Mogar where you can be safe from the plague that lies dormant in your chest. You have no choice but to trust me.\"","Jorl thought long and hard, weighing his options.","\"Let’s do this, then.\" He said. \"What’s our next move?\"","***","Garlen Continent, Distar Region, Verhen Mansion, at the same time.","The sun was down in the Griffon Kingdom when the hybrids had fought the Bight Day, but Lith hadn’t missed a single exchange.","He remained glued to his amulet until the end of the fight, noticing several oddities.","\"Something is off here.\" Lith said. \"I could understand a local Awakened rushing to the scene after Dawn was spotted entering Batara, but how could they film her descending from the sky and bursting through the Blood Minotaurs’ door?\"","\"Maybe an Awakened happened to be nearby.\" Elina shrugged. \"Or maybe they were tipped off by one of the guards that saw Dawn fly over the city walls.\"","\"Don’t be naïve, Mom.\" Lith snorted. \"Awakened have better things to do than walk with their noses up in the sky. As for a bribed guard, the sighting of a Horseman would have caused so much ruckus that no one would have had the time to make a call before it was way too late to catch her entrance.","\"If you ask me, the only possible explanation is that Dawn herself warned someone of her arrival and that someone broadcast the fight on purpose.\"","\"It sounds a bit far-fetched, son.\" Raaz said."]},{"number":4405,"title":"Chapter 4405 Hidden Echo (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Let’s call things by their name, Dad. Lith’s paranoid as usual.\" Tista shook her head.","\"He’s also right.\" Solus said after a brief call to Baba Yaga. \"Malyshka said it’s part of her plan, and that she’ll explain everything tomorrow when she comes here to practice Dread Magic with Lith.\"","\"Wonderful!\" Kamila said with the enthusiasm of someone who had found a parking ticket on her windshield. \"I can understand following the news of the fight between the Organization and the Undead Courts, but what’s the rule about amulets and meals?\"","Everyone put their communication amulets down in emergency mode, refusing any call that wouldn’t be marked as urgent.","\"Thank you very much.\" Kamila sighed. \"We live in the same house, yet we see each other so rarely that I’d like for us to have an actual conversation.\"","\"You’re right, Sis Kami.\" Aran nodded. \"I missed you a lot. Almost as much as Mom and Dad.\"","\"I’m so sorry, son.\" Raaz pinched his nose. \"Being an Awakened is much more work than I expected. Between studying, practicing magic, and doing the bare minimum to supervise the work in my fields, I barely have the time to use Accumulation.\"","\"Our children warned us, and there is no turning back now.\" Elina fought hard to suppress a yawn. \"Gods, I used to love reading, but I swear that if I see another book, I’ll scream.\"","\"How was your day, Kami?\" Lith asked, hoping to change the topic to something more cheerful.","\"Exhausting.\" She replied, bursting his hopes like a soap bubble. \"Dimensional magic is driving me crazy. I’ve been practicing it ever since I was pregnant with Elysia, and I’ve yet to Switch once.","\"I can’t believe you guys crammed so many difficult subjects in just one year.\"","\"Tell me about it.\" Selia snorted. \"I just graduated from Loop to Pilfer, and it took me months just to get there.\"","’I better not tell them that I mastered the Switch spell months ago.’ Jirni thought. ’I wonder if I’m progressing so fast thanks to my innate talent or because magic is not a hobby for me. My life and the future of my little Dripha depend on it.’","\"We all had a stronger core than you and an authentic passion for magic, Kami.\" Lith replied. \"You are training just to keep up with Elysia’s development and be able to chase her around once she grows up.\"","\"I know, but practicing magic full time yet achieving so little is frustrating.\" She replied. \"My greatest success is promoting my core to bright green, but just the thought of how painful the breakthrough to cyan is going to be makes me want to cry.\"","Aran and Leria were only one stage behind her in the development of their cores, and only because their young bodies needed time to adapt to the increasing power they stored.","They had undergone only one major breakthrough, and they still had nightmares about it. The idea that the next one would be much worse made them turn pale.","\"Okay, enough talking about magic.\" Solus said. \"If the mood gets any gloomier, the babies will worry something bad has happened.\"","\"What about me?\" Rena grumbled. \"I was waiting my turn to vent a bit.\"","\"Another time, please.\" Solus raised her hands with her palms out. \"Does anyone have good news to share?\"","\"I do.\" Senton released a deep orange aura. \"I’ve finally broken past the red, and I can now use magic for more than a few minutes before being forced to use Invigoration.\"","Everyone gave him a short round of applause.","\"Congratulations, Dad.\" Leria puffed her chest out with pride for her father. \"I can’t wait to practice magic with you.\"","\"Thank you, pumpkin.\" Senton didn’t remind her that he would stop his magical training right after reaching the green not to spoil his daughter’s joy.","\"I don’t know if it counts as good news, but I can get further than 100 meters before feeling the need to check on Ral now.\" Lith said. \"Soon my homing instinct should calm down enough to allow me to spend a few hours outside on my own.\"","\"This is great news! We can finally go out on a date!\" Kamila said with a bit too much enthusiasm to be polite. \"Don’t get me wrong, I love spending time with you all, but this is starting to feel like a boot camp with no privacy.","\"I don’t get to spend a moment alone with Lith, let alone my thoughts.\" She looked at the babies’ child seats.","Elysia, Raldarak, and Valeron had no concept of personal space. Whenever they felt lonely or wanted to see their parents, they would use Spirit Magic to open even the bathroom door and barge in.","Putting them inside the Doomslayer crib didn’t help since they would cry at the top of their lungs until someone came to reassure them.","\"Mama!\" Raldarak giggled at her, making Kamila feel guilty at the idea of leaving her baby boy’s side even if just for one hour.","\"Don’t worry, Kami. I’ll take you on a date as soon as I can.\" Lith’s words were met with cheers from the babies’ side of the table.","Elysia and Valeron had developed their own definition of date, and had passed it on to the others. According to them, a date was when their parents brought them out of the house, played with them until nap time, and let them try lots of tasty new foods.","\"Dade, Mom. Dade!\" Solkar said, making his older siblings chuckle.","\"Oh, dear.\" Selia pretended to be embarrassed. \"This dashing young man is asking me out. What should I do?\"","\"Change his diaper.\" Protector replied after a couple of sniffs. \"As for the ’date’, anywhere but Lutia is fine. I know that no one is going to bother us again, but I need to relax without constantly looking over my shoulder.\"","***","The following morning, Baba Yaga reached the Mansion as promised and shared her plan to capture Orpal with Lith and Solus.","\"It’s an interesting strategy, but I find it hard to believe that the Master gave up on a stable source of income that easily.\" Lith pondered.","\"Yet it’s what he did.\" The Mother shrugged. \"I question his motives as well, but I couldn’t afford to look the gifted horse in the mouth and took what he offered me. By now, Dawnie should have already conquered five more cities.\"","Lith could tell by looking at the map that they were all medium-sized trading hubs with limited potential or influence over their respective regions, but that much was a given.","Only a madman would give away a gold mine, and Vastor had heavily fortified the Organization branches in the cities he couldn’t afford to lose. Dawn conquering any of them without both factions suffering major casualties would have exposed her agreement with the Master.","\"How is the training of your Indech form going, Solus?\" The Mother asked.","\"It’s going great.\" Solus replied. \"My atrophied mana organs are developing slowly but steadily. All the time and effort Lith spent developing the training exercises with Ryla is paying off.","\"I can already use Swirling Wind to an extent. It’s only a matter of time until I can conjure my elemental bloodline abilities.\""]},{"number":4406,"title":"Chapter 4406 Hidden Echo (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"What about your Dragon and Talos form?\" Baba Yaga asked. \"Did you discover anything about them?\"","\"Not a clue, and not for a lack of trying.\" Solus groaned. \"The only thing I’m sure of is that I don’t have Dragon Eyes either.\"","\"Don’t worry about it. I was in your shoes two years ago.\" Lith patted her shoulder. \"Tista and I discovered most of our bloodline abilities out of survival instinct or in high-stress situations that pushed us to our limits. It will be the same for you.\"","\"Oh, joy.\" Solus said. \"I can’t wait to almost die to learn a trick or two.\"","Lith would have liked to point out that at least, thanks to the Bleed, she had a do-over even if something went wrong, but it was a touchy subject for Solus.","Especially after she had given him permission to extract the life force of the last member of the Awakened group who had tried to kidnap the children.","\"Let’s get to work, shall we?\" Lith said, bringing Elysia with them to the tower as soon as the two women nodded. \"Today, we’re going to ask our baby overlord’s help to discover the final Dread Magic rune. Is that okay with you, baby girl?\"","\"Yah!\" Elysia nodded enthusiastically, making a crown of silvery flames appear over her head.","She also patted Lith’s head right, left, and center in what was the best induction ceremony that her short arm allowed her to perform.","\"Where did you learn the meaning of a crown and all this?\" Lith asked in confusion.","\"You just called her your baby overlord.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"How many overlords do you know who are often your guests and spend lots of time with your children?\"","\"I don’t know what you are talking about.\" Salaark’s voice came out of nowhere as soon as Lith and Solus glared at the ceiling.","\"Gama!\" Elysia conjured a small, badly-shaped scepter of fire that she extended upwards for examination.","\"Grandma, do you really want to teach Ely that it is okay to lie to your family?\" Lith asked.","\"That would be bad.\" Salaark’s voice replied. \"Remember, Elysia, good girls don’t lie. Lying is only for grown-ups.\"","\"That’s even worse!\" Solus snarled as she saw the baby girl nodding. \"Now you are teaching her that she can’t trust adults because they can and will lie to her like you are doing with us! What if she shares your teachings with Val and Ral?\"","\"Agreed. That’s much worse.\" Tyris’ voice joined the conversation, accompanied by the sound of the cracking of knuckles.","\"Fine, I was wrong!\" Salaark sighed. \"Lying is bad, Elysia. Grandma made a mistake, but she promises never to do it again.\"","\"Ok.\" Elysia nodded again. \"Lin bad.\"","\"That’s my girl.\" Lith gently caressed her head. \"Remember the rules, Ely. Do not cast magic until I tell you otherwise. If you damage the tower by mistake, Grandma Ripha will be really sad.\"","\"Please, be careful.\" Menadion said. \"This is my favorite toy.\"","\"Yah!\" Elysia replied as Lith Warped everyone to the Lodestar.","A snap of his fingers filled the room with world energy, forming a clear connection with Mogar’s will.","\"Vinire.\" Baba Yaga traced the chore rune for light magic and spoke its name clearly.","Elysia turned her head to the side, as if she were focusing on a distant echo, while Lith closed his eyes and immersed himself in the flow of world energy.","\"Vinire.\" Baba Yaga traced the rune again, and Lith saw it even in the darkness that surrounded him.","The first light rune rippled through the world energy like the pinched string of a musical instrument, releasing waves that spread in every direction. Yet there was one more sound behind Vinire that became audible only in the brief interval the waves slowly faded away.","It passed too quickly and was too faint to discern, no matter how much Lith focused.","’How does Ely do it?’ ’He thought. ’Can it be a matter of pure elemental affinity or raw talent? After all, she’s born with all six streaks, whereas I-’","\"Vinire.\" Baba Yaga drew the first rune of light, and this time Lith wasn’t focused on the sound it produced but on himself.","It was the reason he noticed that Vinire’s ripples resonated with the light elemental stars in his life force. At first, he only saw a mirror image of the first light rune, but as it faded away, light turned into Decay and the rune distorted into something else.","\"Vinire.\" The phenomenon happened again, confirming to Lith that he hadn’t just imagined it.","He used his silver eye to amplify the power of his light elemental stars and with it their resonance with the first light rune. As soon as the sound turned into an echo, Lith ignited the spark of Decay in his life force.","The cursed element covered the entire surface of the elemental star, and thanks to Lith’s help, the echo lasted much longer than usual. Vinire disappeared, replaced by the other rune that was now more defined.","\"Vinire.\" Lith focused on the sound, following it as it rose, peaked, dropped, and changed.","The more clearly the echo became, the better Lith could see the second rune. It was similar to Vinire, but also different, like a fraternal twin.","While Vinire was a note hummed with joy, the first Decay rune was yelled in anger. Where the sound of the light element was an ode to life sung during spring, its Dread counterpart was a war cry roared on the battlefield.","’Me and my overthinking!’ Lith inwardly cursed. ’It’s just as Baba Yaga explained to me during our first practice session in the Lodestar. Every rune someone calls upon in the world energy resonates with the corresponding elements in their mana core.","’Learning the Dread Magic runes has nothing to do with streaks or talent. It’s about listening to the resonance that takes place within me, where I can study the first magic runes without the interference of Mogar’s will and the other elements.","’Elysia is so much better than me at listening to the runes because she possesses a higher amount of stable cursed elements in her life force and because, unlike me, she follows her instinct blindly.","’World energy and mana are foreign concepts to her, and she doesn’t waste time trying to understand what we are doing. She just listens to the melody the runes produce.’","\"Bi’ra.\" Elysia said after a while, tracing the first Decay rune with her finger.","\"You mean Vikara, right?\" Lith still had his eyes closed and wasn’t even using the Dragon Scales to decipher the baby speak.","He knew the right pronunciation of the first rune for stable Decay because he had just learned it as well after fine-tuning the light elemental stars in his life force with his silver eye.","\"Yah!\" The baby girl nodded, puffing her chest out with pride. \"Bi’ra!\"","A white light formed on her palm, but then she looked at the frown on Menadion’s face and the fear on Solus’.","\"So’y!\" Elysia shooed the Dread spell like an annoying fly.","\"Don’t worry, baby girl. It’s alright.\" Solus kissed Elysia’s head, making her coo. \"You’ve been great. Thank you for your help, Ely. You can go back to playing with your friends.\""]},{"number":4407,"title":"Chapter 4407 Matter and Mana (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"No po!\" Elysia conjured the crown of silvery fire again, claiming the title of overlord of the house for herself.","\"Here you go, your majesty.\" Lith handed her a small bag of baby biscuits he had ground into a fine powder. \"This is your reward. You are free to share it, if you want.\"","\"Dan iou, Dya!\" Elysia held the bag like a treasure, hugging her father before being sent back into the Doomslayer crib. \"Me hep Dya! Loo!\"","She showed her prize to the other toddlers and asked Vyla to split the contents of the bag into their baby bottles. Valeron received a normal cup as the oldest one, drawing the admiration of the smaller babies.","\"What did you do, Ely?\" He asked.","\"Do no.\" She shrugged.","Just because her father asked her to help him in his experiments didn’t mean she had any concept of magical research.","\"Can you show us?\"","\"No.\" Ely shook her head. \"Dya no.\"","Since their father had asked her not to use magic, Valeron dropped the argument and focused on enjoying his milk with biscuits.","Meanwhile, in the Lodestar, Lith had already developed a few tier one Decay Magic spells and was ready to move on to tier two. Before that, however, he taught everything he had learned to Baba Yaga and waited for her to master the spells.","\"This has gotten easier with practice, but it’s none the safer.\" She said after a minor mistake in weaving an unknown spell directly with true magic caused one of her fingers to rot and fall off. \"One stupid mistake and Vikara hurts you more than it hurts your enemy.","\"At least they can hope to dodge or block such a simple spell with a barrier, whereas the little bastard strikes at you from inside your body.\"","\"How could you fail a tier one spell, Malyshka?\" Solus asked. \"You are a powerful mage and have already mastered the other five Dread elements. This should be child’s play for you.\"","\"You’re not wrong, Solus, but you’re not right either.\" The Mother replied. \"I’ve mastered up to tier three of the other Dread elements, true, but only after practicing them with fake magic first.","\"It gave me the time to get used to the fear they instilled in me until I managed to overcome it. Just because they belong to the same branch of magic, the six Dread elements don’t work the same way and instill each a different kind of fear.","\"I bit more than I can chew and paid the price for it. Don’t worry, though. I’m as good as new.\" Her ring finger was back in its place as if nothing had happened.","\"What kind of fear does Vikara inspire?\" Lith asked.","\"The fear of aging.\" Baba Yaga said. \"The fear of growing so old that you don’t recognize the reflection in your mirror. Of becoming helpless and weak.\"","\"This doesn’t make sense.\" Solus replied. \"You are an immortal white core. This kind of fear shouldn’t affect you.\"","\"I can’t age, Solus, but everyone else can.\" The Mother sighed. \"What Vikara shows me is not my own decay, Solus, but that of the people I love. I see the children who live in my tower lose their minds to dementia.","\"I see you and Lith become frail things that beg for the sweet relief of death. I see my undead children lose their sanity as the millennia pass and become worse than Liches. The rot can take place in the mind as well as in the body, Solus.\"","\"Thanks for the depressing picture. Be right back.\" Lith Warped away, hugging his parents, sisters, and then holding Kamila for several seconds without saying anything before returning to the tower. \"Everything is fine. Everyone is fine.\"","\"You could have checked on them with the Watchtower.\" Solus said.","\"I only believe in what I see.\" Lith snorted. \"Also, the Watchtower can’t give anyone a full-body rejuvenation session.\"","\"But everyone is Awakened now, and Rejuvenation has little effect on them.\" Solus was flabbergasted. \"As for Tista, she is a Divine Beast and her life force is intact. She’s probably going to outlive us.\"","\"I know, but I don’t care.\" Lith shrugged. \"I needed to be sure.\"","Baba Yaga’s words had stirred his worst fears and memories. Only certainty that his loved ones were fine could dispel the ghosts of Carl, Yurial, Lark, and Mirim that haunted his mind.","Manohar was more like a poltergeist. A memory so annoying that you couldn’t decide whether to be more saddened or relieved by his passing.","\"I’m sorry. I didn’t mean to upset you.\" The Mother gave Lith a deep bow. \"Yet Solus needed to know. If she ever learns Dread Magic, she’ll face my same fears.\"","\"Don’t apologize.\" Lith sighed. \"I may not experience Dread Magic’s side effects, but I know fear all too well. Are you done with tier one Decay magic?\"","\"Yes, but from the way you talk, I’m guessing you have something in mind other than tier two.\" Baba Yaga nodded.","\"After watching Tezka using Mirror Magic to fight against Jorl, I have a hypothesis I want to put to the test.\" Lith replied. \"As you know, the Cursed Elements affect mana and physical matter each in a unique way.","\"My theory is that it happens not only when clashing with the spells and enchantments of your enemies, but also your own. If we want to develop tier four Dread Magic and live to tell the tale, we can’t overlook such a possibility.\"","\"It’s an interesting idea.\" The Mother pondered. \"At the moment, Mirror and Dread Magic have the same potential. Developing the upper tiers would upset the scale since Mirror Magic can’t be used along with other elements.","\"What do you have in mind, Lith? Two Cursed Elements or one Cursed and the other normal.\"","\"I like to start from what I know.\" A flick of Lith’s fingers conjured the hologram of the fight between Orulm and Acala. \"That spell is called Void Hunger. It mixes Chaos and air, so combining one Cursed element with a normal one is possible.\"","Lith moved everyone to the Firing Range and had Solus leave the room, just to stay safe.","\"I’m not going to weave two elements together and hope for the best.\" He explained to his confused half. \"Yaga is going to shoot a bolt of lightning, and I’ll intercept it with a tier one Decay spell to study how the two elements interact.","\"Worst case scenario, the Decay made from my mana will have only secondary effects on me. The Firing Range should be completely able to shield me. Baba Yaga, instead, has her white core to protect her.","\"Between her nigh-immortality and the Firing Range, there is no way a tier one spell can inflict her permanent damage.\"","\"Let me guess.\" Solus sighed. \"I share your energy signature, but if something goes wrong and I get hurt, the tower would take damage as well. The Firing Range would become less effective, and I would suffer more wounds, starting a vicious cycle.\"","\"Correct.\" Lith nodded. \"As long as you are safe, we are safe, Solus.\"","\"I couldn’t have said it better.\" Menadion clung to her daughter like a Koala to a tree. \"You can begin the experiment anytime you want, Lith.\""]},{"number":4408,"title":"Chapter 4408 Matter and Mana (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Solus diverted enough world energy to the Lodestar to preserve its effects while also ensuring the Firing Range’s maximum efficiency.","\"How are we doing this?\" Baba Yaga asked. \"I hope you don’t want us to shoot spells at each other.\"","\"We’ll aim at the same point, just like Teneb’s Golems.\" Lith and Baba Yaga fired their respective spells a few times to get used to their different speeds and gauge the timing necessary to make them reach a set spot at the same time.","The Firing Range used Ekrasu to neutralize the Decay and earth magic to stop the lightning bolt. Once Lith and Baba Yaga were done with their tests, he Warped a large rock in the middle of the Firing Range.","\"Even if we mess up, the tower will suffer no damage.\" Lith said. \"Let’s stick to the walls. I have an idea of how Decay reacts with elements other than darkness, and it won’t be nice.\"","Baba Yaga unleashed Jolt, the first lightning spell any young mage would learn, while Lith conjured the tier one Decay spell, Blightspark, a heartbeat later.","Thanks to their practice and experience, Lith and Baba Yaga succeeded on the first try. The two spells met centimeters away from the rock with disastrous consequences.","The elemental forces clashed, collapsing on themselves into what looked like a pristine ball lightning. Then, the energy mass exploded into a corona effect with a radius of over 10 meters (33’).","The countless bolts of lightning that streaked across the stone walls carried the power of Decay, leaving thin, shallow gouges in their wake only because the gold-veined white marble that comprised the floor repelled the mystical energies until the Firing Range managed to counter them.","When the combined spell disappeared, the tower had suffered minor damage that Solus perceived as an itch, while the rock Lith had Warped in the room was broken into pieces no bigger than a finger.","\"Impressive damage.\" Baba Yaga looked around the room as the fissures in the floor repaired at a speed visible to the naked eye. \"A tier one spell exceeded the Firing Range of the legendary tower of Menadion.\"","\"Not really.\" Lith pointed at the area past the rock. \"We programmed the Firing Range to counter our two spells, not the energy released by their interaction. The tower was caught unprepared like us, but only because it lacked data.","\"The Firing Range neutralized our pseudo tier four spell before it could come close to us, and we are talking about something as fast as lightning. If we tried again, I doubt the tower would suffer so much as a scratch.\"","A quick glance at the updated defensive protocols of the Firing Range confirmed Lith’s words. The tower had analyzed the phenomenon and found a way to counter spells comprised of Decay and air magic.","\"Was that what you expected?\" Menadion asked.","\"Yes.\" He nodded. \"I noticed that Tezka’s Decay Gates explode as soon as something goes through them, so I assumed that the other elements would react the same way. I had underestimated the violence and the range of the resulting explosion, though.\"","\"If you have some other experiment with the Dread Elements in mind, you should input your hypothesis in the Firing Range.\" Menadion snorted. \"It will allow the tower to create a tentative defensive protocol instead of improvising from scratch.","\"My baby got hurt, you numbskull!\"","\"Mom, it wasn’t even a scratch!\" Solus replied. \"It hurts more when you pinch my belly to remind me that I need to lose weight.\"","\"And it’s working.\" The First Ruler of the Flames patted Solus’ stomach, producing a duller sound than usual.","\"Mom!\" Solus blushed hard.","\"That’s impossible! How did you do it, Ripha?\" Baba Yaga was in utter shock.","\"Why are you so shocked, Malyshka?\" Solus prayed to Mogar to swallow her whole. \"Anyone can lose weight.\"","\"You’re not anyone, Epphy, you’re a glutton.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"Ripha?\"","\"I put a poster of Tyris in a tight-fitting dress inside every pantry and fridge of the tower.\" Menadion replied. \"It kills Solus’ appetite on sight.\"","\"Can we please go back to our experiments, please?\" Solus whined.","\"Next I want to give Cinder Magic a try.\" Lith took a mental note to have a snack later. For science, of course. \"Based on what Tezka’s Cinder Steps do, I expect the secondary element to carry the same kinetic energy as the Cinder Spell.\"","\"So, tier four Cinder Magic should conjure a spell that hits you like a physical blow?\" Baba Yaga couldn’t help but draw a parallel with the Blood Magic she had created for her undead.","\"I wish.\" Lith conjured a hologram of how he imagined a tier four Cinder spell would behave. \"Fire magic controls speed, so while Zero stops things dead, Cinder should accelerate them.","\"A gust of wind should become a typhoon. A stone should move like a cannonball. Something like this.\"","\"That’s very interesting.\" Solus pondered. \"Hard-light constructs, earth, and darkness have the same weakness. They are slow. If you are right, by combining them with Cinder, they’d become as fast as water magic.\"","\"Yeah, but there are also problems that come with that.\" Lith sighed. \"If I use Cinder against one of Yaga’s spells like I just did, the kinetic energy going in different directions will cancel each other.","\"If I try to conjure that kind of magic myself, instead, it’s a tower tier spell for earth and darkness, and even more for light.\"","\"Cinder plus its scattered counterpart are two elements already. Adding light or darkness brings the total up to three.\" Ripha pondered.","\"And since Light Mastery is light element used on itself, it counts for two.\" The Mother said. \"You are right, Lith. This kind of magic is feasible while near your tower, but impossible otherwise.\"","\"I’m not so sure about that.\" Solus grabbed her Sage Staff and paced around the room. \"Give me a minute. I need to think.\"","After a while, her eyes lit up with black light and Lith’s became golden.","\"It’s still as creepy as the first time.\" Menadion said. \"Please, use your words.\"","\"The Lodestar will stop working in less than 20 hours, Mom.\" Solus replied while gesturing Baba Yaga to leave the Firing Range as well. \"This saves us a lot of time we can use to find another working theory in case I’m wrong.\"","Another wave of Lith’s hand switched the broken stone with a new one. At the same time, he conjured the tier one Cinder Spell, Scorching Thrust, in his right hand. Once it was safe and stable, Lith weaved the tier one darkness spell, Plague Shot, in his right hand.","Then he joined his wrists together to form a quasi-tier four spell. The fiery mass of darkness energy moved more slowly than Chaos, but much faster than usual. The spell seeped deep inside the rock, melting its center while a spiderweb of cracks formed across the surface.","\"That’s cheating.\" Baba Yaga frowned. \"Did you use Domination to do that?\"","\"Yes.\" Solus answered for Lith. \"It’s the only way to fuse two different spells into something that moves that fast without it exploding in my face.\"","\"It’s not a technique I can use in a real fight, Solus, but at least you’ve found a way to prove my hypothesis.\" Lith said."]},{"number":4409,"title":"Chapter 4409 Dualistic Nature (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"And you have proved my theory, Lith.\" Menadion pointed at the pristine walls of the Firing Range. \"See? The tower just needs to have a clue of what it’s about to deal with to do its job.\"","More combined spells and broken rocks later, Lith confirmed the effects of all Dread Elements when interacting with mana. Choke gave the associated element the ability to generate multiple magnetic charges of different signs inside its target.","Different parts of the same body would move faster or slower based on the repulsive and attractive forces they experienced, making precise movements impossible.","Corruption distorted the mana with which it came in contact, having an effect akin to the Clean Slate spell for artifacts and mana poisoning for living beings. On top of that, all the Cursed Elements retained their full destructive power.","\"You know, I would be proud of our success if we weren’t just following in Tezka’s footsteps.\" Lith said in between sipping a tonic after the final battery of tests. \"He did all this with full-powered tier four dimensional magic spells and with Mirror Magic at that.","\"I used tier one Dread Magic to conjure scaled-down versions of tier four spells, yet I’m already exhausted.\"","\"Don’t be foolish, child.\" Baba Yaga said. \"Tezka is older than history itself can remember. No one but him and maybe the World Tree knows how long the Suneater has roamed Mogar.","\"He had countless millennia to master his craft in all branches of magic. If he didn’t achieve that much after working for so long on his own creation, he would be a mediocre mage.","\"You, instead, are barely 21 years old and have already achieved a lot without Tezka’s immunity to Decay and innate mastery over Chaos. If that’s not praiseworthy, then we can dismiss Lochra’s legacy as ordinary.\"","\"Thank you for your kind words, Yaga.\" Lith gave her a polite nod.","\"Still so formal.\" She sighed. \"Do I have to take this form to have you relax a bit?\"","She shapeshifted into her Maiden form, taking a much younger appearance and becoming just a bit taller than Solus.","\"No offense, but you could look like a toddler, and I wouldn’t treat you any differently. I know who you are, and treating you like a peer doesn’t come easy to me.\" Lith replied.","\"I like this form better, though.\" Solus said. \"Now I can look you in the eyes as I reproach you for not having a single word of praise for me.\"","\"You are even younger than Lith is, Epphy.\" Baba Yaga tilted her head to the side. \"Of course, your achievements are impressive, but we were talking about Dread Magic, and you didn’t contribute much since you can’t even practice it.\"","\"Then work hard so that you can teach it to me and I can show you how it’s done.\" Solus chuckled.","\"I’ll do my best.\" The Maiden replied with a silvery laugh. \"Since we are at it, I want to try and use your technique to cast Dread arrays, Solus.\"","\"Good idea, but don’t forget to input the effect you hope to obtain in the Firing Range.\" She replied. \"Arrays don’t discriminate between friend or foe and affect everything within their boundaries. The tower is no exception.\"","\"Good point.\" One of Baba Yaga’s arms became blue, while the other remained a healthy pink.","She conjured Zero energy in her elemental arm, waiting until she had completely overcome the fear of the tier one runes before accumulating more mana in her free hand.","\"Any suggestions aside from the obvious?\" She asked.","\"Only one.\" Lith replied. \"Dread Magic is too fast to Dominate it as usual. Whatever spell you have prepared, make it stand still in a spot so that you can weave its energy in a new form without rushing. It’s what I did.\"","\"Thanks, but I don’t think I will.\" The Maiden replied. \"I can take this much damage, and we can learn as much from a failed experiment as from a success.\"","This time, Lith left the Firing Range, giving Baba Yaga all the space she needed. Her first attempt failed miserably, the ray of Zero hitting the wall long before she could alter its rune sequence with Domination in any way.","The second went just as badly. The Maiden managed to slow down her spell, but in the limited space of the Firing Range it wasn’t enough.","On the third attempt, the beam of Zero opened into what looked like a fishing net before reaching the opposite wall from Baba Yaga and being neutralized by the Firing Range.","The fourth resulted in a net thrown in slow motion, while the fifth conjured an irregular dome of Zero that flickered for a couple of seconds before fading away.","\"I’m getting the hang of this, but it’s not easy.\" Baba Yaga flexed her hands open and close to melt the ice coating them. \"Using Domination to form an array from a moving spell is tricky.","\"I have a fraction of a second to rearrange all the runes and find proper anchor points in the ground. The slightest mistake and the array forms with a wrong rune sequence and falls apart.\"","\"That’s why I suggested you to conjure a stationary spell.\" Lith shrugged.","\"Good for practice, but useless otherwise.\" The Maiden had a sphere of Zero appear in the middle of the Firing Range and then Dominated it into a perfect array. \"Who in their right mind would stay near my spell?","\"Anyone with half a brain would escape long before the array forms, and I would have just wasted mana to offer my enemies an opening.\"","\"True, but at least now we can check what a Zero array does.\" Lith threw a pebble inside the magic circle, but nothing happened even after waiting for a few seconds. \"That’s weird. Even tier one magic should have a dramatic effect on something that small.\"","He sent a tendril of Spirit Magic to retrieve the pebble, feeling it become sluggish as soon as it entered the array. Hoarfrost formed around the tendril and made it visible to the naked eye.","By the time the Spirit Magic picked the pebble off the floor, the tendril had become so stiff that it would have frozen solid if Lith hadn’t sent a fresh wave of mana to revitalize it.","\"Interesting.\" As the mana started to congeal again, Lith pulled at the tendril with strength rather than will, forcing it out of the array as quickly as a whip.","Once outside, however, the mana turned invisible and intangible again.","\"Zero magic can make mana solid.\" Solus pondered. \"It’s good to expose and neutralize any cloaked spell that an enemy may use to keep us under surveillance. We could also use it to physically interact with our spells, but I don’t see the point in that.\"","\"It would also be great to pause an experiment or a Forgemastering procedure already at an advanced stage.\" Baba Yaga said. \"Stasis fields don’t work when the energy at play becomes volatile.","\"A mage like you could use a Zero array to take a break and restore their strength with Invigoration. Someone like me, instead, could use it whenever something unexpected happens and buy enough time to study and understand the phenomenon.\""]},{"number":4410,"title":"Chapter 4410 Dualistic Nature (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Even if I fail to regain control of my experiment, I can perform multiple attempts to fix the situation and get an idea of what works and what doesn’t before the wild mana blows up in my face.","\"It would save me a lot of time, especially if I come here and borrow the Eyes.\" The Maiden said.","\"That’s a great idea, yet I’m a bit disappointed by the array.\" Lith used a stick of ice to push a glass of water inside the magical formation, yet no ice formed. \"Regular Zero freezes both matter and energy.\"","\"Yeah, but that’s a single, focused blast, whereas this is still a tier one spell spread over a large area.\" Solus pointed out. \"Also, what would be the point of affecting both? You couldn’t do anything without you or your magic freezing over.\"","\"Kill, or at least trap an enemy without their allies being able to save them.\" Lith replied. \"That would be great against enemies who tend to run away like Meln.\"","\"Let me try again, then.\" Baba Yaga dispelled the first array and conjured another that froze the glass and its contents the moment it formed.","She shot a few water bubbles, and they turned into ice as well, but being made of mana, she could move them freely and recall them without effort.","\"I don’t know if it’s because of tier one or if it’s the nature of Zero arrays, but I meant to affect everything.\" She tried with the other elements, and none of those without a physical component suffered any change.","Earth spells became covered in ice, but their movement speed was the same as always. She then tried using tier two and three Dread spells, but to no avail.","\"Nothing.\" The Maiden said. \"I can only have the Zero target matter or mana, not both. Maybe I could succeed if I double cast Zero into an array with two effects, but that would require tier four and with a double Dread element at that.\"","\"Forget about it for now.\" Lith shook his head. \"You focus on studying Dread arrays while the Lodestar still works. I have something I want to try.\"","He left the Maiden in the Firing Range while he and Solus returned to the bottom floor of the tower.","He conjured the Jerak rune in his left hand and the Iratho rune in his right, trying to change one into the other.","’Do you think it’s really possible to apply Void Magic to Dread Magic?’ Solus asked as soon as he stabilized the Cursed elements and took a break to revise his findings.","’Normally, I’d say no.’ Lith replied. ’Void Magic requires turning an element into its counterpart through the connection they share with the world energy and reversing the sign of the energy at play.","’Cursed elements have not only the connection with their counterpart severed, but they are also polar opposites to each other.","’If turning fire into ice is like pushing the brakes to slow down your car until you can go in reverse, turning Cinder into Zero should be like grabbing a rocket in mid-air, turning it upside-down, and hoping it doesn’t explode in your face.’","’Either you don’t have the strength to stop the rocket, and it rips your arm off, or you do, and your grip destroys the rocket.’ Solus inwardly nodded. ’That’s what I thought.’","’I thought that too, but then I remembered something.’ Lith used a partial mind fusion to replay the events of his audience with Mogar in the Fringe down to the smallest detail.","Lith focused on the part when his own corrupted version used a blue kind of magic.","’I asked Mogar to show me how to tap into Void Magic’s full potential, but back then we hadn’t completed the upper tiers of Void Magic and had yet to discover the existence of Dread Magic.’","’You are right.’ Solus’ eyes went wide in understanding. ’Whatever that deep blue magic was, it had uncanny destructive power that closely resembles Dread Magic. Yet it formed from the combination of the six elements with Spirit Magic. What can that possibly mean?’","’No clue.’ Lith shrugged. ’The only thing I know is that there is some kind of eight element and Void Magic applies to it. Mogar never lied to us. She only gave us clues in the form of riddles.","’After experimenting with Dread Magic and getting hurt by it whenever I failed, I’m confident that deep blue energy was Void Magic applied to the Cursed Elements. I came back here with the hope that the Lodestar can help me figure out how the two disciplines are connected.’","’I wish I could help you, but my life force doesn’t contain Cursed Elements, and I have no innate understanding of it.’ Solus sighed.","***","By lunchtime, Baba Yaga had confirmed the effects of arrays woven from one Dread Element, but had yet to find a way to conjure a magical formation without giving her enemy plenty of time to leave its area of effect.","’The little bastards are too fast.’ She inwardly grumbled. ’ I think Epphy’s method is not suited to cast an array. I have to train more to withstand the number of Dread runes that conjuring a proper tier four magical formation required.’","She had to walk down the stairs to the Lodestar since the tower needed every bit of world energy to keep the floor active for as long as possible.","\"What in the gods’ names are you doing?\" She walked through the door as Lith fired a stream of Zero into another of Cinder.","His red and blue eyes burned like torches, and his willpower filled the world energy in the room to the point that she could feel it crawl along her skin. Yet judging from the disgruntled expression on his face, things weren’t going his way.","\"Failing with style.\" Lith pointed at the puddle of steaming water formed by the conflicting spells.","A brief explanation later, Baba Yaga was up to speed and completely baffled.","\"The idea sounds interesting, yet I don’t see that happening.\" She said.","\"Was Mogar lying then?\" Lith asked.","\"No. That’s impossible.\" The Maiden shook her head. \"Mogar never lies. She has no need to. At most she ignores your questions.\"","\"Then there must be a way.\" Lith pointed out. \"Do you have any idea what that multi-elemental stream combined with Spirit Magic might mean?\"","\"Vaguely.\" She took a chair out of her omni pocket and sat down. \"First of all, I suggest you reconsider your training method. Void Magic requires a high degree of mastery over the elements, and you are just a beginner in Dread Magic.","\"Yet you are trying to manipulate four Cursed Elements at the same time. You are trying to switch the Zero and Cinder you are firing at each other while also manipulating their scattered counterparts to protect yourself.","\"That’s tier five Void Magic, and you don’t even know how to apply it to tier one Dread Magic. In your shoes, I’d use Dread Magic’s dualistic nature to my advantage. Switching a Cursed Element with its scattered counterpart is the simplest Void Magic exercise you can try.","\"If you can’t do that, you’d better wait until we reach a deeper understanding of Dread Magic before trying again.\""]},{"number":4411,"title":"Chapter 4411 Primordial Dread (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"That’s a great idea!\" Lith wanted to resume practicing immediately, but he could feel the mental and physical fatigue of the morning’s experiments catching up with him. \"It doesn’t explain the deep blue energy and the role Spirit Magic plays, though.\"","\"I was getting there.\" Baba Yaga said. \"Consider that Mogar’s shadows are not meant to be taken literally. When she showed you Arthan, she didn’t mean for you to resurrect the Mad King, but that his opus, the Golden Griffon, held the key to mending the cracks in your life force.","\"The same happened with the answer to your question about how to help Solus regain her body. Mogar showed you Ripha at the moment of her death, but our planet was just telling you that you had to trust Ripha’s genius.","\"The tower restored Solus’ form on its own, long before Ripha returned as a Demon. By following this logic, we can assume that whatever process will allow you to use Void Magic on the Cursed Elements doesn’t require all elements.","\"It just applies to all elements. Mogar showed them to you all at once to give you a clue without making the answer too obvious.\"","\"It could be.\" Solus pondered. \"What about Spirit Magic?\"","\"That’s an excellent question, but I’m too tired and hungry to think clearly.\" Baba Yaga raised her hands in surrender. \"I need a good meal to regain my strength and a bit of time to organize my thoughts. Are you coming with me or are you staying here?\"","Lith would have loved to have a light snack and get back to work, but experimenting on Void Magic had turned out to be much more complicated and energy-consuming than finding new Dread Runes.","’The Lodestar can’t suggest answers to me unless I ask Mogar the right questions. So far, I was completely off the mark.’ He thought.","\"I can use a break. Solus?\"","\"I’m right behind you.\" Solus put the Lodestar in stasis and restored the flow of world energy to the other floors to reinforce the security of the Mansion. \"I’m not letting the Lodestar recharge because the little energy it would gain isn’t worth being on edge the whole time. I want us to enjoy our meal.\"","The Mirror Warp brought them into an empty room adjacent to the dining room. After the kids’ bad experience in Lutia, Solus wanted to avoid scaring them.","\"You’re back already? We weren’t expecting you until tomorrow.\" Their arrival pleasantly surprised Elina. \"Luckily for you, I prepared your servings as well. I was going to put them aside for your return.","\"I know how tired you guys are after spending so much time in your lab, and I wanted you to have a proper meal.\"","\"Thank you, Mom.\" Lith used a chore darkness magic spell to cleanse himself of dust and sweat before hugging her.","\"Don’t mention it, sweetie.\" Elina replied.","The meal passed uneventfully. Lith and Solus remained vague about their experiments and spent their time listening to how the others had spent their morning.","Baba Yaga had returned to her hut to eat with her adoptive hybrid children, saving Orion and Jirni from the stroke that meeting her would have given them.","\"Before I forget, Gilly asked me to give you this.\" Kamila handed Lith a piece of paper.","\"How many times do I have to tell her that I’m a married man?\" He grumbled, pretending to be annoyed.","\"Stop being silly!\" Kamila chuckled. \"The only reason that poor girl pesters you is that she can only see her father when you visit Lutia.\"","Gilly was Locrias’ daughter. All the family members of the Sigil Demons had their own living quarters at the Verhen Mansion, but they couldn’t help feeling out of place and preferred living in their homes in Lutia.","\"Tell her that she can have her father-daughter date as soon as I’m done with my current business.\" As Kamila had predicted, the note was a simple request to let Locrias spend quality time with his family.","\"Speaking of business, Master Ajatar will come to visit us soon.\" Morok said. \"He says that he misses his godchildren too much, and doesn’t want them to forget his face.\"","’If only.’ Orion and Jirni inwardly grumbled.","Quylla had scolded her parents multiple times for their poor attitude towards her husband, yet they still resented being passed over for the role of godparents.","\"He can stay here for as long as he wants.\" Solus said.","\"Thanks, but I bet his scaly bottom that this is just an excuse to check on his lair.\" Morok replied. \"You know how Dragons are. Master Ajatar must be worried sick that someone has broken past the defensive arrays and stolen his treasures.\"","After the meal ended, Lith and Solus returned to the Lodestar and found Baba Yaga waiting for them.","\"I’ll use the time we have left to learn more Dread runes and get used to the pressure they exert on my psyche, or I’ll never be able to use tier four Dread Magic.\" She said. \"What about you?\"","\"I already know the runes for the spells I want to create first.\" Lith replied. \"I can do that anytime in the Firing Range. I want to keep working on Void Magic and follow your advice. If you are right, the Lodestar will let me know when I’m on the right path.\"","The Maiden sat cross-legged on the floor, away from Lith to avoid getting caught in the aftermath of a catastrophic failure. She had practiced Dread Magic long enough to grasp the necessary steps to create a tier four spell.","She had to visualize the effects she wanted to obtain with absolute clarity, or the Lodestar would suggest more runes than she could handle and give her a panic attack.","Baba Yaga started with the simplest incantation she could come up with. A blast of Zero surrounded by several air blades and bolts of thunder. Only the air element was quick enough to keep up with Dread Magic.","The others were too slow and would have needed to be carried by the Zero without being frozen, adding another layer of difficulty that the Maiden wanted to avoid. The more complex a spell was, the greater the number of runes it required.","Limiting the interaction between the two elements kept things simple and allowed Baba Yaga to near completion of the spell before the abject terror the Dread Magic runes instilled in her brought her research to a halt.","Zero forced her to relive the worst moments of her past, back when she was just a low-caste Odi who had fled her village to avoid becoming a test subject of the high-caste.","The tower disappeared, and Baba Yaga found herself in the open during a cold winter night, too afraid of being spotted to light a fire. She tasted the blood and raw meat of the red squirrel she had caught with her magic, but she couldn’t afford to cook.","She felt the cold numbing her limbs and making her drowsy as strength abandoned her. Baba Yaga also remembered the crippling fear that she might not wake up ever again if she fell asleep.","Zero Magic also forced her to relive the memories of Ahote, the Firstborn Wendigo, that Baba Yaga had inherited while exchanging her life force with her."]},{"number":4412,"title":"Chapter 4412 Primordial Dread (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The Maiden experienced the desperation and hunger that had led Ahote and her tribemates to feed on the corpses of their kin to survive the seemingly never-ending winter as if it were her own.","She relived all those memories at the same time, and not as Baba Yaga, the powerful white core she was now.","When the visions Zero stirred from Baba Yaga’s primordial fear of cold and fueled by her worst experiences assaulted her psyche, she was back to being a young Odi woman.","A young Odi woman with considerable magical talent, but with a weak dormant mana core who had no idea how to survive in the wilds. Now Baba Yaga was strong enough to light a fire that could melt a mountain, but there was no mana to keep her warm in her nightmares.","The Zero runes with which the Lodestar filled her thoughts spoke of all the terrible things that had happened to her and those that might happen to her were she to lose control over the Cursed Element of water.","Baba Yaga gulped hard, using sheer will to fight back those images, reminding herself of who she was and with whom she was.","’I’m not that person anymore, and part of these memories belong to Ahote, not me.’ She thought. ’The cold can still kill me, but only if I allow it to. I am Baba Yaga, the Mother of all Undead, and I’m in the mage tower of my dear friends, Ripha and Epphy.","’Even if I mess up, they will save me. I know that they can and they will!’ She used those words as a mantra to conquer her fears and add one more Zero rune at a time.","The nightmares from her past would then become even more vivid, arousing details that Baba Yaga believed she had forgotten forever and flooding every fiber of her being with waves of bitter cold.","The Zero element she conjured used the Maiden’s fears to affect the water element in her body, and lowered her body temperature from within. The bite of the physical cold reinforced the memories that haunted her, making them seem as real as the day she had lived them.","With each Zero rune Baba Yaga added, all the work she had done until that moment crumbled. She was back to square one and faced nightmares that became scarier while she became weaker.","The cold robbed her limbs of strength as much as fear paralyzed her mind. The almighty spells she knew like the back of her hand were useless in the visions conjured by the Zero element.","The Maiden could only watch as she moved too slowly to avoid the bites of the wild animals. She saw them coming and remembered where every blow would land, but her stiffened muscles refused to obey her commands.","The only silver lining was that the moment panic made her lose control over Dread Magic, the fear and cold faded away along with the incomplete tier four spell.","On top of that, the more Zero runes she conquered, the weaker the hold of the Cursed Element on her became when conjuring spells of a lower tier.","The danger they posed and the dread they instilled in her never disappeared, not even when she conjured the first Zero rune, Jerak.","Dread Magic was akin to a volatile poison that would explode at the slightest jolt, but practice allowed Baba Yaga to become skilled at handling increasing quantities of it.","Meanwhile, Lith had never stopped working on applying the principles of Void Magic to Dread Magic, but to no avail.","’Baba Yaga was right. I don’t need to conjure two elements for my experiments because conjuring a Dread Magic spell also conjures its scattered counterpart. One element cannot exist without the other.’ He thought.","’ It should make the connection between them clear, yet no matter what I try, the two little bastards just eat at each other!’","Lith worked on the first Choke rune, Bazek.","He had glimpsed the real nature of the elements thanks to his air and earth spell, Mjolnir, and hoped that everything he had learned from his first Void Magic spell would apply to their Cursed versions as well.","So far, reality had begged to differ.","No matter how deep Lith looked inside the Cursed Element, it was devoid of any trace of earth magic and incapable of turning into anything else. He could alter Choke’s shape or size, but any attempt to restore its connection with the world energy failed.","After running out of options, he had decided to try another approach and manipulate the scattered Corruption element to restore the connection between earth and air just enough to make Void Magic possible.","’Even a single drop of stable elements would be enough.’ He thought. ’All I need is a catalyst to start the transformation. Something small that can’t revert the Cursed elements to their natural state and that I can later remove with Domination.’","Lith had gained a fair degree of control over scattered Dread elements, and the relatively weak nature of chore magic was supposed to make things easy for him, yet he made no progress.","Coalescing the scattered Corruption element immediately caused Choke to go wild. The two Cursed Elements jumped at each other like magnets of opposite polarity, leaving Lith with a handful of magnetized pebbles.","Something similar happened when Lith sent sparks of Corruption into the raging storm of the Bazek rune conjured in his palm. He would fail to keep them apart, and grains of dirt fell to the ground.","Using Corruption as the main element produced the same results.","’In their normal state, opposite elements are like water and oil. They don’t mix, and you can keep them in contact.’ Lith thought. ’Cursed Elements, instead, are like fire and gasoline.","’They react violently to each other, and no matter how careful you are or how little of both you use, they always burst into flames. Do you have any suggestions, Solus? ’ Lith asked, receiving no answer.","Solus had given up on her physical form for the experiment. She had returned to her stone body that she had shapeshifted into a circlet and moved on the top of Lith’s head to avoid getting hurt by the wild surges of Dread elements that accompanied his failures.","The idea was to avoid distractions and strengthen the mind link between them. In that form, Solus could see through Lith’s eyes and feel everything he felt, just like old times.","He was back to being her whole world, and that was supposed to help her focus on the conundrum at hand.","’Solus? Are you there? Is everything ok?’ He pushed his consciousness deeper in her mind than he usually would, in the telepathic equivalent of grabbing her shoulders.","’No, it’s not.’ She replied the moment his comforting touch gave her the strength to avert her eyes from the Choke rune. ’Thank the gods that until this moment you’ve kept me out of your Dread Magic experiments.","’I don’t know if I can handle the Cursed Elements. Now or ever.’ Before Lith could ask her what she meant, Solus used a partial mind fusion to show him the effects that Dread Magic had on her."]},{"number":4413,"title":"Chapter 4413 Mental Projection (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Bazek, the Choke rune, stirred the fear of lacking something vital for your survival and the feeling of death slowly creeping in as you failed to get it.","In Solus’ case, it was the desperate need for mana and life force necessary to repair her broken body. After Menadion’s death, she had spent centuries feeling her life slipping away from her as the tower slowly cannibalized itself to prolong her existence.","She had spent her days praying for her mother to return or one of her friends to look for her, but no one ever arrived. Those memories were distant in time and blurred by her amnesia, but after meeting Lith, her life had been far from peaceful.","Solus had experienced the same agony again when Nalear had taken her away from Lith and then when the World Tree had kidnapped and tortured her. Distant and recent past fused into an unrelenting nightmare that held her by the throat.","Even though Solus’ stone ring stuck to Lith’s skin, she couldn’t feel their connection anymore. Panic blinded her to all feelings but despair.","Until Lith had reinforced their telepathic connection, Bazek had thrown Solus’ mind back in her wooden prison, constantly reminding her that every second spent in there might be her last.","Switching her focus to the scattered element of Corruption, Malkor, only made Solus feel worse. It evoked the primordial fear of your body and mind failing you when you needed them the most.","Like when, during a high fever, you know you need to eat and drink to keep your illness from getting worse, but you can’t muster the strength to stand up. Solus knew that feeling best, and had a lifetime of memories about her body falling apart once she had been cut off from a source of nourishment.","Every time she had been seriously injured or had kept her human form for longer than her condition allowed her, cracks had covered her skin and her life force had abandoned her in the form of golden light.","It had happened against the Black Dragon Syrook and under the effects of the parasitic seeds that Maergron, the rightful heir of the Ears of Menadion, had infected her with.","Malkor forced her to relive those moments. To feel the body that she had worked so hard to restore crumble into dust and wonder in terror if she would ever regain it.","Trying to apply Void Magic to the Cursed Elements was akin to standing between spiked walls that slowly closed in on her. No matter where Solus looked, all she saw was her impending death.","’Why didn’t you tell me sooner?’ Lith wrapped her in a telepathic embrace, using his mind to shield her from the effects of Dread Magic.","’I thought I could do it until I couldn’t.’ She replied as she felt the pain tormenting her fade away. ’At that point, I couldn’t think anymore. I forgot where I was and that you were right by my side.’","Solus’ mind shivered like a puppy during a thunderstorm until Lith dispelled the Bazek rune and reality reasserted itself. The visions and nightmares disappeared like mist under the sun, allowing her to breathe again.","’Good gods, Epphy. What happened?’ He also let Menadion inside their Mindspace to reassure Solus.","’I...’ She didn’t know what to say, and threw herself in her mother’s arms, looking for comfort.","A quick mind link brought Menadion up to speed.","’I’m so sorry, Epphy. If it weren’t for my foolishness, you wouldn’t have gone through so much. This is all my fault.’ She said, hugging her daughter tight. ’You practicing Dread Magic, however, is on you.","’How could you do it despite knowing how dangerous it is?’","’I didn’t practice Dread Magic, Mom. I just followed Lith’s experiments through his senses.’ Solus replied. ’Until this moment, Dread Magic unsettled me, but that was it. I watched Lith practice for days, but I never experienced anything aside from the occasional goosebumps.’","’We’re lucky you experienced Dread Magic’s full effect from a safe distance.’ Menadion said. ’If you panicked while handling a Cursed Element, you’d have suffered much worse. This is still too much for you. Let’s get you out of here.’","’Thanks, Mom, but no.’ Solus shook her head. ’This is something I want to try. If I leave, I can’t help Lith with Void Magic, and I’m the only person on Mogar who knows it as well as he does.’","’You won’t be of any help to him if you have another panic attack, sweetie.’ Menadion said. ’You must challenge Dread Magic one rune at a time, like Yaga did. Void Magic requires two runes. You’re asking too much of yourself.’","’Your mother has a point, Solus.’ Lith said. ’I can use your help, but not if it means leaving you traumatized.’","’You too, Lith?’ Solus knew that she was right, but the rejection still hurt.","’Yes, I too care about you. Sue me.’ He replied, making her chuckle. ’If you are so determined to do this, however, there is one thing we can try. It might solve your problem or be just as scary, so think carefully before-’","’I want to do it.’ Solus nodded. ’What do you have in mind?’","’Don’t look at the Dread runes through my mind, but through my memories.’ Lith said. ’It should remove their aura of terror, or at least so I hope. Also, the delay between doing and memorizing is brief.","’If you have any idea, you can share it with me, and I can just start over.’","’Sounds like a plan.’ Solus replied. ’Mom, do me a favor. Don’t access Lith’s memories and focus on me. If I freeze again, I want you to take my stone ring and drag me away.’","’It will be my pleasure.’ Menadion said.","Solus peeked at Lith’s first memory of the Jerak rune and was happy to discover she could study Dread Magic without suffering any side effects.","After confirming that the other Cursed Elements were also safe when observed through a mental projection, Solus used a partial mind fusion to witness Lith’s experiments from the beginning and look for any detail he might have missed.","Much to his and her dismay, she found nothing and came to Lith’s same conclusions.","’You are right, this method is going nowhere.’ She said after triple-checking his memories and letting Lith finish his latest attempt at Void Magic. ’This is an apparently impossible conundrum.","’One element needs a spark of the other to start the process, but the reaction is so violent that there is no time to do anything, even with Domination.’","’Why, \"apparently\"?’ Menadion asked.","’Because of Lith’s vision in the Fringe, Mom.’ Solus replied. ’You’ve been in her Mindscape multiple times. Has Mogar ever lied to you?’","’No. Never.’ Menadion said. ’Lochra and I didn’t figure out all of her riddles, but there was always an answer.’","’This time is no different, Mom.’ Solus pondered the issue as she reviewed Lith’s memories of the encounter with his shadow-self over and over. ’Mogar showed Lith the ultimate form of Void Magic.","’The problem is that we don’t know how to assemble the various pieces of the puzzle to form the final picture.’"]},{"number":4414,"title":"Chapter 4414 Mental Projection (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’What do you say if we use Friya’s method?’ Menadion asked. ’She told us that the key to crafting a dimensional crystal was understanding when she was on the wrong path and looking for the right one.’","Friya had glossed over any important detail of the Suneater’s lessons, but she had shared the struggles that had led her to enlightenment with her friends.","’It’s a good idea.’ Solus nodded. ’Take a break and come here, Lith. Let’s watch Mogar’s answer again with the assumption that everything you’ve done so far is wrong. We need to look for a new path that fits everything we’ve learned about Dread and Void Magic.’","’I’m ready when you are.’ Mind links were fast by nature, and Lith’s interaction with his shadow-self had lasted barely a second before he was forced to retreat.","In a single minute, Lith and Solus studied the fight a thousand times and from every possible angle.","’Dammit, I wish I attempted to get close to that thing more than once.’ Lith snorted. ’We’ve watched that spell until we’re sick of it, yet we haven’t found a single clue about how to replicate it.’","’I wouldn’t be so sure.’ Solus replayed the memory one last time. ’Look at the sequence of the events. The Void Demon Dragon attacked you with the six elements, then he recalled them and merged them into Spirit Magic, and lastly, he switched Spirit Magic with that deep blue energy.","’Since your question was about how to reach Void Magic’s full potential, we can assume that the first part of the attack was either a Tower Tier spell or an application of the technique Grandma showed us.’","Salaark had mastered Void Magic to the point of being also able to control the elemental energies released by the effect of a spell. A fireball would release a flash of light and a shockwave upon exploding, allowing the Overlord to weave all six elements in a new spell with Void Magic.","’The second part is easy to understand. We did the same thing during our apprenticeship under Faluel while learning how to isolate the single elements in Spirit Magic.’","’I remember.’ Lith nodded. ’We combined six elemental streams of equal intensity and injected a spark of life force into them to obtain Spirit Magic. We couldn’t do it without the Hands, though.’","’If I’m right, that’s not an issue.’ Solus replied. ’Mogar showed you the extreme form of Void Magic. What you would achieve when you have complete mastery over all the elements, including those generated by Dread Magic.","’Which leads us to the final part.’ She froze the image at the emerald turning deep blue. ’The sequence is clear. Elemental energy, Spirit Magic, and then whatever that is. According to Mogar, you can’t obtain that blue energy without adding Spirit Magic to the mix first.’","’And how is that-’ Lith stopped talking and started thinking.","Menadion was eager to know what he might have understood from the Solus’ observation, but she knew how dangerous interrupting a mage on the brink of a breakthrough was.","’Answering my question would take him a few seconds, but it might also cost him countless hours of work just to reach this same point again.’ She thought.","’What if this is just a variation of what I did to obtain tier four Dread Magic spells?’ Lith said to himself as he conjured the Bazek rune in his right hand and a stream of emerald energy in the right.","’Maybe I lack the skill to apply Void Magic to Dread Magic in a single step, but what if I split the process into smaller, controlled steps?’","He amplified the earth and air aspects in the Spirit Magic to the extreme, feeling a slight pull at the Choke and Corruption energy in his right hand. At that point, Lith stabilized all three elements with Domination to ensure that not one iota of mana would move without his permission.","He placed the air and earth aspects in the Spirit Magic at opposite sides of the elemental stream, so that the other four would work as a buffer. Choke entered from the left side of the Spirit stream and fed on the earth aspect, while Corruption entered from the left and attacked the air aspect.","Part of the Cursed Elements reverted to normal while an equal amount of the elemental aspects turned into their Cursed counterpart. Still, Lith kept the Spirit Magic balanced by letting the newly formed Dread elements neutralize each other.","The inner layer formed by the other four elements slowed down the process and allowed Lith to force the Dread Elements to form and disappear at a pace he could follow.","The Choke and the scattered Corruption entered the emerald stream of Spirit Magic, painting it deep blue. Lith had no idea what its effects would be and no time to program the Firing Range properly.","He opened a Warp Steps as far away from the tower as he could and released the blue mass of energy where it wouldn’t hurt Solus.","The explosion that ensued generated a noise that could be heard for over a kilometer and a shockwave that shook the treetops of the north side of the Trawn woods so hard that not a single speck of snow was left.","\"That’s it?\" Since Baba Yaga’s focus was already broken, she assessed the destructive power of Lith’s spell before starting over. \"I expected more. Any tier three spell worth its name can do as much, if not even better.\"","\"I know.\" Lith nodded. \"And I would agree with you, if I had used a tier three spell instead of chore magic.\"","\"That was chore magic?\" The Maiden’s eyes went wide in shock. \"I stand corrected. That was amazing.\"","\"Thanks, but it was also very volatile. I had to throw it away in a rush, or it would have exploded in my face.\" Lith replied. \"Moreover, I have no idea how two chore magic spells could unleash such a destructive power.","\"Do you mind taking a look at my memories and giving me a second opinion?\" He offered his hand to Baba Yaga, and she took it.","Solus and Menadion had already reviewed the images several times, but having only theoretical knowledge of Dread Magic, there was only so much they could understand.","\"I’m not sure, but if I had to guess, I’d say that the same elemental layers you used as a buffer to buy yourself enough time to use Void Magic are responsible for the explosion.\" She said after a while.","\"Once you let go of the spell, Corruption and Choke flowed into each other faster and faster until the balance of Spirit Magic collapsed. The barrier formed by the life force fell apart, letting the six elements interact with one another in an uncontrolled way.","\"Congratulations, Lith. Based on what Mogar said, you’ve just cast your first tier six Void Magic spell. The mix of one Cursed Element and its counterpart with the other four regular elements.\"","\"Tier six?\" Lith frowned. \"Do you think there’s also a tier seven?\"","\"If you can perform a tier five Dread Magic spell with two Cursed elements, then yes. Otherwise, no.\" Baba Yaga said."]},{"number":4415,"title":"Chapter 4415 Higher Tiers of Magic (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"We’ve always considered Spirit Magic the sixth tier of magic and Blade Magic the seventh.\" Solus said. \"Is Void Magic so powerful when applied to Dread Magic that it deserves the same ranking?\"","\"This is the first time I’ve heard about this classification, Solus.\" The Maiden replied. \"My answer is yes and no. Yes, Void Magic holds great potential. Switching between two Cursed Elements in battle can deal great damage and bypass many protections.","\"Moreover, according to your own definition, Spirit Magic is tier six and is required to apply Void Magic to Dread Magic, so it should have the same rank.","\"For the same reason, if you conjure a Dread Magic spell with two Cursed elements and you can switch them both, it has higher destructive potential and deserves a higher tier as well.\"","\"No, they are not on the same level. What Dread Magic gains in raw strength, it loses in versatility. This is especially true when you compare Spirit Magic with Dread Void Magic.","\"Spirit Magic can do everything all other spells can do. Attack, defense, and even dimensional magic. It’s a branch of magic in a league of its own with no weak points nor limits. It’s what makes white cores like me nigh-omnipotent.","\"We produce enormous quantities of pure mana that Spirit Magic allows us to shape however we want and cast even complex Gravity Spells that would otherwise exceed our dimensional awareness.","\"Dread Void Magic is indeed more powerful than elemental and Dread tier five magic, but it can only destroy. Maybe, once we get good enough with it, we’ll also be able to shape it into barriers, but always of the destructive kind.","\"You can’t use them to protect the weak, trap your enemies, or build something. So no, Dread Void Magic isn’t at the same level as Spirit Magic. Switching two Cursed elements at the same time would be much more powerful and deserve an upper tier, but only compared to tier six Void Dread Magic.","\"We’d call it tier seven to distinguish the two, but it would still be below pure Spirit Magic in terms of versatility, let alone Blade Magic.\"","\"What if I managed to cast a Tower Tier Dread Magic spell that uses three Cursed elements and their counterpart scattered elements?\" Lith asked. \"Once I apply Void and Spirit Magic, I would obtain a flow of mana where all elements have been replaced by their Cursed version.","\"How powerful would that be?\"","\"Honestly, I don’t know if that would be even possible.\" Baba Yaga shrugged. \"Once you remove the elements in the Spirit Magic, you also remove the buffer area that kept your Dread Void spell stable.","\"Cursed elements are volatile and react violently to each other. I don’t think a spark of your life force would be enough to isolate all six of them. I’m not saying that’s impossible, just that it would be incredibly dangerous.\"","\"Life force?\" Solus echoed. \"That’s how you had the idea to use Spirit Magic to convert a Cursed element into its opposite. You treated them like your Void Flames.\"","\"You got that right.\" Lith nodded. \"When I conjure my Void Flames, I don’t just inject a spark of Chaos into my Origin Flames. It would upset the balance in the world energy, and the resulting Flames would explode in my throat.","\"What I do is coat the elements of the world energy with my human life force so that when the spark of Chaos replaces the darkness element, it cannot reach the light element and stable Void Flames are born.","\"I applied the same principle to Dread Magic, but since I can’t inject a spark of my life force into a Cursed element without it getting destroyed, I used Spirit Magic because it already contains a spark of my life force.\"","\"It is a brilliant stepping stone in the development of Void Magic, but a stepping stone nonetheless.\" Baba Yaga patted his shoulder. \"It’s not something you can use in battle, but it will make an excellent training tool for you and a teaching tool for others.\"","\"I agree with Malyshka, Lith, but I think you’ve bitten more than you can chew.\" Solus said. \"Your understanding of Dread Magic is shallow. You are still stuck at the lower tiers and can’t even shape the Cursed elements according to your will.","\"The only thing you can do right now is shoot them at your enemy. Void Magic is a complex discipline that requires complete mastery over the elements to which it is applied. I say let’s forget about it for now.","\"Focus on tier four and five Dread Magic, and once you’ve figured out what they can do and what your limits are, we can give Void Magic another shot.\"","\"You’re right, Solus, I did get carried away, but put yourself in my shoes.\" Lith said. \"I discovered a new branch of magic, and one that’s almost exclusive to me. I was excited from learning something new every day, and I needed to test how far Void Magic can go.\"","\"I’m not scolding you, Lith. I understand how you feel.\" Solus sighed. \"If anything, I’m envious of you. I love magic as well, yet I’m forced to sit on the sidelines and watch you have fun.","\"To make matters worse, Dread Magic makes your bond with Ely even more special, and ours feel of secondary importance.\"","\"Says the woman who has access to my head 24/7, has Dragon Scales, and most of my life force.\" Lith replied. \"Think about how Kami, who has none of that, must feel. She can’t understand Ely half as well as we do.","\"Dread Magic just rubs salt on her wounds since it adds one more thing from which she’s left out.\"","\"By my Mom!\" Solus went pale at the idea. \"I’ll try to keep my whining to a minimum and away from Kami’s ears, then.\"","\"If you don’t need me anymore, I’m going back to practicing Dread arrays.\" The Maiden said. \"It’s the best way to build up my resistance to the fear effect and expand what we know about Dread Magic without endangering anyone.\"","One of the advantages of conjuring arrays with true magic was that the Dread Runes would exist solely in her mind. Until Baba Yaga injected them with mana, the Dread Runes would manifest their aura of terror but hold no real power.","Failure meant that she would lose her focus and the runes would fade away. If she practiced Dread Arrays with fake magic, instead, each rune would be filled with mana and go haywire the moment she lost control.","\"I’ll keep practicing regular Dread Magic, instead.\" Lith said. \"I’ll move up to tier four only after I can shape the Cursed Elements according to my will. Solus is right. Lacking such a basic ability means my mastery over Dread Magic is lacking.","\"I need more robust foundations.\"","\"And I’ll go back home and ask Ryla to train me.\" Solus replied. \"I can’t help you anymore, and my Indech form needs some serious work.\"","***","Meanwhile, in the Verhen Mansion, everyone was following their morning training routine. Aran, Leria, Lilia, and Leran had moved to the Blood Desert to receive their magical lessons from Salaark’s instructors."]},{"number":4416,"title":"Chapter 4416 Higher Tiers of Magic (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Tista had gone with them as well to practice her combat skills against the Phoenixes of the Nest and better understand the bloodline abilities of her Phoenix heritage.","Quylla had a great time teaching the basics of magic to the newly Awakened Verhens. She was a professor at heart, which made her an excellent but strict teacher.","\"Cast magic until you have no mana, and then run until you have no breath.\" She said. \"Only once your bodies and cores reach their limit are you allowed to have a short break and a snack.","\"Remember to always heal your sore muscles with light magic before using Invigoration, or you’ll hinder your body refinement.\"","\"Is it me, or is this torture?\" Senton asked, wheezing like a bellows.","\"Torture? I’m not giving you one ounce of the tough love I received at the academy.\" Quylla replied. \"As you are, you’d flunk all the first year’s subjects.\"","\"Quylla, dear, this is not an academy, and we do not have the vigor of a fifteen-year-old.\" Elina said amid pants. \"Can’t we take it a little easier?\"","\"If that’s what you want.\" Quylla sighed. \"Remember your words the next time an Awakened comes for Surin, though.\"","She handed the baby girl to Elina, making her turn pale.","\"Mama!\" Surin pulled at Elina’s clothes. \"Num num. Num num!\"","Elina froze in place, having flashbacks of the day of the assault. The baby girl seemed to disappear from her arms, but the warmth and weight Elina felt reassured her it was all in her head.","\"I’ll take five to feed Surin and go straight back to training.\" Suddenly Elina wasn’t tired anymore.","She was too scared of losing her baby girl again to feel anything at all.","\"That was a low blow.\" Rena panted, yet renewed determination lit her eyes.","\"It doesn’t make my words any less true, though.\" Quylla replied. \"Lith won’t always be here to protect you, and there will always be someone crazy or desperate enough to take a shot at you or your kids, Rena.","\"You asked me to teach you because you wanted to be able to protect your families. If you have changed your mind, you can quit anytime.\"","Senton and Raaz gritted their teeth in frustration. Their armor boosted their physical prowess, but so did the equipment any Awakened who might attack them possessed. Vastor’s potions greatly amplified their magical abilities, but they were still weak.","Raaz couldn’t forget how easily the Awakened woman had avoided his attacks once he had lost the surprise effect. He was an Awakened now, but he doubted things would go any differently if they had a rematch.","’At least Raaz got to throw a few punches.’ Senton felt even worse. ’The best I could do was resist the Awakened’s aura of fear and shield my baby girl like a sack of potatoes. Leria is my daughter, yet she protected me.’","As for Rena, she just needed to turn her head to listen to Lenart’s happy laughter as he played with Myrdin to reignite her will to fight.","’My baby boy has already lost his innocence because of those bastards.’ She thought. ’I won’t allow anyone to touch any of them ever again!’","Kamila, Jirni, and Selia, instead, followed Orion’s lessons about advanced magic and sparred with each other to put what they had just learned to the test.","Jirni was glad to have revealed her Awakened status because now she had sparring partners at her core development’s level. Kamila and Selia were both taller and heavier than her, which made up for the gap in their combat skills.","Up to a point, of course.","Selia had no formal training against other humans, and Kamila only knew the fighting techniques Jirni had taught her. The Archon usually had the two women fight together against her to teach them teamwork and be more of a challenge.","\"I’m pretty sure you’re older than me, Jirni.\" Healing magic took care of Selia’s bruises, but it could do nothing for her ego. \"How can you smack us around like dirty rags?\"","\"I’ve learned how to fight when you still complained about not wanting to eat your greens, Selia.\" Jirni replied. \"Also, you are a hunter, not a warrior. You are used to preying on someone who doesn’t fight back.\"","\"You know, I’m proud of my job, but when you put it like that, you make me feel like a coward.\"","\"That wasn’t my intention.\" Jirni raised her hands in apology. \"I simply meant that my combat experience gives me a great advantage over you and that your skillset is ill-suited for direct combat.\"","’An assassin is just a hunter of humans, child, and your light steps and habit of always going for my vitals make you a good substitute for an assassin.’ She actually thought. ’Selia is nothing compared to a Gernoff, but they would never send a green core to kill me.","’On top of that, I’d use Full Guard against a Gernoff, whereas with Selia I can afford to fight without support spells, honing my reaction speed and battle instinct.’","Jirni took care of beating her sparring partners hard enough to temper their bodies without hurting them too much. Selia and Kamila only needed a tier one healing spell to get back on their feet, yet their fighting spirit was a different story.","After one beating too many, they excused themselves and left Jirni to her studies. Kamila taught Selia Dimensional Magic to the best of her abilities, helping the huntress complete the Pilfer exercise.","Much to their surprise, Friya attended the lessons as well, and took more notes than Selia.","\"If this is a joke, it’s not funny.\" Kamila said. \"You’re the only dimensional mage of your generation, and even Tezka recognized your talent. There’s nothing you can learn from me.\"","\"I wish you were right.\" Friya sighed.","\"I beg your pardon?\" Kamila frowned in annoyance.","\"I’m sorry. That came out wrong.\" Friya replied. \"Take my hand. It’s easier if I show you.\"","A quick mind link shared the Suneater’s lesson about the history of dimensional magic with the two women.","\"I have a lot to learn from you just like Tezka did from his apprentices.\" Friya said. \"Your limited talent for dimensional magic forced you to reach a deep understanding of details that I can barely notice because they seem obvious to me.","\"It’s the reason you can teach dimensional magic to Selia while everything I say sounds like gibberish to her.\"","\"So, in your version of the story, you are Tezka, I’m a third-rate Fylgja, and Selia is the village idiot?\" Kamila’s eyes narrowed. \"Someone sure is full of herself.\"","\"That’s not what I meant!\" Friya blushed in embarrassment.","\"Yet that’s sure how it sounded.\" Selia snorted. \"Please ignore the rich kid and resume your explanation, Kami. Maybe, if the village idiot manages to Blink, we can get our first victory on Jirni.\"","\"Pilfer is just the second of many exercises you need to learn Warp Steps, Selia.\" Kamila replied. \"Blink comes after that.\"","\"Let a woman dream, sister!\"","***","\"What in Grandfather’s name did I miss?\" A figure holding a golden token in his hand emerged from the Warp Gate of the Mansion. \"I wasn’t gone for that long, yet a lot seems to have changed.\""]},{"number":4417,"title":"Chapter 4417 A Moment’s Peace (Part 1)","paragraphs":["The man who stepped through the dimensional corridor was 1,82 meters (6’) tall, with handsome features and the lean but muscular build of a warrior. His pale skin highlighted his blonde hair and sapphire-blue eyes, which, along with his refined clothes, gave him a noble appearance.","The stranger knew the safety protocols of the house and waited for someone to come and deactivate the arrays that would trigger the moment he stepped off the raised platform.","All Warp Gates linked to the Kingdom’s dimensional network were susceptible to the Royal Override, but the rest of the Mansion had no such vulnerability.","’I know how much Lith likes his privacy and hates uninvited guests.’ The visitor thought. ’I tried to inform him of my arrival, but he doesn’t respond to his amulet, and neither does Solus.","’I can’t stay here all day, so I’ll call Morok and hope I’m not ruining a convoluted plan of any sort.’","\"Who are you and how did you get my contact rune?\" The Tyrant didn’t recognize the stranger, and his resemblance to Jirni made him suspicious.","’This could be a ploy of the Gernoffs to get to my mildly esteemed mother-in-law.’ He thought. ’I don’t really care for her, but I don’t want to see Quylla cry.’","\"It’s me, you moron!\" The stranger said. \"How could you have already forgotten about your Awakened mentor? I’m Ajatar the Drak- I mean, the Sapphire Dragon. This is the form I take to use human facilities, remember?\"","\"You sure sound like Master Ajatar, but you don’t look like him.\" Morok replied. \"Give me a second.\"","He zoomed in on the hologram until the only thing left were Ajatar’s eyes.","\"That’s really you! I’d recognize your annoyed glare among thousands. I swear to the gods, it always gives me the impression you are wondering whether to bite my head off and check if I need it or it’s just for decoration.\"","\"That’s... surprisingly accurate, but beyond the point.\" Ajatar snorted. \"I’m at the Warp Gate, Morok. You can confirm my energy signature just by looking at me with Life Vision.\"","\"Why didn’t you...\" Morok tried and failed to access the Watchtower and identify the intruder. \"Oh, right. You couldn’t possibly know.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Ajatar asked as the Tyrant Warped to his position and manually added the Sapphire Dragon’s energy signature to the list of those authorized to move freely through the Mansion. \"Also, why can’t I feel the you-know-what?\"","\"It’s a long story.\" Morok used a mind link to bring Ajatar up to speed with the changes in the tower after its latest breakthrough.","’Can I see it, or is there the risk someone might follow us to the keep and discover Solus’ secret?’ The Sapphire Dragon asked.","’More like the risk that Lith kills us both.’ Morok replied. ’The tower’s defensive systems are down when he uses the Lodestar, including the Veil. You are a Dragon now, Master Ajatar, and I don’t think Lith would like you taking a peek at his depowered tower.’","’I’ll ask Lith for a tour when I see him, then.’ Ajatar replied. ’Can I see my godchildren?’","’Of course, but let’s use words from now on.’ Morok said. ’Jirni is already plenty suspicious as she is. She knows there’s something off with this place, and I’d rather not throw oil into the fire by getting caught talking in a lengthy mind link.’","\"Do you think Orikan and Jirya have forgotten about me during my absence?\" Ajatar asked.","\"I don’t know. I don’t remember anything of the time when I was their age, but I was just a regular Tyrant back then.\" Morok shrugged. \"Orikan and Jirya might remember you, but I doubt they are going to recognize you dressed like that.\"","\"Only one way to find out.\" Ajatar stepped through Morok’s Warp Steps and reached the Mansion’s Park.","\"Kids, guess who has come to visit?\" The twins were busy trying to break out of the Doomslayer crib when their father’s voice reached them.","They froze like deer in headlights for a split second before dropping to the floor and acting innocent.","\"Take notes, Master Ajatar. Whenever you hear my children cooing and giggling, it means you’ve almost caught them red-handed.\" Morok said as he unlocked the crib’s magical seals. \"They were up to something, but we’ll never know what.\"","\"How can you be so sure?\" Ajatar asked in confusion. \"They are just babies.\"","\"No, they are very smart babies who play dumb only when they know what they were doing was wrong and want to avoid being scolded. Am I right?\"","The twins nodded, happy for the compliment and already oblivious of what they had attempted just a few seconds ago.","’Father of All Dragons, they are brilliant idiots, just like their father!’ Ajatar thought.","\"That’s right, my cuties.\" Morok took the babies in his arms. \"Do you recognize this handsome stranger?\"","The twins turned to look at the Sapphire Dragon, staring at him with an expression of utter focus.","Orikan’s eyes went wide, and he spoke words that no one older than four months could understand. Jirya argued back and forth with her twin for a while until they both took flight and sniffed their godfather to confirm his identity.","Once they were done, they clung to Ajatar, pulling at his cheeks with their small Tyrant claws and expressing their disappointment with angry noises. They ended their examination by painting Ajatar’s blue with the light from Orikan’s eye and retching.","\"I’m so sorry, Ajatar.\" Orion tried and failed to keep a smirk from appearing on his face. \"They still remember you, but they resent you for leaving. Babies so small have no concept of duty or extraordinary circumstances.","\"Whenever they don’t see someone for a while, they either forget about them or feel abandoned.\"","\"No, they are saying they prefer Ajatar covered in scales.\" Morok replied as the kids blew raspberries and gave the Sapphire Dragon a thumbs-down. \"This is not a nice thing to do, children. You are going overboard. You made yourself clear with the retching.\"","Ajatar shapeshifted into a humanoid Dragon form while staring Orion in the eyes.","The twins erupted in cheers and baby babble, charging at Ajatar like small rockets. He didn’t like the bites and the attempts to rip his scales off much, but Orion’s disgruntled expression was priceless.","\"I missed you too.\" The Sapphire Dragon moved his gaze to the babies as he caressed their hair. \"I brought you a gift to remember me by until the next time.\"","He handed them two identical sapphire scales the size of a napkin, framed with a thin layer of Adamant. Orikan and Jirya couldn’t believe their eyes and bit the scales to confirm it wasn’t just a dream.","The scales, or rather the fragments of Ajatar’s scales, were real, and the twins unwittingly imprinted them while biting them with all their strength.","\"Isn’t it a bit early for you to molt?\" Morok asked.","\"It is, and I didn’t.\" Ajatar replied. \"I chipped my scales more than once during sparring sessions, and those are just two fragments that I collected and shaped to look like perfect scales.","\"I cut them to the millimeter to make them identical and ensure Orikan and Jirya won’t argue over them.\""]},{"number":4418,"title":"Chapter 4418 A Moment’s Peace (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Ajatar pointed at the twins, who were measuring the scale’s length, width, and thickness with their elemental eyes to determine which one was the biggest. Even the metal frame was the same, making Orikan and Jirya sigh in both relief and disappointment.","On the one hand, the twins were happy neither of them would be stuck with a second-rate treasure. On the other hand, quarrelling was a funny way to spend their time, and they were looking for a good reason to go all-out.","\"That was smart of you, Master Ajatar. Orikan and Jirya fight all the time for the silliest reason. \"Sometimes I think they actually enjoy it.\" Morok said, unaware that he was close to the truth.","\"You can drop the honorifics, Morok. I’m not here as your mentor. Only as a godfather. Look, kids, the scales are magical!\" The Sapphire Dragon pulled at the metal frame, and the scale shapeshifted into a baby-sized necklace.","Orikan and Jirya immediately imitated him and put the scales on their necks, throwing the Verhen babies a triumphant look.","\"Tummy ache?\" Valeron the Second asked with sincere worry, ruining the petty gloating of his Ernas friends.","\"Nice move, Ajatar.\" Morok rubbed his beard. \"Did you get the inspiration from Lith’s pendants?\"","\"What pendants?\" The Sapphire Dragon asked. \"I simply noticed how much your children love my scales and ensured they could wear them comfortably. I put a tracking spell on the amulets, among other things.","\"Even if sooner or later they manage to escape, you’ll always know where to find them.\"","\"Especially since, unlike their clothes, Orikan and Jirya will never throw away your scales.\" Quylla gave him a shallow bow as her children moved the pendants under the sunlight to watch them sparkle.","\"Thank you so much, Ajatar. Now we have one less thing to worry about. What other spells did you enchant them with?\"","\"The standard stuff. Self-repair, self-clean, and a few barriers. Here’s a full list of the enchantments.\" He handed her a piece of paper almost entirely covered in thick writing.","\"That’s a lot of enchantments,\" Morok said. \"How much did they cost you?\"","\"Just a few basic ingredients.\" Ajatar dismissed the matter with a wave of his hand. \"Those are my scales. They work both as perfect material and amplifier for my creations.\"","Orion and Quylla knew the Sapphire Dragon was only telling part of the truth. As Forgemasters, they were aware of what kind of ingredients every enchantment would need and how much they were worth on the market.","Yet while the gesture earned Ajatar Quylla’s eternal gratitude, it only put a dent in Orion’s resentment. He and Jirni envied the Sapphire Dragon for having been chosen as the twins’ godparent.","\"Can I play with the kids for a bit?\" The Sapphire Dragon asked. \"My training with the Fire Dragons is not over, and I don’t know when I’ll be able to visit again.\"","\"Sure.\" Quylla said with way too much enthusiasm. \"They are all yours.\"","\"Thanks.\" Ajatar nodded. \"Let’s go, kids. I’m going to show you what Dragonspeed-\"","\"Wah!\" Jirya pointed at the other occupants of the Doomslayer crib. \"Wah, wah, wah!\"","\"Do you want to bring your friends?\" Ajatar asked, but the only answer he got was Orikan joining his sister’s plea. \"Do you want to come?\"","Everyone cheered, bolting out of the open magical containment field and clinging to the Sapphire Dragon.","\"Are you okay with this?\" Ajatar said.","\"Yah!\" Elysia nodded.","\"I was talking with your parents, you little rascal.\" He grunted. \"I can feel your excitement from your Dragon Scales.\"","\"Have fun, but be back for lunch.\" Kamila waved goodbye as the Sapphire Dragon reverted to his full size and disappeared into the sky.","\"Wait.\" Jirni said, raising her hand to get everyone’s attention. \"Can you hear this?\"","The park was so quiet that one could hear the faint rustling of leaves in the wind.","\"Silence.\" Selia’s eyes misted with tears. \"I almost forgot it actually exists.\"","\"Forget what I said earlier, guys.\" Quylla sat down on a lounge chair, taking long sips from the first drink in a while she didn’t have to chug down before something happened. \"Training can wait.\"","Elina looked around the park, torn between the desire to enjoy the rare moment of peace and the urgency to resume the magical practice she needed to protect her children.","\"Are you sure? I mean-\" A soft snoring cut her short.","Quylla had fallen asleep after the first sip, but the happy smile on her face told Elina she regretted nothing. The noise grew by the second as more people closed their eyes for a second just to fall into a deep slumber.","\"Oh, what the heck.\" Elina said after noticing that she, Friya, and Nalrond were the only ones still awake. \"You two hold the fort. I have some serious catching up to do.\"","She lay down on the soft ground and wrapped herself in the wings of her Scalewalker armor.","\"This is a joke, right?\" Friya said in shock when Elina joined the snoring orchestra a handful of seconds later. \"Raising kids isn’t so stressful. Everyone is just pulling our leg.\"","She caressed her slightly bloated womb, aware that in a few months she would join the club.","\"Don’t worry, dear.\" Nalrond hugged her tight. \"We’ve survived the attacks of Divine Beasts and all kinds of eldritch horrors. Dealing with our kids can’t be more difficult than that. Maybe.\"","\"What do you mean, maybe?\" She asked, not feeling reassured at all.","***","\"What’s going on and where are the babies?\" Lith returned for lunch, finding everyone deep asleep in the park.","At first, he suspected the use of a narcotic gas of sorts. Then he noticed that everyone had pillows, blankets, and serene smiles.","\"This can’t be the result of an enemy attack.\" Solus said. \"Shargein is missing too, and there is no news about sudden natural disasters on my amulet.\"","\"Be quiet.\" Nalrond Hushed them. \"Everything is fine. Ajatar took the babies for a joyride, and the sudden quiet knocked everybody out.\"","\"After all this time. Silence.\" Lith closed his eyes, hearing nothing but the beat of his own heart. \"I would love to take a nap if it weren’t too late and I wasn’t too hungry from all my training! I have to cook while they sleep.\"","\"Let’s go. I’m hungry too, and I don’t trust myself at the stove.\" Solus sighed. \"Let them rest while they can.\"","***","The Sapphire Dragon returned exactly at lunchtime, finding a snoring welcome committee waiting for him.","\"Amateurs.\" He snorted as the babies dismounted from his back.","\"You’re back? That was quick.\" Quylla yawned as Orikan and Jirya tugged at her blouse for milk. \"You’ve been gone for just... three hours?\"","\"It felt like a minute.\" Raaz groaned.","\"More like a second.\" Selia whimpered.","\"Come on, sleepyheads. Lunch is served.\" Solus said. \"You are welcome to join us, Ajatar.\"","\"With pleasure.\" He nodded.","The meal was tasty and pleasant, but the Sapphire Dragon sighed more than once.","\"Gods, going back home is going to kill me. Those Fire Dragons got me good.\"","\"Why do you say that? Have they been rude to you? Are they blackmailing you?\" Morok asked.","\"The opposite. They treat me like a king.\" Ajatar replied. \"Your delicious food is as good as what the Fire Dragons eat every day.\""]},{"number":4419,"title":"Chapter 4419 The Quickest Way to the Heart (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Living in a clan means that their members can take turns in the kitchen and prepare proper meals instead of gobbling whole trees and live cattle like Emperor Beasts do.","\"I’ve gotten so used to good food that I dread the moment I’ll have to go back to my old life.\"","\"You know what they say. The quickest way to a man’s heart is through his stomach.\" Lith nodded. \"Do you have any interesting suitors?\"","\"I got plenty, but no egg in the nest, if that’s what you’re asking.\" Ajatar replied. \"I’m not that stupid. Right now, everyone is making a fuss about me because I’m the only Sapphire Dragon on Mogar.","\"If I had a Hatchling with a member of a powerful clan like the Fire Dragons, however, they’d claim the egg, and there would be nothing I could do about it unless I became part of the clan.","\"I won’t let any child of mine become a bargaining chip in a petty political play or be used to put a leash on my neck, Lith. Only an idiot would let his newfound powers go to his head and set up a harem.","\"You draw all the wrong people, and once you’ve spread your seed you can’t take it back. In less than two decades I’d become expendable.\" Thousands of kilometers away, Orpal felt his ears burning for no apparent reason.","\"I need to choose my future partner well, and the Fire Dragons are no candidates. They already have a wide territory, influence, and the Ears of Menadion. I’m just an Awakened regional Lord and have nothing they’re interested in aside from my own bloodline.","\"I would be in no position to dictate my terms of our relationship. The Fire Dragons would get to set the rules, and I could only take it or leave it.\"","Ajatar also possessed the notes regarding his technique for awakening a Lesser Divine Beast’s Guardian bloodline. Still, he had already promised to share them and had no intention of going back on his word.","After the meal ended, Ajatar asked Jirni and Orion for a minute of their time. They moved to the tea room in the Ernas’ living quarters to have some privacy.","\"I didn’t come here only to see Orikan and Jirya.\" He said after Jirni served everyone tea and oven-fresh biscuits. \"I want to ask your help for a project of mine.\"","\"What can we possibly do that the Fire Dragon clan can’t do better?\" Jirni frowned.","The Ernas barely knew the Sapphire Dragon, but according to his background check, he was rich, and the Drake bloodline was ancient enough to have access to any resource Ajatar might need.","’Even a founding pillar of the Kingdom doesn’t amount to much when compared to Leegaain’s original bloodline. Drakes exist for almost as long as he does, whereas the Ernas house was founded a little less than a thousand years ago.’ She thought.","\"You can form a bond of mutual trust with me that goes beyond our shared interests.\" The Sapphire Dragon replied. \"The weapon I Forgemastered for Morok, Grimnir, has become too small after he achieved the violet core.","\"Even worse, it can’t tap into his powers as efficiently as Faluel’s Baby Teeth did. I decided it’s time to fix my mistake and Forgemaster him a bigger, better Davross weapon, and I want to give you the opportunity to contribute.\"","\"And why should we do that?\" Orion snorted. \"You don’t need our help, and I can’t risk you stealing the Ernas’ secret techniques with your Dragon Eyes.\"","\"You don’t know how to cloak your spells?\" Ajatar said in surprise. \"I can teach you how to do that, but first let me answer your question. You should help me to ensure the safety of your son-in-law, Morok Ernas.\"","Hearing their family name attached to the Tyrant still made the Ernas couple flinch.","\"To ensure that no matter what happens to you or me, your daughter won’t become a widow and her children grow without their father. I’m as stingy as any other Dragon, yet I’m willing to part with some of my most prized possessions because I care about Morok and I want to ensure his safety.","\"Moreover, in the unfortunate event something happens to him, and I have to fulfil my role as godfather, I want to be able to look Quylla and the twins in the eyes when I tell them that I did everything I could to protect Morok.","\"I know you don’t like him or me much, but this isn’t about us. This is about the kind of life you want for your daughter and grandchildren.\" Ajatar leaned back in his padded chair and waited for an answer.","His words struck Jirni and Orion like a punch, squeezing the air out of their lungs. The Sapphire Dragon was calm and composed, seeming to have put much more thought into the matter than they ever had.","’The lizard is right.’ Orion thought. ’I’ve been so caught up in my grief for my Little Flower’s death and the Gernoffs’ threat looming over Jirni’s life that I let my dislike for Morok blind me.","’It’s no wonder that my Little One didn’t trust Jirni or me with her babies. I can’t stand Morok, but he’s been nothing but a good husband to my daughter. It’s time I stop whining like a child and start acting like an adult.’","\"We’ll do everything we can to support you, but you have to promise us that whatever you might learn about the Ernas techniques while working with my husband won’t leave your personal notes and that you won’t pass them down to anyone, not even your offspring.\" Jirni said without hesitation.","\"It shouldn’t happen, but even if it does, we have a deal.\" Ajatar offered his hand to Orion, and he promptly shook it. \"I already have the materials I need. Morok is big for a human, but he’s as small as a baby for an Emperor Beast.","\"Four Davross ingots should be more than enough.\" His desire to give his apprentice the best weapons possible was sincere, but his Dragon Greed cried invisible tears of sadness at the thought of giving away so much enchanted metal.","\"I want to do my part, Ajatar.\" Orion replied. \"Whatever you are going to use, please allow me to contribute half the materials. Nothing is worth more than my daughter’s smile.\"","\"As you wish.\" The Sapphire Dragon inwardly sighed with relief. \"The main reason I need your help, however, is that I have no idea how humans fight and I want to keep the secret of the evolved humans’ powers in the family.","\"I don’t trust any outsider with such knowledge. It could be used not only against Morok, but also his children, Lith, and even the people of Zelex.\"","\"You’re damn right.\" Orion snorted.","\"Here is the list of the enchantments I want to put in Morok’s weapons, the shape of their pseudo cores, and the order with which I intend to merge them into a power core.\" Ajatar took a detailed blueprint out of his dimensional amulet.","It contained every detail of the weapons and their abilities, but no mention of the crafting method necessary to assemble the various parts or the Forgemastering technique to combine the pseudo cores."]},{"number":4420,"title":"Chapter 4420 The Quickest Way to the Heart (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’It’s so detailed that any Forgemaster worth their salt can use it.’ Orion admired the elegant simplicity of the blueprint.","\"If you know better enchantments or a better design for an artifact of this kind, I’m open to suggestions.\" Ajatar said. \"I’ll perform all the preparatory steps on my own and assemble the power core before your arrival.","\"We won’t have to share anything, and each one of us will be able to focus solely on their task. You’ll handle the magic circles and conjure the world energy, while I’ll take care of the Forgemastery process.\"","\"I like how you think, yet there is a wrinkle in your plan.\" Orion replied.","\"Which is?\" The Sapphire Dragon asked.","\"I also want only the best for my son-in-law, and I think you are underestimating the importance of the preparatory phase.\" Orion said. \"Here’s my proposal. You show me your best rune sequences for the job, and I show you mine.","\"Then we compare notes and decide which set of runes is better suited to support the power core of the weapons, combining them if necessary.\"","\"I thought you didn’t want to share the Ernas techniques with me.\" Ajatar tilted his head to the side.","\"I don’t, but this requires what, eight rune sequences?\" Orion asked.","\"Ten.\" Ajatar replied. \"One sequence per element, amplification, absorption, dispersion, and cloaking.\"","\"It’s still nothing.\" Orion shrugged. \"If you say that you won’t copy them, I’ll trust your word. Worst case scenario, we are just exchanging a few Runesmithing sets of which some might be inferior to those we already know and only valuable as study material.\"","\"Dream on, human. There’s nothing you can do that my clan hasn’t perfected millennia ago.\" Ajatar snorted. \"Still, I appreciate the thought and am willing to enrich the Ernas legacy with a drop of knowledge of the Drakes.\"","\"We’ll see whose legacy gets enriched, Dragon.\" Orion was just as proud of his own family legacy and the Forgemastering techniques he had created as Ajatar. \"A fair warning.","\"If we use the majority of the Ernas runes, I’ll be the one to perform the Runesmithing process.\"","\"Challenge accepted.\" Ajatar nodded.","***","The following day, while Solus gave Ajatar a tour of the new floors of the tower and the Sapphire Dragon picked Morok’s best tissue samples to use as an amplifier from the Spark, Lith moved back to Lutia.","It gave the Mana Injector the opportunity to advance the Awakening process of that side of the Trawn Woods and Raaz all the time he needed to plan the farm work that would begin as soon as the soil softened.","It also allowed Gilly and the families of the Sigil Demons to spend quality time with their loved ones.","\"You know you can visit me anytime at the Mansion, right?\" Locrias asked.","\"I know, Dad, but there’s nothing we can do there. Even worse, being surrounded by the lavish furniture and Lith’s noble guests makes me feel like a beggar at a Royal Gala.\" Gilly replied.","She avoided mentioning that comparing herself to the women of the Verhen family always did horrors for her self-esteem. After every visit to the Mansion, Gilly looked at her reflection in the mirror and wondered why life was so unfair.","Friya, the handmaidens, and Ryla only made things worse, and the recent Awakening of most of the Verhens had further exacerbated Gilly’s feelings of inadequacy.","\"I hear you.\" Locrias said. \"I’ve never stood in the presence of Archdukes except that in the line of duty, let alone an Archon. Don’t ask me why, pumpkin, but even though I’ve always had a clear conscience, I was always afraid an Archon would dig some dirt on me.","\"If that Archon is someone as shrewd as Jirni Ernas, it’s no wonder you feel uncomfortable at the Mansion.\"","\"Sure, Dad.\" Gilly smiled, lying through her teeth.","She had fallen for Jirni’s doting mother routine line, hook, and sinker. Gilly believed that all those ridiculous rumors about Archon Ernas were just the poisonous words of those who had broken the law and paid the price.","\"Are you sure you want to go to Lutia?\" Locrias asked as they walked hand in hand along the paved road connecting the farmlands to the city. \"I’m wearing Trouble today, and from the Warp Gate in the barn, we could go anywhere.\"","\"Thanks, Dad, but Lutia is fine.\" Gilly replied. \"Also, I wouldn’t be able to enjoy our father-daughter date if I had to worry about what might happen to you if, for any reason, the golem runs out of energy while so far away from Lith.\"","The Spirit Crystal embedded into Trouble’s chest allowed the construct to fuel Lith’s Demons and extended their range of movement. Yet without Lith or an array to recharge the golem, it bled energy with every step it took.","Lith had warned his Demons that he had no idea what would happen to a Sigil Demon if the golem they possessed ran out of Spirit Magic.","Maybe they would just be expelled from their vessel and forced to return to their feather, or maybe their connection with the Void Sigil would be lost and with it the Demon’s tether to the world of the living.","Gilly shuddered at the thought of losing her father for good just for a change of scenery.","\"I know it’s not an ideal solution, but at least Trouble gives you something more than a hard-light construct to touch.\" Locrias said, misunderstanding his daughter’s reaction. \"Do you want me to make it softer? Is it too cold or warm?\"","\"The golem is not a problem, Dad. Quite the contrary.\" Gilly shook her head. \"You’ve gotten really good at manipulating its density, and it almost feels like your real body. It’s much better than holding the hand of a corpse. That would be creepy.\"","\"That’s not a nice thing to say, sweetie.\" Locrias frowned. \"Varegrave and Valia are our friends and comrades.\"","\"I’m sorry, Dad. That came out wrong.\" She replied. \"I mean that since you’ve lost your original body, I much prefer that you wear a golem than a meat suit belonging to another person. That would be creepy.","\"I’d give anything to feel your stupid mustache tickle my skin again.\"","While Varegrave and Valia had returned as Demons seconds after their death and had their corpses perfectly restored, Locrias and Trion had followed Lith and Orpal respectively for months before having the opportunity to answer the Tiamat’s call.","Their bodies were long lost by then, forcing the two Demons to possess a fresh corpse or a Golem whenever they wanted to take a semblance of life.","\"Thanks, baby girl.\" Locrias replied with a sad smile. \"It means the world to me.\"","\"First, no sadness allowed.\" Gilly replied. \"Second, do not call me baby girl in public. I’m almost sixteen now. It would be embarrassing.\"","\"But you always smile when Elina calls Lith her baby!\" He replied.","\"That’s not a smile, Dad. That’s me repressing a laugh.\" Gilly grunted. \"Do you have any idea how funny seeing the Supreme Magus of the Kingdom be treated like that is?\"","\"Enough to not want to be in his shoes, I guess.\" Locrias sighed."]},{"number":4421,"title":"Chapter 4421 Trouble in Ghishal (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Still, don’t say that out loud ever again. You would hurt Elina’s feelings if she heard you. Also, we might meet her and Trion in Lutia. He’s accompanying her for groceries today.\" Locrias said.","\"You should have told me sooner!\" Gilly turned her head like an owl on steroids, sighing in relief when she confirmed no one was close enough to overhear her.","\"How was I supposed to know you’d say something like that?\" Locrias replied. \"Besides, how are things going in Lutia after that scene with the Fastarrows? Are the Lutians treating you and your mother right, or did someone harass you?\"","\"Don’t worry, Dad. Everything is fine.\" Gilly said. \"Everyone treats us with the respect that the family members of a hero of the Kingdom deserve.\"","’I wasn’t worried about you, baby girl.’ Locrias thought. ’I was worried about them.’","Locrias, Valia, and Varegrave had died with honor in the line of duty. Their return as Demons hadn’t diminished their sacrifice nor the respect of the surviving members of the Queen’s Corps stationed in Lutia.","The Corps always looked after their own. Anyone dumb enough to make trouble for the family of one of their comrades would soon have their name recorded in the list of the missing people.","Father and daughter went to Vexal’s bakery first for a breakfast of hot tea and pastries. Vexal served them personally and thanked Locrias for his service. Then they took a stroll along the commercial district, where Gilly avoided the shops that had treated the Fastarrows with hostility during their last visit.","\"How do you remember them all? How does everyone?\" Locrias noticed that more than half of Lutia and most of the tourists still boycotted the establishments.","\"There’s a blacklist and a map, Dad.\" Gilly replied. \"I can’t speak for anyone else, but I’m not giving one coin of my money to people who pick on children just because they are different.","\"If any of those bastards ever dares say anything about you because Lith brought you back as one of his Demons, I’ll give them a piece of my mind!\"","\"That’s not going to happen, pumpkin.\" Locrias shook his head.","\"Yeah, but only because they are smart enough not to say out loud what they think.\" She snorted. \"If they did, I would be the least of their problems.\"","Locrias’ statue at one of the corners of Zekell’s temple made the Demon easy to recognize and impossible to miss in the crowd. Many people greeted him from a distance, and some walked up to him to receive his blessing.","To the followers of the temple, Locrias was a demigod who had defeated death and gained incredible powers. The people who mustered the courage to talk to him hoped to receive either his wisdom or his help.","\"I know it’s a small matter, but please, tell the All-Father that the Ghishal County needs his help.\" A man covered in thick bandages said. \"Living there has become difficult, and not everyone can afford the peace of Lustria.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Lith had only shared the memories that Locrias needed to perform his duties after taking him as one of his Demons, yet Locrias still remembered Lith’s file. \"What’s happening in Ghishal?\"","Locrias knew that the neighboring Ghishal County was ruled by Countess Keyla Lark, daughter of the late Count Trequill Lark.","\"Not much, or you’d read and hear about it everywhere.\" The man sighed. \"Ever since you’ve gotten your Warp Gate here, most thugs and bandits have moved to the Ghishal County.","\"Things got bad when those thugs split our lands like a pie, but nothing that the Countess couldn’t handle. She reinforced the local militia and reimbursed the merchant caravans for the stolen goods, so no one lost money.","\"We thought we would have to endure that mess only for a while, but right when the Countess seemed to have gotten things under control again, the turf war escalated worse than ever.","\"Those bastards have started to invade each other’s territories and rob people blind just to damage their rivals’ ’business’.","\"You can’t have one good day without some thug barging into your store and stealing the money you’ve worked hard for.\" The man’s eyes veiled with tears of frustration. \"Some of my dearest friends had to close their shops, and they are the lucky ones.","\"Many shops had to be closed by the guards because the owners had been killed for a handful of coins.\"","\"I’ll see what I can do.\" Locrias touched the man’s shoulder, using a spell to heal his injuries and share a bit of vitality with him.","\"Thanks, Guardian General.\" The man bowed before walking away, making Locrias flush in embarrassment at the title, and Gilly chuckle.","\"I’m proud of what you did, Dad.\" She said. \"He’s going to have a nice surprise when he changes his bandages. Yet this is supposed to be our time. I don’t like it when you bring your work home.\"","\"I’m sorry, Gilly, but what was I supposed to do?\" Locrias shrugged. \"Send him off and tell him it was not my problem? That poor man needed help.\"","\"I know, and I would never ask you to act like a pompous noble, Dad.\" Gilly nodded. \"Just wait until the end of our date before reporting it to Lith. I don’t want our time to be cut short.\"","\"You have my word.\" Locrias tapped on the Corps’ badge on his chest. \"Do you mind if we drop by Zekell for a second? I want to ask him a few things.\"","\"Not at all.\" She replied with a bright smile. \"You talk with him. I’ll take my time at the Proudhammer Goldsmith. Maybe I can find something you’d like to buy me for my birthday. I’m sixteen this year, Dad.\"","\"Gods, please don’t remind me of that.\" Locrias had feared that moment more than death for fifteen years, and he still did.","The sixteenth year of age marked Gilly becoming an adult. She would start looking for a job, maybe move out of the family home, and worst of all, boyfriends.","\"Why so sour?\" She chuckled. \"Is it for the necklace, the earrings, or because suddenly it’s you who are terrified of having grandchildren?\"","\"What’s this madness? Are you seeing someone already?\" Locrias went pale, and he could have sworn his heart had stopped even though he didn’t have one.","He didn’t mind the jewelry and loved the idea of having grandchildren, but the thought of losing his little girl to some man who certainly didn’t deserve her was more than he could take.","\"Who knows, Dad.\" She replied with a sly smile. \"Maybe if you spent more time home, you would know.\"","\"Fine, I will be more present.\" Locrias grumbled. \"Now tell me, who is this guy?\"","\"No one. I was joking.\" Gilly said, making him sigh in relief. \"Call me when you are done, Dad.\"","\"Girls, am I right?\" Zekell stepped out of his shop to welcome his guests just in time to hear the end of the conversation and see Gilly enter the goldsmith.","\"Didn’t you have only a son?\" Locrias asked in confusion.","\"I do, but I also have a lovely granddaughter, and that brute of Lith took away from me!\" Zekell grunted."]},{"number":4422,"title":"Chapter 4422 Trouble in Ghishal (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Leria spends more time at his home than mine. And don’t get me started about the triplets. Ever since they got their magical beasts, all they do is run through the woods with those furballs!\"","\"I hear you.\" Locrias nodded. \"Now, however, I need you to listen to me. If I leave Gilly in there for too long, I’ll have to buy half your shop for her birthday.\"","\"You say it like it’s a bad thing.\" The blacksmith rubbed his hands with greed.","\"Oh, shut up.\" Locrias told Zekell about the bandaged man and the eerie news from Ghishal County. \"Do you know anything about this?\"","\"Not at all, but that doesn’t mean that man was lying.\" Zekell took out his communication amulet, checking the Web of Knowledge and the interlink. \"No caravan travels while there is the risk of getting caught in a snowstorm or the maw of a pack of hungry beasts.","\"Communications are reduced to a minimum until spring. All I can tell you is that I can’t find any mention of trouble in Ghishal in the news. Yet I have to admit that this situation is weird. This winter I did most of my business via the Warp Gate.\"","He pointed at the local branch of the Mage Association.","\"If the Mage Association heard something about this, they would have told me. Let me ask around a bit.\"","Zekell entered the nearby shops, asking anyone who had recently received or sent a cargo of merchandise outside of Lustria for information about the situation in the neighboring counties. The answer baffled him.","\"No one has heard anything about trouble in Ghishal.\" The blacksmith tormented his well-groomed beard. \"All caravans arrived in one piece and made no mention of bandits.\"","\"This is weird indeed.\" Locrias nodded. \"Thanks, Zekell. I’d better get Gilly and leave before she finds too many things she likes.\"","\"Don’t worry about that. I’ll make you the family discount.\" The Blacksmith said.","\"You mean you’d sell me jewelry at cost as you do with Lith?\"","\"I meant at distant family discount.\" Zekell cleared his throat in embarrassment.","\"Better than nothing.\" Locrias rushed into the goldsmith, opening his seven eyes to look in multiple directions at the same time. \"I’m done, Gilly. We can go now.\"","\"One minute and I’m done as well, Dad.\" She raised her hand to draw his attention, but it was already too late.","Locrias had already seen what she had picked among the vast selection of priceless jewels, and it punched a hole through whatever mana organ had replaced his human heart.","Gilly was in the men’s section of the shop, holding two golden cufflinks shaped after the Royal Crown’s insignia. The same symbol that the members of the Corps carried on their badge and that Locrias had his wife, Cidra, embroider on the breast pocket of his shirts.","\"This is for you, Dad.\" She showed him the elegant design of the cufflinks before putting them on his buttoned cuffs.","\"Why? It’s not my birthday.\" Locrias asked in confusion.","\"Because I love you, silly.\" She chuckled. \"Why that face? You don’t have to worry about the price. I’ve already paid for them with my own money.\"","\"That’s not the issue.\" Locrias had an Adamant-Davross alloy for knees, yet he felt them getting weaker by the second.","\"Then what’s the problem? You don’t like them?\"","\"I love them.\" That was one of those rare times the former captain of the Queen’s Corps was happy not to have a throat. Otherwise, emotion would have choked his voice. \"Thank you for the beautiful gift.\"","\"Don’t mention it, Dad.\" Gilly held his arm. \"But I will if you don’t come back home more often. Mom misses you a lot, you know?\"","\"I miss my girls more.\" Locrias replied as strength returned to him.","They continued window shopping until lunchtime and dined at the Drinking Wolf tavern. Locrias had made a reservation, but even if he hadn’t, the owners always kept two open tables.","One for the Verhens or anyone closely associated with them, and the other for the Vastors. Technically, it was for Tezka, but since he didn’t go anywhere without Filia and Frey, Hida considered the table reserved for the whole family as well.","The new cook had filled the menu with dishes each paired with a different ale, and kept the old one for the non-drinkers. The food tasted much better than before, so father and daughter enjoyed their meal.","Locrias passed the message to Lith via the black chains as soon as they were in range, not to interrupt the date with work. Lith frowned at the news, checking the military database for any unusual reports submitted by the Ranger stationed in the Distar Region.","When he found nothing, he only got more suspicious.","’That man had no reason to lie, and no one would endure that kind of injury for a stupid prank. In my experience, when something is weird, it’s because something bigger is going on.’ He thought as he pressed Keyla’s contact rune.","\"What a nice surprise, Lith. Is there something you need?\"","\"Not at all.\" He replied. \"I called just because I wanted to know how you are doing.\"","\"Wow. Give me a second.\" She kept her hologram on as she pinched her arm and then looked out the nearest window. \"Lith Verhen makes a social call, yet it’s not a dream, and the sky isn’t falling. Who are you and what did you do with my friend?\"","\"Ah, ah! Very funny.\" Lith was annoyed that Keyla found it unbelievable that he had called her without an ulterior motive and even more that she was right. \"Don’t think that I haven’t noticed you have yet to answer my question.\"","\"Everything is fine, Lith. Thank you for asking.\" She replied with a smile that didn’t extend to her eyes.","Not only because she tensed up, but also because the deep bags under her eyes gave her an exhausted look no matter her expression.","\"What about you? How are the kids doing?\" She asked.","\"They are still shocked from the kidnapping attempt, but they are getting better.\" Lith replied.","After a bit of reminiscing about the old times, asking about Jadon, and small talk, Keyla ended the call. Lith was now even more certain that something was wrong, so he contacted Brinja next.","’She’s the Marchioness of the Distar Region. If there’s any problem with the Ghishal County, Keyla can’t keep Brinja in the dark.’ He thought.","\"What do you want?\" As usual, everyone expected a business call from Lith.","Brinja didn’t even raise her eyes from the pile of paperwork she was working on. She was wearing something that looked like a loose jersey with sweatpants, and her long blonde hair was arranged in a messy chignon.","She wore gold-rimmed enchanted glasses that eased the burden of the long hours spent reading on her sky-blue eyes. Milla was in a desk-shaped crib right next to her, playing with squeaky toys that resembled elemental spells.","\"That’s rude!\" Lith said. \"Can’t I call an old friend just to hear about her day?\"","\"The sky is still holding, so no.\" Brinja looked out of the window just long enough to make sure Mogar wouldn’t end there and then. \"What do you want?\""]},{"number":4423,"title":"Chapter 4423 A Friend in Need (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Nice toys.\" Lith refused to admit defeat. \"Where did you get the idea, and what are they made of?\"","\"Fine, I’ll play along.\" Brinja turned to look at the blue gemstone of her amulet and took off her glasses. \"I didn’t make those toys and have no idea what they are made of. Manohar, I mean, Dhiral gifted them to Milla after their last playdate.","\"He called them ’an interactive aid to grasp the elemental structure of the world around us’. He said he shaped them from some kind of foam he grew himself. I was too stunned to follow the rest of his lecture.\"","\"You’re kidding, right?\" Lith could see the first magic rune of each element engraved over and over into the texture of the corresponding toy, forming cartoonish patterns that a baby like Milla would memorize by both touch and sight.","\"I wish.\" As Brinja spoke, Milla squeezed the red toy that emitted a sound that sounded a lot like a baby word for Infiro. \"That boy terrifies me, but if he can help my daughter learn magic, Dhiral will always be welcome in my house.","\"Now, if we have talked long enough to ease your guilty conscience, do you mind telling me what you want? I have work to do.\"","\"Okay.\" Lith told her about Locrias’ conversation with the man from Ghishal and the news he had delivered.","He also shared with Brinja the results of his research and the impression he had gotten after talking with Keyla.","\"At that point, I thought that if she’s not willing to open up with me about her problems, calling Jadon would have been useless. He and Keyla are a tight team. He would have stuck to her same story, and I would have started to second-guess myself.\"","\"It happens when you’re paranoid and see shadows lurking around every corner.\" She nodded. \"Except that, in your case, most of the time you’re right. Calling me was the right thing to do.","\"The Larks and all the minor nobles in the Distar Region answer to me. They need my permission to make any significant change to their fiefs. If something fishy is going on, someone must have mentioned it.\"","She stored the mountain of paperwork inside her dimensional amulet, making space for the most recent accounts from the Ghishal County. It was barely enough. Brinja’s desk was even more cluttered with piles of documents than before.","\"That’s the recent paperwork from Ghishal only?\" Lith was flabbergasted. \"Isn’t it too much?\"","\"No, if you consider that this is a record of everything that happened in the County during winter. From the small villages to the cities, everyone has to report to the local lords, who in turn report to me.","\"It’s one of the many reasons having loyal retainers like the Larks is so important. Since I trust their judgment, I don’t have to read every detail of their reports. They don’t embezzle funds and don’t harass commoners, so they barely need my supervision.\"","Her expression hardened as she sifted through the documents. Brinja organized the reports into several piles, and the more ordered her desk became, the more her eyes narrowed and her frown lines became deeper.","\"I didn’t remember anything noteworthy happening in Ghishal, and I was right.\" She said after a while. \"That man was telling the truth about the criminals of Lustria moving, but it’s not a phenomenon limited to Ghishal.","\"They spread evenly in all the neighboring territories. They caused a spike in the local crime rates and many people got injured in the ensuing power struggle, but it was nothing dramatic.","\"Just the aftershock you’d expect from the sudden influx of powerful players with the means and manpower to carve out a place for themselves in Ghishal’s underworld.\"","\"Then why are you making that face?\" Lith asked.","\"Because these reports are months old.\" She replied. \"Nobles don’t call me every other day unless there is an emergency, especially during winter. The man Locrias met in Lutia is bound to have more recent information than I do.","\"Moreover, even before the snowstorms cut all communications that didn’t go through amulets, there was one oddity that I missed in the reports. The caravans attacked by the bandits were mostly domestic trade.","\"Only a few of the richest caravans moving out of Ghishal suffered more robberies than usual, and none of those coming and going to Lustria were affected. I have too few elements to assess the situation yet, but I can see a pattern already.","\"I’ll have to make a lot of calls to get a better picture of the situation.\"","\"Thanks.\" Lith nodded. \"Please keep me posted. I’m going to pay the Larks a visit and see if they keep lying to my face even after I reveal the few pieces of the puzzle already in my hand.\"","\"I’ll do better.\" Brinja replied. \"I’ll keep you posted and share with you the merits for any issue we might uncover. The Crown made you the Protector of Lustria and a Spellbreaker. This counts as taking care of the Kingdom.\"","\"Thanks, Brinja. Lith out.\" He warned his family of his departure but not the Larks of his arrival.","Lith moved to the tower, using the Warping Mirror to cover a long distance in a single step.","\"Wait for me!\" Solus appeared right after he finished inputting the dimensional coordinates. \"The Larks are also my friends. I want to come too.\"","\"Then I must ask you to take your ring form.\" Lith replied.","\"What? Why?\" Solus blinked several times in confusion.","\"Because even though you know the Larks as well as I do, they barely know you.\" He sighed. \"You didn’t get your body until recently, and Jadon and Keyla haven’t met you outside of Royal Galas.","\"Whatever is going on, they don’t feel comfortable enough to share it with me. Now, things might change if I see them face to face, but not if I bring along someone that they consider a stranger.","\"They would take my interest in their trouble as an active investigation instead of the wish of a concerned friend to help them.\"","\"Damn, if I hate it when you’re right.\" Solus gave up on her physical body and entered the stone ring. \"Leave the tower here. It won’t help us, but it will protect everyone else.\"","Lith needed less than a minute to cover the hundreds of kilometers that separated the Verhen Mansion from the Lark Household. He landed at a safe distance from the main gate, giving the guards time to recognize him before he got too close.","\"Magus Verhen, we weren’t expecting you today.\" A blonde man with captain’s stripes on his shoulders gave Lith a salute. \"Is there something wrong? Do you need assistance?\"","\"Not at all, Captain.\" Lith returned the salute. \"I just decided to pay a visit to Count and Countess Lark. I hope they can spare a few minutes for me.\"","\"Most certainly.\" The man nodded. \"Please, wait here.\"","Normal guards couldn’t afford a communication amulet, so the captain had to send his fastest soldier running to the main building to relay the request. Lith could feel the gazes of young and old men sizing him up like an exotic beast from the legends."]},{"number":4424,"title":"Chapter 4424 A Friend in Need (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Nice move. A surprise visit will make it harder for Jadon and Keyla to send you away, while requesting an audience instead of demanding it shows that you are not pulling rank on them and are here as a friend.’ Solus said.","’Thanks.’ Lith replied. ’And just a few years ago, you’d have scolded me for being a manipulative jerk.’","’Don’t worry, there’s plenty of time for that.’ She grunted.","\"Count Lark welcomes you, Magus Verhen.\" The captain said after listening to the whispered answer of the still-panting soldier. \"He apologizes for making you wait for a few minutes, but there is important business that he must conclude before he can receive you.\"","\"Tell the Count he has nothing to apologize for. I’m at fault for showing up to his doorstep unannounced.\" Lith’s fake contrition seemed so genuine that the soldiers gasped and Solus retched.","\"Also, please tell Count Jadon that I’ll wait for him and Countess Keyla in front of the statue of the late Count Lark. I miss Trequill very much, and I’m going to pay him my respects.\"","The mention of the old Count was enough to make the guards jump to attention. His death was their failure, and none of the survivors of that night would ever forget it.","\"It shall be done.\" The captain gave Lith another salute and ordered another soldier to relay the message. \"Allow me to accompany you, Magus Verhen. I’m not much of an honor guard, but it’s the least the Lark Household can do for you.\"","\"It will be my honor.\" Lith nodded, walking towards the park of the mansion with the captain and two more soldiers marching two steps behind him.","It took them a few minutes to reach the site where Orpal had arranged Lark’s corpse like a scarecrow. To forever delete that image from their minds, his children had built a statue of their father, depicting him while he painted.","Jadon had given instructions to the sculptor so that the statue wore Lark’s old gold-rimmed monocle, but with a metal wire replacing the blue silk string to make sure he wouldn’t lose it ever again.","Lith stared at the serene expression of the statue for a while, reminiscing about his fondest memories with the old Count. From their first meeting during Lutia’s Spring Maiden festival to the test drive of the DoLorean.","It was at that point that the images of the ruin that Orpal had wrought on the Lark Mansion cast a shadow over those happy images. Lith could still smell the burned flesh and see the blood spatters cover the pristine snow.","For a moment, corpses littered the area, and Lark’s dead body replaced the statue as past and present overlapped.","’And this is what makes you a manipulative jerk.’ Solus read his thoughts about how to convince Jadon and Keyla to open up to him and sighed.","’I know, but if I do that, I’ll do it for them.’ Lith replied. ’I’ll do it for Trequill, not because I have something to gain from this.’","’And just a few years ago, you’d have never gotten involved in something like this without a lot of gold lining your pockets.’ Solus said. ’You’ve gotten better, Lith.’","The statue of the old count was maintained regularly, but Lith cleaned it from the snow with water magic and got rid of weeds with darkness magic.","By the time Jadon and Keyla arrived, the statue looked brand new, and the old count seemed to be attempting to capture the tranquil beauty of the park during winter.","Lith felt their hearts throb and smelled the salt of the tears misting their eyes, but he neither turned around nor said anything. He just stuck a finger deep in the ground, using magic to make a single flower bloom.","He picked it up, brought it to his heart and lips, and then set it atop the statue’s pedestal. Solus didn’t say anything either, because this wasn’t a calculated gesture Lith had performed to manipulate his friends.","He was showing his old friend Trequill a new magic trick that would have made Lark’s monocle pop out of his eye socket if he were still alive. When nothing happened, the pain in Lith’s heart was no less than Trequill’s heirs.","\"That was amazing.\" Jadon said as soon as he managed to compose himself. \"A flower blooming in winter.\"","\"Dad would have loved it.\" Keyla sniffled. \"He wouldn’t have asked you to do it again only because he loved his garden too much to let it wither and die after a single day.\"","\"He was indeed a wise man.\" Lith turned around. \"Jadon. Keyla. I’m sorry for bothering you. I promise you this won’t take long.\"","\"Don’t mention it.\" Count Lark said. \"We always have time for a friend.\"","\"Thanks.\" Lith nodded. \"Do you mind sending the guards away? I would like to discuss something in private.\"","\"Not at all.\" Keyla dismissed the soldiers with a wave of her hand. \"Please leave, Captain, and make sure that no one disturbs us unless it’s an emergency.\"","\"Yes, your Ladyship.\" The man rapped his fist over his chest and walked away.","\"What’s this about?\" Jadon asked. \"Do you need help dealing with the citizens of Lutia? We heard about how they treated your friend and his family.\"","\"Thanks, but I didn’t come here because I need your help.\" Lith replied. \"I’ve come because I think you need mine.\"","Before they could answer, Lith replayed the conversation between Locrias and the bandaged man with a hologram. Then he told the Larks about his conversation with Brinja and what had emerged from compiling the information from the reports of Ghishal’s local lords.","\"I don’t know what’s happening yet, but it would be easy for me to find out.\" He said. \"Before you say anything, I want to be clear about something. I trust your judgment and your skills as the rulers of Lustria and Ghishal.","\"I’m not here to question your decisions. Hearing that news about one of your counties worried me, and Keyla’s attempt to minimize the issue hurt me. I’m your friend, and if you don’t want me to poke my nose in your business, you just have to say it.","\"Yet if you treat me like an idiot and try to hide things from me, I can only assume that you don’t trust me with the truth. I’d understand if you blamed me for Lark’s fate or the sudden migration of Lustria’s underworld.","\"Your silence, however, is worse than any accusation you might raise. I’m willing to do everything I can to ease the pain that I’ve caused you, but I can’t do it if you don’t talk to me.\"","\"It’s not that, Lith.\" Jadon shook his head. \"We never blamed you for what happened to our father. Gods, if it weren’t for you, he would have died at the hands of his crazy ex-wife, our mother, years ago, and we with him.","\"Dad loved you like a son, and it’s only thanks to you that Lustria and Lutia have developed so much over just a few years. We don’t blame you for the trouble in Ghishal either.","\"Sure, the criminals left Lustria in droves, but most of them moved to other counties and became someone else’s problem.\""]},{"number":4425,"title":"Chapter 4425 Old Friend (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Everything I saved from the drop in the crime rate I shared with Keyla to help her stabilize her fief, and it was more than enough.\" Jadon said.","\"Or rather, it was supposed to be enough. How the entire Lustria’s budget to fight crime cannot be enough to keep the fraction of its underworld that moved to Ghishal under control is beyond us.\"","\"Then there is a problem.\" Lith said. \"Why did you try to keep it a secret from me?\"","\"Because we are ashamed of our incompetence, Lith.\" Kelia clenched her hands so hard that Lith heard them pop from under the fur muffler. \"Dad ran Lustria like clockwork for decades while corruption ran rampant and the Kingdom was on the brink of civil war.","\"He annexed Ghishal to our fief and laid such a solid groundwork for us before he retired that it barely needs maintenance. Yet what did we achieve? We have a Magus under our roof whose name is enough to make nobles and criminals tremble.","\"The Kingdom is more peaceful than ever, and our fief benefits from your Trains and the new Warp Gate in Lutia. We have more than Father could ever dream, and yet we can’t keep a bunch of small-time crooks in line.","\"We’re ashamed because we are failing our father, Lith. We are failing you.\"","\"What do you mean?\" Lith asked in confusion.","\"The Kingdom may be peaceful, but everyone with an amulet and half a brain knows your life is not.\" Jadon shook his head. \"The Lost City in Jiera, the Indech, your children, and now the kidnapping attempt your family had to endure.","\"We are not stupid, Lith. We know that you must have your hands full with more problems than we can imagine. How could we ask you to add our incompetence to your burden and still be able to look at our father’s statue with our heads high?","\"He would turn in his grave if he knew how badly we are doing.\" The Count sighed.","\"I don’t claim I knew your father better than you did, Jadon, but I think you are wrong about this.\" Lith replied. \"Rather than turning in his grave, Trequill would slap the back of your head and tell you that you should have called me when the problems in Ghishal started.","\"Your father and I barely knew each other when he asked me to protect him, you, and Keyla. He knew it was risky, that I might have said no, and that Nana would have done a much better job than you, but he took that leap of faith because he cared more about you and Lustria than his pride.","\"I’m not a kid anymore, and we’ve gone through thick and thin together, Keyla. Do you really think your father would disapprove of you for asking my help?\"","\"No, he wouldn’t.\" Keyla looked at the statue, hoping for a sign from beyond the grave that never came.","\"I’m glad we are on the same page.\" Lith nodded. \"Before we move inside your home to discuss your situation, there’s something I need to do.\"","He took a deep breath, letting the death energy of his Abomination side seep through the now-closed cracks in his life force and reach his eyes. Lith looked around with Death Vision and watched the Larks die dozens of times in a handful of seconds.","Poison and hidden blades were the most frequent cause of death, making him frown. Tier two spells were the next most probable cause, while death by old age was unlikely.","Lith had no idea what it meant, yet he hadn’t activated Death Vision to check the future of Jadon and Keyla. He was looking for someone he hoped not to find. Sadly, he was wrong.","The soul of Hilya, the former head chef of the Lark Household, was still there, standing near the spot she had died. Her expression was of utter disbelief. She had died so suddenly that she had never understood what had happened.","Over two years had passed since that day, yet Hilya was still confused and unable to move on. When she met Lith’s gaze, she waved at him out of habit, expecting him to ignore her as everyone else had until that moment.","Sadness and despair had blurred her features, taking away a part of Hilya’s humanity along with her hope.","So great was her surprise when Lith waved back at her that she flinched. She moved just one step back, but it was the first step after two years of inexplicable paralysis.","\"Before you ask, I want you to know that I’m not indifferent to your fate.\" Lith spoke to empty air, making Jadon and Keyla exchange a worried look. \"I didn’t act sooner because I hoped you would move on on your own.","\"I wanted to spare you the blind rage that my touch inflicts upon those like you and myself, the pain of seeing your and Trequill’s final moments. I didn’t want to reunite with you just to lose you again.\"","Hilya was Lith’s last resort to convince the Larks to open up with him if everything else failed, and the reason Solus didn’t like his plan from the start. Turning her into a Demon was no longer necessary, but it was still the right thing to do.","He called upon the Void, and his head burst into a crown of blue flames. He called upon only one name and created only one chain with the sole purpose of breaking it.","Hilya heeded her name. She heeded the call and understood its meaning. She opened her arms, letting the black chain plunge into her chest, dragging her out of the limbo trapping her and into the physical world.","The connection forced Lith to relive the head chef’s entire life, while Hilya escaped the numbness that had dulled her senses until that moment and finally released the cry that her sudden demise had silenced over two years ago.","\"Get down!\" She yelled at the statue, mistaking it for the real Count Lark. \"That madman is going to kill...\"","Hilya froze, and so did Keyla and Jadon at the sudden appearance of a member of their family they believed lost forever.","\"No, this is wrong.\" Hilya shook her head as everything she had seen and heard until that moment finally made sense. \"He killed me. He killed everyone else and left Count Lark for last.\"","\"Yes, he did.\" Lith nodded. \"That man was Meln Narchat, my disowned brother. I’m sorry about what happened to you, Hilya. I should have stopped him. You, the Count, and the rest of the old staff died because I failed to stop him.\"","\"You can see me?\" The head chef ignored Lith’s self-recriminations and turned to look at him. \"You can hear me?\"","\"Yes, and so can anyone else now.\" Lith pointed at Jadon and Keyla.","\"Young Master, young Lady! Thank the gods you are alright.\" Hilya ran to them and smiled with deep joy as they followed her movements with their eyes. \"Can you see me too?\"","\"Yes, Hilya.\" Jadon pinched himself and then asked his sister to hit him and prove it wasn’t just a dream. \"I know this must sound incredibly stupid, but I need to ask. How do you feel?\""]},{"number":4426,"title":"Chapter 4426 Old Friend (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"As if I’ve just woken up from a long, sad dream.\" She replied. \"You have no idea how many times I called for you, Master Jadon, yet you never replied. No one ever did.\"","\"Is there someone else here with us?\" Keyla asked after Jadon pinched her hand thoroughly. \"Is Dad still here?\"","\"No, there is only me.\" Hilya shook her head. \"There were others with me at first, but they all disappeared after a while. I wanted to go with them, but I couldn’t leave until I warned the Count.","\"Now, I can finally move on. Forgive this useless servant of yours, Young Master and Lady. Maybe, if I were a bit faster, your father would still be alive.\"","\"Why are you apologizing?\" Lith asked. \"Didn’t you hear what I just said? Trequill’s death is my fault.\"","\"I heard you all right, Young Master, and it was all hogwash!\" Hilya referring to Lith as \"Young Master\" again brought a smile to everyone’s face. \"You didn’t fail anyone. Poltus, the Count, and I were happy none of you were there, or that madman would have killed you as well.\"","Lith had come to terms with Count Lark’s death for a long while now, yet those words lifted a weight from his conscience.","’See? What did I tell you?’ Solus said. ’There was no way that Lark or any member of his staff blamed you for what Meln did.’","’What can I say?’ Lith replied. ’I love it when you are always right, Solus.’","\"Before you go, Hilya, can I ask you something?\" Keyla asked.","\"Anything you want, Young Lady.\" Hilya gave her former mistress a perfect curtsy.","\"Do you think Father is angry with Jadon and me for the current state of the Lark Household?\"","\"I couldn’t move from this spot or talk with your father since the day Meln attacked, Young Lady. Yet I’ve seen and heard quite a few things from here. Even while the Lark Household was still in shambles and you were overwhelmed with grief, the gardeners always praised your dedication to your subjects.","\"You and Young Master Jadon have put the safety of your families and the well-being of the people of your fiefs above yourselves, upholding the Lark family name with honor at great personal cost.","\"I’ve known your father for decades, and I can tell you that if he were here, the Count would ask you to forgive him for the mess in which he left you and be proud of you two beyond what words can express.","\"His greatest fear wasn’t death, but to have failed as a parent. The Count was afraid that his mistakes in raising his children might have ruined your lives and caused the fall of the Lustria County that his ancestors had entrusted to him.","\"Yet I’ve seen the Lark Household thrive thanks to your hard work, and the Count would be overjoyed knowing that his spirit lives on in your hearts, children, and every good deed you perform.\"","\"Thanks, Hilya.\" Keyla gave the head chef a deep bow, to which Hilya replied by falling on one knee.","\"I also have a question.\" Jadon said. \"Now that you are on the other side and know everything, can you tell us if Lith really carries the Lark blood?\"","On the one hand, the idea that his father might have been unfaithful, even to Jadon’s wretched mother, upset the young Count Lark. On the other hand, he needed to know if the bond he felt towards Lith could be deeper than he thought.","\"It doesn’t work that way, Young Master, or I would tell you who your enemies are and where you can find them.\" Hilya chuckled. \"Yet I can answer your question. A few years ago, your father grew so tired of the rumors about his alleged affairs that he commissioned a deep background check on Young Master Lith.","\"No connection was found between the Count and the Verhen family, yet no one believed the report when he shoved it in our faces. We thought your father was just embarrassed and was trying to cover his tracks.","\"So, the house staff raised the money for a background check of our own, and sadly it confirmed everything the Count had shown us. Young Master Lith is not your relative, Young Master Jadon, but I like to think he is.","\"Please, don’t resent this old fool for her silly quirks.\" She said while giving the two true Larks a deep bow.","\"I could never resent you, Hilya.\" Keyla replied. \"Please, when you see my father, tell him that we are okay and that we miss him every day. Our children love to hear the stories about their grandfather more than any bedtime story we’ve ever told them.\"","\"I will, Young Lady.\" The head chef nodded with a smile.","\"Please, also tell Count Lark that I miss him as well, and that I’ll never forget our friendship.\" Lith said.","\"I can do better, Young Master.\" She replied. \"If you allow me, I’ll share with the Count everything your black chain showed me about you. Even though indirectly, the Count would get to meet your children and Solus.\"","\"Please do.\" Lith nodded, and Solus cried with joy from inside her stone ring.","\"If there isn’t anything else...\" Hilya looked around, giving the others enough time to speak any last words to her before it was too late. \"I’ll take my leave. I’m tired, and I need to rest. I haven’t had a moment of peace in over two years.\"","The head chef touched the chain in her chest, and her will severed the connection with Lith. Hilya’s soul released a blinding light that dispelled the pitch-black figure of her Demon form for a heartbeat before it collapsed into a brilliant sphere that bolted towards the sky.","The air in the park suddenly felt clearer, and everyone’s chest felt lighter.","\"Now tell me what’s going on in Ghishal.\" Lith said as soon as his chains confirmed there was no lingering spirit left in the Lark estate. \"Don’t leave out any detail.\"","***","Jadon and Keyla brought Lith inside the main building and into the family tea room. They walked in silence, using that time to collect their thoughts and savor the bittersweet feelings left by the brief reunion with Hilya.","Lith said nothing as well, even after the Larks remained silent for several minutes after the tea had been served.","He adjusted himself in the red silk-padded chair, wondering for the umpteenth time whether there was anything he could have done differently to prevent the late count’s demise.","For the umpteenth time, he reached the same conclusion. There was nothing he could have done.","\"There isn’t much to say.\" Jadon cleared his throat, snapping Lith out of his daze. \"It’s just as we’ve told you earlier. After you’ve become a Magus, even wilder rumors about you started to spread across Lustria.","\"After the attack on your Train, the reveal of your Indech Bloodline, and that little stunt you pulled in the temple of the All-Father after your birthday gala, the criminal cartels started to leave Lustria in search of less deadly pastures.","\"You see, the first thing that crime needs to prosper is fear.\""]},{"number":4427,"title":"Chapter 4427 Change the Board (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Only if their victims are too afraid to call the constables and testify against their oppressors can a bunch of rotten people gain enough power to expand a gang into a dangerous cartel.","\"Your Tablets, your presence, and all the wonders you performed took the fear away, Lith. The people of Lustria trusted you more than they feared the local underworld, so they started reporting crimes and stopped withholding information.","\"Corrupt officials were too scared that a Constable might call your wife to keep taking bribes, while the criminals were terrified of ending up like the Frorl Household if they drew your attention.","\"After all, if Magus Verhen razed an ancient noble household to the ground and killed hundreds of well-armed guards for a boy he had just met, what would he do to a bunch of low-lives if one of their victims turned out to be someone he cared about?","\"Long story short, as the illegal profits plummeted and Lustria became a safer place to live in, more and more crooks moved to the neighboring counties, hoping to restart their criminal careers there.","\"Ghishal was just one of the many possible destinations, and at first, our problems weren’t any different from those of the other local lords. I shared with Keyla the resources I no longer needed to fight crime in Lustria, and things settled down quickly.\"","\"That was until a couple of months ago.\" Keyla said. \"We lowered our guard because winter is a hard time for everyone. Even criminals suffer from the cold and can die in a snowstorm, so we assumed the bandits would stay cooped up at home until spring like everyone else.","\"Moreover, only the bravest and the best-equipped merchant caravans dare make regular travels when the weather is bad. They are the toughest nut to crack, and they never needed our help in the past.","\"We couldn’t predict that an unknown group of gangsters would target those caravans and possess the means to overpower the mercenaries hired to protect them.\" She sighed. \"When the problems started, the merchants reinforced their security, but it wasn’t enough.","\"They changed their routes, but the bandits always found them. We helped the merchant guilds at every step of the crisis, providing them with military escorts and better equipment, but nothing changed.","\"Innocent people still get injured or killed, and the goods get taken away. Ever since this started, we can count on the fingers of one hand the successful trading expeditions in Ghishal.\"","\"This sounds like a serious problem.\" Lith pondered. \"Why did no one hear about it before, and why didn’t you ask for Brinja’s help?\"","\"It actually is far from a serious problem.\" Jadon pinched his nose in frustration. \"The increase in armed robberies is barely noticeable compared to the previous years. The only difference is that they succeed almost every damn single time.","\"If it weren’t for winter, this wouldn’t be an issue. If two out of ten caravans get hit, it’s not a big deal. Trading goes on, and everybody has what they need to have a comfortable life.","\"When two out of two caravans get hit, however, the merchant guilds lose lots of money and people lack even the basic necessities. Everyone has food, but not the necessary tools to repair their house if it gets damaged.","\"Without a stable supply of metal, nails and hammers become more valuable than gold. Anything that breaks can’t be replaced. Potions and medical concoctions must be rationed until a cargo finally arrives.","\"Until that moment, the villages without a Healer need to face the danger of long-distance travel or see their loved ones die. You can guess the rest.\"","\"I see, but again, why not inform Brinja?\" Lith asked.","\"Because all the local rulers are in the same situation.\" Keyla replied. \"What’s happening to Ghishal isn’t an isolated phenomenon, and no one wants to be the first to admit they have lost control of their fief.","\"It would mean publicly declaring our incompetence, especially while some of the other nobles are having much better success dealing with the influx of new criminals.","\"Asking the Marchioness for reinforcements would weaken our position and strengthen the rivals of the Lark Household. Being in charge of a county isn’t a birthright, Lith.","\"We’ve been entrusted with the Ghishal County not only as reparations for our mother’s crimes, but also because the Royals needed a loyal retainer and a capable administrator to clean the corruption exposed by the fall of the Ghishal Household.","\"Jadon and I have done an excellent job so far, but if we suddenly prove to be incompetent fools, the Crown would take the Ghishal County off our hands and put another noble house in charge of it without batting an eye.\"","\"On top of that, asking the Lord of the Region to deal with a few bands of common criminals is akin to using a fireball to kill a fly.\" Jadon said. \"There is no plague, no magically empowered monster, and no rival household sabotaging our efforts.","\"This is supposed to be a routine issue that the combined resources of two Counties should be able to resolve with ease.","\"Keyla and I working together doesn’t ease our burden. It only makes our failure more glaring. If we call Brinja, the only way we get to keep the Ghishal County is that she exposes a conspiracy so big that no one can blame us for not noticing it on our own.\"","\"What if I help you?\" Lith asked. \"Would that put you into trouble?\"","\"It’s all a matter of optics.\" Keyla replied. \"If we formally ask for your help, it would be even worse than notifying Brinja. If you move on your own, however, it’s fine. You are a Magus and an officer of the law.","\"Acting upon the request of the man Locrias met is your right. It would be no different from a Constable investigating a crime that’s been reported to them.\"","\"And that’s exactly how we are going to spin it.\" Lith tapped on the armrest of his chair. \"Kami is still a Constable. She’s on maternity leave, but she can resume active duty at her own discretion.","\"If she brings the babies with her and I accompany them to ensure their safety, no one will question my interest in the matter.\"","’That’s quite the understatement.’ Solus inwardly snorted. ’Only a noble with a death wish would be dumb enough to mess with you while you’re protecting your family. The Royals would burn their households to the ground before you have the time to raise an eyebrow.’","\"It’s an interesting idea, but your presence is bound to send the bandits into hiding.\" Jadon pointed out. \"Even if Kamila finds something, it would lead to a dead end, and the raids would resume the moment you leave.\"","\"True, but only if I help Kami in my official capacity as a Magus .\" Lith replied. \"If I declare I’m only there to protect my wife and remain in plain sight long enough, the bandits should relax after a while.","\"On top of that, even if they lay low and the investigation leads nowhere, the next caravans would still reach their destinations safely. Your people would get the supplies they need, and you can use the respite to identify the breaches in your security.\""]},{"number":4428,"title":"Chapter 4428 Change the Board (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I can still buy you enough time to change the board so much that when I leave Ghishal and your opponent crawls out of their hiding place, they will discover you have changed the rules of the game.\" Lith said.","\"And that assuming you and Kamila won’t discover anything useful nor dismantle a single gang.\" Keyla nodded. \"As the Countess of the Ghishal County, I approve of your plan, Lith.\"","***","Verhen Mansion, a few hours later.","\"That’s not what I meant when I said I wanted to spend a bit of time outside the Mansion, Lith.\" Kamila said after Lith explained the situation to her. \"I wanted to go out on a date, not conduct a field investigation.\"","\"Dade! Dade!\" Elysia cheered, still believing that romantic dates revolved around her.","\"Are you saying you don’t want to get involved?\" Lith asked as he shared a family-friendly version of his plans with the kids via the Dragon Scales.","\"Of course, I will.\" Kamila replied. \"Jadon and Keyla are our friends, and the people of Ghishal need our help. It’s just that this isn’t what I expected when you told me you had big news for us.\"","\"I’m sorry for the misunderstanding, Kami, but I need your help.\" He took her hands into his. \"Keyla is right. If I act alone, the bandits go into hiding, and I won’t have anyone to interrogate.","\"I need someone to dig for information and draw the public attention away from me.\"","\"I have only one question.\" She said. \"You need to move around freely to keep an eye on the caravans, yet you are also supposed to be my bodyguard. How do you plan to disappear long enough to patrol the trading routes without blowing our cover?\"","\"That’s a good question.\" Lith pondered. \"One for which I still have no answer.\"","\"But I do.\" Jirni said, conjuring a life-sized construct identical to Lith down to the smallest detail. \"The Royals have been badgering me for months to resume my duty, and a minor case like this is a perfect opportunity for me to stretch my legs after a year of inactivity.","\"Also, since the phenomenon is widespread and you want to keep the Larks out of it, I suggest setting our base of operation in Esha County. We’ll start our investigation from there and conveniently expand it to Ghishal once we find a lead.","\"It will show the Royals my goodwill and draw the attention of the Royal Court away from your friends, Lith.\"","\"It’s an excellent idea, Jirni, but are you sure you want to leave the Mansion?\" He asked. \"Isn’t it too dangerous?\"","\"Not at all.\" Jirni shook her head. \"I know I’m just a bright green-cored Awakened, Lith, but I never planned on disappearing from the face of Mogar until I became a bright violet.","\"Even at that point, I would still be an easy prey for an entire Awakened bloodline. I asked asylum in your home only to buy myself the time to become strong enough to defend myself, and that’s what I did.","\"If the Gernoffs decide to come after me, they will find me ready.\"","\"And me right behind her.\" Orion grunted. \"Unlike you, I won’t leave Kamila’s side for a single moment, Lith.\"","\"That’s quite the construct, Jirni, and it would be useful to cover for my absence, but I can’t bring two figures of your caliber around and not expect a second criminal exodus.\" Lith replied. \"I want to solve the problem, not pass it on to someone else.\"","\"Sure, but how did you become so skilled in Light Mastery?\" Kamila chimed in. \"I can only conjure holograms at best.\"","\"Nalrond gave me a crash course.\" Jirni replied. \"I’m not ashamed to say that I asked him to teach me everything and leave out nothing. When you know all the answers, Light Mastery is not much more difficult than any other branch of magic.","\"As for your objection, Lith, Orion and I would come undercover as well. I only need to inform the Royals about my involvement in the case, and only because I need any merits this mission might earn us.","\"Also, I bet that the Gernoffs will follow you around and recognize me from my energy signature as soon as we reach our destination. I get the Royal Court off my back for a while and throw a juicy bait at the Gernoffs. Two birds with one stone.\"","\"They will also recognize the construct for what it is and know I’m not with you.\" Lith replied. \"What if they attack you while I’m away?\"","\"They won’t.\" Jirni shook her head. \"Put yourself in their shoes. Kami will be there with the kids, and I’ll stick to her under the guise of her personal assistant. Even an idiot wouldn’t make a move against me as long as I’m with her.","\"The Gernoffs are no idiots, and they won’t make any move at all. They will just watch me from a safe distance and try to figure out where the trap is. They’ve already failed to kill me when they believed me helpless. They won’t repeat the same mistake twice.\"","\"But there will be one, right?\" Kamila asked. \"Please, tell me it’s not just a big bluff.\"","\"Of course I’ll set a trap for the Gernoffs, silly girl.\" Jirni lied through her teeth. \"I’ve prepared several contingency plans to cover for every scenario. Yet I can’t share them with you.","\"I need you to play your role and act surprised when the moment is right, or everything will be for naught.\" Lith knew Jirni enough to doubt her words, but that was it.","’The help request came through Locrias, and I had no intention of leaving the Verhen Mansion until a while ago.’ He thought. ’It’s unlikely that Jirni has prepared something on such short notice, but she’s still Jirni.","’Everything is possible with her. She might have planned for her return to active service months ago and just has to make a few adjustments to prepare the field. The only thing I can say for certain is that if I’m confused, the Gernoffs won’t be able to make heads or tails of this.’","Jirni hadn’t lied about her contingency measures, but the absence of traps was a trap of itself. After being fooled once already, the Gernoffs were bound to play their hand close to the vest.","They would study their opponent and the playfield carefully, and when they found nothing, they would only look deeper.","’If we never stay in the same location for too long, the Gernoffs will not have the time to perform a full recon, and doubt will tie their hands.’ Jirni thought. ’They will keep looking for something they cannot find, and once I notice their scouts have gotten complacent, that’s when I’ll lay my trap.’","\"What about Orion?\" Lith asked.","\"A Constable always moves accompanied by a member of the Knight’s Guard.\" He shrugged. \"Since you are supposed to stay with Kamila, the high command will assign her a perfunctory detail of a single man. Me.","\"I’ll shapeshift into a low-ranked cadet who’s your big fan. Nobody but the Gernoffs will recognize me, and with you standing by Kamila’s side, no one will pay a nameless member of the Knight Guard a second glance.\""]},{"number":4429,"title":"Chapter 4429 Rune Stores (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’What do you think, Solus?’ Lith asked","’A proper investigation does require a few staff members.’ She replied as she moved the law books they owned into the Library. ’Orion is right. Not assigning a detail to the Supreme Magus’ wife would be utterly disrespectful, yet deploying a full Knight Guard squad with you present would be a waste of resources.’","’As for Jirni, since Kamila can’t get away from the babies, it’s only common sense that the Royals assign to her someone to perform all the scutwork and look after the kids while she interrogates the suspects.’","\"Let’s do this, then.\" Lith nodded.","***","Lith called the Royals first, informing them of the situation at hand while keeping Keyla and Jadon out of it.","\"I know it’s no big deal, but I feel responsible for this.\" Lith sounded sincere, because he was. \"Between the Tablets, Lutia’s Warp Gate, and the Trains connecting the cities and villages of Lustria to the capital of the Distar Marquisate, I forced the local cartels to relocate.","\"Ghishal County is under the Larks’ supervision, just like Brinja is in charge of all the areas affected by the sudden spike in crime rates as the ruler of the Distar Region.","\"Do not forget that the Dead King killed both Mirim and Trequill because of me. There is a possibility that this is another of Meln’s ploys to get back at me, and we only noticed it in time out of sheer luck.","\"I won’t rest easy until I’m sure that this isn’t the prelude to the attack of a second Upyr army.\"","He had no idea that using Mirim’s name as a decoy played the strings of Sylpha’s heart like a fiddle. The Queen still grieved the loss of her dear friend and wasn’t willing to leave any stone unturned to punish her murderer.","\"We appreciate you bringing this information to our attention and asking for our approval, Magus Verhen.\" Meron needed but a glance to read the fury hiding under Sylpha’s calm appearance.","\"The matter is far below your notice, but we understand your concern. The Crown hereby temporarily extends your authority as the Protector of the Lustria County to the entire Distar Marquisate.","\"You will be granted access to all information and resources you may need, and can perform a summary judgment of anyone you find involved in crimes against the Kingdom or who obstructs your investigation, no matter their social standing.","\"There is only one exception to this rule. You must inform Marchioness Distar before executing the entirety of a local ruler’s household or stripping them of their authority. The chain of command can be changed, but it cannot be broken at any time.","\"The people of the various counties must always have someone they can call in the event a crisis arises. Is that clear?\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\" Lith replied. \"How long does replacing a ruling household take? Time might be a factor, and being untouchable might make corrupt nobles unwilling to cooperate until it’s too late.\"","\"A few hours at worst.\" The King shrugged. \"Every ruler, no matter how small their fief is, has more than one rival family that only waits for the opportunity to take their place.","\"Such households form a shadow government that follows the major events taking place in the fief and make their own decision, comparing the results achieved by the real ruler with the estimates of what would have happened if they had it their way.","\"It makes an excellent practice for those with real administrative talent and humbles those who don’t have it. Moreover, it helps rival households to build their case before petitioning the Royal Court for a takeover.","\"It’s what happened when Lady Nerea reported the Trahans and the Ghishals, or when Archon Ernas found the evidence of Deirus’ treachery. There was no power vacuum because there was always someone who had waited for years, if not generations, to replace their rival.\"","\"I see.\" Lith nodded. \"Now, with your permission, Your Majesties, there is someone who also would like to exchange a few words with you.\"","Lith gave the Royals a bow and stepped back.","Handing over the communication amulet in the middle of a remote audience was highly unorthodox, but the King and Queen assumed their Supreme Magus had good reasons to do it.","’Maybe he wants to show us Elysia’s magical prowess, or maybe Raldarak developed new unknown features as an evolved human.’ Sylpha said via the mind link.","When Jirni’s hologram appeared in the Throne Room, the Royals furrowed their brows.","\"What’s the meaning of this, Archon Ernas? You have your own communication amulet, and we expect you to use it in private.\" Sylpha asked.","\"Whether this conversation is about state matters or just a social call, it’s improper to perform it in the presence of Magus Verhen, just as it was improper of you to spectate his audience uninvited.\"","\"I apologize for the breach in etiquette, Your Majesties, but I can assure you this is no breach of security and that I have good reasons to resort to this ploy.\" Jirni replied while going down on her right knee. \"Please, allow me to explain.\"","The Royals nodded for her to continue, and Jirni told them about the looming threat to her life and her desire to join Lith’s investigation to test the waters.","\"This explains why you suddenly refused to perform your duty and your prolonged absence from the Royal Court.\" Meron’s eyes narrowed in displeasure. \"Who are these people who are after your life, and why didn’t you inform us of your predicament? We could have helped you.\"","\"No, you could not and you still can’t.\" Jirni shook her head. \"I’m facing a group of Awakened who blame me for the events that followed my daughter Phloria falling prey to the Mad Queen’s slave array, and the treaty you signed with the Council ties your hands.","\"You have to follow Awakened justice on such matters, and since the Awakened are only after my life, not the entire Ernas Household, it would have been foolish of me to force you to choose between me and your newfound ally.\"","’Archon Ernas is right.’ Meron thought after mulling over her words for a while. ’If she asked for our help, we would have been between a rock and a hard place. Siding with Archon Ernas would have destroyed our relationship with the Council, while abandoning her would have humiliated us.","’The Crown would have been proven helpless to protect one of its most loyal and successful retainers. By keeping us in the dark, Archon Ernas protected the peace of the Kingdom and the Crown’s honor.’","\"Also, I didn’t inform you of my predicament earlier because my enemies are powerful enough to have planted their agents inside the Royal Court.\" Jirni continued. \"I couldn’t risk someone overheard our conversation and used it against me.","\"They are unlikely to monitor Magus Verhen’s calls, and even if they did, they can’t stay for long without risking getting caught. I’m confident that after Lith expressed his interest in the minor issue of the Distar Marquisate, my enemy’s agents left the Throne Room.\"","\"The Crown praises your resourcefulness, yet we cannot help but wonder why you want to return to active duty now, and why start from such an unremarkable case.\" Sylpha said."]},{"number":4430,"title":"Chapter 4430 Rune Stores (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Because I should have stalled long enough for the Awakened to grieve their fallen and forget about me.\" Jirni lied with a compassionate smile on her face. \"If I’m wrong and they attack me, they’ll find me ready.","\"I’m setting the where and when we might clash, which gives me a significant advantage. The Awakened don’t have the time to set a trap because I’m choosing the mission. Not you or any upper echelon of the Kingdom that might be under surveillance.","\"This, along with my husband’s and Magus Verhen’s presence, should ensure my survival. If I’m right and nothing happens, instead, I will be able to resume my duty and go back to a normal life.\"","\"I wouldn’t be so sure.\" Meron sighed. \"Awakened are stubborn and can hold a grudge for a long time. Still, I trust your judgment and authorize you and Commander Ernas to participate in the investigation. Is there anything else?\"","\"No, Your Majesty.\" Lith shook his head.","\"That will be all then. I wish you luck. Meron out.\"","***","Before departing for Ghishal County, Lith and Jirni made a few final preparations. Lith asked Tista and Faluel to keep an eye on everyone in his absence and be ready to intervene if he needed backup.","Jirni, instead, asked Nalrond to keep constructs of her and Orion moving around the house and park to keep potential Gernoff scouts from noticing their absence. Also, she stopped by the White Griffon Marth and asked Dhiral for a set of elemental toys for Dripha.","\"Sure.\" He nodded, sprouting what looked like six colored foam bonsai with his Dryad powers and then permanently altering their shape and color with light magic. \"I don’t think Dripha will like them, though.","\"Unlike Milla, her temper always gets the best of her curiosity.\"","\"I’ll keep that in mind.\" Jirni looked at Ryssa, who just shrugged.","\"I swear that I’ve never heard of a Dryad as smart as Dhiral at such a young age. We develop fast, but not that fast, and it takes us years to develop a fraction of the skills he uses in his everyday life.\"","\"Is that a bad thing, Mom?\" The baby boy opened his arms to be picked up. \"Did I do something wrong?\"","\"Of course not, sweetie.\" Ryssa took her son in her arms and kissed his forehead. \"You are just... special.\"","No two years old child on Mogar talked like that or displayed that level of magical mastery aside from talented Dragons like Shargein. Dhiral’s friendship with the Wyrmling was the only thing that kept the baby boy from feeling like a human in a world of goldfish.","\"Since I’m already here, can you please make another set for Surin?\" Jirni asked, eager to spare Ryssa from more unsettling questions.","\"I can do that, but are you sure about it? It’s going to be dangerous, and someone might get hurt.\" Dhiral said.","\"Is Surin that talented?\" Jirni was usually devoid of pointless feelings like envy, but the idea of such a stark contrast between her beloved little daughter and Elina’s last born twisted her stomach into a knot.","’What in the gods’ name runs in the Verhen blood? What’s so special about them?’ She thought before she could regain her cool.","\"No. She’s nothing special.\" Dhiral said, making Jirni sigh in relief until she realized he was probably using himself as the benchmark for a baby’s talent. \"But Ely is. I would keep the Rune Stores away from her if I were you.\"","\"The what?\" Jirni and Ryssa asked in unison.","\"Oh, I’m sorry. I meant the squeaky toys.\" Dhiral replied with the kind smile of a teacher explaining to a kid how a doorknob worked.","After Manohar the Second grew another set of Rune Stores and a bit of chit-chat, Jirni Warped from the White Griffon to the Verhen Mansion.","\"I agree with Brinja. There’s something wrong with that kid.\" She said while handing one set of squeaky toys to Dripha and the other to Elina.","\"Mama?\" The baby girl stared at the colorful Rune Stores with a confused expression for a while.","\"What’s the matter, my love? Don’t you like them?\" Jirni asked.","Dripha took the Rune Store shaped like a drop of water, squeezing it a few times before throwing it away in fury.","\"No!\" She snorted. \"Ha. Ha! Uh ha!\"","\"Gods, I have no idea what she’s saying, but I’m pretty sure those are more than angry noises.\" Jirni said. \"The worst part is I don’t know whether to be proud or worried for her.\"","\"Too hard.\" Valeron the Second translated the baby speak for the grown-ups. \"Dripha is saying it’s too hard.\"","\"Baby girl, you’ve had it for less than a second.\" Jirni said. \"You- you understand what that is? Does she realize that thing is covered in magic runes?\"","\"Yeah, why?\" Valeron looked at her as if Jirni had asked him a stupid question.","\"Okay, this settles it. I’m worried.\" Jirni pondered. \"Remember Dhiral’s warning, Elina. Keep the Rune Stores away from Elysia.\"","\"Please, she’s just a baby, and these are just toys.\" Elina squeezed all the Rune Stores at the same time, making the babies cover their ears.","\"No, they are not.\" Jirni shook her head. \"Keep them away from Ral as well.\"","***","\"So? What do you think?\" Elina asked while Lith examined the set of six squeaky toys.","\"They are well made and hold no enchantment whatsoever.\" Lith used Life Vision, Invigoration, and even a few Forgemastering spells to confirm his findings. \"However, my first impression was correct.","\"The fibers of each toy have been woven to form a pattern from the repetition of one of the first magic runes. This one is comprised solely of Jorun runes that fit into each other like pieces of a puzzle, leaving no empty spaces.\"","\"And?\" Kamila asked.","\"And nothing.\" Solus replied after a full scan with the Eyes of Menadion took less than a second. \"By all accounts, this is just a weird toy. Mom?\"","\"I couldn’t have said it better, dear.\" Menadion examined the Infiro Store with all the means and the knowledge at her disposal. \"There is nothing dangerous about this thing. I think you are overestimating the boy.","\"Dhiral is barely older than two and probably believes that missing dessert is the greatest tragedy of life. If there was a way to help newborns learn magic, do you really think that no one in the Awakened history would have thought about this?\"","\"Babies see and experience things differently from us.\" Lith shrugged. \"I can’t feel anything, yet Dripha says it’s hard to understand, and Val recognized the rune pattern without the keen sight of a Tiamat.","\"And don’t get me started with Ely and the Dread Runes. No one in Awakened history ever discovered those either, yet I don’t remember you questioning her talents or wits, Ripha.\"","\"That’s different!\" She snorted. \"You’re a Divine Beast, and she has Cursed Elements flowing through her body.\"","\"And Manohar the First was the greatest genius I’ve ever met.\" Lith replied.","\"Well, that’s obvious, considering you had yet to meet me.\" Ripha said.","\"Enough arguing!\" Solus put herself between them. \"What do you want to do with the Rune Stores, Lith?\""]},{"number":4431,"title":"Chapter 4431 Unique Combination (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Something that, luckily for us, Dhiral can’t conceive yet. An experiment under controlled conditions.\" Lith said.","\"Is that really necessary?\" Elina swallowed hard.","\"Mom, unless you plan on keeping Surin and Dripha away from the other babies until they grow up, sooner or later they are bound to see the Rune Stores.\"","\"No way! At that age, socializing is of the utmost importance.\" Elina replied. \"I bet that if Manohar the First didn’t feel so isolated all his life, he might have grown into a good man. A decent man. A non-Manohar.\"","Marth and Ryssa felt the same and let their son spend as much time as they could with Shargein. Dragon Eyes allowed the Wyrmling to understand everything Dhiral said, while his unique upbringing allowed him to teach the baby boy just as much.","\"Then we have only two choices, Mom.\" Lith said. \"Either we don’t give the baby girls the Rune Stores and potentially cripple their magical education, or we let them have their toys and prepare for the moment Ely gets her hands on them.\"","\"Let’s go with the second option.\" Elina sighed. \"I don’t want Surin to endure unnecessary struggles. Also, maybe Ely can help us understand the danger the Rune Stores pose, and we can teach her how to use them properly.\"","Lith brought the baby girl to the room and sent Valeron to keep Raldarak company.","\"Dya! Dada!\" Elysia bolted to Lith’s chest. \"Mished ya!\"","She hugged him tight before flying around the room and welcoming everyone back.","\"Good gods, Ely.\" Kamila chuckled as she peppered the baby girl’s face with kisses. \"You haven’t seen us in minutes, not days. Are you becoming a spoiled little imp?\"","\"Nah!\" Elysia dismissed the idea with a wave of her hand. \"Mished ya!\"","\"I missed you too, baby girl.\" Solus said, combing Elysia’s soft hair with her fingers. \"Can you please tell us what you make of this?\"","\"Wah?\" Elysia took the water Rune Store Solus offered her, sniffing, squeezing, and biting it.","\"See? What did I tell you? It’s just a toy.\" Menadion crossed her arms in triumph.","\"Or maybe it takes Ely more than three seconds to learn how to use an unknown tool without guidance.\" Lith replied","\"If you ask me, she seems to have already mastered her craft.\" Menadion snorted as the baby girl squeezed the toy over and over.","\"We’ll see.\" Lith sat back and smiled at his daughter. \"Let her have her fun.\"","A few minutes of Elysia giggling and tormenting her new toy later, Menadion had the smuggest \"I told you so\" grin Lith had ever seen.","\"Well, the good news is that thing is just a harmless toy.\" She said. \"The even better news is that I was ri-\"","Elysia had just let go of the Rune Store, but instead of falling to the ground, it was floating before her. Everyone present activated Life Vision to check for an invisible tendril of Spirit Magic, and discovered that the toy was soaked with water magic instead.","\"That’s why Manohar the Second calls them Rune Stores.\" Lith inwardly cursed. \"They work as a medium between mana and elemental energy. The concentric pattern of the runes allows the toys to retain their corresponding element even if supported by a minuscule amount of mana.\"","\"Okay, maybe I was wrong.\" Menadion said. \"But Ely has a powerful core for her age. How can we be so sure this isn’t just thanks to her natural connection with the water element? Conjuring water is the most basic-\"","Elysia answered her question by conjuring a thick mist around the Rune Store that turned into a water bubble and then froze up a second later.","\"Are you sure this is the hill you want to die on, Ripha?\" Lith asked. \"Aran and Leria are talented kids, but it took them one lesson and an entire day to do that.\"","\"That’s because they don’t have a blue streak.\" Menadion said. \"Also, this proves nothing. Dhiral said the Rune Stores are dangerous for Elysia. How is this dang-\"","Elysia giggled harder as the Rune Store released a focused beam of intense cold that covered everything it struck in a thin layer of ice.","\"Mom?\" Solus asked.","The baby girl improved her control over water magic by the second, having the Rune Store fly faster and shooting more cold beams around at the same time. Elysia still remembered her parents’ instructions and only aimed at pieces of furniture away from her family members.","\"Yes, sweetie?\" Menadion replied as her eyes followed the toy’s increasingly powerful energy signature.","\"Can you please shut up? I believe you have jinxed this house enough for one day.\" Solus said.","\"With pleasure.\"","***","\"How is that even possible?\" Quylla asked while watching the footage of Elysia playing with the Water Store.","\"I’ve scanned the Rune Stores with the tower, and I can explain most of what you’ve just seen. The rest is just guesswork that you have to take with a grain of salt.\" Lith said, and Quylla nodded for him to continue.","’I actually understood everything, but there is no way I can tell anyone I learned to use magic as a baby and I remember about it. My infancy is supposed to be no different from anyone else’s, not the second life of an adult.’ He thought.","\"What I know for certain is that Dhiral waved the fabric of whatever the Rune Stores are made of to be an echo chamber for the first magic runes.\" Lith actually said while squeezing the blue toy and producing a sound that closely resembled Jorun.","\"Yet the phenomenon is not limited to the sound. Each Rune Store constantly resonates with one of the first runes, allowing mana to easily bond with the corresponding element and be trapped inside the toy.","\"The combination of the accumulated mana with the resonance effect turns a Rune Store into an elemental amplifier whose efficiency improves the longer you play with it and resets once all the elemental energy dissipates.\"","\"It would explain why Ely’s chore magic got stronger over time, but not how she grasped the concept of multiple elemental states.\" Quylla pondered. \"That’s supposed to be beyond her.\"","\"And here we enter the realm of speculations.\" Lith lied through his teeth. \"I believe that babies have a stronger connection to the primordial forces of Mogar due to their growing cores constantly absorbing fresh world energy, but they lack the reason to make use of their advantage.","\"The Rune Store repeats the first magic runes in a form babies can understand, giving them infinite tries to establish a connection with each element of the world energy. Once a child reaches that connection, the Rune Store becomes a temporary vessel for a first magic rune.","\"Just by playing with it, a child can get a feel for more runes, as it happened to me inside the Lodestar with the Dread Elements or to Elysia whenever she heard someone use first magic.\"","\"I think he’s right.\" Friya said, knowing Lith was right. \"The first rune of any element is the keystone of all its spells. Once you know it, the rest comes much easier.\"","It was what Tezka had taught her about the first dimensional rune, but Friya couldn’t mention that without going back on her word."]},{"number":4432,"title":"Chapter 4432 Unique Combination (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I too think Lith is right.\" Quylla replied. \"Babies must have a high affinity for magic, or Ely, Ral, and Val couldn’t make so much progress so fast. Yet why did Manohar only warn us about Ral and Ely using the Rune Stores?","\"What’s the difference between them and the other children of our home?\"","\"The unique combination of their mana and talent.\" Lith pinched his nose in frustration. \"With their little mana and short attention span, a normal child using the Water Store would have just a better feeling for the water element and maybe soak the toy enough to make it float.","\"As their core develops, the Water Store would conjure more water and work as a teaching tool that becomes more effective over time. By then the child is supposed to have enough mana for a prolonged play session and be smart enough to control their powers.","\"To an Awakened child with a blue streak and the elemental affinity of an evolved human, however, the Water Store is not only a focus for their elemental powers, but also a weapon.","\"The resonance between the runes woven in the toy and Elysia’s mana allows her to control the water element with only a fraction of the focus that she’d need without the Water Store. In a little over ten minutes, she mustered enough mana to hurt someone.\"","\"What about the other Rune Stores?\" Quylla said. \"Do you think Ely would be able to combine their effects and obtain multi-elemental spells if she used them together?\"","\"Good gods!\" Kamila became as pale as a ghost. \"That’s not something I want to find out. Elina, I think that the Rune Stores will do wonders for Surin, but they are too dangerous for my children.","\"I don’t want to think about what might happen if Ely and Ral mistake the Rune Stores for toys and use them to squabble against each other. Please, make sure to always put them away before every play date.\"","\"You have my word.\" Elina nodded. \"I swear to the gods that if Surin reaches anywhere near that level of mastery, she won’t see the Rune Stores again until she’s old enough to receive Lith’s lesson.\"","\"I’m going to ask Dhiral for a couple of sets of Rune Stores for my twins, but I promise I’ll be careful as well, Kami.\" Quylla said. \"Orikan and Jirya are not Awakened, but they are also evolved humans.","\"I’ll let them play with the Rune Stores only under strict supervision and take them away the moment the twins try some funny business.\"","\"Which probably means after five minutes.\" Morok snorted. \"Elysia is a sweet kid who only wants to have fun with her friends, whereas Orikan and Jyria are the embodiment of competitive spirit.","\"I can already see them work like crazy to one-up each other and end up shooting elemental beams like rice at a wedding.\"","\"If that happens, the Rune Stores will have served their purpose, and we’ll put them away forever.\" Quylla replied.","\"Unless those two little imps don’t join their forces and find a way to make Rune Stores out of elemental energy.\" Morok conjured replicas of the toys with the help of his wings and eyes. \"What then?\"","\"I’ve changed my mind.\" Quylla swallowed hard. \"I’ll ask Manohar the Second if he thinks the twins can safely use the Rune Stores and trust his judgment. He was spot on about Elysia.\"","\"This is the end of Mogar.\" Solus sighed. \"Hearing the name ’Manohar’ and ’trust his judgment’ in the same phrase can only be an ill omen.\"","***","Lith and Jirni were still packing for their trip to Esha when Quylla returned from the White Griffon Academy.","\"That was fast.\" Jirni checked the clock and counted less than five minutes. \"How did it go?\"","\"Manohar, I mean, Dhiral happily agreed to make more Rune Stores, but when he heard they were for my twins, he jumped into Ryssa’s arms and started to cry.\" Quylla sighed. \"I’ve never seen her get so angry before.","\"Ryssa kicked me out of the room and into the Warp Gate that brought me back here in a single move.\" Quylla turned around, showing the footprint of the Dryad on the back of her dress before its self-repair properties made it disappear.","\"Thank the gods.\" Jirni said. \"I mean, look at the bright side, sweetheart. It means that your children possess such a talent for magic that even Dhiral acknowledges them.\"","\"Or maybe that they possess such a talent for destruction and mayhem that even someone named after Manohar is terrified of them.\" Quylla plopped on the nearest chair. \"What about you? Are you done with the preparations?\"","\"Almost.\" Jirni replied. \"Picking our aliases is a critical aspect of this mission. We need someone real, with a spotless background, and that small-time nobles don’t have the clearance to reach at the moment even if they try.","\"Otherwise, someone might notice the same people are in two different places at the same time and blow our cover. Moreover, if a high-status noble performs a background check on our aliases, we’ll be notified instantly.","\"It will expose the presence of new potential investigation targets and prove that something bigger is going on in Distar. It’s just a precaution, but I’d rather not be caught unprepared if these bandits are just the tip of an iceberg we can’t see yet.\"","Once Jirni found Orion’s and her new face for the next few days, she studied their personnel files thoroughly. It was unlikely they would meet someone who knew their aliases in Distar, but Jirni never gambled in the line of duty.","She also watched the available footage of the woman she was going to impersonate, memorizing her speech pattern, mannerisms, and gait.","\"I hope you don’t expect me to learn all that stuff.\" Orion said as he watched his wife turn into a perfect imitation of the original Assistant Constable Ytana Sokra. \"I’m terrible with accents.\"","\"Of course not.\" Jirni said while altering her vocal cords until her voice became identical to Sokra’s. \"I’ve picked a Knight Guard as green as grass for you. He’s as stiff as a mannequin, stammers a lot in the presence of superior officers, and doesn’t say much except for ’yes, sir’ and ’no, sir’.\"","\"Cadets.\" Orion chuckled as he studied the available videos of Asani Trairen. \"I swear to the gods, they act all the same. We call this the Rookie Mold.\"","\"Then it shouldn’t be hard for you to behave like that.\" Jirni nodded. \"Just fix your voice and remember that you must be formal with Lith. He’s no longer your peer, but the man Asani Trairen dreams to be.\"","\"I can do that.\" Orion recorded the original form of his life force in a Life Sculpture before altering the natural sound of his voice.","’What are you going to do, Solus? Do you want to stay at the Mansion to look after the others, or do you want to come with us?’ Lith asked via the mind link.","’If we find a few mana geysers, I can do a bit of both.’ She replied. ’Otherwise I’ll stay with you while you interrogate the nobles and look for anything out of the ordinary on them or in their houses.’"]},{"number":4433,"title":"Chapter 4433 Throwing the Bait (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’The rest of the time I’d rather be at home and keep an eye on everyone. They might need my help if the Gernoffs show their faces.’ Solus said.","’It’s been a long time since you’ve been without a body. Are you sure you are going to be alright?’ Lith asked.","’I’ll be fine, silly.’ She replied, moved by his care. ’Now I’m a stone ring because I want to, not because I have to. This is my choice, and it makes a world of difference.’","The group left the Mansion as soon as Jirni and Orion were done with Body Sculpting. Jirni’s alias was over 5 centimeters (2\") taller, but Jirni settled in Sokra’s shoes better with every step she took.","Orion, instead, was now almost 10 centimeters shorter (4\"), and he found it awkward looking at the world from that perspective. His movements were stiff and clumsy, perfect for an insecure rookie tasked with shadowing his idol.","\"Gods, this is awful.\" He grumbled. \"How can Solus live in a body this small?\"","\"Solus is just 1.54 meters (5’1\") tall, dear, while you are now 1.86 (6’1\"). You are far from short.\" Jirni replied. \"Besides, if you consider her small, what am I? A goblin?\"","\"The cutest goblin on Mogar.\" He replied with a wink.","\"Nice save. Now go back in your character.\" Jirni’s expression tensed into that of a young Assistant Constable assigned to a case that could make or end her career.","Between Kamila’s tight relationship with an Archon and Lith’s status as the first Supreme Magus in the Kingdom’s history, even a simple mission like that was the opportunity of a lifetime for someone like Ytana Sokra.","They walked through the Mansion’s Warp Gate and arrived at their destination, the city of Verka. Jirni had chosen Esha County as the starting point of the investigation because of the presence of a Warp Gate.","It allowed them to move quickly and call for more Constables at a moment’s notice. Kamila would need them if the investigation revealed the involvement of a noble household or a merchant guild.","Awakened or not, she and Lith were just two people and couldn’t search entire buildings efficiently while also keeping the suspects from destroying incriminating evidence.","When they emerged on the other side, at the local branch of the Mage Association, all activity stopped, and the room fell silent enough to hear the labored breath of an old merchant.","The stroller appeared first, and the sight of two toddlers with six elemental streaks was akin to a fanfare announcing who came next. Much to everyone’s surprise, Kamila stepped through the Gate, letting the mages sigh in relief.","Lith emerged a split second later, cutting the sigh short and covering those present in a nervous sweat. Jirni and Orion, or rather, Sokra and Trairen, were two steps behind him, but no one noticed them.","The pristine white wings wrapped around the white and gold Magus robe drew the eyes of those who witnessed Lith’s entrance like the apparition of the ghost of the First King.","\"Magus Verhen, what a pleasant surprise.\" A plump middle-aged man with only half of his head still covered by black hair said. \"I’m Great Mage Hormak, and I’m in charge of Verka’s branch. How can I be of assistance?\"","Hormak wasn’t the sharpest tool in the shed, or he wouldn’t have been relegated to a dead-end position in the middle of nowhere, but even he knew that something was wrong. The uniforms the Verhen couple wore told him that it was no leisure trip.","\"It’s a pleasure to meet you, Great Mage Hormak. I’m Royal Constable Kamila Verhen on His Majesty’s service.\" Kamila replied. \"I need to speak with Count Barla, the regent of Esha, but I’m not familiar with Verka. Where can we find his estate?\"","\"We?\" Kamila’s introduction was enough to unsettle Hormak, but the mention of Lith’s involvement made the plump man stutter. \"I mean, it’s a bit far, but I can bring you there quickly, if you allow me.\"","\"Please, do.\" Kamila nodded.","\"It will be my honor.\" Hormak hadn’t recited the chant for a Warp Steps so fast since his days as a student at the Earth Griffon. \"I’m sorry for the inconvenience, but Verka got its Gate only ten years ago, and the Barla family has ruled over Esha for almost a hundred years.","\"They couldn’t relocate their ancestral mansion and lose the history and tradition it represents.\"","\"Don’t worry, I understand.\" Lith replied. \"It’s the same thing in Lustria with the Larks.\"","’This would be a great opportunity to get acquainted with Verhen and pull my career out of the rut.’ Hormak inwardly whined. ’Yet as long as I have to chant spells, I can’t talk. Stupid high-tier magic!’","A cyan-cored mage like Hormak could only cover about ten kilometers (6.2 miles) with each Steps, and the Barla estate was hundreds of kilometers away from Verka.","Soon he was out of breath and mana, yet there was still a long way to go.","\"I’m sorry. I overestimated my strength.\" He said amid pants. \"The Barla estate is in that direction. You can’t miss it.\"","’I beg to differ.’ Solus said. ’His finger trembles so much that I can’t pinpoint an accurate trajectory even with the Watchtower.’","’Don’t waste your energy. There are better methods.’ Lith replied.","\"Thanks, but my companions can’t fly, and the sight of a flying Divine Beast would make the good people of Esha panic for no reason. Also, we can use a guide.\" He said out loud.","\"Then I need a minute of rest.\" Hormak wheezed as he finally noticed the plain Assistant Constable and the unremarkable Knight Guard. \"Maybe an hour.\"","\"I’m sorry, but my wife is on a mission, and she can’t wait that long.\" A wave of Lith’s hand conjured the family car version of the DoLorean. \"You just need to point me in the right direction.\"","’Gods, I’m such a moron!’ Hormak inwardly cursed. ’How could I forget about the Dolmen? I could have spent this time talking instead of chanting. Maybe at this point I could have even gotten the opportunity to exchange contact runes.’","The Great Mage sat in the passenger seat while the rest of the group sat in the back of the car. Lith brought the DoLorean to a high altitude before moving forward.","\"Just go towards those hills, Magus Vehren.\" Hormak said. \"I must say, the Dolmen is everything I heard and more. You are a genius.\"","\"Thanks, but it’s called DoLorean.\" Lith replied, making the Great Mage add his bad memory to the list of his grievances with life. \"I’m glad you feel comfortable. Usually, people get scared, and I have to go slow until they calm down. This will save us some time.\"","\"This is slow?\" Hormak estimated they were travelling around his own flight top speed, so when Lith moved the lever from the third to the fourth notch, the Great Mage felt his stomach jump in his throat.","\"Is this still the right way?\" Lith asked, ignoring the sudden pallor of his guide.","\"A bit more to the left.\" Hormak whimpered. \"When we get close, you should notice a paved road large enough for a stagecoach.\""]},{"number":4434,"title":"Chapter 4434 Throwing the Bait (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"It connects the Barla estate to the highway. I-\"","\"Got it, thanks.\" Lith’s keen sight spotted the uniform grey of cleanly cut stones on the ground, and he pushed the lever up to five, cutting his guide short.","Hormak had yet to get used to that speed when Lith slowed down and started the landing at a safe distance from the main gate.","\"I am Magus Lith Verhen, and I’ve come to talk with Count Barla. Notify your lord that I request an audience with him.\" Lith said as he stepped out of the DoLorean.","The artifact had already alerted the soldiers of the identity of the unexpected guest, and the pristine wings and robes only confirmed it. The two men standing at the entrance dropped their weapons, opened the metal gates, and got on their knees, keeping their hands above their heads where Lith could see them.","\"What are you doing?\" Lith asked. \"I’m not here to arrest you or Count Barla.\"","\"Thank the gods.\" The guards sighed in relief, glad they wouldn’t share the Frorl Household’s fate. \"I mean, we don’t have a communication amulet, Magus Verhen. One of us should take the horse and report your arrival in person.\"","He pointed at a small shack hosting a buckskin and a saddle.","\"It would take too long, and we didn’t want to waste your precious time.\"","\"That would be rude on my part.\" Lith shook his head. \"We need to follow protocol. Jump in. I’ll drive to the mansion, and you will announce me.\"","The soldier gave a salute and rushed to the passenger door. Then he saw the green robe of the Great Mage and opened the next door. Only then did he realize he had jumped from the pan into the fire.","Kamila looked at him in puzzlement, and the babies sniffed at him like hunting dogs.","\"Wee-wee, Mama. Wee-wee!\" Elysia declared as she handed a fresh diaper to the poor guard.","\"Don’t worry, baby girl. The seats self-clean.\" Kamila replied, making the hapless man curse the earlier moment of weakness of his bladder.","\"I’m so sorry.\" He gave the deepest bow he could without headbutting one of the children. \"I-\"","\"We’ve arrived.\" Lith said as he turned around.","The guard was flabbergasted. In just the time it had taken him to make a fool out of himself, the DoLorean had crossed the external perimeter, the park, and stopped in the stagecoach area.","’Was it Warp, flight, or something else? I can’t believe I have to ask the others to tell me what I just experienced.’ The guard bowed again and stepped outside, inwardly swearing like a sailor.","He was still announcing the arrival of the guests to the butler when Count Agheus Barla walked out the door himself.","He was a man in his mid-forties, about 1,75 meters (5’9\") tall, with ashen blonde hair and beard. He wore a silken housecoat with his family emblem embroidered in gold over his heart over a white linen shirt and black pants.","He had come rushing to the door so fast that he had forgotten to take off his fur-lined slippers and wear shoes.","\"Who’s in there?\" He asked while dabbing the sweat from his powdered forehead. \"The Royals? Marchioness Distar? The-\"","\"Supreme Magus Verhen, Milord.\" Fernon, the butler, said.","\"And his wife. They are both in high uniform.\" The guard said, making the Count fear for his life. \"They are also accompanied by Great Mage Hormak and a few toddlers.\"","\"Toddlers?\" Barla felt life return to his limbs. \"Let’s not keep our honorable guests waiting, Fernon. Have the cook prepare our best tea, and tell him that I want it yesterday.\"","\"Yes, Milord.\" The old butler moved fast for his age, yet his steps didn’t cause a wrinkle in his perfectly ironed shirt.","Meanwhile, Lith and the others stepped out of the car, sending a cold shiver running down the Count’s back.","’The good news is that if they had come to kill me, they wouldn’t have cared about formalities, let alone carried the babies along.’ He thought. ’The bad news is that if they came here so suddenly and in uniform, this is not a social visit.","’I haven’t committed any crime worth the attentions of a Magus, but if Verhen is here for one of my friends and I try to protect them, he’ll kill my entire family. Remember the Frorls, Agheus, and don’t end up like them.’","\"Magus Verhen, Lady Magus, to what do I owe this unexpected honor?\" The Count bowed as deeply as his stiff back allowed him.","\"Constable Verhen, please.\" Kamila said as she showed her badge. \"I’m here in my official capacity. These are my assistant, Ytana Sokra, and my honor guard, Asani Trairen. My husband, Magus Verhen, has come to ensure my safety, as he still can’t leave our children’s side.","\"I need to discuss important matters that require privacy and discretion with you, Count Barla. Can we move to your office?\"","\"Of course.\" The Count nodded like a frenzied parrot, leading his guests along the stairs and hallways that separated the entrance to his private quarters. \"I hope this isn’t anything important.\"","\"All matters regarding the Kingdom are important, Count.\" Kamila replied, putting an end to Barla’s attempts to gauge what kind of trouble he was in.","Meanwhile, Great Mage Hormak stood right next to the DoLorean, wondering what to do.","\"I’ve not been invited inside, but I can’t leave without saying goodbye. What if Magus Verhen needs me to go back to Verka?\" He asked.","Yet his real concern was missing the opportunity to talk more with Lith and maybe exchange runes.","\"Don’t ask me.\" The soldier shrugged. \"They closed the door in my face before I could finish my report. I’m not supposed to stay here, but I can’t go back until I’m dismissed.\"","\"At least we can keep each other company.\" Hormak shrugged. \"Let’s go back inside the DoLorean. There’s no point in staying here and freezing our asses.\"","Once inside, he took a flask of liquor and a few snacks out of his dimensional amulet.","\"Help yourself.\" The mage said. \"Do you have any idea why Magus Verhen came here?\"","\"Not a clue. The Count is a decent man.\" The soldier replied.","\"That’s not what I’ve heard. It seems- What’s this smell?\"","\"It must have been one of the babies.\" The soldier lied through his teeth. \"Don’t worry, Lady Verhen told me the seats self-clean.\"","***","At the same time, inside Count Barla’s office, Kamila had just finished explaining the reasons for her visit.","\"I assure you that whoever reported our little problem to you blew things out of proportion, Constable Verhen.\" The Count said. \"Esha is safe, and numbers don’t lie. The increase in the bandit raids is negligible.\"","\"No, they didn’t, Count Barla.\" Kamila shook her head. \"As you said, numbers don’t lie. As the criminals move out of Lustria, honest people move in. Also, while the number of raids isn’t much different from the past, their success rate skyrocketed.","\"Only a few caravans reached their destinations in the past two months, and none of them came out unscathed. I’m here to understand what is happening and bring those responsible to justice, no matter if they took part in the raids or just tried to sweep the problem under the rug.\""]},{"number":4435,"title":"Chapter 4435 What’s not Written (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Kamila’s cold glare delivered the message, making Barla flinch.","\"I can assure you that I’ve done everything in my power to solve the situation. I’m not trying to deny my failure. I’m just pointing out that the reason the soldiers can’t find the bandits and I didn’t know how many people are seeking refuge in Lustria is the same.","\"Winter disrupts all communications and erases all traces. By the time we know of a raid, either the weather turned bad, and we have to wait until it clears up to move out, or we get on the crime scene, and then the weather turns bad, forcing us to seek shelter before we can collect any evidence.\"","The Count had never left his mansion since fall, but he read the reports and always signed them as a participant to create a paper trail of his alleged efforts exactly for a moment like that.","\"I’m not here to point fingers, Count Barla. I’m here to understand how dire the situation of the Distar Region is.\" Kamila replied. \"I’m starting my investigation in Esha simply because you have a Warp Gate.\"","\"I see.\" The Count inwardly sighed in relief. \"Tell me what you need, and I’ll assist you to the best of my abilities.\"","\"As you said, dear Count, winter disrupts all communications.\" Kamila leaned back on her chair. \"I’m sure that’s the reason you and the rest of the counts didn’t inform Baroness Distar of your common problem.","\"It’s also the reason I came here in person. I need the reports of the bandit raids, the investigations that followed, the citizens’ complaints, everything you have, no matter how insignificant. I’ll be the judge of what’s irrelevant and what is not.\"","\"Yes, of course.\" Count Barla nodded. \"Damn winter!\"","He knew that any missing document or withheld information would be considered manifest incompetence at best and willful neglect at worst. Either way, Barla wouldn’t be the Count of Esha for long.","He took his communication amulet and shared everything he had with Kamila, even his private correspondence with the rulers of the neighboring counties.","’I didn’t have much success, but compared to other nobles, I’m King Valeron.’ He thought. ’If I throw them under the carriage, the constables will focus on them, and maybe they will close an eye on my... patient approach.’","\"Well, this is quite a lot of reading material for such a ’small issue’.\" Kamila said as she scrolled the title list of the documents.","\"I just complied with your request, Constable Verhen.\" The Count nodded. \"Esha may be small, but we have dozens of cities and many more villages. I’ve sent you all the reports since the beginning of winter, just to be safe.","\"You’re free to stay here as my guest until you’re done revising the documents. I’ll be happy to answer any questions you may have.\" Or rather, he would have been happy to have the Supreme Magus in his home.","His presence alone would have been a great honor of which the Count would have bragged until Esha was on everyone’s lips.","\"Thank you for your kind offer, but my husband needs to remain close to a Warp Gate at all times for reasons of national security. We’ll return to Verka, and if I have any questions, I’ll contact you through your amulet.\"","***","Lith opened a Steps leading straight to the entrance, and the soldier was finally dismissed. Lith accompanied him back to his post before taking off the ground.","\"Did you get what you came for?\" Hormak asked to break the ice.","\"Yes.\" Lith increased the DoLorean’s speed one notch at a time.","\"Going back to Verka is easy. Just follow the road, and we’ll be there in no time.\"","\"No need.\" Once the lever hit the fifth notch, the DoLorean accelerated enough to open a Warp Steps leading straight to the Home Stone that Lith had left outside the local branch of the Association.","\"That... was fast.\" The poor Great Mage’s hopes of enjoying his ride and proving to Lith that he was more than an insignificant bureaucrat stuck in an insignificant position shattered like a dream at dawn.","\"That’s the point of a DoLorean.\" Lith replied with pride. \"It’s not as fast as a Warp Gate, but it’s the next best thing. It’s too bad the civilian version can’t exceed level three speed, but most mages can’t keep up with level four.","\"Stopping a criminal who got their hands on a DoLorean would become troublesome, so I removed a few features like the Return Warp.\"","’I’m most mages, you damn bastard!’ Knowing that soon any noble could fly as fast as he did with no effort, talent, or the need to attend one of the six great academies shattered Hormak’s pride. ’I can’t even Warp as far as this thing does.’","\"If you need an accommodation, the Mage Association is glad to offer you the suite for our VIP guests.\" The Great Mage regained his composure and focused on what really mattered. Rescuing his career from the bog it was stuck in.","\"You’ll have the privacy and security worthy of the Royals, and I can also grant you access to our magical labs if you need anything.\"","Hormak needed to befriend Lith or at least appear to be close to him to get himself a way out of Verka. Spending a few days together was guaranteed to achieve at least the latter.","\"Thank you for your offer, but I’m not done yet.\" Kamila replied. \"We have to leave right now, but rest assured I’ll mention your assistance in my report.\"","The group informed the Association’s clerk to set the coordinates for their next destination, the city of Narta in the Zusha County. They disappeared in the dimensional tunnel a second later, bringing with them Hormak’s dreams of future glory.","’Did someone notice anything unusual in Count Barla’s home?’ Lith asked via a mind link.","’Nothing.’ Orion replied. ’I used many Forgemastering spells on the way to his office, but I detected the standard arrays for a country noble’s household and no lingering energy signature on the Count.","’He has not used any artifact of recent aside from his communication amulet and dimensional ring.’","’I used both the Eyes and the Ears, but as Orion said, neither the house nor his owner had anything remarkable about them.’ Solus shared her thoughts only with Lith and Kamila.","’The guy is a mediocre liar.’ Jirni said. ’He was scared about something, but that’s hardly a capital offense. On top of that, when you mentioned the bandit raids, he relaxed. Count Barla may have a few kinks, or maybe he skims tax money, but he’s not involved in our case.","’What about your Demons, Lith? Did they discover anything?’","’Aside from an expensive taste in carpets and paintings, no.’ Lith had summoned his Sigil Demons and sent them to investigate the house as they walked behind the Count. ’I’m pretty sure this was a dud.’","’Hold your horses, Lith.’ Kamila replied. ’Just because the Count isn’t an accessory to the crime, it doesn’t mean he’s useless. The data he shared with us can provide us plenty of leads he was too incompetent to notice.’"]},{"number":4436,"title":"Chapter 4436 What’s not Written (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Then why are we going to Zusha already? Shouldn’t we study Esha’s situation first?’ He asked.","’That would be a waste of time.’ Jirni inwardly shook her head. ’If there is no connection between the crimes, each bandit group has to be studied as an individual organism and treated as such.","’If all of them, or just a few groups, are part of a bigger scheme, however, then we can’t make a move until we see the full picture. We are going to collect the reports from the counties affected by the raids and compile them.","’It will allow us to find evidence not only in what is written in the reports, but also in what is missing from them. We can use Jadon and Keyla as a benchmark for an honest noble to predict what kind of inquiries we should expect from the other counts.","’Comparing the data we receive from the Larks with those from their neighbors will allow us to expose those who are not cooperating with the investigation. At that point, we’ll sort out those who are just incompetent rulers from those who are trying to hide something from us.’","’I see.’ Lith nodded. ’A single county means nothing by itself. You want to check whether the nobles in a similar situation wrote similar reports and omitted the same information. It would prove they are working together.’","In the following hours, the group met many Counts Barla and as many Hormaks. Lith remained in each county just long enough to collect the documents regarding the bandit raids before moving on to the next.","Keyla was no exception. They visited her right before lunch, sparing her the cover story and going straight to the point once in the privacy of her office.","\"Thanks for your help.\" She felt a weight lifting off her chest and her age lines became shallower. \"Do you want to see the kids? They are dying to meet you.\"","\"I’m sorry, but we can’t do any favoritism.\" Kamila replied. \"We’ll stay here just long enough to fool your staff into believing we are interrogating you as we did with the rest of the nobles. They must think you are in their same boat and lower their guard around you.","\"If we are lucky, someone will try to exploit your friendship with Lith to learn the direction the investigation has taken. If that happens, let us know, and we’ll tell you what rumors you must spread.\"","\"Sounds like a plan.\" Keyla exchanged the documents so that the timestamp on her amulet and Kamila’s report would match. \"Do I have enough time to pamper these adorable little imps?\"","\"Be my guest.\" Lith unstrapped the babies, who greeted Keyla with a group hug and were rewarded with plenty of baby biscuits.","By lunchtime, they had visited more than half the counties, and they resumed their travels after a short break for a quick meal and let the kids stretch their legs. Seeing new places excited them, but being forced to sit for so long stressed them.","The adults used that time to make a few calls at the Mansion and ensure that nothing out of the ordinary had happened.","\"Everything is fine.\" Tista said. \"We are taking turns keeping Jirni and Orion ’company’. They would love to be out there with you, Kami.\"","\"Say hello to them for me.\"","\"How is it going? Has the investigation started yet?\" Tista asked.","\"No, but it’s a matter of hours now. I’ll call you back. We have to finish our rounds before the end of the day.\" Kamila collected the last batch of reports after sundown, but a few hours before dinner.","She refused Countess Eliba’s offer of hospitality and returned to Idul’s Association branch.","’What’s next, Jirni?’ She asked. ’I’d know what to do if this was a regular investigation, but you haven’t shared your security plans against the Gernoffs with me.’","’Now we rest.’ Jirni replied. ’I’d love to go back to the Mansion, but we can’t afford the distraction of our families. Also, no one can spy on us inside your home, and we want our marks to always know where we are.","’Only when they believe they have understood our intentions will they crawl out of their holes and make a mistake. Follow me.’","Jirni instructed the Association clerk to open the Gate for the city of Garbam in Bolsa County. From there, she asked for the best hotel in the city, ensuring that at least two clerks overheard her.","The local Great Mage pointed her at the Siren’s Song, which they reached in a few seconds with the DoLorean. It was a five-stories tall historic building, with its walls painted the dull, warm red of a spring sunset.","The signboard depicted a winged humanoid woman perched on a small balcony with her head tilted back and her mouth open.","\"It’s not much, but it will have to do.\" Jirni assessed the potential entry points someone like her would use and how to neutralize them before stepping inside. \"Good evening, are the three top floors available?\"","\"I beg your pardon?\" The receptionist, a young woman in her twenties with light brown hair held up in a bun, blinked several times in confusion.","\"We would like to stay here, but only if the three top floors are available and empty.\" Jirni clarified. \"Supreme Magus Verhen enjoys his privacy and doesn’t like having nosy neighbors.\"","\"Well, of course.\" The receptionist’s eyes darted from the tall man in white to the babies in the stroller, recognizing them from the pictures on the posters. \"You’re lucky. Winter is the only time of the year we aren’t fully booked.","\"Garbam is a beautiful city, and if not for the bad weather it would be swarming with tourists.\"","\"I’ll take your word for that.\" Jirni recognized the lie from a mile away and ignored it. \"We take all the rooms on the third, fourth, and fifth floor. We don’t want to be disturbed, so tell the hotel staff to keep away from us unless we call them first.\"","She emptied a small bag full of gold coins onto the counter while assessing how much it would cost to stay there per night.","\"Of course. Absolutely.\" The receptionist had never seen that much money in her life and couldn’t take her eyes off it. \"Is there anything else I can do to make your stay more comfortable?\"","\"Yes. Don’t tell anyone we’re here, and if someone comes looking for us, send them away.\" Jirni replied.","\"Shouldn’t I at least ask for their names?\"","\"Don’t worry about that...\" Jirni read the name from the tag on the girl’s bosom. \"Alika. They’ll tell you on their own and probably repeat it more than once. You send them on their way and take note of who they claim to be once they are gone.","\"Not one second sooner. We’ll make it worth your while.\"","Jirni put a gold coin in Alika’s hand to emphasize the concept.","\"Yes, ma’am. At your service, ma’am.\" The receptionist trembled from head to toe in excitement. \"If you need anything, just ask for me. Don’t trust anyone else! Everyone here is such a gossip.\"","’And from what I can see, you are no exception.’ Jirni nodded and moved towards the stairs."]},{"number":4437,"title":"Chapter 4437 Impossible Dilemma (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Only true luxury hotels could afford an elevator, and only the cream of the crop had small Gates on each floor. The Siren’s Song was just the best hotel in a medium-sized city, which didn’t mean much.","\"Place one Golem here.\" Jirni said once they reached the third floor, and Lith took Raptor out of his pocket dimension. \"Make it stand guard in the middle of the corridor so that no one can sneak in from the windows of one of the empty rooms without being detected.\"","\"On it.\" Lith placed a few mana crystals at the Golem’s feet, forming a recharge array that would allow Raptor to cast sensory arrays non-stop without depleting its power core.","Then he left Trouble on the fifth floor to stand guard at the roof access and the main corridor as well. With its wings, the construct would have a significant advantage in case of an aerial fight.","The group picked two connecting rooms on the fourth floor for themselves, which Orion warded from all kinds of long-distance surveillance spells and artifacts.","\"This will cost you a lot of gold.\" Lith said once he was certain they were alone.","\"Yeah, and it will be worth every coin.\" Jirni nodded. \"The Gernoffs have probably long infiltrated their spies in the most influential households to keep tabs on my movements in Distar, but they lack the manpower to cover the hotels.","\"I took three floors to keep them away from us and refused room service so as not to give their scouts the excuse to probe our defenses. The Gernoffs are not dumb enough to send someone flying in front of our noses and expect them to come back alive.","\"By the time they have found a viable access point to the hotel’s top floor, because they will, we’ll already be gone.\"","\"What’s with the bag of gold, then?\" Kamila asked.","\"Smoke and mirrors.\" Jirni shrugged. \"Alika will go around telling everyone we’re going to be at the Siren’s Song for a while and our opponents will relax, thinking they can bide their time. Too bad that I just opened a tab. I was careful not to make any reservations.","\"I’ll get back any money we don’t spend and rob anyone who’s tailing us of their certainties. The Gernoffs won’t be able to guess how long we stay at each location and will face an impossible dilemma.","\"Either they take it slow and scout the hotels for traps before approaching us, or they rush in without a plan and rely on luck. The Gernoffs will do the former, but I expect them to pay a few idiots and use them as sacrificial pawns to make us nervous. It’s what I’d do.\"","\"Sounds like a plan.\" Lith nodded. \"What’s our next step?\"","\"Please, go make us dinner.\" Jirni sighed. \"I don’t trust anything cooked by others. Kamila and I will start studying the reports while Orion keeps an eye on us. Once we start crunching numbers, we wouldn’t notice a Dragon stomping behind our backs.\"","Lith was about to propose a codeword to recognize him from a shapeshifter when he realized the scope of Jirni’s plan.","’I’m the only one who can control my golems, so while I can come and go freely, even the best shapeshifter would be attacked on sight. On top of that, nobody can fake an energy signature, and Orion won’t open the door until he identifies me.","’Any attack powerful enough to break past the walls would hurt the children, and the Guardians would kill the assailant.’ He thought. ’That said, do you want to go home and dine, Solus?’","’Yes, please.’ She sighed. ’I miss my body, and I’m starving. I haven’t eaten anything since breakfast!’","He threw the stone ring out of a window on his way down, and Solus shapeshifted into a small bird. As soon as she was far away enough from the city and certain that no one was following her, she took the DoLorean out and drove it back home.","Bolsa County bordered Lustria to the west, so the trip took her only a few minutes.","The chef wasn’t happy to have an intruder in his kitchen, but between the gold bag and Lith’s white robe, he didn’t argue. Lith used only fresh ingredients after testing them with Invigoration, cooking many dishes at once with magic.","\"See you tomorrow for breakfast.\" He stored everything in the pocket dimension and cleaned pots and pans with a single pulse of darkness magic.","\"Great Mother almighty!\" The chef brushed his fingers against the metal, expecting it to be oily yet finding it immaculate. \"Thank the gods mages are rare, or we’d be all out of work. The bastard did in a few minutes what takes us hours!\"","Lith put the Eyes on Menadion as he walked up the stairs, checking that no one inside or outside the building was using spells to track his movements.","’The good thing about non-enchanted buildings is that they offer no interference.’ He thought. ’I can scan an entire floor without getting so much as a pang.’","Before entering the room, Lith called Orion on his amulet to announce his arrival. Orion opened the door immediately and studied the newcomer with Life Vision from a safe distance. He also checked that Lith’s figure matched his hologram, just to be safe.","\"Paranoid much?\" Lith asked.","\"It means a lot coming from you.\" Orion snorted. \"Did you notice anything weird?\"","\"Aside from a cadet questioning his commanding officer, no.\" Lith snorted back, making Orion turn pale.","\"I’m sorry, sir! It won’t happen again.\" He tried to get back into character, but it was too late.","\"It’s too late for that.\" Lith replied. \"If someone heard you, our cover would already be blown. Luckily for you, cadet, I Hushed us.\"","\"Gods- I mean, thank you, sir.\" Orion waited until the door was closed and the silencing arrays in place before addressing Lith casually again. \"Dammit, I’m not used to undercover jobs anymore. I made a rookie mistake.\"","\"Don’t worry about it.\" Jirni patted his arm. \"It’s the first day. There’s almost no chance someone is following us. Just be more careful from now on.\"","\"I will.\" Orion nodded. \"Where’s the food?\"","Lith took a whole cart covered with steaming dishes out of his pocket dimension, making even Jirni’s stomach gurgle in anticipation.","\"That’s one of the things you can’t train into silence.\" She sighed. \"Gods, it smells delicious.\"","\"Thanks. Did you discover something already?\" Lith and Kamila fed the babies before sitting down to eat themselves.","\"Not even we are that good.\" Jirni replied. \"We’re barely started with Esha County. It will probably take more than one day just to sift through the documents if we go to sleep.\"","\"That’s a long time.\" Orion said. \"Do you plan to pull an all-nighter?\"","\"It’s one of the perks of being Awakened.\" Kamila nodded. \"The first reading is to look for patterns and anomalies in a single county. Then we’ll look at the compiled data to evaluate how each county is faring against the bandit raids and if the methods they employed justify the results.","\"We expect counties that used similar approaches to the issue to have obtained a similar outcome. If one county solved the problem and the others didn’t follow their lead, one has to wonder why.\""]},{"number":4438,"title":"Chapter 4438 Impossible Dilemma (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Same thing if a particular method is conveniently effective for one noble yet useless to everyone else.\"","\"Is there anything Orion and I can do to help you?\" Lith asked.","\"Just keep us safe.\" Jirni turned to look at the children. \"Gods, this is the first time Dripha is dining without us. I wonder how she’s doing.\"","\"I miss her too, but we couldn’t bring her along.\" Orion shook his head. \"It would be like carrying a sign that says ’I’m with Jirni Ernas’ over our heads. Let’s hope our baby girl isn’t taking it too badly.\"","***","Meanwhile, at the Verhen Mansion, Dripha was inconsolable. For the first time in her brief life, no matter how much she cried, her parents didn’t come. Lucky, Friya, and Quylla did her best to pacify the baby girl, but to no avail.","She barely ate during the day and nothing at all past sundown.","\"Have you tried shapeshifting into Jirni?\" Solus asked.","\"Yes, but we must have done something wrong because Dripha started to cry again after a single spoonful of food.\" Quylla replied. \"Imitating Dad failed even more spectacularly. She didn’t buy it for one second.\"","\"It’s not my fault.\" Morok massaged his pulsing temples. \"I did my best Orion impression, but there’s no way I can look at her with his loving eyes or that silly rumbling voice he makes when he feeds her.\"","\"Same.\" Nalrond said. \"Is there any chance you can bring Jirni and Orion back home tomorrow, Solus? A baby that young missing too many meals might be dangerous.\"","\"I’m more worried about Dripha growing up afraid of being abandoned.\" Friya cradled the baby girl in her arms like she had seen Jirni do countless times, but Dripha only cried harder.","\"I’ll do what I can.\" Solus replied.","Tired and defeated, the Ernas put Dripha back into her crib. She fell asleep almost instantly, too tired to keep fighting. When she woke up later at night, her eyes fell on the Rune Stores still piled up in a corner of her crib.","The last time Dripha had seen her parents was that morning, when Jirni had handed her the toys, and she had thrown them away again. In her silly, childish mind, Dripha believed that everything happened because of her.","So she came to the conclusion that her parents had abandoned her because she had refused to play with the Rune Stores. Dripha crawled to the nearest toy, squeezing it again and again to listen to the sound of the Brezza rune.","She could almost feel something clicking inside of her every time the Air Store squeaked. A faint connection to the air element, which, to a mind so young, was difficult to grasp.","This time she didn’t give up, hoping that if she learned what that weird sound was, her parents would take her back.","***","Gernoff’s secret compound, earlier, that same day.","\"What do you mean, she’s gone?\"","\"That we can’t find Jirni Ernas anywhere.\" Calam Gernoff replied. \"It took us a while to notice her disappearance, but she and her husband have been replaced by a couple of masterfully made constructs, but constructs nonetheless.","\"We had to wait until they took their afternoon walk in the park to be sure, but the Spyglasses confirmed our suspicions. Those things have the wrong energy signature.\" He referred to the artifact that extended Life Vision’s range.","\"How much advantage has she gotten on us?\" Jiza asked.","\"A few hours at worst.\" He said. \"She was spotted early this morning. Also, her baby girl is still with the Verhens. Jirni Ernas can’t have gone far.\"","\"It’s worse than that.\" Jiza drummed her fingers on her desk. \"This is a trap, and one for which she must have prepared carefully.\"","\"What makes you think that?\" Calam asked.","\"I will explain it to you in a minute.\" She took her communication amulet and asked the network of the Gernoffs’ spies and informants for updates about Jirni’s known associates that she had kept under surveillance.","\"It’s just as I feared.\" Jiza sighed, meeting her aide’s inquisitive look. \"Think about it, Calam. If Jirni wanted to disappear for a few days, all she had to do was leave with her daughter, Friya, using a mission on Faluel’s behalf as her cover story.","\"Friya is a Harbinger candidate and a dimensional mage, which gives her not only the means to move in ways we can’t follow, but also the protection of the Hydra clan.","\"Friya’s pregnancy would be a perfect excuse to bring Jirni with her, and any attack on them, assuming we can find them, would be an act of war against the Hydras.","\"Our household would go from seeking rightful justice against a traitor of Oghrom’s blood to being the sworn enemy of an Emperor Beast clan. Even worse, the other Lesser Divine Beasts who seek to learn the Hydras’ bloodline awakening technique would hunt us down to earn the Hydras’ favor.","\"Whether we succeed or fail in killing Jirni, we’d have a bloody conflict on our hands we have no hope of winning. Had Jirni done that, we would have been forced to sit back and wait for her return, giving her the time she needs to accomplish her goals.","\"Instead, she had her construct follow her routine and walk where she knew that our spies could see it. It’s a foolish move that can only be explained if it’s not us she wants to deceive.\"","\"I agree.\" Calam nodded. \"Her enemies in the Royal Court have no Life Vision, and the constructs are so well-made that they are indistinguishable from the originals. In her shoes, if I wanted to fool us as well, I’d have the constructs remain inside the house.","\"Maybe make them visible from the outside only through special enchanted windows. This way, the arrays surrounding the Verhen Mansion and the enchantments would make it impossible to check the energy signature unless one came very close.\"","\"Exactly.\" Jiza pressed a button on her amulet, projecting the news about Kamila’s investigation and her assistants. \"Look at this. I’m supposed to believe that Jirni Ernas disappears, and that this Assistant Constable, whose whereabouts were unknown until this morning, suddenly pops out.","\"I’m willing to bet this Trairen is no other than Orion Ernas, and that the entire investigation is nothing more than a cover for a much bigger scheme. Otherwise, why would Jirni Ernas leave the safety of the Verhen Mansion for such an unremarkable case?","\"Why use a disguise even a baby can unravel with Life Vision? Why make it so easy for us to notice her absence and locate her?\"","Calam thought long and hard about those words but found no other plausible alternative to Jiza’s reasoning.","\"There’s a glaring flaw in her plan, though.\" He said. \"Jirni Ernas left the little Dripha at the Mansion. With Verhen and his kids gone, nothing would stop us from taking Dripha hostage and using the girl to draw Jirni in the open.\"","\"And you think an opponent of that caliber would make a stupid mistake like that?\" Jiza clicked her tongue in disappointment. \"Once again, it’s too obvious. She’s clearly provoking us, hoping we take the bait.\"","\"What kind of bait?\" Calam bit his cheek, ashamed of his naivety."]},{"number":4439,"title":"Chapter 4439 Death by a Thousand Cuts (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Maybe Kamila Verhen is pregnant again.\" Jiza shuddered at the thought. \"She never announces her pregnancies, and the rest of Mogar always learns about it the hard way.","\"If we attack Jirni while she’s away from Elysia and Raldarak, but the Guardians deem us a threat to the baby in Lady Verhen’s womb, the Gernoff Household would go extinct, and all our contingency measures would be for nothing.\"","The youth pictured Jirni Blinking away from a deadly spell aimed at her, leaving Kamila in the line of fire. The Guardians had spared the Griffon bloodline and part of the Verendi Council because they weren’t involved in the assassination attempts.","The Gernoffs wouldn’t be so lucky. All the members of the Gernoff family knew about Jirni’s execution and were willing accomplices in Jiza’s plans.","\"As for Dripha, there are too many unknown variables. Maybe Jirni left her with a dangerous bodyguard like Shargein, or maybe she’s relying on the same enchantment that killed our assassin during Verhen’s birthday gala.","\"I wouldn’t rule out that Jirni wants us to take Dripha either.\"","\"Why would she do that?\" Calam’s tone remained level, but his face showed the shock he felt at those words.","\"Kidnapping Jirni’s daughter means breaking into Verhen’s house.\" Jiza explained. \"Facing his spells and potentially injuring his relatives. Whether we succeed or fail, the entire Verhen bloodline would become our sworn enemy along with anyone who wants a Blade Weapon.\"","The aide was about to suggest not leaving witnesses when he remembered that Friya would be among them. Lith wouldn’t let the lack of evidence stop his quest for vengeance, and neither would the Hydra bloodline.","\"In one move, the Gernoff Household would find itself isolated in the Council and surrounded by enemies.","\"The Lesser Divine Beasts who are after the Hydras’ bloodline awakening technology and the humans after the secret of human evolution would gladly offer the Gernoffs’ heads on a silver platter if it meant getting what they wanted.","\"And it gets even worse.\" Jiza studied Calam’s expression to read his thoughts. \"Friya Ernas has no obligation to officially announce when she completes the ritual that will transform her into a Harbinger.","\"What if Jirni knows her daughter is already a Harbinger and is using her as a living surveillance device? If I’m right, the moment we attack the Verhen Mansion, Faluel will witness everything through Friya’s eyes and call the rest of her family to arms.","\"The entire Hydra clan would come after our strike team first and us later. Fyrwal would take the attempt on her daughter’s Harbinger personally and call in favors, maybe even ask Tessa for help.","\"Now imagine this. A furious Lith Verhen with all the evidence he needs to carry out his vengeance without anyone interfering and the will to turn the weapons of our enemies into Blade Weapons. How long would our family last against such force?\"","\"Not even one second.\" Calam replied. \"The blood of Oghrom and his legacy would be wiped out from the face of Mogar without fulfilling their sacred duty. Jirni Ernas would live, and Oghrom’s will would be forgotten.\"","\"Yet being cautious doesn’t mean staying idle.\" Jiza said. \"Find out if Jirni Ernas is really disguised as Assistant Constable Ytana Sokra. If it’s her, have her followed 24/7. I also want the Mansion under strict surveillance.","\"Verhen’s absence gives us the time and opportunity to study his defenses. Whatever Jirni Ernas has prepared, it must not work on us a second time.\"","Jiza Gernoff was unaware that Jirni had prepared nothing, and the deeper the Gernoffs looked, the more entangled they would become in an illusory web of their own making.","***","The following morning, Jirni and Kamila were almost done reading the reports of the bandit raids in Lustria’s neighboring counties and the countermeasures the local lords had adopted.","\"I’m going to prepare breakfast.\" Lith said. \"Any special request?\"","He had spent the night patrolling the area with his Sigil Demons, but even the Eyes and Ears of Menadion had found no trace of a tail.","\"Just one. Don’t.\" Jirni said. \"We’re relocating in Ratham for ’further inquiries’.\" Lith could almost hear the air quotes. \"We need to change our location often to keep the Gernoffs on their toes, and our enemies thinking the investigation is going nowhere.\"","\"Do you know where we are going to stay next?\" He asked, wondering why Solus had yet to return.","\"Whatever hotel the Association recommends will be fine.\" Jirni replied. \"I want to make it easy for the Gernoffs to find us.\"","Lith had no idea what her plan was, but he trusted Jirni enough not to ask questions. He accompanied Jirni to the reception where she checked them out of the rooms and got the unspent money back.","The group had just stepped out of the Singing Siren hotel when Solus’ contact rune lit up on Kamila’s amulet.","\"I’m sorry to bother you, but we have a small problem.\" She said.","’This is a great move.’ Lith thought. ’Solus is using her lunch break to create herself an alibi. Now Jirni thinks that Solus has always been at the Mansion with the others and won’t suspect a thing.’","\"What problem?\" Kamila asked.","\"Dripha hasn’t eaten anything in half a day and keeps crying.\" Solus replied. \"We’ve checked her with Invigoration, and she’s fine. She’s just... sad. We’ve tried everything we can, but even ’Jirni’ and ’Orion’ here can’t calm her down.\"","’What does this mean?’ Jirni asked with a mind link. ’We never had such a problem in the past.’","’None of our children was as smart as Dripha, but I was always with them.’ Orion replied. ’I took both our parental leaves while you went back to work.’","\"We didn’t call you earlier because we hoped Dripha would eat once she got hungry enough.\" Solus continued, unaware of the silent conversation. \"Quylla can keep Dripha hydrated with her Injection spell, but I’m worried skipping so many meals might be dangerous for a young baby.\"","\"Don’t worry, we’ll be right back.\" Kamila said as she looked at Lith.","He turned the DoLorean towards Manar County, picking a route that would also bring them close to Lustria. As soon as the car was within range of the Home Stone that Solus had stored in the Armory, a Warp Gate brought the group into an empty wing of the Mansion.","\"You should thank Friya.\" Lith answered Jirni’s silent question. \"After receiving Tezka’s lessons, her abilities have improved by leaps and bounds.\"","\"That’s of secondary importance.\" She said, and for once she was honest. \"Where’s my baby?\"","Lith opened a Steps to the nursery, and the Ernas couple reverted to their true appearance before walking through it. They found Dripha exhausted and asleep, still holding the Water Store in her small hands.","\"Wake up, baby girl. You need to eat.\" Jirni lifted Dripha in her arms, and the baby girl cried with joy.","Her mother’s smell, the sound of her heartbeat, and tone of voice were exactly as Dripha remembered. She clung to Jirni’s chest without letting go of the Water Store, believing that her relentless study of the toy was the reason for her mother’s return."]},{"number":4440,"title":"Chapter 4440 Death by a Thousand Cuts (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"What’s the matter, young lady? Don’t you know that you won’t grow as strong and tall as your dad if you skip your meals?\" Orion’s soft voice and loving gaze made the baby girl cry harder.","Dripha would recognize those eyes amid thousands.","\"Guys, give us a minute.\" Orion said.","\"Take all the time you need.\" Kamila replied. \"Val, Ely, and Ral will be happy to see their family.\"","\"I swear, Mom, I did everything as you taught me.\" Friya said. \"Dripha acted completely normal until the afternoon snack. When she didn’t see you coming back, she got upset and refused to calm down.\"","\"Is it true, young lady?\" Jirni asked, and Dripha nodded while sucking avidly from her baby bottle.","\"You’re right, dear. She’s way smarter than a normal child her age.\" Jirni sighed. \"Dripha can tell us from our holograms.\"","\"How is this possible?\" Orion asked.","\"I don’t know.\" She replied. \"It might be anything. Maybe it’s Manohar’s last gift to me. Something similar to whatever he did to Marth. He’s been my rejuvenator for over a year and modified my body to give me an edge on Deirus.","\"Or maybe it’s just whatever is in Lustria’s water. No offense, Elina, but Surin isn’t normal either.\"","\"None taken.\" Elina shook her head.","Orion and Jirni took turns feeding and reassuring the baby girl until she fell into a peaceful slumber.","\"Please, keep us posted.\" Orion’s heart bled as he had to pry his finger out of his daughter’s hand. \"We’ll come back as soon as we can if Dripha stops eating again.\"","Later, when the baby girl woke up and noticed the disappearance of her parents, she was both saddened and relieved. Saddened because she missed them, and relieved because she believed that as long as she learned how to use the Water Store, they would come back.","***","Lith’s group used the Mirror Warp to cover most of the distance separating them from Manar County and reach their destination with a small delay. Kamila asked Countess Manar for clarifications she didn’t need, while Jirni asked the nearest branch of the Association for a good hotel.","It was almost dinnertime at the Morrigan’s Lake when the Constables put all the pieces of the puzzle together. The picture they painted was unsettling, and the too many blanks left only made it worse.","\"I can’t be certain of anything at this point, but if there is a conspiracy afoot, it’s a well-thought-out and timed one.\" Jirni compiled the data in simple graphs and paragraphs that even a layman could understand.","\"As Lith became more famous and influential, crime became less profitable in Lustria. The smartest cartels started disbanding or moving away ever since Lith became the Supreme Magus.","\"Trains, Tablets, and everything else dried up an already shallow pond, leaving the criminals no other choice but to leave or be arrested. The rise in crime rates in Lustria’s neighboring counties is just a natural consequence of that, and to be honest, it’s something the local lords should have predicted and prepared for.\"","\"When you look at it this way, the bandit raids also appear like a reasonable phenomenon.\" Kamila said. \"The new arrivals gave the local crime lords new blood and skilled manpower, and the incompetence of the local nobles paved the road for their success.\"","\"Yet you said, appear.\" Lith pointed out.","\"That’s because, if you take a closer look, only a few counties are ruled by incompetent lords, and the strangest part is that they are amongst the least affected by the bandit raids.\" She replied.","\"Which looks absurd if you consider that Jadon reported the decrease in Lustria’s criminal population as soon as the phenomenon started, Keyla prepared more than adequate countermeasures, yet it did her no good.","\"Also, I want you to consider that Lustria has always been relatively peaceful. It had its share of crimes, but just what human greed and opportunity are bound to breed. If you also consider that such a relatively small number of criminals didn’t flock into a single county, the current situation doesn’t look normal anymore.","\"Lustria’s criminals were no genius masterminds. They achieved no more than their counterparts in the neighboring counties, yet after the change in scenery they seem to have stepped up their game by a significant margin.","\"They succeed where everyone else failed, leave no trace, and somehow fence the stolen goods without using any of the established channels that the local lords monitor at all times.","\"As Count Barla said, numbers don’t lie, and these stats make no sense. It would take ten times the number of criminals that lived in Lustria to achieve these results, and each cartel should have a competent boss and face no power struggle.\"","\"Which is ridiculous.\" Orion snorted. \"Even an honorable organization like the Knight Guard has its fair share of naysayers, let alone a bunch of scumbags who only look after themselves.\"","\"And that’s not the only abnormality we discovered while sorting through the reports.\" Jirni said. \"When the forces deployed by the army and the Association foiled the raids and captured the bandits, all they got was small fish.","\"Your run-of-the-mill delinquents with little skill and even less brains. When they were interrogated, they didn’t hesitate to sell their comrades, yet the Constables always arrived too late.","\"The hideouts were empty, and no stolen goods had been retrieved. Interrogating the prisoners about their leaders didn’t reveal anything useful either. According to their testimonies, it was business as usual.","\"The boss would point them at a specific point of the road, and the henchmen would wait for the merchant caravan in ambush. You can imagine the rest.\"","\"Standard tactics can’t be so effective against veteran soldiers.\" Lith pondered. \"What about their sources? Keyla told us that she changed the routes many times, but the bandits always managed to find the caravans even after she issued an information blackout.\"","\"That’s another oddity we can’t explain.\" Jirni shrugged. \"Most of the local lords did a pretty good job, but the bandits were always one step ahead. Some counts didn’t even bother changing their security protocols, yet they stopped about half the raids.\"","\"This makes no sense.\" Orion’s eyes narrowed as he sifted through the graphs. \"The amount of money and resources each county lost is unremarkable by itself, but once you put them all together, they reach a staggering figure.","\"In two months, the Griffon Kingdom lost thousands of gold coins. How could Brinja not notice it? This is big enough to warrant the deployment of a full squad of Constables, if not even an Archon!\"","\"The answer to your question is the reason Jirni said these attacks were well-timed.\" Kamila replied. \"Nobody noticed because of winter and rivalries. The bad weather cut off most communications, and bandit raids are far from unusual.","\"The reports started coming in only when the constant loss of resources became alarming. Moreover, as you noticed, the value of a single caravan is almost negligible.","\"By the time the village heads contacted Keyla, Ghishal County was already dying by a thousand cuts.","\"From that moment on, she has been so busy dealing with the bandit raids taking place in multiple areas of her fief at the same time that she lost sight of the big picture until it was too late.\""]},{"number":4441,"title":"Chapter 4441 Many Eggs in one Basket (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"But Keyla did notice that something was wrong with Ghishal when the reports started flooding in.\" Lith said. \"Why didn’t she ask Brinja for help then?\"","\"For the reasons Keyla explained to you when you visited the Lark Estate and that Kamila just mentioned. Rivalries.\" Jirni said. \"All the local lords compete not only with their neighbors, but also with the other nobles of comparable influence in their fief.","\"Keyla and the other struggling nobles didn’t want to admit how badly they were doing, so they played into the hands of the bandits by minimizing their issues and using their personal funds to compensate the victims of the raids and hire more guards.","\"Brinja didn’t notice what was happening because those she trusted to act as her eyes and ears in the various counties played dumb to save their faces.\"","\"This gives us a better picture of the problem, but offers us no solution.\" Lith replied. \"What do you think we are dealing with?\"","\"It could be anything, but if I had to guess, I’d say someone is staging several coups inside the Distar region.\" Jirni said. \"It’s the only explanation that covers all the facts. An inexplicable small issue that snowballs into a failure big enough to cost the local lords their fiefs.","\"If I’m right, we’re dealing with a bloodless takeover that is making lots of people rich and will increase their noble status without having to move a finger. The rival nobles leak the information to the bandits, probably in exchange for a share of the loot.","\"The bandits succeed, the local lord changes tactics, the rival nobles leak it again, making it ineffective. Rinse and repeat until people like Keyla are removed from office despite their noble sacrifices and valiant efforts.\"","\"What about the nobles who are successful in dealing with the bandits?\" Lith’s jaw clenched in outrage.","\"They are relatively successful, Lith.\" Kamila replied. \"Half the caravans still get hit, but compared to Barla and Keyla they look good. Also, remember what I’ve said about rivalries.","\"Were everyone equally unsuccessful, the local lords would have shared their problems and reported them to Brinja. They didn’t do it because a few of them had no such problem, and no one wanted to admit defeat first.","\"The bandits failing on purpose to keep the nobles from working together is the best-case scenario, though. Worst case scenario, the successful rulers are in cahoots with the bandits.","\"As I told you, most of the ’successful nobles’ were deemed incompetent by the Royal Court. According to my research, they were about to be replaced.\"","\"But now that they have proven their valor, they will keep their seats.\" Lith nodded in understanding.","\"It’s a nice theory, but if we present it to Brinja without any evidence, it won’t change anything.\" Jirni said. \"She must judge the performance of her retainers based on facts and numbers, not coincidences and speculations.","\"She will of course launch an investigation, but it will find nothing more than what we already did. To make matters worse, predicting the bandits’ targets will become much harder once spring arrives.","\"There will be so many merchant caravans going around that it will be impossible to find the bandits that helped the nobles stage the coups among all the common criminals that know nothing about this.\"","\"In other words, unless we do something now, Keyla is going to lose Ghishal County.\" Lith nodded.","\"She and Jadon aren’t the only ones affected by the issue, but yes.\" Kamila replied.","\"Give me a second. I need to make a call.\" Lith took his communication amulet and pressed Keyla’s rune. \"I’m sorry, but there is no time for pleasantries. Are you alone?\"","\"No, but it’s an easy fix.\" A minute later, Keyla was alone in her office and up to speed with the results of Jirni’s investigation. \"Good gods. You were right, Lith. I should have called you as soon as the trouble in Ghishal started.\"","\"This is no time for recriminations.\" Lith replied. \"How is it going with the merchant caravans? Did my arrival stop the bandit raids as we predicted?\"","\"That’s too early to say.\" Keyla said. \"Carriages are much slower than your DoLorean, Lith. I shipped essential goods as soon as news of your presence spread, and so far, everything is going fine.","\"The caravans have already reached a few villages and delivered their cargo. Usually, the chances of being attacked decrease with each stop. The more merchandise gets unloaded, the less valuable the cargo becomes and the faster the convoy can move.","\"Unless the carriages transport luxury goods, they aren’t worth robbing after about half the merch is delivered. I’m confident the rest of the deliveries should not encounter any problem, but if this is really about a coup, then everything goes.\"","\"Keep me posted about the caravans.\" Lith pondered. \"If I’m right, the mastermind behind this won’t dare make a move until they make sure that I can’t get far from my children.","\"We’ve already collected everything we need for our investigation, but we’ll prolong our stay by five more days with the excuse of needing clarifications about a few documents. In the meantime, I want you to act as if you know nothing.","\"Pretend to be happy about the successful caravans and start the arrangements for a single major shipment. A cargo big enough to recoup part of your losses and restock most of the villages until spring.\"","\"I can do that, but why should I? It’s too soon to put so many eggs in one basket.\" Keyla asked.","\"Because it’s a trap.\" Lith replied. \"If this is a coup, whoever is behind the scenes can’t risk seeing the work of months go into the gutter because of a single caravan, and the bandits will gladly agree if the pot is large enough.","\"Yet don’t change your routine. Contact only those you have used until this moment and keep everyone else in the dark. Don’t lower your security. Increase it if you can afford it. Also, I suggest you organize multiple lesser caravans to use as decoys.","\"On the surface, it must look like you are splitting the cargo among many convoys to limit the damage if one of them gets hit. Yet your ’real intention’ is to bet your future on a single well-guarded shipment.","\"After all, I’ll still be in a nearby county, and you’ll ’assume’ that the bandits are too scared of me to make a move.","Moreover, if someone questions your judgment, point out that nobody knows the decoy caravans carry rocks and that even if they get robbed and the bandits expose the trick, by that point it will be too late to stop the real caravan.\"","\"It’s a good plan, but I bet there’s more to it.\" Keyla nodded. \"How will you secure the cargo, though?\"","\"The same way I’ll find the proof of the coup against you.\" Lith said. \"I’ll take part in the expedition as a Snow Thrower. When the bandits attack, I’ll be right there to capture them and work my way up the chain of command.","\"The bandits will lead me to their leader, and their leader will point me at their source inside your court. Then I’ll let Jirni and Kami do the honors.\""]},{"number":4442,"title":"Chapter 4442 Many Eggs in one Basket (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Won’t our trick become obvious if you disappear soon after the caravan departs?\" Keyla didn’t sound convinced.","\"No, because we have more than one Light Master here.\" At a wave of Lith’s hand, Kamila pretended to cast a spell, and Jirni conjured a body double of Lith. \"I’ll travel with the caravan while also staying with my children.","\"Kami will keep my double in plain sight so that if someone tails us, they’ll believe my movements are still restricted.\"","\"I’ll start the preparations immediately.\" Keyla said with a wide smile. \"I’ll let you know when and where you must come to retrieve your identification as Snow Thrower. Keyla out.\"","The next day, both caravans in Ghishal had completed the deliveries, and the rest of the nobles hurried to ride Keyla’s coattails. Lith’s group changed hotels every day, but kept a strict routine of questioning the local lords and taking the children out for a stroll.","Jirni acted as a perfect personal assistant, filling all the paperwork for Kamila and performing the menial tasks. She often moved through the cities with only Orion by her side as if she hadn’t noticed the Gernoff scouts keeping an eye on her.","’This is dangerous. They could attack us at any time.’ Orion said with a mind link as their shoulders brushed.","’In the middle of the day and in public?’ Jirni snorted. ’That’s not how the Gernoffs operate. They won’t risk Lith Warping here and exposing their presence. Awakened laws don’t protect common criminals.","’If the Gernoffs kill a bystander or destroy public property, Lith can go after them as a law enforcer of the Kingdom. On top of that, Oghrom would turn in his grave if his descendants resorted to such brutish tactics.","’One strike, one kill was his creed, and his descendants uphold his will to this day, or I wouldn’t be in this situation in the first place.’","Jirni and Orion also had to return to the Mansion discreetly to feed Dripha and reassure her everything was alright. They asked for Friya’s help, and she Forgemastered many Home Stones for them.","A single Warp Steps crossed hundreds of kilometers with the artifact’s help, allowing the couple to reach the Mansion quickly without the need to use a Warp Gate.","The baby girl was overjoyed to see her parents at the end of most of her training sessions with the Rune Stores, further reinforcing the misunderstanding. During one of these trips, Lith outlined the rest of his plan.","\"I can’t use a communication amulet while undercover, but I can’t afford to be off the grid for too long.\" He said to Kamila and Solus. \"If something bad happens, I want to be there and the tower to be able to tap into its full power.","\"Solus, you’ll stay with Kami most of the time and come to my side whenever you assume she’s safe. I’ll recharge you, and you’ll keep me posted about the developments.","\"Also, I want you to sprinkle Jirni’s construct with your Domination. You have my same energy signature, so if the Gernoffs or whoever is behind the attacks take a peek at my hologram, they’ll mistake it for me.\"","\"An Awakened robbing merchants is preposterous, but I agree with the rest.\" Solus nodded. \"Jirni can’t use Life Vision without blowing her cover, and even if she finds the perfect moment to use it, I’ll notice it with the Ears and recall my magic before she notices.\"","On the fourth day since the start of the mission, Keyla called Lith to inform him that the caravan was fully loaded and the personnel were assembling for departure.","\"Here is your ID, your contract, and my personal token.\" She handed him an enchanted piece of paper which he imprinted, a regular piece of paper, and a silver coin with the Lark family emblem embossed on its front and Keyla’s profile on its back.","\"Don’t worry. Every member of the caravan is someone I personally recruited, and they have their own token. Imprint it, please.\" Lith did as bidden, and Keyla brought an identical piece of silver near his coin.","Keyla’s token glowed for a moment, and Lith’s did the same a second later.","\"Only tokens imprinted in front of me and activated by my master token are capable of recognizing each other.\"","\"The enchantment is pretty simple.\" Lith pointed out. \"What if someone kills the original owner, imprints the token, and then uses first magic to light it?\"","\"Your token won’t react, exposing the imposter.\" Keyla replied. \"The first rule is never to use them in groups, only in pairs. Otherwise, someone might conjure a glow bright enough to eclipse the real enchantment and fool the real members of the expedition.","\"One more thing. You can’t go out like this. Even without your Magus robe, you stick out like a sore thumb.\"","\"I know.\" Lith shapeshifted into his original body, taking the appearance of Derek McCoy.","He was now shorter, leaner, and meaner. He had the soft gaze of a contract killer and the kind face of someone who had woken up on the wrong side of the bed for at least a year.","\"You’re still too tall and stick out, but this is the perfect look for a magico mercenary.\" Keyla studied Lith’s Earth appearance with curiosity. \"The frown will keep everyone at arm’s length, and no one will question your qualifications.","\"I swear to the gods, if I met this person at night I’d cross to the other side of the sidewalk. You truly are a perfectionist, Lith.\"","\"Thanks.\" Lith snarled. \"I don’t know when or if I’ll be able to update you on my situation. I can’t risk one of the other members of the expedition getting suspicious. If they talk with the wrong person and we have a mole, our plan would fail.\"","\"Not really. The news that I have the Supreme Magus on my side would make a lot of people happy and restore part of my reputation.\" Keyla replied. \"It’s better than nothing.\"","\"But it’s not enough.\" Lith shook his head. \"Once your enemies know they have been exposed, they will become much more careful, and I might not be able to stop them next time.\"","He looked Keyla in the eyes, expecting her to become nervous or scared, yet she smiled at him.","\"Thank you, Lith.\" She gave him a deep bow. \"Thank you for worrying so much about me.\"","\"I-\"","\"You didn’t fail my father.\" Keyla cut him short. \"Now go. And be careful out there.\"","\"I will.\"","***","The caravan head, a burly man in his fifties, frowned upon seeing Lith/Derek.","\"I’ve been in this business long enough to know everyone. Who the hell are you?\" He asked while extending his silver token.","\"Tarak of Cerea. Hero for hire.\" Lith’s voice oozed enough sarcasm to make the burly man smile.","The two tokens glowed upon contact, and Lith felt an itch on his fingers that caught him by surprise.","\"Aha! I knew you were a newbie. This explains a lot.\" The caravan head said. \"I’m Gelm of Setria, but you can call me Chief. Why would Lady Lark hire someone who has never used a noble token before?\""]},{"number":4443,"title":"Chapter 4443 Snow Thrower (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Because I’ve worked for the Lark family in the past.\" Lith replied. \"I’m used to moving alone, though, so I’ve never needed one of these things. Is it supposed to-\"","\"Yes, it glows.\" Gelm squeezed Lith’s hand to stop him from mentioning the sudden itch he had felt. \"It’s how we recognize the new guys. The surprised look always gives them out.\"","\"I see.\" Lith nodded. \"Are there any more surprises I should be aware of, Chief?\"","\"If the gods will it, this is the first and last.\" The head caravan sighed. \"Give me your papers, please.\"","Lith handed Gelm his documents, and the man frowned as he read them.","\"You look more like a throat cutter than a Snow Thrower, but I guess you’re a man of many talents.\"","\"You have no idea.\" Lith’s smirk sent a shiver running down Gelm’s spine.","\"Minor academy?\" He asked.","\"Do I look like someone who has that much money to waste?\" Lith scoffed. \"I’m a self-taught, and I’m much better than any of those posers.\"","\"Lady Keyla believes you, and that’s enough for me.\" Gelm replied. \"Your task is simple. Clear the road ahead of the caravan from the snow with the help of your partner, but stop as soon as you feel tired.","\"You must be able to fight if push comes to shove, and we have hired enough Snow Throwers to keep travelling all day if necessary. You’ll patrol the caravan with the other mercenaries while you recover your mana. Leave everything else to us merchants, Tarak.\"","\"I can do that.\" Lith nodded. \"When do we leave?\"","\"As soon as I make sure everyone is who they say they are.\"","***","The caravan departed from Ghishal’s main city, Derana, a few minutes later. Since Gelm had never met Lith before, he put the unknown mercenary in the first shift as Snow Thrower to assess his skills before they got too far away from the capital to find a replacement.","\"Jorun!\" Lith and the man sitting beside him spoke the word of power and traced its hand sign with the practiced skill of someone who had performed the same task countless times.","Snow Thrower was the name of the magicos specialized in using their powers to remove any natural obstacle a caravan might encounter during winter, be it snow, ice, or fallen trees.","A skilled Snow Thrower let the horses advance at a steady pace, spared them from frostbite, kept them from slipping and falling off the road, and preserved their stamina.","A Snow Thrower would also expose holes and traps, and remove any obstacle that would have otherwise forced the caravan to stop, making it easy prey for an ambush.","’At least this Tarak is not one of those useless fellows who need to use tier one spells.’ Gelm inwardly nodded in approval. ’Only true Snow Throwers need only chore magic to do their job.’","The alleged focus that Lith ’needed’ spared him from making small talk. He used his colleague, a yellow-cored magico called Verban, to assess how tired he had to pretend to be.","Lith wore enough cloaking rings to appear as a bright yellow core, and needed to play the part. He kept working for half an hour after Verban left his station, and then joined the guards patrolling the area until lunchtime.","The caravan stopped on the side of the road. The merchants lit fires and prepared a warm meal for everyone, allowing men and horses to recover their strength.","\"Good job out there, but there was no need to show off.\" Gelm said. \"Start and end your shift with your assigned partner. It will save you mana and avoid pointless competition. You know how you magic users are.\"","\"Actually, I don’t.\" Lith shrugged. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Now you are scaring me.\" The head caravan looked Lith in the eyes and shuddered at seeing his honest curiosity. \"All those who failed to enroll in one of the great academies always act as though they have to prove something to the rest of the world.","\"They believe themselves to be unsung Lith Verhens and use their powers for magical measuring contests on every occasion they get, trying to prove they are the best.\"","\"Really? This is new to me.\" Lith shrugged.","\"And that scares me.\" Gelm replied. \"You’ve clearly never worked with other magicos, which makes me wonder in what circumstances you met Countess Lark and what you did for her to earn her trust.\"","Lith had never competed with anyone, even during the academy. At best, he had had a friendly rivalry with Quylla, but even that had lasted only until the plague in Kandria. The mission had helped him greatly develop his mana perception, the only aspect he lacked.","After graduating from the White Griffon, Lith had worked alone and gained such a reputation that most mages gave him a wide berth upon hearing his name. Magicos didn’t even dare look in his direction except to ask for his autograph.","\"I’m sorry, but it’s not a good business practice to reveal confidential information about a client just to appease the curiosity of someone I’m unlikely to ever meet again, Chief.\"","\"If you have any problems with Her Ladyship’s decision, you have to bring them up to her.\" Lith said, ending that conversation.","Questioning a noble’s judgement was always a bad idea unless they came up with something idiotic enough to endanger the lives of the caravan members. Questioning a noble’s judgment about the people they trusted in time of crisis was the fastest route to unemployment.","\"If that’s how you want to play it, Tarak, it’s fine by me.\" Gelm grunted. \"Just do me a favor. Stay out of trouble. Most importantly, don’t stir up trouble with the rest of the Snow Thrower crew.","\"You may be good at your job, but you alone sure aren’t enough to bring us all safely to our destination.\"","***","Jiza Gernoff’s secret compound, at the same time.","\"This is exactly as I feared.\" Jiza drummed her fingers on her oakwood desk as she sifted through the report of the Gernoffs’ scouts. \"The situation is much worse than I expected.\"","\"I agree with your assessment of the situation.\" Calam Gernoff, her aide, nodded. \"The Assistant Constable and the rookie Knight Guard who travel with the Verhens have been confirmed to be Jirni and Orion Ernas.","\"Moreover, Lith Verhen has left the group and has been replaced by a mere construct. It’s the same obvious trick Jirni Ernas used to leave the Verhen Mansion. This kind of tactic can only fool fake mages.","\"There is no way Verhen or Ernas thought we wouldn’t notice. The entire scenario doesn’t add up. If it’s a trap, it’s too obvious. If it’s not, then our opponent must have lost her mind. Neither option is credible.\"","\"Indeed.\" Jiza turned to look out the window, and the sun lost its warmth as it reflected in her ice-blue eyes. \"There is only one plausible explanation. The obvious trap is a cover for the real trap.","\"Jirni Ernas is taunting us to make our move. Have our scouts uncovered something new about the defensive measures Verhen left behind?\"","\"Nothing you don’t already know.\" Calam shook his head, his short, wheat-blond hair shone like gold."]},{"number":4444,"title":"Chapter 4444 Snow Thrower (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Our scouts have only established the presence of Verhen’s golems and the arrays they fuel. There was no time for further probing because the group relocated to a new city with the DoLorean.","\"Our agents lost the Ernas, and we had to wait until gossip exposed their new location to re-establish a surveillance perimeter. Useless to say, we had to start everything over from scratch.\"","\"Patience, Calam, and remember the Gernoff’s creed. One strike, one kill. We don’t fight. We execute. No matter how long and tedious a job may be, it’s only thanks to his meticulous preparations that our forefather failed only once.\"","The mere mention of Tezka the Suneater upset every Gernoff, but their annoyance showed in such subtle ways that only another Gernoff would notice.","\"Jirni Ernas leaving the safety of her haven is already plenty of good news.\" Jiza steepled her slender fingers. \"It’s a change in her pattern, and any change is bound to create openings. It’s up to us to find and exploit them.","\"Have our operatives keep the surveillance and recon the area around the hotel with extreme caution. They must not approach the target until they have gauged the full scope of her defensive measures.\"","\"We could infiltrate a couple of agents as hotel staff, and maybe pay a few local thugs to test the waters for us.\" Calam said.","\"It can work on a lesser opponent, but not against Verhen or Jirni Ernas. The golems would slaughter any thugs we sent, no matter their numbers. No one in their right mind would think they have been entrusted with anything but fake intel and bother taking them alive.","\"The only thing we would achieve is to alert the enemy of our presence and give them a good reason to relocate again. Sending our agents is off the table. We’ve already lost too many Gernoffs during our previous attempts on Jirni Ernas’ life.","\"I won’t risk more without the certainty their sacrifice won’t be in vain. There are only a few of us, and if we suffer too many casualties, House Gernoff will have to close its doors for a generation, if not two.\"","The Gernoff Household had hundreds of members who regularly had children as part of their duty. Yet the blood of Oghrom flowing through the babies’ veins wasn’t enough to guarantee that any of them would grow into a skilled mage or operative.","All the children underwent the family training from their fourth birthday, but most couldn’t make it through. They either broke mentally or physically, and were judged unfit to enter active duty after they recovered.","Those who dropped out of the training course became Awakened no different from those of the other bloodlines. They became nobles, bureaucrats, and administrators who managed the Gernoff lands, leaving the true Gernoffs free to do their job without worrying about money or politics.","Among the few who graduated from the course, even fewer people were cleared for fieldwork. Some lacked the tactical mind of a true Gernoff, while others crumbled under pressure or didn’t have the guts to do the dirty jobs.","People like that became instructors who led the initial phases of the family training for the next generations from the safety of the Household walls. Their role was to separate the wheat from the chaff and save the real Gernoffs from wasting their precious time.","The number of active field operatives was small, and upholding Oghrom’s standards rarely allowed the number of graduates to exceed a dozen per generation.","Those killed by Tezka on the day of Dripha’s birth and by Jirni on the day of the Gala were elites among the elites. Their loss had dealt two major blows to the Gernoff household, and Jiza couldn’t afford a third.","***","The caravan’s trip proceeded without a hitch, but that was to be expected. They were still too close to major settlements, and the security of the roads was too tight. Any attack was bound to leave witnesses, and it was clear the Larks’ invisible enemy wanted to avoid that.","Moreover, it would have been a pointless risk. The first deliveries barely put a dent in the cargo’s value. They consisted of just a few items the merchants had received last minute and had to drop off to cities along the way.","The truly precious crates were intended for the small villages that had suffered the most from the lack of basic necessities. Keyla was sending her most unlucky subjects not only everything they needed to live comfortably until spring arrived, but also compensation for their sufferings.","’Waiting until the caravan gets deep into the Ghishal’s backcountry is not a smart move. It’s a basic strategy.’ Solus said via the mind link. ’The longer the merchants travel on the road, the more tired they get.","’This damn bad weather is pushing everyone to their limits, but the magicos have it worst. They exhaust their mana during their shift as Snow Throwers, and then they have to help the soldiers when they are supposed to recover their strength.’","’Yeah.’ Lith inwardly nodded. ’The magicos burn their energy twice as fast and rest much less than the merchants. It’s no surprise the bandit raids have been so successful. Whoever planned this, he’s no fool.","’Did you discover anything noteworthy about our travel companions or cargo?’","’No.’ Solus had taken a good look at the crates’ content and the caravan members with Invigoration to bypass any cloaking item or enchantment. ’Regular humans and regular merch.","’The strongest guy here has a green core, but I’m not surprised he failed to enroll in one of the great academies. He reaches the bare minimum mana to cast tier five spells and his talent is unremarkable.","’There’s no way he could learn much in a single day before he ran out of mana and needed rest.’","’Thanks, Solus.’ Lith replied. ’Go back to Kami and the others. I can deal with the rest.’","’Don’t mention it.’ She said. ’I’m going to travel by flight in the hope of spotting a mana geyser. It would make our communications and movements much easier.’","Lith dropped the stone ring on the ground, and Solus burrowed her way out of sight. Once she emerged away from the caravan, she shapeshifted into a small bird and bolted towards Kamila’s signal.","As for Lith, he had discovered the truth behind Gelm’s words first-hand. He never had the same Snow Thrower partner twice, and all the magicos silently challenged him to an endurance contest.","The first to take a break and join the soldiers would be marked as the loser. Lith never formally received or accepted any taunt, but the expressions of his alleged teammates spoke volumes about their feelings.","He didn’t care about coddling their egos, and followed a simple routine.","He peeked at their cores with Life Vision and then did what he was supposed to do. Anyone weaker than his fake bright yellow core was left in the dust, while those with bright yellow cores were defeated with a margin that depended on how much they annoyed him.","He always lost against dull green cores and above, but while his \"betters\" cheered and toasted during dinner as if they had just become Magi, Lith cared so little about his rare \"defeats\" that it usually spoiled the mood around the campfire."]},{"number":4445,"title":"Chapter 4445 Lead by Example (Part 1)","paragraphs":["It was hard to brag when the other guy barely acknowledged your existence or remembered your face.","\"Tarak of Cerea, nice to meet you.\" Lith said with a straight face whenever someone tried to rub their victory in his face.","\"Why are you introducing yourself again? We’ve already exchanged pleasantries at the beginning of our shift!\" Jalen, the most recent winner of the unofficial contest of magical prowess, said in outrage.","\"Did we?\" Lith stared at him in utter confusion. \"I’m sure you did a good job since I would remember you if you slacked off.\"","\"A good job?\" Jalen echoed, his nostril flaring and his face reddening from incredulity.","\"Yeah, that’s what we get paid for.\" Lith tilted his head to the side, making the magico feel like the biggest fool on Mogar. \"Is there something you need my help with?\"","\"No, I just came to offer you a drink.\" Jalen actually had brought nothing, so he handed Lith his own tankard.","He did it not out of friendship, but because he couldn’t live with making a pathetic exit right after such a pathetic entrance.","\"Thanks, much appreciated, whoever you are.\" Lith took the beer mug with two hands. \"It would have been polite of you to introduce yourself after I told you my name.\"","The other magicos burst into laughter, ruining Jalen’s plans for an honorable retreat and making him inwardly curse Lith. To make matters worse, Lith wasn’t even being sarcastic.","Without Solus, remembering names and faces of people he didn’t care about was beyond him. He remembered his travel companions only by nicknames related to their most outstanding characteristics, like their pungent smell or crooked teeth.","All things he couldn’t use as monikers without starting a fight.","The following day, Lith went to talk with Gelm as soon as he woke up.","\"We have to be careful today, Chief.\" He pulled a map of the area out of his pocket dimension without even saying good morning. \"Here, here, and here are the perfect spots for an ambush.","\"Also, there’s a very bad choke point here, and it gets even worse if there are big trees in the area that the bandits can cut at the last moment to box us in. In their shoes, I’d pick this as the attack spot.","\"The hill road is all twists and turns, and there is nothing we can use for cover if they throw big spells at us. Once the fallen trees cut our retreat path, getting out of there alive would be nigh-impossible.","\"We would have to ditch the horses and move on foot, and with the snow covering the terrain, anything but the paved road is a trap in itself.\"","\"Thanks for the warning, kid, but do you really believe we didn’t realize it on our own?\" Gelm grunted as he put on his suspenders, gesturing to his assistant to get him a cup of strong, hot tea.","\"I’m not saying that you are incompetent.\" Lith replied. \"I’m just pointing out that either you are incompetent or our enemy must have a few aces up their sleeves. Otherwise, Countess Lark wouldn’t have sent me here.\"","Gelm turned red, but he couldn’t argue with facts.","\"Are you saying the other spots are safe?\" He asked, hoping to bait Lith into making a fool out of himself.","\"No. As I said, they also are perfect spots for an ambush. They are far from safe.\" Lith talked with the calm, lecturing tone of a teacher dealing with a dumb student. \"I’m just pointing out that whoever attacks us before we reach the hill road is either a normal bandit or expendable pawns meant to waste our strength.","\"We’ll pass through all these places today. If we consume too much mana before the real ambush point, your magicos will be worse than regular mercenaries since they will lack both the swordsmanship and the vigor of someone who didn’t waste years practicing magic.\"","’And here I joined the club of the biggest idiots on Mogar.’ Gelm thought. ’I think I finally understand why Lady Lark sent this guy to help us. He’s not just a pain in the ass for his allies. He’s also a scourge on his enemies.’","The caravan chief assembled the combat personnel for an emergency briefing and shared with them Lith’s assessment of the situation.","\"If we get out of here alive, we have to thank Tarak for this.\" Gelm closed his short speech by giving credit where credit was due, hoping Lith would go easy on him when submitting his report of the mission to Keyla.","\"Why? What did I do?\" Everyone turned to look at Lith, and he stared back at them as if they had gone insane. \"I just stated the obvious. If you want to thank me, at least wait until I deserve it.\"","Gelm and most of the magicos choked on their breakfast, while the merchants’ muffled laughter broke the morning silence despite their best efforts to suppress their hilarity.","A few hours later, Lith was still on shift as Snow Thrower when the caravan approached the first potential ambush spot.","’Glasses, glasses on my nose, where the hell are my foes?’ He never engaged in a fair fight if he could avoid it, so he wore the Eyes on Menadion when the caravan was still at a safe distance from the choke point.","’Right there, my king. Kill them all so we can go home.’ He replied to himself as he spotted a dozen people armed with steel blades and bearing at best bright red mana cores.","He didn’t react or say anything, remaining silent and steady as a statue as he always did to avoid chatting with his assigned partner.","\"Ambush.\" Lith said in a flat tone when a bandit emerged from the woods, letting the rest of the caravan realize the danger they were in.","The bandits were still yelling their battle cries and the merchants screaming to prepare for battle when a rain of ice arrows ended the fight. Everyone turned around, finding Lith standing on the roof of his wagon with a wand in hand.","The high ground gave him a perfect view of the area and a clear line of fire on his enemies.","\"Why are you staring at me? What if there are other bandits? Can you dodge arrows that come from behind?\" Merchants and magicos cursed, unaware that Lith had already triple-checked that no enemy was left alive.","\"That was quick thinking and even quicker action.\" Gelm gestured to the magicos to make themselves useful and move the corpses off the road. \"Yet I have to ask. Why didn’t you spare at least one of our attackers to interrogate them?\"","\"To learn what? Where do not buy our equipment?\" Lith pointed at the cheap fur-lined jackets and boots of the bandits and their standard-quality weapons. \"Do these guys look like someone who can have caused you so much trouble?\"","\"No.\" Gelm had to admit after studying the corpses and noticing the bandits weren’t well fed either.","\"My point exactly. These guys are incompetent idiots at best and unwitting bait at worst. They could only buy the real bandits time to stage a real ambush. The longer we stay here, the more we’ll play into their hands. Let’s get a move here!\" Lith yelled, and everyone obeyed."]},{"number":4446,"title":"Chapter 4446 Lead by Example (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Darn, this guy is an ass, but his charisma is undeniable.’ Gelm inwardly cursed. ’He gives no speeches and doesn’t act nice, but he leads by example. Tarak is so damn competent that everyone already trusts his judgment more than mine after watching him fight once.’","Lith helped the soldiers to get rid of the bodies, and once they were piled up on the roadside, he ordered them to search the corpses.","’Now I can keep an eye on everyone.’ He thought. ’If a member of the caravan is a mole and the bandits were part of the plan, the traitor now can’t take anything from the dead bandits without me noticing.’","The bandits had very little in their pockets, mostly partially eaten beef jerky.","\"They must have left their horses and belongings somewhere near.\" Lith said. \"They can’t have reached this place on foot, and without supplies or magic, they wouldn’t have survived the night in the wilds. Wait for me here.\"","Before anyone could raise an objection or remind Lith of his position in the chain of command, he took flight. Lith used the Eyes of Menadion to search for something with a magical energy signature and his extra five eyes to look for traces of the bandits’ movements.","’The Eyes haven’t found anything, but that doesn’t mean much.’ He thought. ’No one would waste a powerful artifact on cannon fodder. At most, whoever is behind this gave them a letter with instructions about how to deal with the aftermath of the assault that the bandits were supposed to destroy, but they kept it as insurance.’","It didn’t take Lith long to spot the clearing where the bandits had left their steeds from above, but a quick search proved him wrong.","’Nothing.’ Lith sighed. ’This was just a crime of opportunity. Those morons must have heard about the raids and thought that they could steal the cargo and frame the professionals. I’m wasting time here.’","Yet Lith’s paranoia wasn’t so easily appeased. A flick of his wrist made the snow in the clearing float, allowing him to look for freshly turned ground.","’Nothing again. Those guys were just morons!’ Lith expanded the area of effect of his spell as far as his Tiamat eyes could see, but the result was the same.","He cursed the amateur highway robbers and returned to the caravan.","\"Did something happen while I was away?\" He had left for less than five minutes, but a powerful mage only needed one to slaughter an entire village.","\"Yes, Karlten puked his guts out.\" One of the mercenaries replied.","\"I’ll take that as a no.\" Lith snorted. \"Let’s move. And remember, when the real fight starts, I expect you to form a perimeter around the caravan. Don’t fight alone if you don’t have the skills. Fight as a group. There is strength in numbers.\"","It was basic common sense, but after seeing many mercenaries fumble with their weapons in panic, Lith felt it was necessary.","\"I’m sorry, but I need to ask.\" Morkan, one of the few who had \"defeated\" Lith, asked. \"How did you react so quickly and win the fight without any help?\"","\"Only magicless thugs would come out of their hiding spots screaming.\" Lith snorted. \"They gave out their position in the hope that fear and surprise would make us easy prey.","\"A real professional would never do that. They would have shot poisoned arrows or spells at us to whittle our numbers before charging forward. Also, they would have done it silently to exploit the ensuing chaos.","\"While everyone argued between running away and helping the injured, the bandits would have snuck behind us and slitted our throats. Why fight when you can just win?\" Put it like that, Lith’s question made Morkan consider a career change.","\"Since we were clearly dealing with amateurs, I prioritized reaching a vantage point to end the fight quickly. I assumed that since every Snow Thrower thinks themselves better than me, they could hold their ground against someone without magic powers for a few seconds.","\"My wand did the rest.\" Lith showed the mercenary the enchanted piece of wood.","\"Is that military grade?\" Morkan asked.","\"Yes.\" Lith nodded. \"Get good at what you do, befriend a few nobles, and getting one of these babies is not so hard. Do you have any more questions, or can we get back on the road?\"","\"No, and thank you.\" Morkan ignored the sarcasm in Lith’s voice and gave him a deep bow, feeling like an idiot who had survived that long on the job only by dumb luck. \"Sorry for wasting your time.\"","\"Let’s move!\" A snap of Lith’s fingers conjured the noise of snapping reins, and the horses trotted forward even though none of the drivers had done anything.","Lith resumed his position on the lead carriage, wiping the snow off the road as if nothing had happened.","’Fuck!’ Most mercenaries thought. ’A mage’s strength isn’t measured in the raw amount of mana he possesses, but how he uses it. Even if I defeated Tarak, I would still be a weakling compared to him.’","The journey proceeded smoothly until they approached the second potential ambush spot.","\"We’re almost there.\" Lith spoke with a normal voice, his words drowned by the clopping before it reached the nearest carriage, but his words were passed on by the merchants and mercenaries.","The former dropped flat on the floor while the latter put their hands on the hilts of their weapons, preparing for the worst.","’There’s no one here, but I can’t tell them that.’ Lith thought. ’I must appear competent, not a psychic.’","After they passed the second ambush spot, Lith took out his communication amulet and pressed both Solus’ contact rune and Keyla’s.","\"Status update. We’ve reached the Gadora Hills. First contact with the enemy. Low-level threat, no casualties or damage suffered. We’ve just passed the halfway point through the hills. Tarak out.\"","\"You have one of those?\" Gelm asked as soon as he recovered from the shock. \"Who did you call?\"","\"The countess, Chief. Who else do you think I answer to?\" Lith replied with a snort.","\"I mean, how can you afford it, and why didn’t you ask for reinforcements?\" The caravan chief said.","\"One, I’m that good, and two, to what end?\" Lith shrugged. \"This is a communication amulet, not a Warp Gate. Even if I gave our position to the nearest branch of the Association, it would take them too long to get here.","\"And why would they do that? Because something might happen and you are scared? Do you really believe yourself so important? That real mages should drop everything and fly here to your rescue?\"","\"No.\" Gelm started wondering if he had eaten something rotten and a parasite was now feasting on his brain.","The caravan reached the third potential ambush spot, but nothing happened.","\"Only the big one left.\" Lith said. \"Ready your weapons and conjure your most powerful spells. Once we get past the last choke point, we won’t need much mana to get to safety.\"","Lith held a wand in one hand and kept the other extended to push the snow off the road. The mercenaries wished they could afford such a powerful alchemical tool as they chanted their spells and traced the hand signs."]},{"number":4447,"title":"Chapter 4447 No Game Works (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Fake mages consumed their mana upon casting a spell, so they had to choose their weapons carefully, or they would waste their strength for nothing.","The Eyes of Menadion spotted several people ahead of the caravan, many of them with a mana core above the orange and a few armed with magical weapons and alchemical tools.","Lith performed a deep scan for cloaking items or unusual life forces, but shared none of his findings with the other magicos.","The attack started the moment the caravan reached a sharp left curve that forced the horses to slow down, exactly as Lith expected. A large tree in front of the caravan fell with a loud noise that covered the sound of flying arrows and bolts of ice.","Lightning wands would produce bright flashes impossible to miss and might set the carriages aflame, destroying their precious cargo.","\"Now!\" Lith yelled at the top of his lungs the moment the tree started to tilt, his voice reaching far beyond the back of the caravan.","If not for his timely warning, many people would have died before the fight even began, and a few of them died anyway. Only the magicos who had prepared wind and ice shields managed to save the civilians they were tasked to protect.","Earth magic conjured a much sturdier protection, but it was also slower, and failed to cover anyone but the magicos until it was too late.","’Amateurs.’ Lith inwardly sighed.","\"Don’t stop! Don’t try to turn around! Keep moving forward!\" A wave of his hand conjured two stone pillars at the roadside, lifting the fallen tree high enough to clear the path.","When the second tree fell, cutting off the only escape route that the caravan was supposed to have, the bandits cursed their bad luck. They couldn’t follow a trotting horse for long, and those attacking from the rear were left in the dust and had to run just not to lose sight of their companions.","\"Not so fast!\" Hegron, the unit leader, threw a Fire Seed far ahead of the road, conjuring an explosion on par with a tier three Fireball.","The bang and the raging fire scared the horses so much that the caravan stopped abruptly and a few carriages toppled over.","\"Now! Don’t let anyone escape! Either they surrender or die!\" Hegron said as he charged forward.","\"Quiet.\" A word from Lith and a touch of Tiamat Fear calmed the panicked horses immediately. \"Stay.\"","He stepped down from the carriage while raising his blade. The fight was too chaotic and too many people were running around to use a wand from that distance. Lith pretended to be wary of his enemies, but he was just baiting them to reveal their true prowess.","A man covered in winter camouflage garb that left only his green eyes exposed bolted at Lith with a rapier in one hand and a poisoned dagger in the other.","’Is he really this weak, or is he just wearing a cloaking item like me?’ Lith parried both lunges and was amazed to discover the person in front of him truly was an orange-cored human.","\"Next.\" Lith said.","The bandit pivoted on the balls of his feet to ride the momentum of the parry and unleash more attacks before Lith could react, but a flash from the wand and a bolt of ice put an end to the bandit’s life.","\"I said next!\" Lith shot in the back whoever dared ignore him and tossed the bandit’s corpse at Hergron to intercept a second Fire Seed.","The ensuing explosion was too far from the caravan to threaten the soldiers and covered the road with gore, making the bandits slip.","Two more armed men came at Lith from either side, displaying solid teamwork and swordsmanship. One fell to an ice dart before he could get near Lith, and the other died at Ragnarök’s edge.","Lith moved like a normal human, and the bandit blocked, but the weight of the hand holding the angry blade amounted to several tons. The bandit’s longsword shattered, and his body was cut asunder before he could understand what had happened.","\"Next.\" A hail of poisoned arrows flew at Lith only to be deflected by the gravity sheathe of the Voidwalker armor.","His sword and wand kept finding the exposed backs of the bandits, but now he was crippling rather than killing them.","’If these guys are just regular humans, I need them alive to interrogate them. I don’t care about delivering the cargo. If I find the head of the snake, I can cut it. Then the body will wither, and Keyla’s standing as Ghishal’s ruler will be safe.’","\"Die, you arrogant bastard!\" Hegron threw a Fire Seed at Lith just for it to be enveloped in a cocoon of air magic and harmlessly stopped in mid-air.","\"Thanks for the assist.\" A flick of Lith’s finger sent the Fire Seed hitting the ground a few meters behind the next wave of bandits.","The explosion threw them off their feet and dismantled their formation. With their numerical advantage and now superior teamwork, the soldiers pushed the bandits back, wounding them deeply.","\"Don’t kill them!\" Lith yelled. \"It’s the only way to find the rest of their gang!\"","\"Retreat!\" Hegron put the next Fire Seed back into the Safe Bag and cursed his bad luck. \"Retreat! Re-\"","As no hidden champion stepped forward nor a secret weapon appeared, Lith dropped the mask and released his killing intent.","\"Run for your lives!\" Hegron yelled. \"Every man for himself!\"","Yet he found himself unable to follow his own order, and so did the rest of the bandits. Their legs seemed to have turned into lead, and nobody could muster the strength to take a single step away from the battlefield.","Lith moved to the wounded, both allies and enemies, healing them but for completely different reasons. He saved the soldiers because they were Keyla’s people, while he brought the bandits back to health because he might have to kill a few to set the example.","As he moved along the caravan, he carried the healthy bandits around with invisible tendrils of Spirit Magic. The human bundle grew thicker as he collected his prizes, and the number of wounded people decreased.","\"Everybody take five.\" Lith said. \"I have work to do. You are free to watch, but try not to puke. It would upset the horses.\"","The merchants were utterly confused and the bandits terrified, so no one questioned his words.","\"Who are you really?\" Gelm asked.","\"A man on the job.\" Lith shrugged. \"Now shut up.\"","He bound and gagged the bandits like prime roasts after ensuring they had no poison pills in their mouths or means of suicide hidden in their clothes. A thorough search of their belongings didn’t provide him any clue about their identity.","Lith found no recurring tattoo or insignia on their equipment that he could associate with a known gang or criminal organization. Those men clearly knew each other well, but if not for the way they fought together, Lith would have thought they were complete strangers.","\"I’m going to interrogate you all, and you are going to answer my questions.\" Lith said. \"Cooperate, and I’ll hand you to the authorities alive. If you don’t, bad things will happen to you. Is that clear?\""]},{"number":4448,"title":"Chapter 4448 No Game Works (Part 2)","paragraphs":["No one answered or moved.","\"I’ll take that as a yes.\" He replied. \"Let’s start with you. Name?\"","\"Ask your mother!\" A rough man with chestnut moustaches said. \"Oh, wait, she doesn’t know it either. She just calls me dadd-\"","A flick of Lith’s hand and the bandit’s neck turned 180° with a crunching sound without being touched. His body fell limp on his former colleagues, covering them in drool and piss.","\"I love my mother.\" Lith said to his now terrified audience. \"This guy got it easy. I’ll rip the balls off of the next man who mentions her. Then I’ll heal his wound and force him to eat his own nuts.","\"After that, I’ll cut off his little friend and make him eat it too. I won’t kill him, though. I’ll have the authorities keep him alive and make an example out of him.\"","Lith paused, letting the picture sink in the bandits’ brains and stomping the corpse’s manhood into mush to underline the concept.","Merchants and soldiers shuddered while holding their privates for dear life, while the bandits’ eyes became pinpricks from terror.","\"You, there. What’s your name?\" Lith asked, and the man remained silent. \"I asked you what your name is. Talk.\"","The man refused to obey, but that was as far as his defiance could go. He was too terrified of using the wrong insult to say anything.","\"Lesson number two. Playing the silence game with me doesn’t work.\" Lith said with the mean, lecturing tone of a college professor. \"No game works with me. And you know why? Because I cheat. Let me show you.\"","He grabbed the bandit’s head and forced his jaw open, releasing a stream of darkness magic from his eyes that seeped into the prisoner’s mouth, nose, and ears. The darkness element robbed the man of his vitality and made him wither to a speed visible to the naked eye.","\"There. I took away ten years of your lifespan.\" The man now looked in his forties, with several grey streaks in his hair and many age lines on his face that hadn’t been there until a moment ago.","\"Your name, or the next time it will be twenty years.\" Lith’s eyes flared up with darkness, making the bandit yelp.","\"You can’t do this.\" He sobbed as he noticed liver spots that punctuated his hands. \"This is Forbidden Magic. The Kingdom will kill you for this.\"","\"Not at all.\" Lith replied with a soft smile. \"Forbidden Magic is consuming your life to gain something. I didn’t get younger or stronger from this. I just shortened your lifespan. Consider it like an amputation, but instead of a finger, I took away the time you have left to live.\"","Lith had done nothing of the sort. Darkness magic weakened its victim and removed their moisture, causing an apparent but perfectly reversible aging process. One day of rest and plenty of liquids and the bandit would have become as good as new.","Yet he didn’t know that. He couldn’t even think clearly at the idea that an inhuman monster like that could exist, and he was staring at it in the face.","\"Okay.\" Lith released another blast of darkness magic while the bandit was still shell-shocked.","\"Ygar!\" The man yelled, but it was too late. \"My name is Ygar! Please, stop!\"","\"You didn’t answer me quickly enough, and you paid the price, Ygar.\" Lith conjured an ice spell so that the bandit could see the sixty-year-old man he had become. \"Next question. Are you part of an organization?\"","\"Yes.\" He cried like a baby seeing how his luscious black hair had become grey and thin.","\"What is it called? Don’t waste my time, or else...\"","\"Blood Axes. We are the Blood Axes!\" Ygar wetted himself as the third blast of darkness magic encroached on him.","\"What a ridiculous name.\" Lith snorted. \"Yet as someone who once shaped swords out of beer, I don’t have much of a right to criticize a bunch of losers’ naming taste. Next question. Who is your informant?\"","\"My infowhat?\" Ygar asked in honest confusion.","\"The mole. Your accomplice inside the countess’ court that leaks information about the caravans’ routes to your gang.\" Lith clarified.","\"I just joined the Blood Axes after running away from Lustria. I didn’t even know we had one of those!\" The bandit sobbed, and Lith believed him.","\"What about your boss? Who is he and where can I find him?\"","\"I don’t know his real name, only that he goes by the nickname of Mak of the Mad Ax.\" Ygar replied. \"I don’t know where he is, though. I’ve never met the guy. I’m still a rookie. I was supposed to earn the gang’s trust by completing this job.\"","\"Fine.\" Lith snorted in annoyance.","The heart rate, the eye movements, and the smell the bandit exuded all spoke of pure terror, not deception.","\"Then who’s your handler?\" Lith asked, correcting himself when Ygar’s dumbfounded look told him that the bandit didn’t know that word either. \"The leader of this unit. The one who gives you grunts the orders.\"","Lith was certain that, at some point during the ambush, he had heard someone yelling commands, but he was in the middle of the fight and with his memory, all bandits looked the same.","\"I...\" Ygar swallowed hard. \"I can’t tell you. The Blood Axes have a vast network. If word that I’m a snitch spreads in prison, they’ll kill me.\"","\"Loyalty. I can respect that.\" Lith nodded. \"But respect doesn’t mean I’ll go back on my word. I warned you about what would happen if you didn’t cooperate.\"","The darkness faded, and a blinding light replaced it as Lith conjured the first Decay rune, Vikara. Before Ygar could beg for mercy, the Cursed Element seeped inside of him and accelerated his metabolism several thousandfold.","He aged at a speed visible to the naked eye. His hair and nails grew longer while his limbs shrank into twigs. The other bandits stared in horror as the young man they called Ygar turned into a spindly old man with a beard almost as long as he was tall.","\"...\" Ygar opened his mouth to talk, but only a wheeze came out.","Light abandoned his eyes as life escaped his body.","Lith waved his hand, and a tendril of Spirit Magic brought him another bandit. At the same time, a gust of wind hit Ygar’s corpse, and it crumbled into a fine dust that was scattered across the Gadora Hills.","\"You can talk, or you can end like him.\" Lith replied. \"I still have many of you to interrogate, and I only need one of you to talk. Think carefully before making your decision.\"","The moment Lith removed the gag, the man spilled his guts in more than one way.","\"My name is Arno. I’m a Flying Dagger, I mean, a Blood Ax. I left my old gang and joined these mooks a few weeks ago. I know shit about their leader.\" The young, pockmarked man said amid barfs.","\"I only heard about him and joined his crew because the pay was good. I...We take orders from Kharam. That guy! He’s the one you’re looking for.\" Arno tilted his head towards the group of bound and gagged bandits."]},{"number":4449,"title":"Chapter 4449 Dread Link (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"The one wearing a camouflage suit, white rabbit gloves, and snow deer boots.\" Arno said.","\"Is he telling the truth?\" Lith asked, and all the other bandits except the one Arno had singled out nodded like frenzied parrots. \"I’m inclined to believe you, but this was all too easy. How do I know you’re not framing a poor idiot?","\"Maybe you are the one I’m looking for, and your loyal subordinates are covering for you. You friend Ygar was quite tight-lipped, after all.\"","\"Screw Ygar! He was a moron.\" Arno spat as if speaking that name left a bad taste in his mouth. \"Ask Nadrim if you don’t believe me. He always brags he knows more about the gang than anyone else.\"","\"Who?\" Lith furrowed his brow.","\"The bald one with the white rag on his face.\" Arno replied. \"He’s been a recruit for a bit longer than me, and claims that during the years he’s learned a few things.\"","\"Well, Nadrim, you’d better talk fast, because I’m getting bored of this already.\" Lith brought the man matching the description to him, and removed his gag with a flick of the wrist.","\"Arno is right.\" Nadrim had a grizzled beard and the cold eyes of someone who would do and had done anything in his life to survive. \"Kharam is a lieutenant of the Blood Axes. If someone knows where to find Mak, that’s him.\"","\"Again, proof?\" Lith said with a flat voice.","\"All the real members of the Blood Axes must get a tattoo of the gang somewhere on their bodies.\" Nadrim replied. \"Low-level grunts must put them in visible places like hands or forearms as a show of loyalty.","\"High-level executives, instead, must hide the tattoo so as not to draw the attention of the constables in the event they get arrested. Mak is the one who pays to get a Healer to remove the grunt tattoo and make you a new one once you enter his inner circle.\"","\"How do you know all this, and why should I care about this story?\" Lith asked.","\"Only a young idiot like Arno or Ygar enters a gang without doing their due diligence.\" Nadrim said. \"I’ve lived to my ripe age because I avoided those who would use me as cannon fodder and always got insurance.","\"As for your second question, feel free to strip everyone. You won’t find any tattoos on most of us. Kharam, instead, has a tattoo on his right hip, where no one would find it unless they force him to take off his pants.\"","Lith nodded and brought Kharam to him. He found the tattoo depicting two crossed red axes right below the waist.","’This ink is years old and enchanted.’ Lith thought. ’It’s enchanted with a weak spell that makes the tattoo hard to remove and keeps it from fading. It must be a deterrent to keep trusted people from running away and starting a new life.","’Taking the tattoo off would require a skilled Healer. Even if one burns the flesh, the enchantment would make the ink resurface.’","\"Nice to meet you, Kharam. Let’s cut to the c-\" The bandit spat in Lith’s eye the moment the gag came off.","Unfortunately for him, a mere thought sent the lump of saliva back into Kharam’s face as if he had spat towards the sky.","\"You’re a cheeky bastard, aren’t you?\" Lith said. \"Either that, or you’re just stupid. Didn’t you see what I’ve done to that other guy, Igor?\"","\"I’m not stupid, you damn brute. Quite the contrary.\" Kharam smirked. \"You could afford killing a few losers to make the others fall in line because there’s plenty of them. Now you’ve found me, and that’s why I’m much safer than I was a second ago.","\"You are not stupid either and know there is only one of me. You can’t afford to kill or mutilate me. If I die, you’ll never know where to find Mak. You need me to find him, and I know it.\"","\"Aren’t you scared of my interrogation techniques?\" Lith asked.","\"No, because you’re on the clock, my murderous friend.\" Kharam chuckled. \"If I don’t report to Mak in a few minutes, he will relocate our headquarters, and you’ll never find him. I assume that whoever hired you won’t be happy if you fail, will they?\"","’I’d call his bluff since I can’t sense a communication amulet, but there is more than one way to deliver a message.’ Lith scanned the area with the Eyes of Menadion, spotting a messenger bird that kept itself in proximity to the bandits, ready to answer the right call.","’He wasn’t bluffing, and without the proper command, I can’t send the bird to Mak and follow it.’","\"You make a good point.\" Lith nodded.","\"Then you’d better stop wasting time talking and start listening.\" Kharam snarled. \"Here’s my conditions-\"","\"Here’s my counter offer.\" Lith grabbed the bandit by the throat and squeezed it just enough to shut him up.","Then he sent two tendrils of Spirit Magic plunging inside Kharam’s body.","One attached to his brain and the other to his mana core, activating a powerful mind link. Kharam felt a foreign presence lingering in his thoughts, but had no way to stop it.","’Don’t worry, I can’t read your mind.’ Lith’s voice resounded in the bandit’s consciousness. ’I can only speak to you and show you things, and you can do the same. Tell me what I want to know, and I’ll stop.’","’Stop what?’ Kharam was still sending his thoughts through the telepathic connection when the tendrils of mana began tracing the first Decay rune into his mind.","Lith didn’t conjure its power, though. After all, the bandit was right about his situation. Lith couldn’t afford to kill him, and he was running out of time. Without the fear of death, most threats were empty promises.","The time constraint meant that Kharam’s life became more valuable with each passing second, and that Lith couldn’t torture him too hard without the risk of him passing out or losing his mind.","Lith’s need for reliable information was Kharam’s shield, or at least so he believed.","’This is something I like to call \"Dread Magic\". Let me show you why.’ With each line Lith traced, the Vikara rune neared completion, and the primordial fear of aging bloomed in the bandit’s mind.","Years seemed to pass in the space of a few seconds. Years during which his body weakened and his vigor waned. Kharam saw himself repeating the same day countless times, becoming one day older as the cycle repeated itself.","Soon he couldn’t carry heavy bags anymore. His joints ached when he woke up or got out of his bed. His breath became ragged, and his hairline receded bit by bit. As more time passed, Kharam was forced to spend his days sitting around, too weak and tired to do anything.","He spent years reminiscing about his youth with whoever he met, acting like the old coots Kharam had always despised. Then, dementia took his mind, and he was reduced to a shell of the man he once had been.","He had become a drooling, pitiful man trapped inside his own body. The few moments of lucidity only made his condition more painful."]},{"number":4450,"title":"Chapter 4450 Dread Link (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Kharam remembered how being young felt. He remembered the strength of his limbs and the prowess of his mind. Yet now all was lost, and when death finally came, it was a relief.","\"Ready to talk now?\" Lith said out loud, snapping Kharam out of the illusion.","His smug expression crumbled, his confidence fled his chest, and his breath became fast and shallow as reality reasserted itself.","\"I’m alive.\" He said. \"I’m young again!\"","For the rest of the bandits, the merchants, and the soldiers, he just sounded insane. Less than a second had passed, yet Kharam’s attitude had flipped, and he spouted nonsense while crying with joy.","’I’ll take that as a no.’ Lith dragged his prey back into the Mindscape and traced the First Chaos rune, Ekrasu.","The pristine white of the Mindscape disappeared, replaced by an absolute blackness. Kharam was the only thing left, but not for long. He could feel himself die, and his skin fell off in dry flakes, leaving the muscles underneath exposed.","His body fell apart layer by layer, and unlike Vikara, Ekrasu made it clear that Kharam didn’t have the luxury of time either. He had seconds at best, and then his life would be over.","Everything he did or thought would mean nothing. Protecting Mak from the mysterious man would become meaningless since Kharam wouldn’t be there to rejoice. His life would end, and nothing and no one was waiting for him on the other side.","’Please, no! I’ll talk!’ But Kharam’s time had already run out.","His muscles stopped moving, and suddenly he was nothing. In his final instants, he could see life on Mogar go on. Kharam had died as he had lived, for nothing. No one remembered him. No one called his name.","He had left nothing behind, and now it was as if he had never been born. His existence had been as relevant as a rabid dog. Something dangerous, but that could easily be put down and whose death would only make the world a better place.","After that, even his mind faded, and what remained of Kharam’s consciousness was trapped in an eternal, silent darkness. Unthinking, unfeeling, and unblinking, his soul was forced to relive every moment in his life when he could have made a difference.","The moments when he could have amounted to something, yet his actions brought him one step closer to oblivion. Kharam couldn’t sleep, dream, or act. He had no imagination, only memory of what he had done and lost.","There was no changing the past, and every time the same events played out the same way in an endless loop. Kharam could only face the failure that his existence was and how he had chosen every day of his life to be a man no better than a flea.","\"Okay, then. Let’s talk.\" Lith said as Kharam bawled his eyes out.","\"I don’t know who the informant is. Mak is afraid one of his lieutenants might replace him if they know enough to conduct business without him.\" The bandit cried with joy, feeling the sun on his skin and knowing that he might still live.","He might still change his life and mean something to someone. Be remembered even if just for a silly thing. Be more than human garbage quickly tossed away and forgotten.","\"What I know is that we were just a bunch of nobodies until Mak got a new friend. Suddenly he acted all smart and had brilliant plans and thoughts that were not like him at all.","\"He always knew when and where the caravans would be, and even the contents of their cargo. Yet if you questioned his source, he would remain silent. A few lieutenants tried to discover his secrets, and Mak cleaved them with his axes.\"","\"I’m not a biographer. Just tell me where to find him.\" Lith said.","\"Do you have a map of the county?\" The bandit asked, and Lith took one out of his pocket dimension.","\"Here.\" Kharam bit his finger, appreciating the pain that proved he was alive and leaving a stain of blood in the middle of the Verrun Woods. \"Beware, though. His mysterious friend taught him many things.","\"The base is protected by powerful arrays, and Mak is never alone. He armed his guards with military-grade alchemical tools, just like the Fire Seeds I used earlier. Also, he has a communication amulet to talk with his new friend.","\"He just needs a bit of time to call them and escape. I’m almost certain this friend must be a powerful mage. There is no other way they can know so much.\"","\"Why are you telling me all this?\" Lith had no idea what Kharam had seen in the visions Dread Magic had induced.","He assumed he talked out of fear, yet the bandit’s voice was full of concern for Lith.","\"Because I know you’re going to kill me, and I have one final request for you. Please, remember me. Remember that Kharam of Nira helped you out. Mention me every time you tell the story of how you killed Mak the Mad Ax.","\"Don’t let me be forgotten. I beg of you.\"","\"I will.\" Lith said, putting the restraints back in place.","’Or rather, Solus will. She has an eidetic memory. I barely remember Gelm’s face.’ He actually thought.","\"I have to ask you to take this human garbage with you and hand them over to the first city with an army branch you can find.\" Lith bound the hands of all those with a mana core above the bright red behind their backs and silenced them.","\"I might need to talk to them again if it turns out I’ve been deceived, and as you’ve heard, time is of the essence.\"","\"Tarak of Cerea doesn’t exist, does he?\" Gelm stuttered every word.","\"There might be one somewhere, but sure it’s not me.\" Lith replied. \"I’m sorry for ditching you like this, but I do have a contract with Lady Lark, and the caravan’s safety is a secondary objective.","\"Finding the one behind all the raids you’ve suffered in the past few months is my top priority.\"","\"What should we say to the army? Who are you, really?\" Gelm had met Lith only a few days ago and liked him like a cavity, but after witnessing his martial and magical prowess, Gelm wanted Lith to stay with the caravan in the event of a third ambush.","Until that day, Gelm had considered magicos like Jalen the best bodyguards a merchant could ask for, but now they seemed awfully lacking.","\"Tell them to call Lady Lark and that I’ll contact them myself as soon as I’m done with my mission.\" Lith replied. \"My identity is confidential, but the army can ask Lady Lark. She knows who I really am. Bye!\"","Lith bolted off the ground, disappearing in the distance in the blink of an eye.","\"Don’t ask me why, but I have the suspicion Tarak let us win.\" Jalen said, drawing countless curses and insults from his battle brothers.","***","Lith used his newfound privacy to update Keyla on the most recent developments and ask Solus for reinforcements.","\"Is everything okay on your side of the field?\" He asked.","\"There are plenty of Gernoffs around us, but they keep themselves at a considerable distance.\" Solus replied."]},{"number":4451,"title":"Chapter 4451 Grindstone Fortress (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Everything is fine back at home, instead. Dripha has started eating again.\" Solus said. \"Meeting her parents regularly seems to have helped her regain her appetite. Are you sure you want me to join you? The Gernoffs might attack at any moment.\"","\"Unlikely.\" Lith replied. \"Jirni didn’t factor you in her plans, yet she felt safe sending me away. We might not know what she’s plotting, but the Gernoffs must have an inkling of it, or they wouldn’t be so cautious.","\"This case gives me plenty of reasons to be worried, instead. The mysterious friend of the Blood Axes has inside knowledge of Keyla’s plans, a vast network of operatives, and enough resources to protect their assets across the Distar Region.","\"I need you there to be my eyes, ears, and, if necessary, my second brain. I might miss something important if shit hits the fan. If that happens, everything we have worked so far would be for nothing.\"","\"What about Tista?\" She asked.","\"That would be the perfect way to scream my name from the rooftops and let everybody know of my involvement. She’s far from inconspicuous, no matter the form she takes.\"","\"I see what you mean.\" Solus nodded. \"You can disguise Ragnarök as a regular sword, but a human using battle claws is unheard of. Not to mention seeing a man and a woman who both have uncanny magical powers moving together in Distar would make things too obvious.","\"I’ll be there in a second.\"","She used the Mirror Warp to reach a point close to Lith’s flight path, and they met halfway. Only then did Lith share the results of his experiment with the Dread Runes.","’Conjuring the runes in Kharam’s mind was a stroke of genius. A mean, ruthless stroke, but genius nonetheless.’ She said.","’I guessed that if even a mage as powerful as you can barely stare at the Dread Runes, a regular human like him would fold like a cheap shirt. I was right.’ Lith replied. ’Did you find a mana geyser along the way? We could use the Prime Engine.’","’Sorry, but no. We’ve already reached our destination, and we didn’t run into a single one.’ Solus pointed at an allegedly deserted area of the Verrun Woods where the Eyes spotted a large dome of energy in the distance.","’It’s an underground network of tunnels. Not the kind of thing a gang of bandits would build. Especially because those temporary arrays are worth more than what they earn in a year. Whoever their backer is, they have considerable magic skills.’","’How many ways out of there?’ Lith asked.","’Between secondary entrances and secret passages, half a dozen, but none is magical.’ Solus replied. ’There is no trace of dimensional devices.’","’It makes sense.’ Lith nodded. ’A Warp Gate would cost too much, while an old Gate would lead us straight to this mysterious friend.’","’There is also no way to deactivate those protective arrays from the outside.’ Solus pointed out. ’We can only breach them. What’s the plan?’","’We hit them so hard and fast that the Blood Axes won’t understand what’s happening until it’s too late.’ Lith took several deep breaths of Invigoration, calling upon his Sigil Demons and bringing them all to seven eyes as he shared his plan.","’Are the six of us enough, or do you think I should summon a few more Demons?’ Lith asked Locrias and Varegrave, the only ones who had experience leading a small strike team against a large number of weaker enemies.","’We need at least six more.’ Varegrave said. ’We need to attack all the access points at the same time to spread the bandits’ forces thin and keep our mark from escaping.’","Lith had to word his call safely to avoid conjuring feral Demons who would kill anyone in a frenzy and potentially eliminate Mak the Mad Ax before he could interrogate him.","***","Inside the Grindstone Fortress, at the same time.","Mak the Mad Ax had earned his nickname on the battlefield after one of his victims survived the encounter by dumb luck and spread word of his ruthless fighting style, yet he was far from insane.","Whenever blood and limbs weren’t flying around, he was cold and calculating. It was the reason he had never been arrested, and the Blood Axes gang had expanded its influence so much. At the moment, however, he was mostly worried.","’Success or failure of a single ambush is of little importance. As long as my men avoid capture, there will always be another chance.’ Mak thought.","’I’ve given my lieutenants clear instructions to report to me whenever they encounter an anomaly or finish a mission, yet it’s been too long since I’ve last heard from Kahram.","’Even if the Lark caravan was heavily guarded and he still decided to proceed with the attack, by now he should have contacted me and reported the outcome of the battle. Maybe I should-’","A sudden tremor of the underground stronghold derailed his train of thought.","The walls and ceiling of his operation room quaked so hard that dust fell from above, and the wooden tokens that marked the position of the known caravan and his forces across Ghishal County toppled over.","Mak took the command crystal he always carried in a pouch hung to his neck and tapped into the detection arrays that enveloped his fortress.","They were supposed to give him a detailed status about the integrity of the defenses, the number of casualties or injured among his men, and the number and strength of the enemy forces.","Yet all he could see was a fuzzy mess, as if he were trying to peer into a broken monitor that showed static most of the time.","’What happened? How could so many powerful arrays be damaged like this in one second? The only thing I know for certain is that whatever attacked us compromised the structural integrity of the magical formations beyond their ability to self-repair.","’Until they are dispelled and conjured from scratch, the arrays will work at less than one-tenth of their full capabilities. I must contact Ankhuta and tell him to-’","The magical formation surrounding the operation room was relatively intact, so it managed to warn Mak in time. The solid door deformed with a noise of cracking wood and flew off its hinges, coming straight at him.","Despite the warning, the improvised projectile was too fast for him, and it would have hit Mak like a truck if not for the gravity sheath of his armor. The thick wooden door was deflected before it could hurt him and crashed against the east wall, exploding into splinters.","An unknown, not too tall man with a deep frown on his face and a red blade dripping blood in his hand walked through the doorframe. He stared at Mak even though he was still cowering behind the large table that supported the map of Ghishal and the wooden tokens.","Lith waltzed through the room as if he were familiar with the place, because he was.","After summoning his Demons, Lith had also conjured several tier three Zero spells right above the center of the concentric dome formed by the fortress’ defensive arrays.","The hail of Cursed ice had frozen many runes essential to the magical formations to work, greatly weakening their effects."]},{"number":4452,"title":"Chapter 4452 Grindstone Fortress (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Then, Lith and his Sigil Demons had unleashed six weak Blade Tier spells against the dome, attacking it from multiple directions at once. They had held back to avoid flattening the Mherka Hills and killing Mak, but the final result was still impressive.","Six fissures cut deep into the ground, reaching far below and beyond the Grindstone Fortress. The forces stationed near the points of impact had been slaughtered and all the defensive measures destroyed.","Lith had exploited the ensuing confusion and the many cracks in the damaged arrays to find the quickest path to reach Mak the Mad Ax before he could call his mysterious backer for help.","The Eyes had already spotted him before the attack thanks to his cyan core and powerful equipment. Compared to him, everyone else in the fortress was as weak as a baby.","The problem was that the arrays were so carefully overlapped that the Eyes of Menadion couldn’t peer clearly into Mak’s personal quarters.","On top of that, breaking through so many magical formations would have taken time that Lith didn’t have. The combined onslaught of Blade and Cursed magic had solved the problem, while the Demons’ simultaneous charge worked as a diversion.","Lith encountered only a few people who tried to stop him on his way to the operation room, and he disposed of them without ever slowing down. He advanced in a whirlwind of Davross and a hail of blood, reaching Mak in just a handful of seconds.","\"Whoever you are, you are in a world of trouble.\" The burly giant wielded the crimson twin axes that gave his gang its name and threw himself at the intruder. \"I’m-\"","\"Not interested.\" Lith cut the Blood Axes asunder with a single horizontal slash of Ragnarök. He grabbed Mak by the neck and lifted him off the ground like a grocery bag. \"The treasury. Where is it? Where is everything you plundered?\"","Mak would have loved to stand his ground and smile in defiance, but his feet dangled in the air, and his mouth was wide open in a desperate attempt to breathe.","’I don’t want to die! Not like this!’ He thought as blind terror and despair ravaged his mind and heart.","\"I need you alive. Not in one piece.\" Lith grabbed Mak’s right hand and crushed it in his grip. \"The treasury. Where?\"","Pain snapped the Mad Ax out of his daze, and he hurriedly looked at a door behind him. Lith threw Mak against the door, using him as a living ram. The thick wooden door broke, but so did the Mad Ax’s left shoulder and elbow.","The enchanted armor had kept him from becoming a pincushion of wooden splinters, but it couldn’t save his pride, body, and mind from shattering like glass. Mak was a seasoned warrior who could gauge the might of any opponent in three exchanges.","He had lasted only one before Lith overpowered him, but the strength of his grip and the violence of his toss made up for the two remaining exchanges.","’That guy is a monster.’ Mak thought. ’He will flay every bit of my skin and pulverize every bone in my body if I don’t do what he says.’","\"Where?\" Lith moved in a blur, reaching the Mad Ax and lifting him again before the gang leader could finish to assess how desperate his situation was.","Mak pointed at a hidden passage in an apparently solid stone wall, but the invader just nodded. Two vertical and one horizontal swings of the angry blade cut along the door’s outline, severing its hinges and deactivating all the traps.","Lith kicked the stone slab in, sending it flying and neutralizing the magical formations between him and the fortress’ vault.","\"What is this shit?\" Lith had hoped for a massive Adamant door, something he could take home as a bonus.","Instead, he was staring at a cave whose entrance was blocked by enchanted stones.","Mak tapped on Lith’s hand, trying to signal him that he needed to breathe in order to reveal the password. Lith plunged Ragnarök into the stone like a key into a lock, and the door opened on its own.","Inside the room, Lith found piles of gold, ingots of non-magical metals, and several precious gemstones of various shapes and sizes. The Blood Axes had clearly sold everything they had stolen at a fair price.","\"That’s it?\" Lith snorted. \"This isn’t even half of what has been stolen in Ghishal.\"","’It amounts to one-third of the total sum, if we take into account fencing prices and the gang’s expenses. Bandits don’t live on air.’ Solus said after making an accurate estimate of how much the Blood Axes were supposed to have earned and how much Mak had to pay his followers to keep them from revolting or leaving him.","\"I stand corrected. This is less than one-third of the value of the goods stolen so far.\" Lith echoed her words for Mak to hear. \"Is there another gang in Ghishal I’m not aware of? Answer me.\"","His voice was the rumble of thunder that announces a storm, and his Abomination Touch was death’s chilling embrace. Mak shook his head, feeling tears stream from his eyes.","While staring at Lith’s cold eyes, he didn’t feel like a ruthless bandit anymore, let alone a warrior worth that title. He had found himself in the shoes of his helpless victims, facing someone who held his life in his hands and handled it like garbage.","’Why did no one warn me that Ghishal County is filled with monsters? ’ Mak wasn’t worried about losing his wealth anymore. No price was too much to escape that nightmare. ’If I knew that Keyla Lark had someone this powerful among her retainers, I would have never listened to that lying piece of-’","The news of Lith’s investigation came to his mind, and suddenly the identity of the invader wasn’t a mystery anymore. Mak found no solace in the answer to all his questions. He fell limp like a rag doll, knowing he was doomed.","\"One third.\" Lith echoed, uncaring of his prisoner’s mental breakdown. \"One third for you, another for whoever leaked the intel about the caravans to you, and the last one for the mysterious friend that set up the arrays. Am I right?\"","Mak nodded, his eyes empty and his mouth opening and closing like a dying fish.","\"Who’s your inside man?\" Lith loosened his grip on the Mad Ax’s throat.","\"Baron Carkas.\" Mak replied.","\"Can you prove it?\" Lith asked, as a wave of his hand emptied the vault, leaving only dust behind.","Mak took dozens of small rolls of paper out of his dimensional amulet. Each one contained detailed information about the caravans’ routes and the mercenaries hired to protect them.","Each roll was signed with just a C, but by cross-referencing the rolls with Count Carkas’ penmanship, a good Constable was likely to identify him. If the information they contained matched Keyla’s secret plans the Count had access to, however, having him charged would be child’s play.","Mak was supposed to destroy the paper rolls after reading their contents, but the Mad Ax wasn’t that stupid. If anything went wrong, without the paper rolls the nobleman would have pinned everything on him, and no one would have believed Mak’s side of the story."]},{"number":4453,"title":"Chapter 4453 Loose Ends (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Even if a Royal Constable did believe Mak, no judge would have trusted the word of a criminal caught red-handed over that of a loyal servant of the Kingdom without solid evidence to support his claims.","\"What about your friend? The one who set the magical protections of this place? What does he or she look like?\" Lith asked.","\"He looks like an average guy. Just like you.\" Mak replied. \"But he is strong. Not as strong as you, but too much for someone of his size.\"","’We’d better leave.’ Solus said. ’ There was a silent alarm hidden among the arrays. Whoever conjured the magical formations has been notified of their destruction the moment we took them down.","’If this mysterious mage comes here and is as powerful as Mak says, you won’t be able to exert your full power while protecting the prisoner. In our hidden enemy’s shoes, I’d kill Mak rather than rescue him.","’Without his testimony, Keyla would still be in hot water, and the investigation will fail. We need him to link Baron Carkas to the Blood Axes and both of them to the mysterious friend.","’Also, don’t forget you are considered the best tracker in the Kingdom. Whoever is behind Mak can’t let him live nor risk you identifying him, or you could follow his trail and expose his involvement in the other regions as well.’","\"This will do. For now.\" Lith nodded.","’Anything I should know before we leave, Solus?’ He also thought.","’Nothing magical, if that’s what you mean.’ She replied. ’The gold was in the vault, so there shouldn’t be anything valuable left around.’","\"My axes.\" Mak said, his voice as broken as his spirit. \"Please, don’t leave them behind. They are all I have left.\"","The sounds of battle had died down along with the members of the Blood Axes. Only twelve Demons were storming the fortress, but each had the power of a bright-violet core Awakened and couldn’t be killed.","\"Sure.\" Lith retrieved the partially self-repaired weapons, but not out of the goodness of his heart.","’I went a little overboard from not seeing Ral in days. Without Mak’s signature weapons, no one will believe that this sobbing mess is the infamous Mad Ax who terrified Ghishal for months.’","Lith Spirit Blinked out of the fortress and then Warped towards Ghishal’s capital, Derana, where Keyla currently resided. He flew there at Dragonspeed while carrying Mak like a sack of potatoes and breaking whatever was left of his sanity.","When Lith arrived at the city’s outskirts, the bandit king had long since fainted. His eyes had rolled back into his skull, and he foamed at the mouth.","Lith entered through an open window, landing in the middle of the countess’ study, where she was discussing her latest plans to ensure Ghishal’s survival until spring with her most trusted aides.","\"Hi, Keyla.\" Lith said in front of his flabbergasted noble audience.","Countess Lark was about to call the guards when she remembered about Lith’s disguise and recognized his voice.","\"This is Mak the Mad Ax, the leader of the gang who tormented you, the Blood Axes. He was in cahoots with Baron Carkas, and they both received help from a mage I’ve not yet identified.\"","Lith dropped the contents of the fortress’ vault into an empty corner of the room and had Baron Carkas’ paper rolls form a pile on Keyla’s desk.","\"Call you-know-who to collect and examine the evidence. I’m going to arrest Carkas before the mastermind who helped him stage the coup makes him disappear. Bye!\"","Keyla was still staring at the treasure, the papers, and the unconscious burly man on her carpet when Lith bolted out the same way he had come in.","\"Who was that man, Your Ladyship?\" Chamberlain Feritha asked, pointing out the window. \"What’s the meaning of this?\"","Keyla quickly regained her composure, studying her aides’ reactions and checking whether anyone among them was more scared than surprised by the sudden turn of events.","\"Why don’t we ask Captain Rolthias?\" Keyla asked. \"You have been staring at our prisoner from the moment he was dropped on our doorstep. You should be relieved that the crisis is over and we can finally feed our citizens, yet you seem awfully worried.","\"It doesn’t make sense. Unless you are an accomplice of Baron Carkas and the one who leaked the caravans’ secret routes that Carkas passed on to the Mad Ax, of course.\"","\"I am relieved, Your Ladyship. I’m just surprised and confused like the rest of my esteemed colleagues.\" Rolthias said, but he became even paler, and his voice trembled so much that not even a blind man would believe him.","\"Guards!\" Keyla pressed the alarm on her desk, summoning the elite soldiers of her personal guard. \"Arrest Rolthias and detain him in the dungeon for treason. Do not let anyone approach him for any reason and place two guards inside his cell at all times.\"","\"Yes, my liege.\" The soldiers moved in lockstep, surrounding and neutralizing their former captain before he could unsheathe his blade. \"What about him?\"","They pointed at Mak and his axes.","\"Arrest and detain him too, but handle him with care.\" Keyla said. \"I’m afraid his sanity hangs by a thread, and I need him. For now.\"","***","Lith had contacted Kamila and Jirni on his way to Derana, just like he had Solus chart the quickest route to Baron Carkas’ estate.","’His fief is not too far from Ghishal’s capital.’ Solus pointed out. ’If Jirni is right and this was all part of a coup, it makes sense. Only a noble near Derana and who controls several major trading hubs of Ghishal can hope to replace Keyla.","’The Royals would never consider entrusting a county to someone who lives in the middle of nowhere and is not already deeply involved with the political scene of the Distar Marquisate.’","’Good point, but let’s save your in-depth analysis until after the mission.’ Lith replied. ’I had almost forgotten you’re a chatterbox when your life is not on the line.’","’Meanie!’ Solus telepathically pouted. ’I was just trying to warn you that this Carkas might be old money and nobility. Maybe even older than the Larks. His magical formations might be a tough nut to crack, especially after getting his share of the profits and receiving a hand from our hidden enemy.’","’It’s a good thing I haven’t dismissed my Demons, then.’ Lith said. ’Also, you could have cut to the chase and spared me the lecture.’","’And now you’re being rude!’ Solus grunted. ’These telepathic conversations last less than a second. Am I so boring that you feel the need to tell me to shut up?’","’I’m sorry, Lith. I swear she wasn’t like this back in the day, or I would have added a mute button to the tower.’ Ripha chimed in from her feather.","’What side are you on, Mom?’ Solus snorted.","’Mine!’ Ripha replied. ’You haven’t stopped talking for one second ever since we got the loot. I just want to hear my own thoughts instead of having yours filling my mind.’","’I’m sorry to interrupt your brilliant conversation, but it’s time to get to work.’ Valia cleared her throat in embarrassment. ’Lith has just brought us to our destination.’"]},{"number":4454,"title":"Chapter 4454 Loose Ends (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’If I hear one more thought that doesn’t belong to me, I swear that I’ll start charging you all rent!’ Lith said. ’Get out of my head, and I mean literally. Solus, you can stay. Just focus on recon, please.’","’Way ahead of you.’ Solus used the Eyes and Ears of Menadion to perform a full scan of the Carkas Estate.","She examined the various permanent arrays, studied their effects, and searched for any weak point the Demons could exploit.","’The good news is that this place is nothing much. It’s worse than the Frorl Estate, but much better than the Blood Axes’ underground fortress.’ Solus said. ’The bad news is that this is the ancestral house of a noble bloodline loyal to the Crown.","’You can’t break in as Tarak from Cerea. You must follow protocol, or the origin of any evidence we collect will be rightfully questioned. A smart lawyer would claim that, without a proper chain of custody, there is no way to know if Carkas is truly guilty of treason or if you’re just framing him to save Keyla.’","’Thanks, Solus.’ Lith nodded. ’I got so used to barging inside my enemies’ lairs that I forgot warrants are a thing. And that even though I’ve already asked Kami for one.’","Kamila had requested the search and arrest warrants from her superior, and Jirni had signed them instantly based on the evidence at hand. Then Kamila had forwarded the paperwork to Lith, putting him on the right side of the law.","\"This is Supreme Magus Verhen!\" Lith said, his voice magically amplified.","’Say that again. This time with your face and while wearing your Magus robe, though.’ Solus pointed out. ’Also, maybe project a Manohar’s ego-sized hologram of yourself. Otherwise, everyone will take you for a madman.’","’Good point.’ Lith shapeshifted into his Mogarian appearance and had his adventurer clothes turn into his golden and white Magus uniform.","\"I’m here on His Majesty’s service to arrest Baron Elmun Carkas for multiple charges of accessory to murder, aggravated robbery, fencing, and conspiracy against his fellow nobles and the people of the Ghishal County.","\"You have three seconds to depower the arrays of the Carkas Mansion and drop your weapons. If you don’t comply, everyone inside the magical formations will also be considered an accessory to all the charges and treated accordingly to the law. One!\"","Lith assumed his full Tiamat form, blotting out the sun with his wings and plunging the noble household into an unnatural darkness.","\"Two!\" Double Edge appeared in his hands, and he and the Sigil Demons began to weave their respective Blade Spells.","Varegrave and the other Demons sealed the magic runes inside themselves so no one would notice, while Lith conjured strings of colossal runes with each swing of his blade.","He released so much mana that the defensive magical formations became visible to the naked eye just to resist the pressure exerted by the nascent Blade Spells.","\"Three!\" The array field went down, but Lith ordered his Demons to hold their position, ready to unleash their Blade Spells the moment the magical formations were reactivated, or someone tried to sneak in or out of the mansion.","Lith shrunk to his human size and bolted past the external gate and through the park, landing right before the main entrance.","\"Open up!\" He said, and the double doors swung open while his voice was still echoing.","\"Please, have mercy.\" The butler was a middle-aged man with red hair, a moustache, and a livery. \"My family lives in here. We haven’t done anything wrong. We are law-abiding citizens of the Kingdom. I swear.\"","\"Then get out of here and wait in the park.\" Lith replied, keeping only his seven eyes and pristine wings out as his badge of office. \"Do not try to leave the estate, though. My Demons have instructions to kill first and ask questions later.\"","The butler and the rest of the house staff standing beyond the threshold swallowed hard. They cleared the path for Lith and ran to pick up the members of their respective families and bring them to safety.","Lith didn’t need a guide to reach the Baron’s chambers. Jirni’s warrant came with a detailed blueprint of the mansion with the living quarters of its master marked in bright red.","Lith flew onto the balcony of Carkas’ office and opened the glass door from the inside with a thread of Spirit Magic.","\"Baron Elmun Carkas, you’re under arrest.\" Lith said, staring the terrified noble in the eyes.","The Baron was a man in his fifties, with grizzled black hair and ice-blue eyes. Between his tall, lean build and the monocle he wore, Carkas reminded Lith of Trequill Lark enough to make him grit his teeth in annoyance.","\"You have the right to remain silent and still. Make one wrong move, and the next conversation I’ll have will be with the coroner. Do you understand your rights as I have explained them to you?\"","\"Yes.\" The baron found himself drenched in a cold sweat when he met Lith’s cruel gaze.","Carkas was sure to have never crossed paths with Lith, but he could feel the hatred radiating from the Magus’ figure.","\"Then, turn around and let me cuff you.\" Spirit Magic forced Baron Carkas to his knees and hogtied him like a prime roast without waiting for his compliance. \"I’m not going to leave until I’m certain I’ve found-\"","’A Warp Steps is about to form on the caron’s right!’ Solus warned him.","’Shit!’ Lith had no idea of who or what might come out of the dimensional corridor.","Maybe Carkas’ mysterious ally had decided to step out of the shadows to save him, or maybe it was just an assassin sent to dispose of the baron now that he had become a loose end.","’A Warp Steps means that either someone is crossing a long distance to come here, or that they want to cast a spell from wherever they are and confirm the kill. I can’t wait to find out which!’ Lith used the same tendrils of Spirit Magic that he had conjured to restrain Baron Carkas to pull him away.","At the same time, Lith erected several mystical barriers to protect himself and his prisoner as he charged forward. The attacker had the advantage of surprise, and Lith needed to get his hands on Carkas before whatever was about to emerge from the Warp Steps.","With the Baron dead or gone, proving the conspiracy in Ghishal would be impossible, and Keyla was likely to lose her title of countess.","’If Carkas has even half a brain, he keeps all the incriminating evidence on himself.’ Lith thought as he pushed the baron behind him and unfolded his wings to shield him from both spells and sight. ’Searching this place won’t do us any good.","’I bet that even if Jirni turns the entire estate upside down, she’s going to find only breadcrumbs.’","A strong open hand came out from the Warp Steps, and it was aimed exactly where Carkas had been and would still be if not for the Ears of Menadion and Solus’ warning.","It moved too fast to belong to a non-Awakened, and it was not a speed a magicless human like the baron could survive. The hand swatted the spot where Carkas had stood until a heartbeat ago, hitting the floor with enough strength to make it collapse."]},{"number":4455,"title":"Chapter 4455 Behind the Scenes (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’I was right. This isn’t a rescue attempt. They wanted to kill the baron!’ Lith thought as a man stepped through the Warp Gate, a curse still escaping from his lips as he turned to face Lith.","The man wore a simple adventurer set comprised of grey pants, a white shirt, and a brown leather jerkin. His skin was as dark as ebon, and his eyes blazed with bright violet mana as he looked around for his prey.","’That guy is not from Verendi. He has shapeshifted to hide his true identity!’ Solus had never met the man before, but she had already faced someone with a similar life force. ’That guy is an Ishara. A Divine Beast species of the Rathi continent.’","The foreign man froze when he saw Lith, and his face twisted into a mask of confusion.","\"You’re Lith Verhen!\" He said as if Lith were the last person on Mogar he had expected to meet that day. \"We don’t need to fight. I’m-\"","’One of the bastards who tried to kill Solus and now is messing with the Larks!’ Lith didn’t let the Ishara finish the phrase and met him with Ragnarök in his hand.","The man released the tier four spell meant to kill Carkas, but the thunderbolts wreathed in flames didn’t even scratch Lith’s barrier. With no time to unsheathe his weapon, the Ishara reverted to a humanoid-sized version of his true form.","His extended hand shapeshifted into a massive scorpion-like pincer, and a second set of arms emerged right below the first. The pincer grabbed the angry blade’s sides, but it would have failed to stop the attack if not for the secondary humanoid hand grabbing Lith’s wrist.","’I said stop! I don’t want to fight you, Verhen!’ The Ishara used the physical contact to establish a mind link.","’And I totally believe you.’ Lith’s thoughts were infused with so much sarcasm that the rest of Mogar was left dry. ’ Jerak!’","He conjured the First Zero rune in his mind and pushed it through the mind link. The Ishara froze at its sight for a moment, giving Lith the opening he needed. The Cursed ice coating the Ishara’s limbs let the angry blade slip free of their hold and resume its attack.","Lith cut both arms off at the elbow and released a tier five Battle Mage Spell, Final Eclipse, from one of his spell-holding rings. A jet of darkness-infused violet flames hit the Ishara like a truck and sent him crashing through the east wall.","’Solus, keep the baron safe!’ Lith focused on his prey, determined to kill the Divine Beast before it could call for reinforcements or say anything that might force Lith to stay his hand.","’On it!’ Solus stored the fragments of the Ishara’s severed limbs before they could revert to their full size and squash Carkas like a bug.","Shapeshifting compressed a Divine Beast’s mass, allowing them to disguise themselves as members of any other race, but it didn’t change their nature. The room was too small to contain even one hand of an adult Divine Beast, and the baron would have been killed on the spot if not for Solus.","The Ishara cursed his bad luck and conjured a Spirit Barrier from his enchanted armor to stop the onslaught. The black flames not only pushed him back, robbing him of his footing, but they also blinded him to Lith’s movements.","The Tiamat lunged, activating the seven crystals on his blade and charging it with elemental power. Ragnarök sparked as it channeled the air element inside its Davross blade and punched a hole into the barrier.","The Ishara survived only because he had the time to pull out his ax and shield. The curved surface of the buckler deflected Ragnarök, while the Adamant ax exploited the pincer’s longer reach to fall on Lith’s wrist like a guillotine.","To ensure his victory, the Ishara also infused himself with Life Maelstrom, becoming ten times faster and stronger. Unfortunately for him, Lith knew what an Ishara could do and had used the cover of the Final Eclipse to draw a deep breath.","A jet-stream of Void Flames hit the Ishara like a punch to the gut and faded away upon hitting their target. The Life Maelstrom neutralized the black flames before they could harm the Ishara, but at the cost of its own power.","The silver lightning faded, returning the Ishara’s combat prowess to normal, whereas the Vital Storm coursing through Lith and further amplified by the Davross’ air element was unaffected by the Void Flames.","Lith flicked his wrist, turning the failed lunge into a descending diagonal slash. He was too fast for the Ishara to react, and the Davross of Ragnarök’s blade cut through the Divine Beast’s Adamant armor with ease.","Lith severed the Ishara’s head and right shoulder from his torso, and he also pierced the Divine Beast’s heart with an ice spike just to be safe. The Ishara died instantly, and Lith stored the corpse inside his pocket dimension.","’He will be evidence of the conspiracy, while his equipment will make some nice loot.’ He thought.","’It will also light a beacon on you.’ Solus warned him. ’Isharas don’t strike me as people who work alone. Their bloodline is dying, and they consider every member of their race irreplaceable.","’Even if that guy didn’t have a partner, now that his contact rune is gone, the other Isharas will come running.’","’At that point, I won’t be able to fight against multiple Divine Beasts alone and protect the baron at the same time.’ Lith completed the phrase for her as he ran to retrieve the unconscious figure of Carkas.","Solus had kept the baron safe, but the killing intent released by the battle between Awakened was too much for a simple country noble.","\"I’m Supreme Magus Verhen, and I require immediate assistance.\" He said in his communication amulet. \"I’ve just faced an unknown hostile Divine Beast, and there might be more converging on my position. I’m- Trace my position!\"","The Ears spotted several Warp Steps opening in the baron ’s private quarters, so Lith couldn’t afford to move slowly enough to be heard anymore. He grabbed the noble and left the same way he had entered the room, from the balcony.","’It will be much more difficult for them to surround us now that we have enough space of maneuver. I don’t intend to fight against multiple Divine Beasts if I can avoid it.’ A light pressure on his wrist guard activated a silent alarm.","Only a few people among those Lith trusted could hold their ground against such powerful opponents, but few were better than nothing.","Memories of the time a group of Awakened had joined their forces to kill Valeron the Second flashed in his mind and made Solus shudder. Back then, Lith had barely snatched victory from the jaws of defeat thanks to the baby boy’s Life Maelstrom.","Now he wasn’t facing Fae, humans, and Emperor Beasts. His enemies belonged to a race of Divine Beasts who could use both Life Maelstrom and Doom Tide, while he had neither.","Lith opened a Warp Steps that led dozens of kilometers away, but the dimensional corridor collapsed on itself before he could cross it."]},{"number":4456,"title":"Chapter 4456 Behind the Scenes (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Lith, we are surrounded.’ Too many Warp Steps formed around them to point at all of them, so Solus projected their positions in his mind.","\"Stop right there, Verhen. We can still resolve our issues without further bloodshed.\" A tall man emerged from a dimensional tunnel, bearing the features of a living god.","He had flaming red hair, blue eyes, and the kind of body that only someone blessed by good luck and who had Awakened at a tender age could achieve. His bulging muscles stretched the fabric of his silk clothes with his every move, giving the impression he could tear them up just by taking a deep breath.","\"Hand Folkas’ body and that pitiful human you’re carrying to us, and we can end it here peacefully. You have my word.\" Lith wouldn’t have wasted time talking if not for the Isharas’ superior numbers and perfect battle formation.","\"I don’t know you or your kind, Scorpy, so forgive me if I trust your word as much as a fake coin.\" Lith replied.","\"Right.\" A flash of understanding passed over the Ishara’s face. \"I forgot you don’t dabble in either human or Awakened politics. I’m Ankhuta, and I speak on behalf of the Ishara race.\"","The wording of the phrase raised several red flags in Lith’s paranoid mind.","’He mentioned politics and introduced himself as the spokesman of an entire Divine Beast race.’ Lith thought. ’I smell some kind of diplomatic bullshit trap, but I have no idea what it is, or how I can dodge it. Solus?’","’Awakened don’t write books about their traditions, and I’ve attended as many Council meetings as you. Zero.’ She replied. ’Speak as little as you can and be vague until we understand what we are dealing with.","’Follow the instructions that Sylpha gave you back when she sent you to parley with the Undead Courts.’","Solus replayed the Queen’s words in Lith’s mind in case he had already forgotten the details of his mission in Othre as a Ranger, and she was right.","\"You have meddled in our affairs and killed a member of our species, but I’m willing to overlook your transgression since you were doing your job and Folkas failed to introduce himself.\"","’That’s how they got here so fast. The dead Ishara must have called his allies the moment he realized who I was, and they witnessed our fight.’ Lith thought, thanking his good luck that Solus hadn’t come out of her ring to help him deal with Folkas.","’Keep your lies to a minimum, then.’ Solus suggested. ’We are walking a tightrope and can’t see what waits for us at the bottom if we lose our balance.’","\"I’m not the one at fault here, Elder Ankhuta.\" Lith replied, following the Awakened etiquette by the letter. \"I’m the Supreme Magus of the Griffon Kingdom, and I was performing my duty when your kin attacked me first. I acted in self-defense.\"","\"Yes and no.\" Ankhuta would have loved to drop formalities and give the Tiamat a gruesome death, but too much was at risk. \"Yes, you defended yourself, but I assure you Folkas meant you no harm.","\"No, you’re not completely innocent. You’ve interfered in an important operation of the Ishara clan. Something that has been reviewed and approved by the Awakened Council first, and then by the Beast Lord of Distar, Faluel.","\"Feel free to call her if you don’t believe me.\"","\"My thoughts exactly.\" Lith took his amulet and pressed Faluel’s rune.","Yet instead of answering the call, the Hydra suddenly appeared by his side with Gungnir in her hands.","\"What’s going- Oh, gods-dammit!\" Faluel shrank to her human form, but she didn’t dispel the crackling energy that coursed through her glaive. \"Lith. Elder Ankhuta.\"","She gave both men a polite nod.","\"Why have you requested my presence?\"","\"It’s astounding how quickly you reacted to your former disciple’s call for help.\" The Ishara snorted. \"Especially considering that it took you days to grant us an audience when we requested it from you through the proper channels.\"","\"Business and friendship are each in a league of their own, Elder. Especially when your business benefits only you and my friendship with Lith bears the sweetest fruits.\" She swung Gungnir in the air, accumulating more power within the glaive.","\"I see.\" Ankhuta stared at the Blade Weapon with greed and stopped wondering how she had arrived that fast.","\"Faluel, Elder Ankhuta says that you authorized him to interfere with Ghishal County’s affairs.\" Lith said. \"That the Council knew the Isharas were going to replace the rulers of Distar with their political puppets. Is that true?\"","\"Yes, but it’s not like that.\" The Hydra scratched her head in embarrassment, making her prismatic hair sparkle like gemstones under sunlight. \"The Isharas simply asked my permission to start businesses in Distar and establish connections with the local nobles.","\"I warned them that Lustria was off the table and gave them the green light. All Awakened need to interact with human society when they need money, and as long as they don’t trigger a war or expose the Council, everything goes.\"","\"As you can see, we have done neither, Verhen.\" Ankhuta smiled in triumph. \"We left Lustria alone in accordance with Lady Faluel’s instructions and exerted our influence in the neighboring counties so subtly that there is no mention of our scheme even in the local news.","\"We upheld our side of the deal and didn’t break a single law of Garlen’s Council. You did.\"","\"That was short-sighted of you, Faluel.\" Lith ignored the Ishara. \"Ghishal is ruled by one of my dearest friends, and the Isharas have hurt a lot of innocent people. And for what?\"","\"For profit.\" Faluel was about to reply, but Ankhuta cut her short. \"We are far from our homeland, and have no rights over Garlen’s mana geysers and natural treasures. We did what we had to do to acquire the resources we need.","\"We are part of the Hydras’ bloodline awakening project, but building a lab to conduct our own experiments takes a lot of money. We didn’t harm a single human out of fun or malice.","\"We limited our involvement to giving a hand to criminal organizations that were already established in the various territories. We didn’t help them track the caravans, nor did we play any role in the actual robberies","\"As for Baron Carkas, he’s our liaison with human society. It’s only natural that we help him gain more power and influence so that he can better serve our interests. It’s what every Awakened bloodline has done from behind the scenes since the beginning of time.\"","\"For the sake of avoiding pointless conflict between our bloodlines, Verhen, I can even offer you to call off the entire operation in Distar if you provide us Isharas with everything we need until the completion of the bloodline awakening project.\"","\"How kind of you.\" Lith sneered.","\"I didn’t know you cared about Ghishal, Lith.\" Faluel glared at the Ishara. \"I also didn’t know what Ankhuta would do. The Council is no bureaucratic office. We don’t require a detailed explanation or business plan.","\"We only outline what an Awakened can and cannot do, and explain the consequences of violating the Council laws. So far, the Ishara have done nothing wrong.\""]},{"number":4457,"title":"Chapter 4457 Different Roles, Different Rules (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’I knew it.’ Lith recognized the convened signal for impending danger. ’Faluel can’t use a mind link without disrespecting the Isharas and can’t speak openly in front of Ankhuta, but he did lay a trap for me. If only I knew what kind of trap.’","’Those reports about Verhen being incapable of leaving his children’s side were a lie.’ The Elder Ishara inwardly snarled. ’He must have worked to expose Carkas while playing babysitter as his cover, and we fell for it hook, line, and sinker.’","Little did he know that Lith had actually spent most of his time with the babies until Jirni and Kamila had completed their investigation.","The early reports about him were accurate, and the Ishara scouts had failed to notice the construct replacing Lith because, after a few days of boredom, they had interrupted the surveillance.","’We stayed out of Lustria on purpose to avoid any conflict until the right moment and remain below Verhen’s notice. If he keeps his guard low around us, thinking that we hate his brother as much as he does, luring him into an ambush would have been easy.","’Now, instead, not only has he become aware of our presence so close to his home, but he also has a good reason to resent us for messing with Countess Lark. The Clan Leader will rip my exoskeleton off when he learns about this.","’Still, every cloud has a silver lining. If Verhen refuses to back down in disregard of the Council’s laws or attacks us, it will mark the start of a feud between the Ishara and Tiamat races.","’As soon as the Bloodline Awakening project is complete and we’ve built our secret facility, we’ll have the justification to strike Verhen in retaliation for today’s offense. Everyone will think we’ve taken his corpse to study it and won’t suspect we’ve taken him alive.","’All that remains to see is if Verhen is as cunning as they say, or if he will act recklessly against us out of his affection for his human friend.’","’ Think, Solus. Think. This can’t be too different from the nonsense of the Royal Court.’ Solus thought. ’The Council also runs on power and diplomacy. What would you expect if instead of a bunch of Awakened you were dealing with a powerful noble family?’","’That’s it, Solus. You’re a genius.’ Lith’s eyes widened in understanding. ’I think I know what’s happening here. Remember how the bastard introduced himself. Not as an individual, but as the Ishara’s spokesman in Distar.","’Which means that he speaks for his entire bloodline, and that any action I take against him will be interpreted as an act of aggression against the Isharas’ clan, not against the leader of a group of Divine Beasts who plotted Keyla’s ruin.’","’By my Mom, you’re right.’ Solus recalled all the notions of Court etiquette buried in her memory and gave him an array of potential answers.","\"I understand, Lady Faluel, and I thank you for coming here in a hurry.\" Lith gave her a polite bow. \"I can use your help, but not as the Beast Lord of the Distar region. You see, Elder Ankhuta, there’s something you’ve failed to consider.","\"I’m not here as Lith Verhen the Awakened. As I told you earlier, I’m here in my official capacity as the Supreme Magus of the Griffon Kingdom and the Protector of the Counties of Lustria and Ghishal.\"","He took his official badge out of his pocket dimension, showing both the Ishara and Faluel the title the Royals had appointed him with at the start of the mission.","It gave him the power and the authority of the Crown and upturned the rules of the game.","\"The treaty between the Griffon Kingdom and the Awakened Council is clear. Awakened rules do not apply to common criminals, or those caught breaking the Kingdom’s law.","\"No matter the origin of their power, anyone who kills and steals will be considered an enemy of the Griffon Kingdom and dealt with accordingly. I don’t care about what the Awakened Council authorized you to do.","\"As an official of the Kingdom, it is my duty to uphold its laws and apprehend criminals. Elder Ankhuta, you’ve just confessed your complicity in a series of crimes aimed at accruing wealth and replacing the current nobles of Distar with your human associates.","\"I have recorded your confession and forwarded it to the Royals as we speak. Let’s see what they think about your territorial conflict.\" Before Ankhuta could say a word, Lith pulled out his communication amulet and projected the hologram of the Royals.","\"I’m appalled by the criminal behavior of the Ishara Clan and the lax moral stance of the Awakened Council in mortal affairs.\" Meron’s voice was as cold as ice. \"What the Isharas need or want is irrelevant to the Crown.","\"We select our nobles to be the best and the brightest. To serve the interest of the people of the Kingdom and protect them from all threats. What Baron Carkas did is nothing short of high treason.","\"He sold his country to a foreign power and served the Isharas’ interests even at the cost of his own subjects. He endangered countless innocent lives and left entire remote villages starving only to pursue a higher noble title he clearly doesn’t deserve.","\"Baron Elmun Carkas failed his duty as a retainer of the Crown and is hereby stripped of all his titles and possessions. Elder Ankhuta, you are also charged with treason, murder, and conspiracy against the Griffon Kingdom.","\"If you and all the Isharas involved in the coup surrender now and turn yourselves in, the Crown will consider the matter resolved. We don’t blame the entire Ishara bloodline responsible for the crimes of a few of its members, but those few will pay the price for their crimes.","\"Supreme Magus Verhen, capture those who comply and execute those who try to escape justice.\"","\"Lady Faluel Nyxdra, I request your help as my personal friend and one of the four founding pillars of the Griffon Kingdom.\" Lith said. \"Your family has never relinquished its noble title nor reneged on its allegiance to the country your ancestor helped establish.\"","\"The Crown supports Magus Verhen’s request.\" The King nodded. \"In the name of the eternal friendship between the First King and Fyrwal the First, please help us, Lady Faluel.\"","Meron had no idea that Fyrwal was still alive and was none other than Faluel’s mother. Ankhuta, however, knew it all too well.","\"House Nyxdra answers the call, Your Majesty.\" Faluel adjusted her grip on Gungnir, pointing its blade at the Elder Ishara’s throat. \"Fight me if you dare!\"","’Fuck!’ Ankhuta clenched his teeth as the silver lining disappeared from the massive thundercloud of trouble looming over his head. ’Verhen used my own weapons against me and turned the tables.","’By acting on behalf of the Kingdom just like I do for my clan, we Isharas have lost justification for any future conflict, even if we now end up fighting to the death. Moreover, Verhen hasn’t declared his hostility against my entire bloodline, but only against those like me who tried to upset the political balance of the Distar Region.","’To make matters worse, the bastard recorded and transmitted our entire conversation in real tim e!’"]},{"number":4458,"title":"Chapter 4458 Different Roles, Different Rules (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Verhen turned what was supposed to be an Elder’s explanation of how the Awakened Council conducts its business to a young runt into the confession of an arrogant, dumb criminal.’ Ankhuta inwardly snarled.","’I can’t talk my way out of this anymore. I can only fight. And the worst part is that Verhen also got Faluel involved not as the Beast Lord of Distar, but as an heir of the Nyxdra Household.","’If we so much as hurt Faluel, her mother won’t give a damn about our reasons or what role her daughter played during the fight. Fyrwal will likely demand my head and those of everyone who hurt Faluel.","’If the Isharas refuse her request, then she’ll have an excellent reason to declare us her sworn enemies and kick us out of the bloodline awakening project! I can’t have that happening.’","\"I’m not going to fight you, Lady Faluel, but I’m not going to turn myself in either.\" The Elder Divine Beast released a bolt of silver lightning, empowering himself and his equipment. \"Blood of Selkis, teach these weaklings a lesson!\"","The Isharas followed his order and released bursts of Life Maelstrom, overwhelming Lith and Faluel with their mere numbers and the intensity of their aura.","\"This doesn’t look good.\" The Hydra said as Lith imbued her with Vital Storm. \"Please, tell me you have a plan.\"","\"I do.\" Lith activated the Full Guard spell of his armor, spreading a vast bright violet aura that would hide the energy signatures of the Eyes and Ears of Menadion.","At the same time, he pressed the emergency rune on his wrist guard. A jet stream of Void Flames struck one of the Isharas in the outer ring of the encirclement in the back, stripping her of the power of the silver lightning.","A blast of Blight Flames hit the Ishara a heartbeat later and set her mana ablaze. While everyone looked around to locate the source of the sneak attack and the burning Ishara tried to save her life, Tista hit her at Dragonspeed.","The two Divine Beasts crash-landed like a meteor, and Firefang’s claws caught the Ishara on the rebound, doubling their destructive power. The Adamant blades severed the Ishara’s head and punched a hole through her heart, killing her on the spot.","\"House Verhen answers the call!\" The Hekate roared before throwing herself into the fray.","’We can’t kill Verhen because we need him yet, and we can’t kill his sister either!’ Ankhuta inwardly cursed. ’If she dies, he’ll be the one to have justification to kill us on sight and ask anyone interested in his bloodline to give him a hand.’","\"Beat them an inch from their lives!\" He actually said with mad fury.","The death of every stable Ishara bloodline was a terrible loss for his clan. The Elder had been entrusted with the Distar Region to avoid trouble with the locals and ensure that everything went smoothly.","After exposing the Isharas’ agenda and losing two promising youths, Ankhuta knew that his future was at stake even if he won the battle.","The clan leader wouldn’t kill him outright because Ankhuta still had a long life ahead of him and could produce many offspring. Yet no one in the clan would hesitate to sacrifice Ankhuta if it meant appeasing the Royals’ wrath and preventing more senseless deaths.","Two Isharas came at Tista from opposite sides, and she hurled a twin jet of True and Frozen Flames that they easily dodged. Only when they were too close to dodge did she unleash a burst of Void Flames from each battle claw.","The Life Maelstrom faded, slowing the Isharas down and making them feel as if their bodies had turned into lead. Tista was empowered by the Vital Storm, instead tripling her combat prowess.","She lunged, slashed, and cut as she moved from one Ishara to the other with the grace of a ballerina.","She couldn’t focus on one of them, or she would lose the advantage gained from her surprise attack. The Hekate failed to kill the Isharas, but she maimed them and kept them from releasing more Life Maelstrom.","\"Stop her!\" A female Ishara yelled as she conjured her tier five Spirit Spell, Blasting Wave. \"Rescue our brethren while I keep her busy.\"","\"In your dreams!\" A flick of Tista’s claws activated the many magical formations she had placed across the battlefield while waiting for Lith’s signal and kept inactive until that moment to prevent the enemy from noticing.","Gravity, Spirit, and Dimensional arrays appeared at the focal points of the Isharas’ battle formation, making it crumble. Gravity sent the heavily armored Divine Beasts crashing against the ground, unable to withstand the weight of their own bodies.","Spirit arrays conjured multiple Griffon Fetters and anchored them in place. Every Ishara captured by the magical formations was unable to move from their current spot, and the emerald chain neutralized most of their strength.","The Dimensional arrays Warped entire groups of Isharas hundreds of kilometers away, leaving them stranded in the middle of nowhere and with no idea of how to find their allies before it was too late.","\"You shouldn’t underestimate me just because I’m not famous!\" Tista conjured a barrage of spells with each attack and block, and more with the Mouth of Menadion. \"I’m the second strongest member of the Demon race, jackass!\"","A hail of tier four and five spells blew two depowered Isharas’ limbs to bits while also keeping their remaining allies from getting closer. Tista had her spells detonate all around her, creating a thick fog of mana that blinded Life Vision and made it impossible to spot her from a distance.","The Isharas could only come close to her and risk getting hit by her Void Flames or shoot their spells blindly and risk hitting their brethren.","As for Faluel, she had no Void Flames and was just an Emperor Beast. Even with her seven heads, she was lighter and weaker than the smallest Ishara. The Life Maelstrom widened the power gap between them so much that her battle experience became negligible even when she faced a much less skilled opponent.","\"Stay back!\" The best she could do was keep her distance and cast seven spells at a time as fast as she could.","The problem was that her opponents knew it, and Faluel couldn’t do anything to stop them from closing in for close-quarters combat and pummeling her. The Isharas surrounded her like a swarm of wasps and stung at her with their acidic tails.","There were so many of them, and they moved so fast that the Hydra failed to keep up despite Full Guard and her seven pairs of eyes. It took the blood of Selkis only three hits to destroy the Spirit Barrier of her armor and six more to tear down any defense Faluel could conjure.","Then it became a bloody dance of pincers, blades, and stingers.","The Isharas attacked her with perfect coordination. Every time Faluel intercepted a blow, she remained wide open and another Ishara struck her side before she could regain her balance.","The Hydra could only partially avoid the ensuing crippling blow by twisting her body. Blood spurted from her wound, and the impact threw her off guard long enough for a third Ishara to attack her."]},{"number":4459,"title":"Chapter 4459 Not Weak (Part 1)","paragraphs":["So far, Faluel had managed to deflect crippling blows by conjuring explosive spells in front of the enemy’s weapons at the last second and detonating them at point-blank range.","The Hydra was immune to her own mana, and the ensuing shockwaves hurt her much less than the Adamant blades would. The Isharas, instead, took the full brunt of the explosions and were blown away, giving Faluel precious moments of respite.","\"Come on, suckers. I can do this all day!\" She lied through the teeth of her third head as it took a deep breath of Invigoration to replenish her mana and heal her body.","\"That’s a game two can play!\" A male Ishara lunged with his spear while his two team members regained their strength with their breathing techniques.","Faluel parried his thrust and intercepted the stinger of his tail with one of her mouths. She bit as hard as she could, her fangs pumping acidic venom into his tail. The Ishara grunted in pain and unleashed two more attacks with his pincers.","The Hydra blocked them as well, but she needed to extend two more heads, forcing herself into an uncomfortable stance. Just like the Isharas wanted.","\"Got you, lizard!\" The pincers of the Ishara focused the two Life Maelstrom-amplified spells he had conjured and shot them at Faluel.","She conjured the opposing elements to neutralize the threat, but the Ishara’s magic was much stronger and denser. His spells pierced through her defenses and hit her stumpy torso like sledgehammers.","The other two Isharas joined the attack as soon as the Hydra crashed to the ground and the air was squeezed out of her lungs.","\"Weak.\" A rumbling metallic voice resounded as the volley of tier five spells rained down on Faluel.","She ignored the distracting voice and conjured the Hands of Menadion on top of two of her heads in the form of crowns. The artifact’s enchanted blades countered the elements imbued in every spell Faluel struck down, but she had only two blades to face the magical onslaught.","\"Weak!\" The voice roared louder as Gungnir lunged forward on its own and released part of the Blade Energy it had stored into a golden dome that shielded Faluel from harm.","\"What the fuck?\" Faluel allowed herself to stare at the glaive with one of her heads. \"You can talk?\"","\"WEAK!\" Gungnir’s battle cry manifested as a shockwave of air magic that pushed Faluel to her knees and the Isharas back. \"Not weak! Not me!\"","The glaive escaped her grip, bolting against the nearest Ishara while wreathing itself in a giant hard-light construct shaped like a Dragon.","\"What is that?\" The male Ishara could see with Life Vision that Gungnir held the power of an incomplete Blade Spell, but a Blade Spell nonetheless.","A fraction of that energy was enough to kill a Divine Beast if struck directly.","He Blinked away, but the Dragon construct was faster. The Ishara kept Blinking away from Faluel, but the conjured creature kept getting closer.","\"Fuck!\" Realizing he had no way out, the male Ishara conjured a powerful Spirit Barrier.","He also unleashed every spell he had at the ready against the conjured Dragon after boosting them with a spark of Life Maelstrom.","Great was his surprise when the roaring spheres of fire, darkness, and earth met no resistance as they hit the construct. The deadly spells phased through the shining Dragon harmlessly while Gungnir bolted forward unimpeded.","\"Fuck! This thing is not a construct. It’s just a hologram!\" The Ishara realized his lapse in judgment only when he struck at the Dragon’s maw closing on him and discovered it was an empty threat.","\"Not weak! Not me!\" Gungnir had wasted no mana in theatrics.","The glaive had simply channeled part of its aura outward in the shape of a Dragon to hide its real flight path until the very last moment. Gungnir recalled the mana dispersed in the hologram and focused it on its tip.","The resulting Blade Strike punched a hole through the male Ishara’s chest, severing the humanoid upper torso from the scorpion lower body.","\"Not me!\" Gungnir performed a U-turn and blew the Ishara’s head to bits on its way back.","The Soaring Dragon Blade Spell reappeared, and it dove at the two remaining Isharas.","\"You finish off the Hydra!\" A female Ishara said to another. \"I’ll deal with that thing. It can only target one of us, and now we know what-\"","\"Not weak!\" The hologram sprouted a second Dragon head, each staring at a different Ishara.","The mass of light was large enough to hide Gungnir’s position, making it impossible to tell which Ishara was its real target.","\"That thing could be anywhere! What do we do?\" Asked the second female Ishara.","\"Run!\" The first replied.","\"Good gods.\" Faluel muttered as the hologram grew a third neck from which another head sprouted. \"The little bastard is learning.\"","Gungnir struck the slowest of the Isharas, using half of the energy it had left to blow her body to bits on impact. Then, the glaive plunged into the ground at Faluel’s feet, the shockwave forcing her to stand up and grab its haft to support herself.","\"Not weak!\" It growled. \"Not us. Stand. Fight. Feed me!\"","\"I can definitely believe you’re Lith’s craft.\" Faluel panted, using Invigoration to replenish her strength and her other six heads to cast her Blade Spell, Venom Fang, as fast as she could. \"You’re barely a month old, and you’re already a nagging pain in my ass!\"","The golden energy enveloping Gungnir grew in size as new mana flowed into the Adamant weapon.","\"Talk less. Cast more!\" The glaive grumbled, avidly absorbing every drop of mana she released.","\"I need help!\" The only survivor of the three-man unit didn’t feel confident facing the Hydra alone. \"If we don’t stop Faluel, she’ll cast a real Blade Spell!\"","Not with all of her seven heads focused on the last remaining Ishara. Not with the murderer of her best friends in Faluel’s grip and filled with new power.","Meanwhile, Lith faced Ankhuta and two more Isharas alone. The good news was that Tista’s arrays had scattered the enemy forces, and it would take them a while to assemble and coordinate their efforts again.","The bad news was that Lith was still outnumbered and outgunned. Life Maelstrom made each of the Isharas’ many limbs a threat Lith had to watch out for and bestowed them physical and magical prowess that eclipsed his own.","Their long weapons gave the Blood of Selkis the reach advantage, while their pincers worked both as a secondary attack and a tool to shoot hyper-compressed spells with pinpoint accuracy.","Their long tails were slightly shorter than the polearms, but they released jets of a powerful acid even if blocked or dodged.","The splashes of acid inflicted on Lith only shallow wounds, but he had to be careful they never came close to his eyes or his open mouth whenever he breathed a burst of mystical flames.","\"You are an annoying bastard, Verhen!\" Ankhuta snarled as he unleashed a barrage of quick thrusts of his spear and two anti-Dragon spells, Frozen Wasteland, from his pincers.","The tier five spells conjured a cold wave with water magic and drained the humidity in the surroundings with air magic."]},{"number":4460,"title":"Chapter 4460 Not Weak (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The two effects synergized in a loop that instantly dropped the temperature by dozens of degrees in their area of effect even when they missed their target.","The Dragon blood flowing in Lith’s veins made his Tiamat form weak to cold, so he couldn’t let any of the Frozen Wastelands come anywhere close. The situation would have been bad even if he fought the Ishara Elder alone, but Lith also had to stay on guard against Ankhuta’s apprentices.","The two younger Isharas were less skilled than their master, but they always remained behind Ankhuta and fired spells on Lith to keep him on the back foot.","The Elder’s apprentices moved to close-quarter combat only when Lith was already cornered, making any opening they unwittingly left in their defense impossible for the Tiamat to exploit.","Lith had held his ground until that moment only because Solus filtered the redundant information from the Ears and Eyes of Menadion, sparing him the mental burden that the artifacts would put on him.","The two pieces of Menadion Set allowed him to read the trajectories of blades and spells, moving out of every attack’s way before it even started. Lith had also infused Ragnarök with Raging Severance and circulated the water element in the Davross of the blade to further enhance its effects.","Every time the angry blade clashed with one of the Ishara’s polearms, the latter became covered in a thick layer of ice that sealed its enchantments and slowly drained its power core.","When one of the compressed spells came too close to home, Lith intercepted it with Ragnarök and severed the spell’s connection with the world energy, neutralizing it before it could unleash the power of the elements.","This tactic was particularly effective against water spells like Frozen Wasteland.","In such a case, however, Lith replaced the water element in the Davross with Jerak. The Cursed Element combined with Raging Severance to turn such spells into a a solid block of ice that plummeted like a brick and harmlessly exploded when it hit the ground.","Ankhuta had no explanation for the phenomenon, but he was still confident in his victory.","’No matter what dirty trick Verhen uses, if he can’t attack, he’s destined to lose.’ He thought. ’I only need to land one solid blow. The moment Verhen falters, my disciples will finish him off.’","’I can’t keep up like this. It’s only a matter of time before I make a mistake or they get lucky. When that happens, I’m dead.’ Lith was aware of the problem as well and pushed his brain to the limit to find a solution.","’Do you want me to step in?’ Solus asked while reading the mana flow of the incoming Isharas’ spells with the Ears and warning Lith of their hidden strategy thanks to the Eyes.","’And to what end?’ Lith replied. ’If someone sees you appear out of nowhere, it won’t be just the Isharas to ask us questions we can’t answer. Moreover, you don’t have the raw strength to face them either, and without you the Eyes and Ears would become useless to me.","’Divided we’d be a much easier prey, Solus. Our only chance of victory is to face them together and play dirty!’","Lith intercepted Ankhuta’s spear and covered it in ice from Raging Severance. Before the Ishara Elder could move aside to let his disciples follow into his attack with their own, Lith activated the red and black memory crystals in his armor, conjuring a tier five Final Eclipse.","A sphere of black flames enveloped Lith and washed over the master and apprentices’ trio.","’Now!’ Lith used Void Magic to turn Final Eclipse into Frozen Crescent, a pillar of icy light.","At the same time, he activated the blue and silver crystals in his armor to double Frozen Crescent’s destructive power. Ankhuta and his disciples found themselves trapped in a thick layer of ice that somehow amplified the effects of the Raging Severance that already plagued their weapons.","The power cores of the Isharas’ equipment bled mana at an alarming rate, yet Lith still had one card to play.","’Jerak Skan Ghirash!’ He conjured the tier three Zero Spell, Arctic Despair, right into the very center of the Frozen Crescent.","The Cursed Element spread through the normal ice like a disease, dropping the temperature below -200° C and turning the frozen pillar that encased the Isharas into Zero.","The Blood of Selkis felt the heat escape from their bodies and with it, their lives. The Isharas unleashed the spells they had prepared to deal with Lith against themselves, shattering their icy prison before the cold lulled them into an eternal slumber.","Lith bolted forward with his blade aimed at Ankhuta’s head, to take the Elder down before he could warm himself up.","\"I admit my arrogance and recognize your strength.\" The Elder Ishara said as he released a swirling blue sphere of Doom Tide.","The two younger Isharas conjured two much smaller domes of Doom Tide to ride their master’s bloodline ability until it expanded far enough away from him to Blink to his side.","The growing number of Lesser Divine Beasts born in the Ishara clan had forced them to consider the death of any pure-blooded child of Selkis like an unacceptable failure and develop techniques that maximized their youngest members’ chances of survival.","Lith took the Doom Tide in full, instead, failing to resist its overwhelming pressure.","’It’s not the first time I deal with someone who can use Doom Tide, but it’s the first time someone also imbues it with Life Maelstrom against me!’ Lith inwardly cursed as the blue energy blast swept him away.","The Isharas had all the time they needed to free their weapons from the Raging Severance and heal the damage they had suffered from the Frozen Crescent. Their equipment, however, wasn’t so lucky.","’Master, my weapon’s power core is below half mana capacity. We need to retreat.’ One of the younger Isharas said.","’Don’t be an idiot, Venkhara.’ Ankhuta replied. ’Verhen can conjure Blade Spells. If we turn our backs on him, he’ll use us as sheaths for his sword. Give him no quarter!’","’What do we do now?’ Solus racked her brain, but aside from throwing a sucker punch or handing the Fury to Lith, there wasn’t much she could do.","’Let’s keep on playing dirty.’ Lith replied.","Doom Tide had depleted the area around him of world energy. Bloodline abilities, elemental spells, enchanted equipment, and anything that required Mogar’s essence wouldn’t work until the balance was restored.","Allegedly.","Lith had indeed failed to stop the Doom Tide, but he had used Swirling Wind to drain as much world energy as he could from the Ishara’s bloodline ability, reduce Doom Tide’s destructive power, and envelope himself in a thin layer of dense world energy.","Ankhuta and his disciples charged forward without even bothering to use their weapons, aware that without the protection of their enchantments, the Adamant blades might suffer permanent damage when clashing against Davross.","Lith, instead, held Ragnarök in his hands, following the enemy movements with his seven eyes.","’Verhen’s effort is commendable, but the fate of this fight is already sealed.’ Ankhuta pointed out the many flaws in Lith’s guard to his disciples via the mind link. ’Take him down!’"]},{"number":4461,"title":"Chapter 4461 Never Again (Part 1)","paragraphs":["The three Isharas came at Lith in unison in a triangle formation, forcing him to face one of them while exposing his back to another and his side to the last Ishara.","Master and apprentices began their attack by simultaneously lashing at the Tiamat with their tails. One bolted at Ragnarök itself, aiming to destroy the angry blade while there was still no world energy to fuel its self-repair enchantments.","The second tail was aimed at Lith’s Voidwalker armor. A single dose of acid wouldn’t inflict any permanent damage to something that big, but it would be enough to reduce the armor to a useless lump of scales and metal until the end of the fight.","The third and last stinger was aimed at the small gap between Lith’s gorget and helm. A successful strike would sever his spine, leaving him paralyzed from the neck down.","’We can take Verhen hostage, end this stupid fight, and teach him a lesson.’ Ankhuta thought. ’We won’t let him go until he pays the weregild for all the Isharas he killed and returns their bodies and equipment.’","Lith’s tail intercepted the stinger coming from his back, striking it from below with the bone spike on the end of the Tiamat’s tail.","The Adamant-coated bone spike pierced into the stinger like a hook, while the rest of the tail wrapped itself around the Ishara’s, throwing her around like a fish dangling from a line.","Ragnarök severed the stinger in front of Lith from the rest of the composite tail while releasing a burst of red flames that cauterized the wound on both ends and made it harder to heal.","Lith’s upside-down right wing splayed its bones into a hand-like pose and caught the stinger coming from the side, pulling it away. Venkhara hit only air, and the sudden tug forced him into an uncomfortable position from which he couldn’t unleash the Spirit Spells he had prepared.","At the same time, a blast of mystical red flames struck the three Isharas, burning their flesh and mana alike. The Balefire conjured by Lith’s red eye also ravaged their defenseless equipment, melting the metal and consuming what world energy was left in their power cores.","The three Isharas screamed in a pain that darkness fusion couldn’t suppress as the mystical fire also burned the runes of the spells they had conjured inside their bodies.","’Balefire isn’t as strong as Origin Flames and won’t neutralize Life Maelstrom like Void Flames, but I can release as much as I want without messing with my breathing rhythm.’ Lith thought.","’Also, not having to squeeze the air out of my lungs allows me to do this!’","The Tiamat pushed his muscles and fusion magic to their utmost limit, twisting his body and sending the female Ishara caught in the grip of his wing to crash into Ankhuta.","The impact disrupted their focus and doubled the amount of Balefire engulfing them.","’If I conjure my Spirit Spell from so up close, Venkhara and Ishuta will get caught in the conflagration.’ Ankhuta inwardly cursed. ’And that if Verhen doesn’t use Ishuta as a meat shield!’","He was about to finish the thought when Lith whipped his tail and slammed Ishuta on top of her allies. The damage the Isharas suffered was minimal thanks to the Life Maelstrom coursing through their sturdy bodies, but that wasn’t Lith’s goal.","The Tiamat could now focus the Balefire on a single, tangled target, and release a jet stream of Void Flames that would hit all three Isharas at once.","The Blood of Selkis was flabbergasted when Lith managed to produce one more kind of mystical flames despite the alleged lack of world energy.","Surprise turned into grief as the silver lightning abandoned their bodies and the tier five Spirit Spell, Primordial Roar, shattered Ishuta like glass and still had enough power to blast the other two Isharas away.","\"This is impossible!\" Ankhuta roared as he unleashed his Spirit Spells, and Lith dodged them with ease, burning them with another burst of Balefire. \"How can this be?\"","Meanwhile, Tista was still surrounded, and her situation worsened by the second.","Once they had overcome the initial surprise, the Isharas caught in her magical formations had managed to either escape the confines of Tista’s arrays or just break them apart with sheer might.","Realizing the danger that the Hekate posed to their survival, only a couple of Isharas went to help Inara deal with Faluel while the rest focused on Tista.","’Fuck me sideways!’ The Hekate used Ethereal Aegis to turn her body into a mass of living Flames and escape a deadly trap, also burning a Divine Beast inside out in the process. ’There are too many of them, and I have only two more bursts of Void Flames stored inside of Firefang.","’Once I consume them, I’ll be alone against a bunch of monsters who are over twice as strong as me and have enough limbs to sell a few at the local market and still have plenty to spare to turn me into a meat skewer!’","The bloodline ability consumed none of her mana and saved her life, but rebuilding the flaming parts of her body destroyed by the hail of enchanted blades and spells the Isharas had thrown at Tista drained her stamina.","The Blood of Selkis had no idea how Ethereal Aegis worked and stopped their assault for a moment in confusion.","’There must be a cost to using that ability, or Tista Verhen’s fame as an immortal warrior would have spread far and wide.’ The Divine Beasts thought almost in unison before chasing after the Hekate.","Tista flew amid her own magical formations, using them to keep the Isharas at bay, but Life Maelstrom made them faster than Dragonspeed. On top of that, small units of Isharas kept their distance and dismantled the arrays, removing the obstacles that kept their brethren from cornering their prey.","’Oh, screw it! There’s no time like when you are still breathing.’ Tista thought as the encirclement tightened on her so much that she couldn’t escape without using Aethereal Aegis again and consuming most of her life force.","She flapped her wings with all of her might, throwing her colored feathers in every direction in a storm of prismatic daggers. The Isharas dodged, blocked, and deflected most of them, suffering little to no damage from the few feathers that hit their marks.","The Isharas thought it was just a desperate bluff to slow them down when the Prismatic Wind stored in the feathers conjured a tornado. Tista had developed an array version of Lith’s Mjolnir spell, and the Isharas were the first to experience its effects.","Air magic produced strong winds, air blades, and lightning bolts, while the earth element conjured stone spikes, walls, and shields. Together, the two elements magnetically charged both the rocks and the Isharas caught in the storm.","The repulsive effect further accelerated Tista’s stone constructs while the attractive effect turned the Blood of Selkis into living lightning rods.","Last but not least, Void Magic constantly switched one element into the other. Many Isharas crashed into solid walls that hadn’t been there a moment ago, while others aimed their spells at stone projectiles that disappeared like mist just to reform a heartbeat later and hit their target."]},{"number":4462,"title":"Chapter 4462 Never Again (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Even a bright violet-cored Awakened lacked the strength to conjure a natural disaster without long preparation, but Void Magic turned air and earth into an electromagnetic storm that fueled itself by the second.","The sheer focus required to deal with so many opponents and manipulate the elements with such degree of finesse made Tista wheeze with effort. She needed a few seconds to use her breathing technique and recover her strength, or she wouldn’t last much longer.","’Come on, you bastards. Get scared and fall back. Conjure a Silverwing’s Annihilation or something. Anything slow that will group you for a burst of Void Flames will do!’ She thought.","Yet the Isharas kept pressing forward without giving her a single moment of respite.","’Well, thank you for nothing!’ Tista met the long blade of a glaive with her left battle claw, producing a rain of sparks as the enchanted metals screeched.","The Ishara conjured two hyper-focused elemental spells from his pincers, and the Hekate extended her right hand with the palm out. A burst of Void Flames devoured the two spells and removed the Life Maelstrom that empowered the Divine Beast.","Tista didn’t slow down, severing his neck as she moved past him and kicking the corpse into the line of fire of her pursuers. The Isharas failed to adjust their aim in time, and their spells blew the remains of their friend into bits.","\"Rebura!\" A feminine voice shrieked in grief. \"We might have still saved my brother, you bitch!\"","Tista extended her middle claw in condolences and conjured the Spirit Barriers of the Mouth of Menadion and Ishka’s Honor.","’One breath. I need just one breath to-’ A heavy war hammer hit the concentric barriers from above, sending the Hekate to slam against the ground and cutting her short.","With no longer a high-speed moving target, all the Isharas’ spells reached their mark. A hail of Life Maelstrom-boosted tier five spells shattered the Spirit Barriers and reached Tista.","It was then that twelve bursts of Void Flames struck the Isharas from behind and as many quasi-Blade Tier spells killed them on the spot. The seven Demons of the Darkness formed an external perimeter around Tista, while the five Sigil Demons Blinked to her side.","’Sorry for not stepping in earlier, but we are too damn small to matter in a brawl.’ Varegrave said with a mind link.","’We couldn’t even unleash our Blade Spells because we’ve already used them once today.’ Trion said. ’Another shot and our equipment will become purely ornamental.’","’Also, don’t forget about Doom Tide.’ Locrias said. ’Being so close makes us an easy target. We have to scatter, or these cowards will take away the world energy and overwhelm us with their sheer numbers.’","’You’ve saved my life, and that’s all that matters. Thank you.’ Tista took a single breath of Invigoration that the Swirling Wind conjured by the Demons around her filled to the brim with world energy. ’Now let me help you.’","Her body healed, and her strength returned as she unfurled her wings.","Valia charged forward and ordered the Demons of the Darkness to follow her. Queen’s Blessing turned them all into Void Demons, shrouding them with black flames and infusing them with Vital Storm.","The Void Demons were now three times stronger, and their touch would consume Life Maelstrom. They might still be unable to kill an Ishara, but their opponent now would lose the edge that the silver lightning gave them until they managed to get rid of the Demons.","Tista bolted off the ground while the Void Demons scattered amid the Isharas to keep them from using Doom Tide. She wasn’t alone anymore, but her chances of victory were still slim.","Even with their new strength, the Sigil Demons were still weaker and slower than the Isharas, and the mass gap with their enemies made their blows an annoyance at best. The Demons of the Darkness also had no equipment, so if not for their ability to breathe Void Flames, the Isharas would have ignored them.","A Demon’s spells were powerful, but without Lith, they couldn’t recover their strength and became weaker the longer a fight went on.","’It’s been an honor serving one last time.’ One of the Demons of the Darkness beat his fist against his chest and detonated the energy stored in his darkness body into a brilliant flash of Void Flames.","The conflagration of black flames washed over the nearby Isharas, sending them flying and stripping all those too slow in raising their Spirit Barriers of their Life Maelstrom.","’From below, we rise!’ Another Demon of the Darkness exploited the ensuing confusion to dart in the middle of the enemy formation before overloading his black core.","’Don’t waste their sacrifice and heal yourself, Tista!’ Ripha yelled telepathically. ’No Ishara died. The Demons have just bought you a few precious seconds. There’s no telling if this trick will work a second time, and there are only five Void Demons left.’","Tista nodded, taking deep breaths of Invigoration until Life Vision spotted six Blinks surrounding her from all sides. She shot the last burst of Void Flames into the dimensional door in front of her and impaled the Isharas that emerged from the other Blinks on her free battle claw and tails.","The blows hurt the Isharas and foiled the attacks of their weapons, but didn’t disrupt their focus, nor could they do anything against the Isharas’ pincers and tails.","Focused spells sent Tista spinning from one Ishara to the other like a pinball, while the acidic stingers melted her wings into stumps.","’We need help. Real help!’ Ripha and the other Sigil Demons fought like lions, but they could only prolong the Hekate’s life for a few seconds.","Lith heard Menadion and turned his head, witnessing his sister’s struggle thanks to his keen Tiamat sight. He watched her beautiful wings become black and burn. He watched gushes of her blood fill the air as her life force weakened.","Time froze as the figure of Carl’s corpse overlapped with Tista’s body. Her scales seemed to turn black as Lith pictured her as an adult Elysia, no longer under the Guardians’ protection and dragged into a fight that wasn’t her own.","’Not again.’ Something inside the Tiamat broke, and the elemental energy stored inside his body flowed faster and faster from one eye into the next, forming a perfect circle. ’Never again.’","Ankhuta exploited that moment to perform a flurry of thrusts with his spear, keeping Venkhara behind him and ready to strike. The Elder Ishara’s attack ended with the first strike.","When Ragnarök intercepted the spear tip, Ankhuta felt as if he had struck a mountain. He almost lost his grip on his weapon, his hand going numb from the sheer violence of the impact.","’What was that?’ The Elder Divine Beast thought as he studied the Tiamat with Life Vision. ’Verhen is still weaker and slower than me. Yet he suddenly became much heavier and sturdier. I...’","The parry had coated the spear with Raging Severance, and Ragnarök released a burst of Balefire at the Ishara immediately after. Lith conjured Mana Storm from the tip of the angry blade, his attacks seamlessly flowing into each other."]},{"number":4463,"title":"Chapter 4463 Payback (Part 1)","paragraphs":["The mana bullets rained on Ankhuta from every side, and his depowered equipment offered him no protection against the emerald onslaught.","Venkhara abandoned the cover of his master’s back to move on the offensive, hitting Lith with a simultaneous barrage of glaive strikes, pincer cuts, and tail lashes.","Lith didn’t block any of them. Each attack landed exactly where Venkhara had aimed it. However, none of them cut deep. The Tiamat seemed to wear another layer of armor over his scales, and his body was denser than Orichalcum.","Lith exploited the moment the limbs of the young Ishara stopped inside his flesh to grab Venkhara’s spear with his free hand, the pincers with his upside-down wings, and the stinger with his mouth.","Lith’s fangs bit into the enchanted metal and released the Origin Flames directly into Venkhara’s body. At the same time, his wings pulled his pincers in opposite directions while his hand kept the spear still, locking the Ishara into place.","Lith’s tail, however, was free to move. It plunged into the scorpion bottom half from below and bisected it horizontally. Venkhara was still alive when the Tiamat ripped his pincer arms from his shoulders and set him ablaze with bright violet flames.","\"No!\" Ankhuta yelled in fury as his last disciple turned into ashes.","He released more Life Maelstrom and infused it into the strongest Doom Tide he could conjure.","Which wasn’t much. The world energy was still thin, and Lith had access only to what he had stockpiled with Swirling Wind.","The Tiamat placed his hand on the expanding blue dome and shattered it like glass. His open palm met no resistance as it closed around Ankhuta’s throat and released a Final Eclipse from one of his spell-holding rings that snuffed out the Elder Divine Beast’s life.","The darkness element sapped what was left of Ankhuta’s strength, while the fire element burned him to cinders.","Lith took a deep breath as he swooped down towards Tista, giving new strength to his Demons.","’There’s no need to save your mana. Go all out.’ His thoughts reached the Sigil Demons through the black chains, and they wove the final part of their respective Blade Spells.","\"Incoming!\" An Ishara yelled, and those in the backline of the combat formation turned around to unleash a volley of spells at the Tiamat.","None of them reached their mark. No matter their tier or element, every spell faded away the moment it got close to its mark. Lith landed like a meteor in the middle of the magical onslaught, wreathed in Balefire.","The Isharas attacking from a distance witnessed their best spells dissolving into thin air, no matter how much willpower they poured into them. Those who entered the range of the angry blade with their weapons found them covered in ice, their enchantments frozen still.","Ragnarök’s edge, however, had no such problem.","It cut through Orichalcum and Adamant like a hot knife through butter, severing hafts and limbs alike. Lith wrapped Tista in his wings and used his tier three Spirit Magic spell, Mother’s Embrace, to treat her wounds.","’It’s just like when we were kids, big sister.’ He said via a mind link. ’Just breathe, no matter how hard or painful it is, and everything will be alright.’","\"Elemental magic doesn’t work. He must have Forgemastered his armor with a portable array.\" An Ishara said.","\"That’s absurd, but it’s the only plausible explanation.\" Another replied. \"Use Spirit Magic!\"","Many attacks slipped past Lith’s guard despite the Ears of Menadion and Full Guard, but they rarely hit their target. Not because Lith moved so fast that the Isharas surrounding him couldn’t follow, but because the enchanted blades harmlessly phased through him.","The Tiamat lunged with Ragnarök, but the Blood of Selkis ignored the attack. There was no one within Lith’s reach since the Isharas had retreated so as not to get caught in the tier five Spirit Spells they would soon unleash.","Lith’s right arm and blade fell to the ground into a back puddle, while the shadow they projected gained a third dimension and pierced an Ishara’s chest from behind.","\"Screw it! Fire at will!\" Another Ishara said, and Lith nodded in approval.","At his signal, the remaining five Demons of the Darkness exploded in unison, throwing the enemy formation into disarray and stripping the Isharas and their spells of the Life Maelstrom empowering them.","Lith put Tista down and covered her with his own body, focusing the Spirit Barriers of his equipment around her because even though the Spirit spell would tear his armor apart, at least his own mana contained in the black flames couldn’t harm him.","The Sigil Demons waited for half a heartbeat to unleash their Blade Tier spells, squeezing every drop of mana stored in their bodies and equipment. Five beams of black-reddish light flashed for a second, each one turning scores of Isharas into dismembered corpses.","\"Well, this sucks, but I’m too pissed off to care!\" Faluel too had just completed her Blade Spell, Venom Fang, killing the Isharas surrounding her on the spot and aiming what was left of its energy at the remaining Divine Beasts.","The spell manifested in a pillar of light shaped like a prismatic snake baring its fangs. Everything it touched broke down into a sizzling mass, as if it had been doused in a powerful acid.","\"Snake. Lame.\" Gungnir had no tongue, but it managed to click in disappointment.","\"Hydras have snake necks, you buzzkill.\" She replied. \"What’s wrong with my spell having the form of a snake?\"","\"No Dragon. Leviathan.\" Gungnir replied with a matter-of-fact voice.","\"Fuck! You’re right.\" Faluel cursed as she bolted to the rescue of her apprentices, weaving a second Venom Fang with all her seven heads as the barrage of Spirit Spells reached its target and exploded in an emerald dawn","\"Everybody, retreat! Don’t waste your lives and run!\" The Ishara left in charge wove a Warp Gate that led as far away as he could remember, quickly followed by the rest of the survivors.","Lith Verhen was still alive.","The Void Flames had weakened the tier five Spirit Spells and neutralized the Life Maelstrom they contained. Balefire had further weakened the spells, but there were dozens of them, and they had all been aimed at the same spot.","The Voidwalker armor had crumbled under the repeated shockwaves generated by the Void Demons’ explosions and the Isharas’ tier five Spirit spells, leaving most of the Tiamat’s body exposed until the Davross-Adamant alloy rebuilt itself.","It allowed everyone, Faluel included, to notice that his scales had all become emerald. Strings of light connected his seven eyes, letting all the elements that coursed through his wings conjure their power at the same time.","’That’s what happened!’ Solus looked at his six wings, noticing that each one of them was wreathed in the elemental light of its corresponding eye. ’Lightforged increased his mass, Arcane Bulwark his defense, and Vital Storm amplified their effects threefold.","’In this state, Lith isn’t limited to using one elemental ability at a time like Ryla. He can use them all at once. It already happened when we fought Ruugat of the Earth.’","\"You’re not going anywhere, Isharas.\" Lith’s voice was an angry snarl. \"Not this time.\""]},{"number":4464,"title":"Chapter 4464 Payback (Part 2)","paragraphs":["He held Ragnarök aloft and unleashed his Blade Spell, Ruin, flooding it with Vital Storm and the air element of the Davross blade. Reddish-black waves of light mercilessly struck the Isharas in the back and killed them on the spot.","Some of them managed to open a Warp Steps, but they were killed before they could cross to the other side. Lith poured even more mana into the Blade Spell when that happened.","The resulting explosion would kill or maim anyone in the proximity of the exit point, and the resulting dust cloud made the positions of many of the Isharas’ gathering points visible from a distance.","\"Damn, if that’s what a Blade Spell can do, I still have a long way to go.\" Faluel said after comparing the destructive power of the two spells.","\"We can discuss this later.\" Lith replied as the Voidwalker armor covered him again. \"Can you please reopen those Steps? Maybe there’s someone we can take prisoner and get some answers.\"","\"Sure.\" One of Faluel’s heads said while the other six used their newfound knowledge of dimensional magic to reignite the lingering energy of the collapsed Warp Steps. \"Couldn’t you just spare one of these guys?\"","\"It doesn’t work like that.\" Lith shook his head. \"I can split Ruin into many parts, but it’s still one spell. If I made one beam non-lethal, no Ishara would have died, and I couldn’t risk them using Invigoration.","\"They would only have needed a few breaths to regain their strength, whereas the mana stored in my equipment and consumed by Ruin would have been lost.\"","\"I understand.\" Faluel replied. \"It’s just that I’m still new to Blade Spells, and I hoped they might be more versatile.\"","\"They are as versatile as any other spell, but once you decide their purpose, there’s only so much you can change.\" Lith shrugged. \"Once you cast a fireball, can you make it so that only one specific quarter of it produces a non-lethal explosion?\"","\"No.\" Faluel shook her head. \"A mana imbalance would make the spell collapse, while an imbalance in the willpower stored in the fireball would make its effects unreliable.\"","The Warp Gates opened again, revealing that no Ishara had survived the Tiamat’s wrath.","\"Same thing with Blade Spells.\" Lith replied. \"Now, time to get our loot.\"","Lith and Faluel collected every piece of the Ishara’s equipment left, which wasn’t as much as they hoped. In the heat of battle, even Solus had failed to notice that many armor and weapons had Warped away upon losing their imprint.","Yet not all artifacts had behaved the same way. Only the most powerful equipment, or what was considered part of an Ishara bloodline legacy, had been imbued with such a powerful enchantment.","Everything else, however, was still where its owner had fallen.","\"Please, tell me there’s enough to repay my debt with my share.\" Tista said while checking the contents of the Isharas’ dimensional rings. \"Even better, tell me there is enough Adamant to repay my debt and put some of it aside.\"","\"There is enough to repay your debt.\" Lith snarled. \"Now I have enough to make a Double Edge for Solus’ Sage Staff and proper Adamant weapons for everyone.\"","Lith hated splitting the collected resources with Tista and Faluel, but he was also aware that, in their shoes, being sent away with a handshake after putting their lives on the line for him would have soured their relationship.","’Moreover, Tista is my sister. I want her to have a stash of enchanted metal for herself, or when she decides to have children, she will be strapped for resources. Any person who knows about her situation might exploit it to manipulate her and drag her into their own mess.’","’Finally!’ Solus said. ’I’m proud of you, Scrooge MacStingy. For once you are thinking with your heart instead of your wallet. Yet the best part is that now we have everything we need to craft a full suit of equipment for me!’","’Thanks.’ Lith sighed. ’I can believe I got my hands on so much Adamant just to lose most of it in a heartbeat.’","’It’s not an expense. It’s an investment in my safety.’ Solus replied. ’We’ll need to Forgemaster my armor carefully. It must have enchantments and properties that justify the presence of the mana crystals that are actually a part of my body.’","’I hate to interrupt you, but we are drained.’ Ripha and the other Sigil Demons returned to their respective feathers . ’Also, don’t forget that the Isharas and whoever witnessed the fight saw us use our Blade Spells.’","’I haven’t forgotten.’ Lith replied. ’I’m aware we’ve lost the element of surprise on that, but it was worth it. Without your help, I could never have defeated so many powerful Divine Beasts.’","\"Hey, Lith, now that it’s over, can you explain to me what you did earlier?\" Faluel unwittingly chimed in, interrupting the telepathic conversation.","\"You need to be more specific.\" Lith said.","\"I’m talking about when your scales turned emerald green, and you beat the crap out of the Isharas even though they were infused with Life Maelstrom.\" The Hydra replied.","\"Oh, that.\" He nodded. \"I have no idea. If I had to guess, however, I’d say it’s the power of my Indech’s Spirit eye. It fuses and harmonizes the elements into Spirit Magic, allowing me to use all my Indech bloodline abilities at once instead of one at a time.\"","\"What?\" Tista and Faluel said in unison, but while the Hydra was shocked, the Hekate was ecstatic.","\"Do they simply work together, or do they synergize? I’m asking for a friend.\" Tista said.","\"They synergize.\" Lith replied. \"All the other Indech bloodline abilities get amplified by Vital Storm. Without that boost in power, I would have never managed to switch only a fraction of my body with Umbral Shift or to endure so many blows with Lightforged and Arcane Bulwark.\"","\"That’s how you survived the explosion of so many Spirit spells!\" Faluel’s eyes went wide. \"Bulwark coated you in a mystical barrier, Lightforged increased your mass, and Vital Storm amplified them both.","\"In that moment, you surpassed the abilities of a Divine Beast and turned the tables.\"","\"I’d appreciate it if you kept it to yourself, Faluel.\" Lith performed a final sweep of the battlefield with the Eyes and Ears of Menadion, checking that he hadn’t missed anything.","\"Don’t worry about that. You know I can keep a secret.\" The Hydra replied. \"And speaking of secrets, do you know that this little fellow talks?\"","She raised Gungnir with pride, but the glaive remained silent.","\"Oh, come on! You were all chatty before, and a piece of work at that. He has gotten your attitude, Lith.\" Faluel shook the weapon and circulated her mana inside of it, yet nothing happened.","\"He?\" Tista asked.","\"It didn’t sound feminine, so yes, it’s a boy.\" Faluel shrugged. \"What a prick! Trying to embarrass me in front of my friends. Here, let me show you.\"","A quick mind link showed everyone how Gungnir had moved on its own and even manipulated the Hydra’s incomplete Blade Spell to kill two Isharas.","\"I call that Blade Spell Soaring Dragon!\" She said with pride.","\"It has multiple heads, though. Like a Hydra.\" Lith pointed out."]},{"number":4465,"title":"Chapter 4465 Reward and Punishment (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Or like Ufyl.\" Tista said. \"Wouldn’t Soaring Dragufyl be better?\"","Lith and Faluel turned to stare at her, and Tista could even feel the silent gaze of Solus and the other Sigil Demons on her.","\"I apologize, Lith. I always thought you had a terrible naming sense, but your sister takes the cake.\" Faluel patted his shoulder.","\"Apology accepted.\" Lith sighed. \"Seriously, Tista. The next time... just don’t. I’m saying this for your own good.\"","\"Why? What’s wrong with Soaring Dragufyl?\" Despite the crimson-red scales that covered her face, the Hekate managed to turn an even deeper shade of purple.","’The \"soaring\" part is okay.’ Solus replied. ’It’s the \"Dragufyl\" that’s messed up. It sounds like a disease.’","’You guys have no taste.’ Tista pouted. ’And you’re mean!’","’This can wait.’ Lith replied. ’Please, be quiet now.’","He activated his communication amulet again, and the hologram of the Royals filled the space before him.","\"The issue with Ghishal has been temporarily resolved and the criminals punished according to the law, Your Majesty.\" Lith said. \"The Isharas refused to surrender, and we had to kill them.\"","\"That many?\" Sylpha was impressed. \"Just the three of you?\"","\"We also had the help of my Sigil Demons.\" Lith said. \"We wouldn’t have done it without their help. I believe they deserve a proper reward.\"","Valia, Varegrave, and Locrias were still active-duty members of the Royal Army and were paid for it. They also received bonuses for acts of extreme valor like their still-living colleagues.","The Sigil Demons no longer needed money, but their families did. Everything the Demons earned while serving under Lith went into a trust fund. It gave the fallen members of the Queen’s Corps the certainty that their loved ones would lack nothing even after the black chains came undone.","Lith knew it was only a matter of time before his Sigil Demons deemed they had fulfilled their duty and moved on. He wanted Locrias and the others to prolong their existence because they wanted to.","Not out of worry for those they left behind.","\"And the Crown agrees.\" Sylpha nodded. \"Our loyal subjects will be properly compensated. We’ll assign them a fair share of the acquired goods.\"","\"What goods?\" Lith asked in confusion. \"The Isharas didn’t have their share of the robberies on them, and everything stockpiled by the bandits and the corrupted nobles already belongs to the Kingdom.","\"Without the money the Isharas took, there isn’t even enough to compensate all the families of the bereaved and cover for the losses the Distar Marquisate has incurred.\"","\"Ah.\" A light of understanding sparked in the King’s eyes, and his expression softened. \"I forgot you are not familiar with many laws of the Kingdom. I suggest you sit down, Magus Verhen. You’re not going to like what I’m about to say.\"","There was a mix of compassion and sadness in Meron’s voice. The same Lith had used countless times as Nana’s apprentice to deliver bad news to the families of the patients he had failed to save.","\"Please, tell me everything.\" He said after conjuring a stone chair for himself.","\"First, allow the Crown to praise you for your latest achievement.\" Sylpha said. \"You have noticed a problem that everyone else ignored or dismissed, uncovering a much larger scheme that threatened the stability of our Kingdom.","\"You have assembled your own team, prepared contingency measures, and everything you needed to conduct an undercover mission without any burden for the already depleted vaults of the Distar Region. For that, you have our gratitude.\"","\"And mine as well.\" The hologram of Brinja Distar appeared.","It was smaller than the Royals’ and stood to their side exactly like Brinja would have done during a session of the Royal Court.","\"Without you, I would have lost all my loyal retainers and had them replaced by filthy traitors. I would have become blind and deaf to the affairs of my own region. A Marchioness in name only, and the Isharas would have become the true rulers of Distar.","\"Also, by making me aware of the issue and giving me the opportunity to contribute, you have saved my reputation in the Royal Court. Instead of passing for a foolish ruler who needed to be rescued, your reports show I’ve done everything within my purview to support you.\"","\"Marchioness Distar is right.\" Meron nodded. \"She has earned merits from this crisis, and her competence in ruling Distar cannot be called into question even by her more nitpicky and fierce rivals.","\"At the same time, however, your investigation has uncovered a large-scale operation conducted by a foreign force that wouldn’t have been possible without an appalling combination of stupidity, greed, and incompetence of the local counts.","\"For this reason, once the Royal Constables are done separating the Isharas’ noble accomplices from the innocent fools, the latter are going to be punished as well. Even Countess Keyla Lark won’t be an exception.\"","\"What? Why?\" Lith stood up in outrage. \"Keyla also contributed to the investigation to the best of her abilities, just like Brinja. She gave me every bit of information I needed and forged the fake identity I used to expose the Isharas.\"","\"Indeed.\" Sylpha nodded, raising her hands with her palms out to placate him. \"Yet while Marchioness Distar is blameless in all this, Countess Lark was doing what we consider the bare minimum to fix a problem of her own making.","\"If she and all the other innocent local rulers of Distars put their pride aside and made Marchioness Distar aware of their circumstances, countless lives would have been saved, and the influence of the Isharas wouldn’t have spread so far and wide.","\"Countess Lark and all the other counts but Jadon Lark are the Isharas’ unwitting accomplices. They played in the enemies of the Kingdom’s hands and orchestrated their own downfall without even noticing.","\"Such irresponsible conduct can’t go unpunished. Pride can’t come before duty. Rivalries can’t outweigh the lives of our citizens. Every person who died because the local rulers refused to inform Marchioness Distar of the situation is an unacceptable loss.","\"From absolute power comes absolute responsibility, Magus Verhen. The local nobles of Distar have made their decisions and will be held accountable for them.\"","Lith felt bad for Keyla, but he couldn’t argue with the Royals’ reasoning.","’They are right. Doing anything less would breed corruption and complacency.’ Solus said. ’If there is no consequence for being careless or incompetent, nobles have no incentive to put their citizens first.’","\"For this reason, the gold you’ve retrieved will be only used to compensate the bereaved families and the merchants for their losses. Whatever is left will be entrusted to Marchioness Distar to use it as she sees fit.","\"The local nobles have made their bed, and now they can lie in it. They won’t see a single coin of what they have lost due to their own foolishness, and it will be up to them to rebuild the wealth they have squandered.\"","Lith raised his hand, and Meron permitted him to speak.","\"Not to be... well, myself, Your Majesty, but the Ishara called Ankhuta mentioned the Hydras’ bloodline awakening project and a secret lab for their species.\" He said.","\"We are aware of that.\" Sylpha nodded. \"We listened to your conversation with him.\""]},{"number":4466,"title":"Chapter 4466 Reward and Punishment (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Yeah, but... there is no way the money the Isharas extracted from the Distar Region is enough to cover the expenses for such a big lab and for an indefinite time. The project could take months for the Hydras to complete, and then the Ishara will need even longer to adapt it to their needs.\"","At those words, the King and Queen became pale as ghosts, and Brinja inwardly thanked the gods for being a mere marchioness.","\"Winter comes for the entire Kingdom, and communications are cut off during the cold season in the vast majority of regions. I think it’s unlikely the Isharas came up with such a brilliant tactic just to infiltrate Distar.\"","\"It would indeed be both foolish and dangerous.\" Sylpha swallowed hard. \"They knew you live there and tried to steer clear of you.\"","\"I wouldn’t exclude that they infiltrated Distar last, after tightening their grip on the rest of the Kingdom.\" Meron tormented his finely trimmed beard like a man who had just woken up from a nightmare and discovered that reality was much worse.","\"We need to start parallel investigations in all the other regions, especially in the north!\" The King slammed his fist against the armrest of his throne. \"If the Isharas are the political plague they appear to be, we have only so much time to uproot their power base before it’s too late.\"","\"Don’t worry, Your Majesty.\" Jirni’s hologram appeared on the opposite side of Brinja’s. \"I’m already familiar with the Isharas’ methods and tactics. I had the opportunity to thoroughly examine the reports from Distar, and I know what to look for.","\"For this reason, I’m volunteering as the lead Archon in the investigation and hereby request to be allowed to return to active duty. I have one condition, though.\"","\"Name it, Archon Ernas.\" Sylpha said, using Jirni’s title to inform her that her offer had been accepted and her request granted.","\"My youngest refuses to eat in my absence, and she’s already suffered while I was away for work.\" Jirni held her head straight. \"I need to spend my lunch breaks at home to ensure my daughter is properly fed and grows healthy.\"","\"That’s it?\" Meron dismissed the issue with evident relief. \"The Crown never expected you to travel across the Kingdom like a Warp Beast and conduct the investigation on your own, Archon Ernas.","\"Your role will be to supervise the work of the other Constables and examine the reports of your fellow Archons to ensure they don’t miss anything. You will spend most of your time behind a desk, and perform field work only when the other Archons fail.\"","’Be still my heart.’ Jirni inwardly rolled her eyes. She hated being swamped with paperwork and reduced to a bureaucrat the most.","\"We are glad to have you back, Archon Ernas.\" The Queen said. \"The Crown will provide all the manpower and resources you might need. The Isharas started their coup months ago, whereas we kept losing battles we didn’t even know were being fought.","\"We need to make up for the lost time and act swiftly. Most trails are already cold after so long, and after suffering today’s defeat, the Isharas will rush to cover their tracks.","\"We can’t afford to give them the time to double-check their operations of the past few months and clean up any mistakes they might have made. They are going to be much more subtle from now on and careful not to leave anything that might trace back to them.","\"When are you available to report for duty and lead the investigation, Archon Ernas?\"","\"Right now, if necessary.\" Jirni replied.","\"It is.\" King Meron nodded. \"What about Lord Ernas? Will he join you?\"","\"I will, Your Majesty.\" Orion rapped over his breastplate. \"I’m also ready to resume my duties as General of the Army, Lord Commander of the Knight Guard, and field officer of the Knight Guard.\"","\"Excellent.\" Sylpha said. \"This will ease the burden on Lord Gunyin Ernas and put an end to the endless squabble about your prolonged leave of absence. Especially if the Ernas Region turns out to have been covertly overtaken by the Isharas as well.\"","\"I’m sorry, Your Majesties, but what about Countess Lark?\" Lith chimed in. \"I believe she deserves some grace. If not for her, I would have never started the investigation, and we would all still be unaware of the Isharas’ scheme.\"","\"If it’s your request, then we can extend some leniency to her, but punishment is unavoidable.\" The King replied. \"With all due respect, Supreme Magus, being your friend is not a mitigating circumstance.","\"Any noble you’ve befriended in the past would have done the same as Countess Lark, so there is no merit in that. Do you agree, Countess?\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\" Keyla’s hologram appeared further away and even smaller than Brinja’s, making her seem weak and pitiful. \"To be honest, I deserve a harsher punishment than my peers. I could have asked Magus Verhen’s help long ago, yet I didn’t.","\"The other counts and countesses of Distar can at least say to their defence that they had no one trusted to call. If Magus Verhen hadn’t come to me and offered his help, I would never have told him about Ghishal’s struggle.","\"If there’s someone who deserves a reward, it’s the man who informed Captain Locrias.\"","\"We agree on that, but leniency will be extended to you anyway.\" The King swept the air with his hand to signal it wasn’t up for debate. \"Magus Verhen asked for it, and the Crown will deliver.","\"Moreover, we are glad you recognise your faults. It means you’ve learned from them. Now, back to you and your Sigil Demons, Magus Verhen. I want you to know the Crown will reward them with a part of our share of the spoils of war.","\"Nothing they will receive will come out of your share.\"","\"What do you mean, my share?\" Lith swallowed hard, feeling a sudden pang in his wallet.","\"Supreme Magus Lith Tiamat Verhen!\" The Queen jumped from her throne.","Her furious gaze as she used Lith’s full name and title reminded him of Elina when she was about to give him the earful of a lifetime.","\"You are one of the highest authorities of the Kingdom who has requested the Crown’s approval to conduct an official investigation aimed at uncovering a potential threat to the Distar region, are you not?\" She asked, and he nodded for her to continue.","\"Then, according to the Kingdom’s law, half of everything collected during the mission belongs to you and the other half to the Crown.","\"You can’t expect the Kingdom to pay the bills of your hotels and restaurants, your many annuities, the security detail of your friends and family, and then expect us also to let you pocket anything valuable you find while working for us.","\"You’ve already gotten yourself in trouble when you ’liberated’ the corpse of the Black Dragon Syrook. I expect you to deliver to us every speck of Adamant and Divine Beast corpse the Kingdom is due. Did I make myself clear?\"","\"Yes, Mom. I mean, Your Majesty.\" Lith sighed.","\"Good.\" Meron nodded. \"Magus Verhen, deliver all the evidence and the Kingdom’s share of the spoils of battle to Lutia’s branch of the Mage Association.\""]},{"number":4467,"title":"Chapter 4467 Deep Roots (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"We need the evidence you collected to start the investigation and our share of the Isharas’ spoils to keep the Royal Court from accusing you of repeating the mistakes of the past. Once you’re done with that, consider yourself dismissed. Meron out.\"","\"Wait, what about me?\" Faluel asked to empty air. \"What about my share?\"","\"What about mine?\" Tista whined.","\"I called you here, Faluel. The Royals just seconded my request. They didn’t order or ask you to do anything. As for you, Tista, you’re House Verhen as well. You can bet your shares will come out of mine.\" Lith groaned.","\"Which means that we got half of what we expected. Tista, you’re not out of debt. Faluel, screw you from the bottom of my heart. You’re filthy rich, but I’ll give you a third of the loot nonetheless.\"","\"Spoken like a true leader.\" Faluel chuckled. \"If you need me, you know where to find me.\"","A sudden cough drew everyone’s attention to the holograms that were still there. Only the Royals had hung up the call.","\"I wanted to thank you for your hard work before saying goodbye, everyone.\" Brinja needed sheer willpower to stifle a laugh. \"I guess it can wait. Feel free to keep cursing the Royals once I’m gone. Brinja out.\"","\"Same. Keyla out.\"","\"I’ll wait for you at home. Jirni out.\"","***","\"What about you, Kamila?\" Jirni asked, cutting off the creative streak of expletives Lith was using to refer to the current Royal family. \"Are you going to go back to work as well?\"","\"Part time, maybe.\" She scratched her head in embarrassment. \"I can help you as much as you need while at home, but I can’t make any promise about the field work. Ral is just a few months old, and he’s going to have only so many first times.","\"If I miss his first step, his first word that’s not mom or dad, or his first flight, I’d never forgive myself.\"","\"That’s fair.\" Jirni smiled. \"Yet I could have used your help. Especially with the Gernoffs.\"","\"We’ll see about that.\" Kamila replied. \"I like you, Jirni, but feelings won’t bring me back home in one piece at the end of the day.\"","\"Your feelings for me, no. Yet those of Lith for you sure can.\" Jirni said with a casual tone. \"After all...\"","\"No!\" Kamila replied. \"Not again! At least not so soon, dammit. I have yet to get a single full night’s sleep!\"","***","Even though the coup in Ghishal had been averted, life for Jirni, Kamila, and Lith remained hectic. Many counties of the Distar Region were in the same situation as Ghishal if not worse, and Lith had lost the advantage of surprise.","The investigation teams moved swiftly and discreetly, and the Royals replaced every influential clerk in the county with someone of proven loyalty until the constables cleared the local personnel of any suspicions, but it didn’t help much.","The nobles helped by the Isharas had destroyed any incriminating evidence right after learning of Ankhuta’s death, and the Blood of Selkis had helped the bandits move to a safe location in exchange for their \"insurance\" material.","Jirni found many clues and weird coincidences in every county that pointed to a specific noble who would benefit from the fall of the current count, and a specific bandit group that seemed to always be at the right time and place, but no evidence.","’I can’t interrogate a noble with no substantial proof of my suspicions, let alone so many loyal retainers of the Crown.’ Jirni pondered in frustration. ’I can torture their bandit associates since they are murderous scum, but only if they get caught in the act, and Lith can’t find a single one of them.","’If even he, with all his secrets and his absurd powers, can’t find those criminals, regular investigators have no chance of success. Still, I’ll have them keep looking. Maybe numbers and luck can beat the odds.’","While Kamila and Jirni worked from home, Lith and Solus moved across Ghishal, using the tower and dimensional magic to deliver everything Keyla’s citizens needed to the poorest and most isolated villages.","The farmers and small merchants reacted to his arrival with fear, thinking only the presence of a deadly monster could bring the Supreme Magus of the Kingdom to such remote places.","Once he distributed the food and the supplies the villagers had missed for so long and healed their ailments for free, however, their attitude changed. The people of Ghishal treated Lith like a god descended among mortals, throwing themselves at his feet and pledging their eternal gratitude to him.","\"Thanks. Much obliged. Sorry, I have a lot more villages I have to visit before the end of the day.\" Lith said as soon as he was done, and then Warped away.","Things only got worse once he left and the local village head had time to read Keyla’s message attached to the additional emergency supplies that they were entrusted with.","\"Gods, we truly have been blessed.\" Each village head used different words, but their spirit was the same. \"Magus Verhen did more than personally deliver the goods to ensure our survival. He paid for them out of his own pockets!\"","He pointed at the specific line in the message for all his fellow villagers to read.","\"Every morsel of food and iron nail we’ve received is a gift of the Supreme Magus.\" The second part of the speech came out much colder than the first. \"If any of you bastards so much as steal a piece of bread from their neighbors, it would be like stealing from Magus Verhen himself and spitting on his face!","\"Anyone caught in the act or with more supplies than they are supposed to have will be chained at the pillory during the next snowstorm. Is that clear?\"","The village head always glared at the troublemakers and those of ill repute, to let them know their words were no empty threat.","’That was very generous of you.’ Solus smiled at Lith as they Warped to their next destination. ’Basic necessities don’t cost much, but for someone as stingy as you are, even this is a huge leap forward.’","’I’m sorry, Solus, but I’m not generous.’ Lith replied. ’I feel bad for Keyla for not receiving any reward for the mission. Her treasury is already almost depleted, and I don’t want her to spend what little she has left.","’Besides, this isn’t really my money. I’m just spending my share of the non-magical treasures we’ve recovered. I have no use for a few gold bars and coins, whereas they can make a big difference for these people.’","’Still, the old you wouldn’t have even considered doing something like this.’ Solus gave him a warm smile. ’Especially since after helping Keyla, you have to help all the other counts.’","’Excuse you?’ Lith stopped in his tracks. ’Why should I do that? I don’t know nor give a damn about those pompous fools.’","’You won’t do it for them, but for their people.’ Solus replied. ’If you don’t, the rest of the citizens of Distar will believe that you only care about Lustria and Ghishal. They will feel rightfully hurt and offended, and become envious of the people of those two counties.’"]},{"number":4468,"title":"Chapter 4468 Deep Roots (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Fuck me sideways!’ Lith’s eyes widened in realization. ’Business and all forms of travel inside the region would suffer. My gift will make a few people happy in the short term but sow discord that can only get worse with time.’","’Yep.’ Solus chuckled. ’See? The old you would have never taken his paranoia hat off, even to help a friend.’","’What about the other regions?’ Lith’s wallet found itself covered in his cold sweat. ’Do I have to help them as well?’","’It would be nice of you, but no.’ Solus shook her head telepathically. ’Everybody knows and expects you to treat Distar differently because it’s your birthplace. You are also a personal friend of the Larks and Brinja.","’Envy and resentment have been there since you became an Archmage. This will just add a drop in the sea of what’s already there.’","’Thanks, Solus. I needed a piece of good news.’ He sighed in relief.","’Don’t twist my words like that!’ She pouted. ’I’m just telling you that you can avoid helping the people of the other regions, not that you should! You’re an insensitive jerk and...’","She was still nagging at him when he Warped away. Solus too had to take part in the deliveries to stabilize Ghishal quickly, so she swallowed the rest of her speech and Warped to her next village.","She wasn’t as famous as Lith, but the welcoming she received wasn’t much different. Solus always said a few good words as she treated the villagers and cleared their houses of the accumulated snow before leaving.","Yet the gratitude and the praise she received from the people of Ghishal were the only good things she heard.","\"I’ve bad news, and I’ve horrible news.\" Jirni held a conference call with the Royals, Lith, and all the Regional Lords of the Kingdom. \"The bad news is that after revising the reports of my fellow Archons and Constables, I’m certain that Distar isn’t the only region where foreign forces plotted to overthrow the county nobles.","\"The same happened in all regions of the Kingdom except for Valeron. I can only assume the Isharas preferred to stay away from the capital of the Kingdom and the Royals because of the massive forces stationed there.\"","\"All of them? Even the Ernas region?\" Gunyin Ernas asked after raising his hand and receiving permission to speak.","\"Yes, even yours, Archduke Ernas.\" Jirni spoke to her son like she would to a stranger, something that even the most seasoned politicians found unsettling at best. \"If it’s of any consolation, you’re in good company.","\"Not even the proud Essagor avoided this plague, nor did the six great academies themselves. We are all in the same boat, and there is no time for recriminations.\"","Vastor, Marth, and many other influential figures of the Kingdom took those words as a personal failure. Their lands were an extension of their being, and the idea that someone had infiltrated their territories made them feel violated.","\"Yet that’s not all. The horrible news is that we are well past the point of no return.\" Jirni delivered the next blow without caring that the nobles were still recoiling from the previous. \"The Isharas had the entire winter to set up shop and start cleaning their traces.","\"After being exposed by Magus Verhen, they’ll lay low and focus on tying up any loose ends left. We only have so long before the luck of a constable matters more than their effort and competence in uncovering a lead.","\"Based on what we got so far, I have little hope to replicate the success of Ghishal anywhere else. I recommend the Royals not to demote or promote anyone, but that’s just palliative care.","\"This cancer has already spread across the Kingdom and taken root. We can’t be sure of anyone’s loyalty, and many nerve centers of power might work against us without us ever knowing.\"","\"What are your recommendations, Archon Ernas?\" Queen Sylpha asked, her eyes flaring with mana and fury.","\"To continue the investigation and examine every document to build dossiers about our suspects. Once we’re done with that, I suggest keeping an eye on them to limit their movements.","\"We can’t arrest or detain them, but letting the corrupt nobles profit from their crimes would be a slap in the face of their victims.\" Jirni sighed. \"We can only hope that with time and pressure they will make a mistake that allows us to expose their crimes.\"","\"This is preposterous!\" Duke Tanash trembled in fury. \"Why don’t we just order the Council to clean its own mess? All of this happened because the Isharas received the Council’s permission to do whatever they wanted!\"","\"Careful with your words, Tanash.\" A glare from the King silenced the duke. \"How do you plan to order a bunch of old monsters to do anything without violating the treaty between the Council and the Kingdom?\"","\"They broke it first.\" Tanash stuttered. \"They should pay the price.\"","\"The Council didn’t authorize the Isharas to commit crimes, you fool.\" Meron snorted. \"It just authorized them to make money in Garlen. It would be like blaming a local lord because a peddler turns out to be a robber.","\"If the Council follows your logic, then it could blame the Crown for everything that’s wrong with their lives. After all, we gave the corrupt nobles their titles and lands. We failed to keep them in check just like the Council did with the Isharas. Did we not?\"","The duke was about to say that it wasn’t the same thing, but it sounded foolish even to him. That and the King’s scowl sealed his mouth.","\"Rest assured that we’ll inform the Council of what happened and will demand they take the appropriate measures.\" Queen Sylpha said. \"Yet there is only so much the Council can do.","\"No one expected an entire Divine Beast bloodline to move to Garlen. Everyone underestimated the ambition and goals of the Isharas and paid the price for it. We need to tread carefully, or we’ll have another war in our hands.","\"After Thrud and with the Dead King sniffing at our doorstep, the Griffon Kingdom ill-needs one more force threatening our national security. Anything else, Archon Ernas?\"","\"Only one minor request, Your Majesty.\" Jirni replied. \"I’d like to start my assignment by cleaning my own home. I’ll continue helping and supporting the other Archons, but I want to focus on purging the Isharas’ influence from the Ernas Region and protecting my loyal subjects.\"","\"Granted.\" King Meron nodded. \"The Crown will pursue every lead, but I order all the Regional Lords to establish their own special forces and investigate locally. The Crown lacks the manpower to sift through every small village and city, but you don’t.","\"Use the riches you’ve accrued so far, or you might not make more in the near future. King Meron and Queen Sylpha out.\"","A similar, but much less polite and cordial conversation between the Royals and the Council Representatives took place a few minutes later.","\"This is unacceptable!\" Sylpha snarled, slamming her delicate fist on the armrest of her throne while glaring at Raagu. \"How could you have been so blind and foolish? Don’t you Awakened know how to protect your own interests?"]},{"number":4469,"title":"Chapter 4469 Cursed Crown (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Do you not realize that whoever your descendants are, whatever merchant group you established to earn money, will face the threat of the Isharas? It’s only a matter of time before our problem becomes your problem as well.\" The Queen asked.","\"We are neither blind nor foolish, Sylpha.\" Raagu said, but her voice lacked conviction. \"We have been... naïve. We never asked how many Isharas were going to cross Garlen borders nor questioned the scope of their activities.\"","\"Naïve at your age?\" The Queen scoffed. \"I think the word you’re looking for is senile.\"","\"Sylpha!\" Raagu and the King said in unison, but while the former was outraged, the latter was embarrassed.","’Have you forgotten what you said to the Royal Court a few minutes ago? We need to tread with caution while dealing with the Awakened Council!’ Meron said via a mind link hidden by their touching elbows.","’I don’t expect the old hag to solve our problems with a snap of her fingers, but she could at least apologize instead of spouting bullshit.’ Sylpha snorted.","’Calm down, dear, or we’ll add the Council to our already extensive list of political enemies.’ Meron shared her frustration, but not the way his fiery wife chose to express it.","\"I apologize on behalf of the Queen.\" Meron said, drawing the glare of both Sylpha and Raagu on himself. \"Her words were unacceptable, but her rightful anger can’t be denied. The Council did a poor job, and the Kingdom is paying the price.\"","He made them both unhappy, undeniable proof that he was a good diplomat.","\"What are you planning to do about this, and what kind of help can we expect from you?\" The King threw the ball in the Council’s court, putting slight but firm pressure on the representatives.","’He’s implying that if we turn our back on the Kingdom and wash our hands of the problem, he’ll do the same when our businesses are affected.’ Inxialot, the Lich King, thought. ’Wait a second. Where am I? Who are these people?’","He looked at the right palm of his hand, where the words \"Council duty\" were written in bright letters.","’Oh, right. Who just finished talking, and who am I supposed to side with?’","He looked at Raagu for clues, but what was left of his face gave the impression he was glaring at her in approval of the King’s words.","\"I...\" The human representative returned the stare for a second, finding it hard to believe that Inxialot could care so much about something happening outside his research lab. \"I mean, the Council will conduct a thorough investigation.","\"The Isharas have violated none of the Council laws, but that doesn’t mean we can’t look into what they are doing and share what we discover with the Crown. If our investigations expose evidence of their criminal activity, the Isharas can’t blame us.","\"Moreover, we’ll try to locate their bases and estimate their numbers to ensure that the Blood of Selkis won’t undermine the authority of the Council as they are doing with the Royals.\"","\"That’s acceptable. For now. Meron out.\" Meron hung up the call before Sylpha could give another Council representative a piece of her mind. \"Happy now?\"","\"Sort of.\" She grunted. \"I still think you’ve let them off too easily.\"","\"I didn’t.\" The King shook his head. \"I just gave them the time to process the information and realize the magnitude of their blunder. Awakened are powerful and prideful creatures.","\"Scolding them like children will only anger the Council Representatives and make them refuse to cooperate. Now instead, I’m playing on their pride. I’ve pointed out their mistake to them and challenged, not ordered, them to fix it.","\"This way, they’ll spare no effort because they’re doing it for themselves, whereas if they felt like I was strong-arming them, they would have done nothing about the Isharas just to spite us.\"","\"I know, dear, but the thought that those bastards of the Isharas have managed to infiltrate our Kingdom so soon after we finally got rid of Thrud infuriates me.","\"The fact that those idiots of the Council even gave the Isharas their blessing, instead, makes my blood boil!\" Sylpha snarled, yet her grimace of fury swiftly turned into confusion.","\"Now that I think about it, the Isharas are not native of Garlen. They come from the Rathi continent, and their dead foremother’s turf is nowhere near the Kingdom. Shouldn’t Lady Tyris’s rules about external interference apply to them?","\"Why didn’t she stop them and smite them into oblivion?\"","\"Because they have followed my every rule and not overstepped any boundary.\" The First Queen walked through a dimensional fissure so thin that she seemed to materialize out of thin air. \"I understand your anger, Sylpha, but rest assured.","\"The Blood of Selkis has no intention of making the Griffon Kingdom their new dominion. The Isharas didn’t seek control over influential figures to gain political power in the Royal Court either.","\"They picked solely the most insignificant nobles that could still contribute to their schemes. The Isharas are only after wealth, and will leave our country as soon as they get their hands on the Hydras’ bloodline awakening project.","\"If they use Forbidden Magic or try to seize control of the Kingdom, however, I will stop them immediately. You are not responsible for the coming of the Blood of Selkis, and I don’t expect you to deal with them alone were they to siege the Kingdom.\"","\"Thank you, My Queen.\" Sylpha stared at Tyris’ sky-blue day dress in a daze.","It left only her neck and hands exposed, and lacked any frill or exotic decoration. The only noteworthy thing about Tyris’ attire was the woman who wore it. The simple but elegant fabric of the dress couldn’t hide the voluptuous curves of her body more than a passing cloud could eclipse the splendor of the sun.","Yet that wasn’t the reason for Sylpha’s stunned silence either.","’That’s a bright color!’ The Queen thought, telepathically shaking her husband like a bear would a tree laden with ripe fruit. ’I’ve never seen Lady Tyris wear a bright-colored dress before. It even has a few golden embroideries!’","’Good gods!’ Meron gasped as the realization dawned upon him. ’Her mourning period is over. Lady Tyris might look for another husband at any moment. Why? Gods, why did it have to happen under my reign?’","’What’s wrong with you?’ Sylpha was glad her husband wasn’t affected by the Guardian’s stunning beauty or her radiant smile, yet she hadn’t expected such a negative reaction either. ’How is this bad news?’","’ Lady Tyris might look for another husband.’ Meron repeated once more with feeling. ’Which means we’ll have to deal with a swarm of powerful individuals who will ravage our land to get her attention at best, or witness the birth of a new royal bloodline at worst!’","’You are right!’ Sylpha went pale in horror. ’Why? Gods, why? Didn’t we endure enough? Couldn’t this wait until the next ruler took the throne? Is this crown cursed?’","\"Please, stop freaking out like that.\" Tyris’s peal of silvery laughter sounded like the first rain after a year-long drought. It could end a war or start many, depending on the circumstances. \"I assure you I’m not going to trouble you in any way.\""]},{"number":4470,"title":"Chapter 4470 Cursed Crown (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"My grieving is still fresh, and I don’t plan to enter another relationship any time soon. I just want to stop hiding from the world and start living a bit.\" The First Queen said.","\"Forgive our insolence, Your Majesty.\" Sylpha dropped to her knee in shame, realizing how shocked her expression must have been for Tyris to read her mind like an open book. \"Also, with all due respect, fresh?","\"You’ve mourned our beloved Valeron Griffon for over seven hundred years. No one would blame you even if you remarried tomorrow.\"","’Whose side are you on, woman?’ Meron inwardly groaned.","\"Thank you, Sylpha.\" Tyris’ cheeks flushed in such a lovely manner that the King could already count four wars on the horizon. \"Can we go back to the Ishara issue, please?\"","\"No!\" Sylpha replied, hungry for gossip about the Guardian’s personal life after decades of nothing. \"I mean, yes. Is there something else we should know about them?\"","\"Only one thing.\" Tyris nodded, making her long hair sparkle like a golden waterfall under the mystical lights of the Throne Room. \"The Blood of Selkis is desperate, Sylpha. They believe that their foremother’s death cast a curse on their species.","\"The Isharas have convinced themselves that Mogar is slowly turning its back on them and soon will slam the door in their faces. They are wrong. Mogar leaves little room for doubt in such matters.","\"Yet this doesn’t make the Isharas any less dangerous. Never underestimate a cornered beast, Meron, even when that corner is only a figment of its mind.\"","***","Verhen Mansion, at the same time.","\"What do you mean, the Isharas have infiltrated all regions?\" Lith asked in disbelief.","He and Solus had just finished delivering basic supplies across the Distar region and had returned home for lunch when Jirni shared her latest report with the Verhens as well.","\"Exactly what I just said.\" Jirni furrowed her brows at his unusual reaction. \"Why so surprised? Can you identify a pattern I missed?\"","’Lith has never cared about politics as long as no one bothers him. On top of that, the Isharas attacked only the nobles at the bottom of the power ladder. Even if you put them all together, they can’t even harm his little finger. Then why is he reacting like that?’","\"No, but all regions means all regions.\" Lith said, and when he noticed that everyone looked at him like he had gone insane, he added: \"If those bastards stage a coup in the Kellar region, Baron Wyalon might be in danger!\"","The Verhens gasped at the revelation, worried about their friend and moved by Lith’s care for the distant nobleman.","\"My silver mines are in danger!\" Nalrond jumped from his seat, drawing many reproachful glares on him. \"I mean, our mines. I have only a small share, but it’s all I have.\"","\"Exactly!\" Lith said, receiving a volley of frowns. \"The Isharas want money and magical resources, and guess what? Silver is both. I need to contact Eiros as soon as we’re done eating.\"","\"That’s what you are worried about?\" Kamila said in disbelief. \"Your silver mines? Not our friend, his loving family, or our house in Belius?\"","\"Please.\" Lith snorted. \"I would worry about Eiros if the Isharas killed their victims instead of gently pushing them off their throne. I can have him reinstated as Jambel’s baron with a snap of my fingers.","\"As for our house in Belius, you investigated the matter with Jirni, Kami. You should already know the Ishara avoided all important cities. Messing with Belius would be like playing with fire in a coal mine.","\"My silver, instead, can’t be recovered once stolen, and there’s no telling how much those bastards can mine even in a few days if no one bothers them. They are Divine Beasts with Life Maelstrom.","\"It wouldn’t surprise me even if they already stripped my mines bare of every vein I found of precious metal.\"","\"Well, yes, but you’re still an insensitive meanie!\" Kamila couldn’t object his reasoning, but she still didn’t like Lith’s delivery.","\"No! Dya no ba!\" Elysia clung to his father’s head, shielding him from all vile accusations with her small body.","\"Dya.\" Ral couldn’t use such big words yet, but he nodded in approval.","\"Dad’s not a meanie, Mom.\" Valeron the Second said while clenching his family pendant. \"Dad is good.\"","Contradicting a small child was already hard. They were so cute with their round faces and big eyes that most Verhens considered ruining their precious happy smiles a criminal offense.","In Valeron’s case, however, it was much worse. With his thick, luscious hair, shiny silver eyes, and the handsomeness he had inherited from his parents, he looked like a cute little sprite begging for affection.","Kamila could only retreat when faced with the firing squad of adorable stares.","\"You are right. Your dad is not a meanie.\" Kamila said. \"I apologize. Now stop looking at me like that. You’re making me feel like a monster.\"","\"Mama!\" The babies jumped on her next to defend their mother from such a vile accusation. \"Mama goo!\"","\"Thank you, my adorable little imps.\" Kamila sniffled, feeling like she could die of cuteness overload at any moment. \"I apologize again.\"","While the rest of the family awwed at the tender scene, Jirni tapped her foot in annoyance, waiting for the moment to give her daughters a piece of her mind without ruining the moment for everyone.","\"What’s the meaning of this, young ladies?\" She asked after the Verhen babies left the room to chase after Shargein’s tail.","\"The meaning of what- Good gods!\" Friya gasped in surprise seeing Dripha in her mother’s hands and the Water and Air Stores floating around the baby girl.","\"I trusted you two to take good care of your little sister while I was away, not to set up a magical boot camp for Dripha and force her to use these contraptions.\" Jirni’s nostrils flared in annoyance, which was a bigger reaction than she usually showed in a life-or-death situation.","\"Look at her. She’s exhausted. How could you do something like this? This is the Ernas Household, not the...\" Jirni stopped herself before she said something she would regret.","Even in her anger, she noticed that the only emotions on her daughters’ faces were surprise and worry.","’There’s not a hint of the guilt and remorse I should expect to find while confronting them. Quylla and Friya didn’t know anything about this.’ She thought.","\"We didn’t do anything to Dripha, Mom. I swear!\" Quylla said.","\"Nothing? Are you telling me you’ve left her alone until my return?\" Jirni’s eyes narrowed at the confession.","\"No! I mean, sure, we fed, changed, and played with her, but we didn’t teach Dripha magic. We even took the Rune Stores away whenever she was with the other babies, no matter how hard she cried.\"","\"She cried when you took away the Rune Stores?\" Jirni looked at her baby daughter, who giggled and smiled, happy to have her mother with her again.","\"Goo, mama?\" Dripha asked.","\"What?\" Jirni replied.","\"Goo?\" Dripha patted her little hands on her chest. \"Yoo ’tay ’ow?\"","Dripha clenched Jirni’s fingers with her little hands.","\"Yes, baby girl. You’re good. The best.\" Jirni held Dripha close to her chest, inwardly cursing the Gernoffs for the umpteenth time."]},{"number":4471,"title":"Chapter 4471 Broken Clock (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Mommy is back and will stay home with you. Most of the time.\" Even Jirni didn’t have the heart to lie to her daughter like that, knowing that Dripha might remember and her tiny heart would be scarred once Jirni went back on her word.","\"Yay!\" Dripha didn’t understand much of what Jirni said, but she understood enough. \"Mama ’tay. ’tay.\" Finally at peace, Dripha fell asleep, and the Rune Stores fell to the ground.","\"What’s going on, Mom?\" Friya asked in confusion.","\"Dripha thinks that your father and I abandoned her because of these stupid things, and that we’ve returned for the same reason.\" Jirni emitted the softest snarl her daughters had ever heard. \"I’m going to kill someone for this.\"","Lith could only imagine the fury seething below Jirni’s stoic expression, so he decided to give her some privacy and conduct his business elsewhere. He moved to the master bedroom and pressed Baron Wyalon’s rune.","\"Nice to see you again, Lith.\" The Baron smiled. \"I heard you’ve made a killing again. Both literally and metaphorically.\" He laughed at his own joke.","\"It’s nice seeing you too, Eiros.\" Lith replied. \"How are you doing? How is winter in the north treating you?\"","\"Like usual.\" The Baron shrugged. \"Freezing temperatures, long snowstorms, and of course, plenty of stupid criminals and monsters. Same old, same old.\"","\"Didn’t you hear about what happened in Distar?\" Lith asked.","\"I did.\" Wyalon replied. \"It was all over the news, and I even got a vague royal proclamation ordering me to stay on guard against an even vaguer impending crisis. Why?\"","\"Please, keep what I’m about to tell you between us.\" Lith said, and the Baron nodded for him to continue. \"The issue with those Isharas might not be limited to the Distar region.","\"The Kellar region might be in the same situation, if not even worse. Soon an official investigation will start, and the Royals will send you a Constable to help you deal with the problem.\"","\"I see.\" Wyalon nodded. \"You were afraid Jambel might be facing more than its fair share of bandits and that your silver might have been stolen. Am I right?\"","\"Yes, sorry.\" Lith sighed. \"Well? Am I right as well?\"","\"Not even close.\" The Baron replied. \"Nothing weird happened. Our bandits were the usual cream of the crap you can find around these parts, and not a single crate of your silver has been reported stolen.\"","\"Seriously?\" Lith furrowed his brows. \"This is great news. I’m very happy for you. I was about to offer you my help and come there to help with the investigation.\"","\"Your presence is always welcome. You don’t need to wait for a crisis to come visit me, you know?\" Wyalon folded his arms.","\"Yes, and I’m sorry, but life is a bit hectic here. How are Mirias and your kids?\" Lith asked.","\"Mirias still has her fainting problem.\" The Baron referred to the panic attacks that his social blunders gave his wife. \"As for my kids, well, they’re not kids anymore. Kotu is engaged to a nice young lady now.\"","\"A noble?\" Lith asked.","\"No, she’s a teacher.\" Wyalon replied. \"She seems nice. I will tell you more once I complete her background check and have a full picture of her family and friends.\"","\"That’s... thoughtful.\" Lith said. \"Maybe a tad too much?\"","\"Too much?\" The Baron snorted. \"My son is the future Baron of Jambel, and this is his first relationship. What would you do if this was about Ral or Ely?\"","Lith opened his mouth to reply, and his mind went over several scenarios involving his Demons following his children’s alleged suitor wherever they went for months. Maybe even Jirni having a private chat with them.","\"I see your point.\" Lith raised his hands in surrender.","\"Good.\" The Baron nodded. \"You can come to pick up your silver anytime you want. I could use a bit of shadow tailing, and your kids would love the snow.\"","\"I’ll think about it. Have a nice day, Wyalon. Lith out.\" He hung up the call and pressed Zolgrish’s rune next.","’There is no way the Isharas didn’t harass at least him.’ Lith thought. ’He’s no Awakened, and almost half that comes out of my silver mines ends up in his pockets. I can’t stand that idiot, but I need him to run the mining operations.’","The Lich didn’t reply, but even Lith’s paranoia found that normal. Unless Zolgrish needed to talk with Lith, it could take a few hundred calls until he finally picked up his amulet.","\"Who are you and how did you get my rune, sugar lips?\" Zolgrish said when the hologram of the rotten ruin of his face finally appeared.","\"That’s Scourge, Master.\" Ratpack, his undead chimera assistant, groaned. \"He male.\"","\"Really?\" Zolgrish gasped. \"Then why does he have long silver hair and wear makeup?\"","Ratpack sighed in exasperation, using his enchanted feather duster to remove the spiderwebs, insects, and dirt filling his master’s empty eye sockets.","\"This is amazing! It’s like a thick fog has finally lifted from my eyes. Have you studied Healing magic without my knowledge, Ratpack?\"","\"No.\"","\"Zolgrish. I’m still here.\" The conversation had barely started, and Lith could already feel a massive headache coming.","\"Who are you and how did you get my rune, stranger?\" Zolgrish yelped in surprise and turned to face the source of the unknown voice.","\"That’s Scourge, Master.\" Ratpack emitted a high-pitched whine. \"Same call as before.\"","\"I have no idea what you’re talking about, Ratpack.\" The Lich replied. \"What do you want, Starch? I’m busy!\"","Lith briefly explained the problem with the Isharas, certain that Zolgrish had no idea what had happened outside his lab since the last time he had left it to buy more ingredients.","\"Isharas? Bandits?\" He asked in confusion. \"Do we have those, Ratpack?\"","\"No and yes.\" The small undead replied. \"Plenty of bandits every year, Master. Mediocre specimens, but still specimens. Your words.\"","\"No more than usual, Ratpack?\" Lith asked, receiving a no in reply. \"This is nice to hear, but how is this possible? Faluel asking them to stay away from Lustria is one thing, but why would Inxialot do the same?\"","\"Good question, Seth.\" Zolgrish nodded. \"If they steered clear of your lands both in Distar and Kellar, it would mean they have avoided you on purpose. That the Ismaels wanted to escape your detection in preparation for some bigger, nefarious plan.\"","\"My thought exactly.\" The Lich’s brilliant intuition surprised Lith. \"Is there a way to check how things played out?\"","\"Of course! I just need to call my master.\" Zolgrish pressed Inxialot’s rune and added him to the call.","\"This is Inxialot the Lich’s house. Who am I talking to?\" A deep tenor voice came from off-screen.","\"It’s me, Inxi! Zogh-zogh!\" Zolgrish replied.","\"Oh, that moron.\" The voice replied with what Lith recognized as a low growl. \"One moment, please.\"","Lith heard a soft thud, and then a small black cat bolted across the floor and out of the door.","\"That was rude!\" Zolgrish grunted. \"Ratpack is a moron, but I don’t say that to his face.\"","\"I’m right here, Master.\" The small undead sighed.","\"Most of the times.\" Zolgrish shrugged.","\"Who are you, and how did you get my rune, you undead piece of trash?\" Inxialot snarled, his eyes burning with the red light of undeath."]},{"number":4472,"title":"Chapter 4472 Broken Clock (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I was in the middle of a groundbreaking experiment!\"","\"It’s me, Master Inxi! Zogh-Zogh.\" Zolgrish replied.","\"That explains a lot, but not why you dared disturb my work!\" Inxialot snorted, releasing a thick dust cloud from his nostrils that would have put a Dragon to shame.","\"I... Why did I call him again, Ratpack?\"","\"Oh, for the love of...\" Lith cursed and proceeded to explain the situation in Jambel and his suspicions about it.","\"Nice theory, Larp, but you are way off the mark.\" Inxialot brushed his worries away with a sweep of his hand. \"The Isharas did ask my permission, and I told them to fuck off or face my wrath.\"","\"I’m lost here. Who is this Lamb, and how is he involved in this story?\" Zolgrish asked.","\"Scourge and Lamb same person.\" Ratpack said. \"He also called Lith Verhen.\"","\"Why did you do that, Inxialot?\" Lith ignored the non-Awakened Lich’s rambling and forced the Undead Representative to focus. \"We are not friends.\"","\"What a silly question, Bong.\" Inxialot replied. \"Jambel’s territory belongs to Zolgrish, and as his master, everything he has belongs to me! I’d never let those overgrown scorpions steal my silver.\"","\"As long as you only take his share of the metal, I’m okay with it.\" Lith nodded. \"Thanks, Inxialot. Much appreciated. Lith out.\"","\"Stop right there, master!\" Zolgrish roared in outrage. \"If what is mine is yours and what is yours is yours, what am I supposed to be, your slave? This goes against our apprenticeship agreement!\"","\"Are you sure? Nero, give me a hand to find the contract.\" Inxialot said.","\"There’s no need for it. I have my copy right here!\" Zolgrish snorted. \"It says: ten pairs of socks, ten shirts, six pairs of pants...\"","\"That’s laundry list, Master.\" Ratpack slapped his forehead. \"Contract gone. Mold destroyed it centuries ago.\"","\"Here you go.\" Nero returned a few seconds later with a pristine parchment covered in protective runes.","\"Is this a map? Where am I supposed to go and why?\" Inxialot asked in confusion.","\"Master!\" Zolgrish jumped in fright, already oblivious to the previous conversation. \"How did you override the safety measures of my amulet, and how long have you been spying on me?\"","\"I have no idea.\" Inxialot replied. \"How did I do that, Nero? Most importantly, why am I wasting my time on this moron?\"","The Emperor Beast disguised as a house cat rolled his eyes and gave him a recap of the situation.","\"I see. Let’s read the contract together.\" Much to his dismay, there was no clause that allowed him to seize his apprentice’s possessions on a whim.","\"See? I was right!\" Zolgrish roared in triumph.","\"Zolgrish!\" Inxialot jumped in fright, having no idea why his apprentice’s hologram was in the middle of his lab. \"How did you override the safety measures of my amulet, and how long have you been spying on me?\"","\"I did no such thing!\" Zolgrish snorted in outrage. \"I think. Maybe. Ratpack?\"","\"Look! A Tyris’-shaped stain on wall!\" The small undead said.","\"Did you remember to call Raagu?\" Nero said. \"She asked your help dealing with the Isharas.\"","Both assistants knew that if left to their own devices, their masters could go on like that for days. So Ratpack brought Zolgrish out of the holographic field, and Nero tricked Inxialot into hanging up the call.","Meanwhile, at the Verhen Mansion, Solus still couldn’t believe her own ears.","\"This is incredible! Even if by mistake, Inxialot did a job as good as Faluel.\"","\"Even a broken clock is right twice a day.\" Lith shrugged. \"Eiros is also right, though. We should help the Kellar region next and take the opportunity to visit him. We’ve made plenty of good memories in the north when I served as a Ranger, and Eiros is a friend.","\"No matter how good a lord he is, winter in Kellar is no joke, and Eiros could use our help.\"","\"It’s an excellent idea, but I’m worried about Jirni.\" Solus said. \"We can’t bring all the family with us without leaving her vulnerable. Without the tower and the babies, she would be an easy mark for the Gernoffs.\"","\"Let’s discuss it with her.\" Lith replied. \"Besides, I doubt that even the Gernoffs have operatives in Jambel. Without someone local, collecting information or going unnoticed in such a tight-knit community is slightly easier than stealing a Dragon’s egg.\"","Lith informed his family of his plans, and he and Solus departed for the Kellar Region to take part in the relief efforts.","The people of the north were normally as cold and unforgiving as its climate, yet Lith discovered that many cities had warmed up to him and welcomed their former Ranger with affection.","\"Thank you for the supplies, Ranger Verhen.\" The head of a small backwater village consisting of barely thirty-two houses said. \"You have no idea how much your cargo means to us. We had to strip the bark from the trees and eat it to survive until now.\"","\"Please, don’t mention it.\" Lith shook his head. \"Also, I’m not a Ranger anymore, Elder Sakh.\"","\"Nonsense!\" The old man grunted. \"As I see it, a Supreme Magus is nothing but a Ranger with shoulders broad enough to bear the weight of the entire Kingdom. You’re just doing for everyone what you did for the Kellar region, and for that we’ll always be grateful to you.\"","Lith was not used to receiving such praise without a hidden agenda and remained speechless for a second longer than it was polite.","\"I’m surprised you lasted this long without a single casualty.\" He cleared his throat, eager to change the topic. \"How did you do it?\"","\"Thanks to you, Ranger Verhen.\" Sakh stood beside Lith like a gargoyle, shooing away all those who tried to waste his time with small talk after being healed of their ailments.","Before leaving a village, Lith also offered his services as a Healer, saving the people of Kellar money and the harsh travel that reaching the nearest city during winter required.","Sakh ensured that everyone got their share of supplies, got treated, and left after a polite thank you instead of holding the line.","\"With three Lost Cities gone, Kellar is flourishing again. Shorter and safer trading routes are now available to big and small merchants. Goods travel faster and are cheaper than in the past.","\"Also, the Mage Association has reclaimed plenty of corrupted lands and made them fertile again. There is a lot of work to do, and our brave boys are no longer forced to accept the measly wages that local landowners and merchants offer them.","\"They can leave the village safely and find jobs that pay well. \"Our youths earn enough to make themselves a life out there and afford sending money home to put food on the table of their old parents.","\"It’s amazing how a single man can change so many lives.\"","\"That’s nice of you to say.\" Lith replied more awkwardly than before.","Once he finished healing the villagers, Lith cleared the houses and streets from the snow. He checked the well to make sure no animal corpse had fallen into the water.","Otherwise, when spring came and the ice thawed, the carcass would rot and make the water toxic. He returned to the tower, still in disbelief at how much the north had changed."]},{"number":4473,"title":"Chapter 4473 Ruined City (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’Well, that’s a nice surprise.’ Solus said after Lith shared Sakh’s words with her via a mind link. ’It explains why the people of the villages I visited were so kind to me. I bet that everyone in the Kellar region knows you and every member of your family.’","’You’re probably right.’ Lith sighed. ’You know what’s sad, instead? That during my two years as a Ranger we have marked every single mana geyser in the Kellar region, whereas we’ve lived most of my life in Distar and know only the location of a handful of mana geysers.’","’That’s because we worked here, and every mana geyser was an opportunity to get home faster.’ She chuckled. ’You never gave a damn about any city of Distar aside from Derios, the Lark Estate, and Lutia.","’We have never taken a single tour of the Distar region before this mess with the Isharas, whereas we know Kellar like the back of our hand.’","Of course, not every place in the Kellar region was the same, nor were its people. Some villages and even cities still disliked foreigners and didn’t bother hiding it. Lith and Solus were rudely received a few times, but they let it slide unless certain lines weren’t crossed.","No city had ever earned their spite like Maekosh, and when Lith reached it, he was far from shocked when he discovered that its citizens had become even more bitter and ungrateful than he remembered.","\"Look who’s back. The barbarian with a badge from the south.\" Xelos, the owner of the Prancing Griffon tavern, spat on the ground to emphasize his joy at the unexpected reunion.","\"I have no idea who you are, but I’m pretty sure it’s for the best of both of us.\" Lith replied with a flat tone.","\"Please, forgive Xelos’ poor manners.\" Baroness Enja, the local ruler, had come to supervise the delivery of the goods, afraid that the mean people of Maekosh might once again incur Lith’s wrath with their attitude.","\"This winter has been hard on everyone.\" She said, and she meant it.","The Baroness had almost run out of basic necessities after sharing everything she could afford with the less fortunate. Enja wasn’t a generous woman, but if too many people died on her watch, she would have lost her seat as a Baroness even without the Isharas’ meddling.","\"Hunger has plagued Maekosh for over a month, and my beloved citizens have been driven to the brink of despair. If you also consider that many among us fell ill and succumbed to colds and flu because too starved to fight back, you can understand why they are on edge.\"","\"Actually, I can’t.\" Lith snorted, taking the crates out of his pocket dimension one at a time. \"I bet those people would have survived if you had a Healer, and also that your people drove out any gentle soul who tried to set up shop here.\"","The crowd cursed, and the Baroness flushed at those words, because they were the truth. No foreigner lasted long in Maekosh, even those the city desperately needed.","\"And whose fault do you think it is that we are reduced to beg a southerner for food?\" Mikos, a local brewer, growled in outrage. \"It’s all because of you, *Magus* Verhen.\"","The man managed to make the highest title a mage could aspire to into a slur.","\"It’s only because you helped that traitor of Oshek that Maekosh is dying! Ever since he opened and expanded his two-bit brewery in Lutia, no one is willing to buy a single keg of our beer at the usual fares!","\"We are forced to sell at a loss or see the merchants who until a few years ago begged down on their hands and knees to buy our goods turn around and leave!\"","The number of barrels the local breweries produced each year had always been limited by the available surplus wheat stocks, just as only the bravest and boldest merchants dared to face the harsh journey to reach Maekosh.","Oshek, instead, lived in one of the Kingdom’s most fertile regions, and the Warp Gate in Lutia made buying and moving the barrels of his beer quick and easy. Moreover, the owner of the Drinking Wolf had always asked fair prices for his products.","While Maekosh’s brewers sold only to luxury merchants, who in turn supplied only the wealthy, Oshek did business with anyone who could afford it.","As Oshek’s fame as a brewer spread, he had improved his equipment, bought an entire building for his brewery, and produced so much Maekosh-quality beer that no merchant in their right mind wasted their time and money haggling with those like Mikos.","\"Mikos!\" Baroness Enja withered him with a look, or rather, she tried. \"Don’t mind him, either, Magus Verhen. I assure you Mikos doesn’t mean what he said.\"","\"I’m sure he did, and I do mind him, Baroness.\" Lith stopped unloading the crates altogether and turned towards the brewer. \"If you want to glare at the one responsible for Maekosh’s situation, Mikos, you only have to look in the mirror.","\"Unless the wheat you grow around here requires gold as fertilizer, your so-called ’usual fares’ are a daylight robbery. The only reason merchants put up with your nonsense and those who could afford your beer bought it for all this time was that Maekosh had a monopoly.","\"If any of you had a shred of business talent, with all that money you would have long since expanded your breweries, lowered your prices, and turned Maekosh into the Kingdom’s capital of the beer, drawing countless tourists here.","\"Instead, you idiots just pocketed the money and shot your own feet over and over. Look around you. Nothing has changed since my tour as a Ranger, yet even the smallest villages I visited have gotten better.","\"Maekosh still has the unflattering record of being the only middle-sized city in the entire Kingdom with no Healer, no thriving merchant guild, and no chance to ever get a Warp Gate. Is it not?\" Lith’s words hit all those present like a punch to the gut.","The city had actually gotten poorer and dirtier since his last visit, while the rest of the north flourished. Maekosh could have benefited from the disappearance of the three lost cities like the rest of Kellar, if only its citizens allowed it.","\"Magus Verhen-\"","\"I’m not done, Baroness.\" Lith’s tone was level, but his voice was as sharp as steel, cutting her short. \"Instead of wasting your energy whining, you people should appreciate me coming here to help you, or at least keep your mouths shut.","\"I don’t expect your gratitude, but I demand your respect. I’m not your scapegoat Ranger anymore. I’m the Supreme Magus of the Kingdom, and I’ve taken some of my precious time to deliver basic necessities to you, paying them out of my own pocket.\"","\"As you should.\" Ysha, a middle-aged woman, sneered in reply.","\"Excuse you?\" Lith’s eyes narrowed, and his voice lowered into a cold hiss.","The Baroness wanted to speak, but she had seen the look on Lith’s face countless times on countless other people over the years.","It was the grimace of someone fed up with her subjects’ attitude and wouldn’t spend a second longer in Maekosh, even if she paid them their weight in gold."]},{"number":4474,"title":"Chapter 4474 Ruined City (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"You brought down our businesses, and I’m sure you’ve also ruined our reputation as soon as you became popular and made lots of noble friends at the Royal Court.\" Ysha spoke as if she were Lith’s employer and was about to fire him.","\"The least you can do is compensate us for the trouble you’ve caused us. Moreover, aren’t you ashamed of whining like that? As you said, you are the Supreme Magus of the Kingdom. It’s your duty to help us.","\"Why should we be grateful to you just for doing your job?\"","Lith’s eyes widened for a second in disbelief. Then a mirthless smile appeared on his face and reached his eyes.","\"You know what? I’ve changed my mind.\" At a wave of Lith’s hand, the crates went back into his pocket dimension at once. \"I’m done here. You can all starve to death for all I care.\"","\"Magus Verhen, you can’t be serious!\" Enja said, turning as pale as a ghost.","\"I sure can.\" He shrugged. \"This was an act of goodwill, not something I had to do. My goodwill is gone. You’ll have to wait for the official shipment. It will be here in one week. Two at most.\"","\"I understand your anger, but please, at least allow me to buy the supplies from you. Half the city will be dead in two weeks. We can’t wait that long.\" The Baroness said.","\"Fine. One thousand gold coins. Payment up front and no credit.\" Lith extended his open hand as if he expected Enja to carry so much money on her.","\"One thousand gold coins?\" The Baroness trembled like a leaf and color flushed from her face. \"That’s more than Maekosh itself is worth. Walls and all!\"","Her people were good with numbers, and knew she was right. If one didn’t consider the private homes and their contents in the city’s estimate, Maekosh didn’t come even close to that number.","\"Supply and demand, Baroness. It’s a concept that your people know all too well and exploited all their miserable lives.\" Lith replied. \"Winter is over, and there are no longer controlled prices. I can ask as much as I want.","\"Consider this the price of your citizens’ lives weighed down by their obnoxious hubris and insufferable attitude. You can have them pay you back by taxing the air they breathe. I don’t care. Either you give me my money in the next five seconds or I Warp.\"","\"I would if I could, but I don’t have that much gold anymore.\" Enja lowered her head in shame.","All those present gasped, finally realizing the consequences of their actions. Even the most headstrong and prideful of the people of Maekosh had seen footage of Lith fighting. They knew that attacking him would have only resulted in their premature death.","’I know you don’t.’ Lith inwardly scoffed. ’This city has never been rich, and with the Isharas messing up with your supplies, you must have spent most of your personal fortune just to keep this shithole standing.","’To make matters worse, you’re no Keyla, and even she will get no financial aid from the Royals as punishment. Maybe the baroness could give me jewels or artifacts worth a thousand gold coins, but she knows she’d never make that money back.","’She would become permanently poorer, and her household would slowly decline until someone else takes her place.’","\"I’ll give you everything I’ve left, but please, at least sell me enough food for the children.\" The Baroness said. \"They have no fault and don’t deserve your wrath, yet if you leave, they’ll be the first to die, and Maekosh will have no future.\"","\"Gold first.\" Lith’s hand was still extended, and if her words struck a chord inside of him, there was no sign of it.","The Baroness took a small purse from her dimensional ring that contained three platinum coins, the equivalent of three hundred gold coins, and emptied it on Lith’s palm.","\"It should be enough.\" Enja kept a straight face as she inwardly said goodbye to the last remnants of her family fortune.","\"It is.\" The coins disappeared from Lith’s hand and materialized in the Baroness’ purse. \"Bring the children here, so that I can give them their food and heal them.\"","Enja felt the familiar weight of the coins and understood his intentions.","’Magus Verhen tested me. He wanted to see whether I was as bad as the rest of my citizens. He also allowed me to literally buy the lives of the children. Had he gifted me the supplies, I bet the people would have rioted and killed each other for them .","’My citizens would have claimed that the food came from an official of the Kingdom and hence belonged to everyone. This way, instead, the supplies are my property, and I can defend them with the full strength of the army if necessary.’","The Baroness nodded and had the children of Maekosh step forward.","\"What about the elders?\" She said tentatively while Lith healed the ailments and took out crates of supplies that the baroness’ personal guard brought to her mansion’s vault. \"They too are weak and frail.\"","\"They contributed to creating this mess by raising their children to be as idiotic as they are.\" Lith replied. \"They have made their bed; they can lie in it. Permanently.\"","The finality in his words made everyone shudder, and a few children cry.","\"There is no reason to be afraid, young man.\" Lith patted the hiccupping boy’s head. \"Don’t you like fairy tales?\"","He asked, and the boy nodded.","\"Then consider yourself the hero of the story, and learn the lesson your parents failed to teach you and learn themselves. Treat others like you want to be treated, or the day will come when you’ll be treated as you treated everyone else.\"","The boy still didn’t understand why the scary man in front of him was so angry with his parents, but at least his body didn’t hurt anymore. The cold that had haunted him for weeks was gone, and he could breathe again.","The oven-fresh jam bread the man had offered the boy also tasted amazing. The sweetness of the strawberry jam and the softness of the bread made him feel alive again, quieting down the growling of his stomach for the first time in months.","\"This is for you, Captain Legato.\" Lith handed her enough supplies for her, the Baroness, and her soldiers. \"You and your soldiers need your strength to protect the future of this city.\" He nodded at the children.","\"Fail me, steal a single morsel of food, and it will be the last mistake you ever make.\" Lith placed his hand on her shoulder, healing her as well.","Light magic was supposed to be warm and comforting, yet what flooded Legato’s system was cold and overbearing. It fixed her body while also letting her know that Lith could have torn her apart with that same spell.","\"I won’t fail you, My Lord.\" She rapped her fist against her breastplate. \"I swear it on my life.\"","***","Lith and Solus visited Jambel last, and the welcome they received was nothing like Maekosh’s. The city was clean, orderly, and everybody was well-fed and -dressed."]},{"number":4475,"title":"Chapter 4475 Shared Grief (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Baron Wyalon had faced winter as usual, using the nearby woods and twin lakes for extra food as soon as the supplies dwindled and merchant caravans became unreliable.","The Baron had become a leading figure for the local nobility as much as the Larks were in Lustria, and not only because both nobles owned a military-grade DoLorean.","Wyalon knew how to take care of his people, never delegating the harshest tasks and always leading his troops into battle.","His citizens admired and respected the Baron because he led by example and was the first to do everything he demanded from others. He was the rule to his rules, not the exception.","\"Please, you can give me a parade later.\" Lith raised his hands for silence, and the people of Jambel complied as one. \"First, you need to get yourself something to eat that’s not fish or game. Then we’ll treat all your wounds and illnesses.","\"Please, split into orderly lines and step forward one at a time.\" Lith took out the supplies all at once, and the Baron’s soldiers split them into individual packages.","Lith, Solus, Tista, and even Aran and Leria took part in the distribution. The children were Awakened, skilled Healers, and most importantly humble. They always admitted when the task was beyond their abilities and never hesitated to ask for help.","Wyalon also stood in line, and all those in front of him offered to let him go first, but he refused.","\"Before the Supreme Magus, I’m just an ordinary citizen.\" The Baron said. \"You need food and healing as much as I do. I can wait my turn.\"","\"But you are also our lord and protector.\" A man said. \"You are the reason no monster tribe broke past our city walls, and my family lived to see this moment. If you don’t go first, I would feel like the most ungrateful person on Mogar.","\"Please, my lord, I’m not doing this because I have to, but because I want to.\"","\"I can’t refuse your gratitude without being a jerk.\" Wyalon sighed and stepped forward. \"But I really don’t mind waiting.\"","Yet no one moved a single step until the Baron stood before Lith, receiving magical treatment and the supplies for his family. Then it was his wife and children’s turn. No one complained or made a peep.","The citizens of Jambel smiled, living the honor of their lord like their own.","\"Where’s Kotu’s girlfriend?\" Lith asked.","\"She’s not a member of the family, yet. She can wait in line like everybody else.\" Wyalon’s voice cut the air like tempered steel.","\"Dad!\" Kotu said, blushing in embarrassment.","\"Shut up, lad, and don’t you argue with your father.\" Mirias snarled, her voice even colder than her husband’s. \"Remember where we are. Remember who we are!\"","Kotu had spent his life watching his parents argue over the silliest things, so when they agreed on something, he knew he’d better keep his mouth shut.","Jambel had expanded significantly since Lith’s last visit and its population had increased, yet it took less than an hour to hand out the supplies and heal everyone.","The people of Jambel were polite and respectful toward each other, giving the Healers a small bow before making space for the next person in line.","\"It’s nice to meet you, Clila.\" Lith said, surprised to find her in his line. \"How is Jambel treating you?\"","\"It’s nice to see you too, Magus Verhen.\" The young woman had fully matured since their last encounter in Amrok. She had gained weight and muscle in the right places, gaining a rosy complexion despite the cloudy weather.","\"Jambel is great, and its people are amazing. I only wish that Elfy could be here with me. He would have loved this place. I can almost hear him planning tours of the lakes and organizing fishing expeditions for nobles.\"","\"That’s actually a great idea.\" Lith replied. \"Maybe he wasn’t the only one with the knack for business.\"","\"Maybe, but the pain is still too fresh.\" Her eyes became veiled with tears. \"If only-\"","\"So, I’m guessing you aren’t Kotu’s mysterious girlfriend, then.\" Lith knew the pain of losing a brother better than anyone else, and rushed to change the topic to something he knew would make grief the least of Clila’s worries.","\"No!\" She went from crying to blushing up to her ears.","\"I wish!\" The Baron sighed loudly enough for everyone to hear.","He had remained by Lith’s side to keep him company and oversee the distribution of supplies.","\"Dad!\" Kotu blushed just as hard as the entire Jambel chuckled at his expense.","\"I’m not dating anyone.\" Clila was holding back the line, but everybody loved gossip, so they listened quietly while pretending to chat with the person behind them. \"I’m too busy getting used to my new life in Jambel for that.","\"Besides, the young lord is a noble, whereas I’m just a store clerk.\"","\"Nonsense!\" Mirias dismissed Clila’s objection with a shake of her head. \"No one is ’just’ something. My Eiros was ’just’ a soldier, and look at him now. If you change your mind and want to get to know my son, dear, you’ll always be our honored guest.\"","Clila had a squeaky-clean past, and Lith personally taking care of her trip to Jambel after asking the Wyalons to take care of her, made the young woman an ideal daughter-in-law.","\"Mom!\" Kotu blushed even harder as the people of Jambel giggled and commented on what a cute couple they would make. \"Not you too!\"","\"Thank you for your offer, Your Ladyship. I’ll never forget your hospitality and generosity.\" Clila cleared her throat in embarrassment and desperately tried to avoid giving the Baroness a clear answer.","\"See? So humble and respectful.\" Mirias looked at the young woman with a starry-eyed gaze. \"Not like a certain someone I know.\"","\"How can you say that, Mom? You’ve never met Asryl!\" Kotu wished for Mogar to swallow him whole, but the planet had no intention of ruining its fun.","\"I was talking about your sister, but thanks for the heads up, son. I’ll remember that.\" The Baroness gave her children a withering gaze that brooked no further argument.","Kotu silently cursed his own big mouth while Irie joined her brother in his plea for a sudden demise.","Clila finally understood that anything she said would be twisted and used to further the Wyalons’ agenda, so she gave Lith a quick bow and disappeared amid the crowd.","Once the Verhens finished distributing the supplies, the Baron invited them to his home for lunch and to stay in his guest house for as long as they wanted.","\"We gladly accept, Eiros, but only if you let me do the cooking and we use my ingredients.\" Lith replied. \"It wouldn’t be fair to force you to consume the food I just gave you to feed my family.\"","\"More for me, then!\" The Baron said with a laugh.","\"Dear!\" Mirias paled at his bluntness, restoring the family dynamic. \"Please, Magus Verhen, there’s no need for that. We have plenty of chefs, and our pantry is full.\"","\"I insist.\" Lith said with a smile, putting an end to the argument.","The only thing ruder than making a guest work was rejecting a kind offer."]},{"number":4476,"title":"Chapter 4476 Shared Grief (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The meal was hearty and delicious, but the dessert was even better.","Lith served everyone a molten chocolate cake with plenty of powdered sugar and fresh cream. The heat of the chocolate and the cold of the cream hit the spot and filled what little space was left in everyone’s stomach.","\"Gods, that was delicious.\" Mirias did her best to suppress a burp. \"I’m afraid I’ll have to go on a diet after this, Magus Verhen.\"","\"I hear you.\" Solus patted her stomach.","\"Thanks, Mirias, but please, call me Lith.\" He replied.","\"I wouldn’t dare! I mean, fine... Lith.\" She spoke the last word as if she expected to burst into flames, and when Mogar kept spinning and the sun shining, the Baroness sighed in relief.","***","\"Are you sure Jirni is safe at the Mansion?\" Kamila asked after they moved to the guest house for the afternoon nap.","\"She said so, and I believe her.\" Lith shrugged. \"Besides, she’s still swamped in paperwork. Supervising a Kingdom-wide investigation is a full-time job.\"","\"I feel guilty just being here.\" Kamila sighed. \"The silver lining is that Jirni has plenty of company and can join us whenever she wants.\"","She took a Home Stone from her dimensional amulet and placed it outside their room window.","\"By the way, this is nice, but it doesn’t count as a date. Too many extras.\" Kamila nodded at the toddlers that had just fallen asleep.","\"I never said it was.\" Lith smiled. \"I thought that since I had to come to Jambel, I could use the opportunity to check on the Wyalons and Clila.\"","\"I know, and it was really nice of you.\" She imprinted the Camellia, and its four flowers shifted to the icy-blue of the water element. \"Where are you going?\"","\"I’m not tired, and neither is Val.\" Lith took the boy out of the crib and into his arms. \"We can use a bit of alone time without Ely throwing a fuss.\"","\"She’s so jealous and bossy. I wonder who she gets that from.\" Kamila sighed as father and son exchanged a glance.","\"It’s a mystery.\" Lith replied. \"See you later, and call me if anything happens\"","He Blinked out of the house and then Warped outside the city walls. One more Steps from there brought him to the edge of the faraway woods.","\"It’s alright, Val. You can shapeshift here.\" Lith said, and the baby boy’s hair turned emerald and his eyes silver. \"That’s not what I meant, silly.\"","Lith shapeshifted into a human-sized Tiamat while holding Valeron’s hand, and the baby boy quickly followed suit, turning into a small Bahamut.","\"Come on. Fly all you want. You are free.\"","The baby boy took a short sprint on his stumpy legs and flew towards the sky, quickly followed by the Tiamat. Lith always gave Valeron the Second some space, but kept close enough to reach him in a single Blink.","The baby Bahamut loved those moments when he had his adoptive father all to himself. Valeron felt safe flying in Lith’s shadow, and dared to attempt aerial maneuvers that pushed his small frame to its limits.","He soon flew faster than an arrow, yet Lith was always behind him, the distance between them unchanged in a silent promise of love and protection. Valeron enjoyed knocking the snow off the treetops with swift sweeps of his claws and scaring the birds with his squeaky roars.","Away from walls and barriers, Valeron felt normal again. He didn’t have to hide who he was and who his parents were. He was just a small Divine Beast playing under his father’s watchful eye, just like Elysia and Raldarak always did.","Valeron screeched his challenge to Mogar and infused himself with Life Maelstrom. He became almost five times faster and bolted upwards, as if he were trying to reach the sun.","Lith followed him without losing a beat. His adoptive son wouldn’t have outsped him even if his small body could actually withstand the silver lightning’s full prowess instead of just barely half.","The baby Bahamut turned around, squealing in joy when he saw the familiar black figure exactly where he was supposed to be. No matter what he did, Lith didn’t give up on him and was always by his side.","Valeron pushed himself as hard as he could, flying higher and higher until the air grew so thin that the boy struggled to breathe. When fatigue weighed down on his body and his lungs burned from the strain, the little Divine Beast performed a U-turn and dived into his father’s arms.","Lith felt the little boy’s weariness through the Dragon Scales, but also his excitement and the trust he had in Lith.","\"Let me show you true Dragonspeed, little fellow.\" Lith held Valeron close to his chest and flapped his wings with his true strength, turning into a black blur that soared through the sky.","It scared the baby boy, but only for an instant. His body adapted to the new speed as he leaned against his father’s chest, the thrill of speed and awe for the vastness of the horizon replaced fear.","Lith flew over the twin lakes, circled the woods, and reached the peak of the barony’s highest mountain. Valeron didn’t feel cold thanks to the heat radiating from his father’s body, while air magic ensured he had no problems breathing.","Once he was done with the tour of Jambel’s wilderness, Lith returned to the woods. Father and son sat on flat stones before each other, their inner fire melting and evaporating the snow covering their seats without them even noticing.","Valeron loved those little outings with Lith because not only did he have his father all to himself, but also because it was the only time the young boy could ask Lith all the questions that tormented him without upsetting his siblings.","Elysia had only a vague understanding of Valeron the Second’s circumstances, while Raldarak had none. Valeron couldn’t talk about his original parents in front of his siblings, mostly because he himself didn’t know what to say.","His young mind failed to comprehend how people who loved him so much and whom he considered good and loving parents could have become enemies. Luckily for Valeron, he didn’t need mind links or words to convey his doubts.","The Dragon Scales allowed Valeron to ask complex questions and express concepts he could barely grasp in a form Lith could understand. At the same time, the Scales allowed Lith to answer the baby boy’s questions without sharing information that would traumatize him.","[Do you hate my parents?] Valeron asked via the Dragon Scales. [AN: the words in square brackets are expressed through feelings, not words.]","[I don’t hate your father. I have great respect for him, and I tried until the last moment to reach a peaceful solution to our situation.] Lith replied, adding images of his encounters with Jormun via a mind link.","During those peaceful moments, Valeron loved to see his father through Lith’s eyes. To smell Jormun’s scent, observe his gestuality, and hear the tone of his voice exactly as Valeron remembered it.","[I don’t hate your mother either, but I can’t forgive her.] Lith continued. [She did things that forced us to fight, and she took someone precious from me.]"]},{"number":4477,"title":"Chapter 4477 Improved Design (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Lith kept the mind link shut, yet Valeron saw something at the edge of his father’s Dragon Scales. The young boy witnessed a twisted version of the loving Thrud he knew, her smile twisted and cruel.","Then, the figure of another woman appeared. She was very tall, with long brown hair streaked blue, and wore sleek silver armor. Valeron experienced the deep feelings Lith had for her and noticed the strongest ones were nostalgia and grief.","\"Phloria?\" Valeron asked, the name forming on his lips for no reason. \"Who is Phloria?\"","\"An old friend, son.\" Lith gave the boy a wan smile. \"She’s gone, but there’s not one day that I don’t miss her.\"","Valeron couldn’t feel anything through the Dragon Scales, which could only mean that Lith was shutting them off on purpose, not to hurt him.","[There was no way to solve the conflict peacefully?] He asked the only question that truly mattered.","[No. There wasn’t.] Lith replied. [But there are too many things I can’t explain to you because I wasn’t there. You can ask your grandparents, though.]","He tapped on the warrior pendant on Valeron’s neck, and the young boy held it tight, conjuring Leegaain and Tyris out of thin air.","\"What is it, child?\" Leegaain knelt to get to Valeron’s eye level and caressed his head.","The young boy just extended his small, scaled hand, and the Guardian listened to his grandson’s request.","\"Valeron wants to borrow our memory.\" Leegaain said after turning to Tyris. \"He doesn’t want to know the details about the war. He just wants to see all the memories of his parents we have. Especially those where he was with them.\"","\"I envy you Dragons so much for your Dragon Scales.\" Tyris sighed, offering the Father of All Dragons her hand. \"No need for complex speeches or sharing personal memories to have an honest conversation.","\"The Dragon Scales allow you to express what you feel, without leaving any space for misunderstanding.\"","\"About that.\" Lith said. \"I’m curious about why Dragons have such a power, and Griffons don’t.\"","\"Because Dragons have problems expressing themselves.\" Leegaain replied. \"Being cold and reserved is in our nature, and Dragon Scales help us to open up.\"","\"Griffons, instead, know all too well how to express themselves.\" Tyris said. \"Our problem is keeping our feelings under control. If we had Dragon Scales, we’d probably scare each other to death, especially our children.","\"We’d project in their mind such an intense love and fear that something might happen to them that they’d grow up scared of their own parents as much as of the outside world.","\"I never wanted any of my children to leave me. If it were up to me, I’d keep them close to my bosom their entire lives. Letting them go is the most painful thing I’ve ever done, and I’m happy I didn’t have Dragon Scales to guilt them into staying with me.\"","\"Grandma?\" Valeron understood nothing, but he could see the deep sadness in Tyris’ eyes.","\"Yes, beloved?\"","\"I love you.\" He extended his arms for an embrace, and the Guardian was happy to oblige.","\"I love you too. More than you’ll ever know.\" She held him tight to her chest, the scent of Valeron the First the boy carried reminding Tyris of everything she had loved and lost.","Silent tears streaked down her cheeks as the two men looked at each other in awkwardness.","\"So... what’s with the new dress?\" Lith cleared his throat. \"It’s a new fashion choice, or is it today the anniversary of something?\"","\"Great Mother almighty!\" Only then did Leegaain notice her attire as well. \"Your mourning period is over!\"","\"Yes, but why do you say it like it’s some sort of natural disaster?\" Tyris furrowed her brow.","\"You know why.\" He sighed. \"Everyone does.\"","***","The Verhens stayed in Jambel for a couple of days before returning to the Mansion. During that time, Lith gave the babies tours of the region, and Kotu ended up breaking up with his girlfriend.","Baron Wyalon’s investigators had yet to complete the background check on Asryl, but the moment Kotu introduced her to Lith, it was no longer necessary. The many horrible and truthful things she had heard about him made her fold like a lawn chair.","Lith asked normal, polite questions that she answered honestly in panic, revealing her true nature. At the end of that brief conversation, the Wyalons looked daggers at Asryl, and Kotu felt Mogar collapse under his feet.","\"I’m sorry for him.\" Lith said after explaining everything to Friya and Quylla. \"But in the end, he dodged a poisoned arrow.\"","\"More like a fireball.\" Quylla replied. \"How did Kotu’s parents take it?\"","\"They couldn’t have been happier.\" Solus chuckled at the memory. \"I bet they’ll start inviting Clila over at the first opportunity they get.\"","\"How did things go while we were away?\" Lith asked.","\"Nothing new.\" Friya shrugged. \"I’m pretty sure we’re surrounded by Gernoffs, but I can’t find them. Believe me, I tried.\"","\"You are right.\" Solus conjured a hologram of the Mansion’s surroundings and highlighted many anomalies in the world energy’s readings. \"This kind of distortion can only happen if someone wearing a full Darwen suit is within the Ears’ range.","\"You could walk right next to them, and Life Vision would detect nothing. If they are camouflaged as well, regular sight should be just as useless.\"","\"Do you want us to take them down?\" Lith asked.","\"No. If the Gernoffs realize you’ve bested their Darwen suits, they will just change their strategy and start wondering how you did that.\" Quylla replied. \"They are not stupid, and Mom isn’t the only one who has questions about your prowess.","\"If the Gernoffs have records on the Ears of Menadion and suspect you have Ripha’s tower, they will orchestrate a scenario that will put their theory to the test. You might reveal your secret without even realizing it until it’s too late, Lith.\"","\"I’m indeed paranoid, and if the Ears reveal an invisible threat and I prepare against it, that would be enough to confirm the Gernoffs’ suspicions.\" Lith nodded.","\"What are you going to do next?\" Friya asked.","\"We’re staying here for a few days.\" Solus replied. \"The arrays of the tower will confuse the Gernoffs, and Kami wants to help Jirni with the investigations. The situation is not good, but at least they are narrowing down the problem by identifying the nobles on the Isharas’ payroll.\"","\"Speaking of Isharas, how much is left after giving half the loot to the Royals?\" Tista asked.","With Lith and Solus travelling around Distar first and Kellar later to help with the relief aid, there had been no time to split the spoils of battle.","\"We fought twenty-four Isharas, but only twelve corpses were salvageable.\" Lith replied. \"Six went to the Royals, which leaves us with six more to split between us, Faluel, and you.\"","\"We’ll there’s only one of me, and I already have Ishka’s Honor.\" Tista nodded. \"I should have enough for two more armors, then.\"","\"If we had any idea how to dismantle an Ishara’s corpse, maybe.\" Solus shrugged. \"As for the equipment, eight sets Warped away on their own the moment they lost their imprint.\""]},{"number":4478,"title":"Chapter 4478 Improved Design (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Of the sixteen sets left, six were of high-grade purified Orichalcum and only ten of purified Adamant. The Royals got eight sets, and we have eight left to split between us.\"","\"So, I get one set of Orichalcum equipment and one and one-third Adamant sets?\" Tista asked, and Lith nodded in reply. \"How is that not enough to cover my debt?\"","\"Because they are not made of pure metal.\" Lith sighed. \"They are made of Isharas’ chitinous shell coated in metal.\"","\"Fuck!\" Tista snarled. \"Those stingy bastards!\"","\"Put yourself in their shoes.\" Solus replied. \"They have huge bodies and a collection of limbs. An armor made entirely of metal would waste too many resources. Also, the shell of their kin works as an amplifier, and all Isharas have Life Maelstrom.","\"One spark of silver lightning and their equipment becomes ten times better. It’s the perfect design for them.\"","\"And a damn rip-off for their enemies! I bet the eight armor that Warped were made of solid metal.\" Tista grunted.","\"You’re probably right, but what are you going to do?\" Lith shrugged.","\"More like, what are you going to do, Lith?\" Quylla asked. \"I doubt even your pocket dimension can host so many corpses of that size, and the Crucible can’t hold so much metal.\"","\"You’re right on all accounts.\" Solus nodded. \"We had to make multiple trips to deliver everything and leave Tista and Faluel behind to watch the loot. After that, even more trips to bring our share to Lutia.\"","\"I plan to swap the normal Orichalcum stored in the Crucible with the high-grade purified Orichalcum.\" Lith said. \"It should turn into Adamant quickly and help Tista pay off her debt.\"","\"Thanks, lil bro!\" She hugged him tight.","\"Also, we’ve put one of the Isharas’ armor and weapons in the Thievery to study them.\" Solus added. \"The rest we’re about to move to the Desert to get Grandma’s help in dismantling everything and learn how to use the corpses.\"","\"That sounds nice.\" Friya said. \"Do you mind if we come along? I’m bored.\"","\"No problem, but we’re leaving the tower here.\" Lith replied. \"We’re using the Warp Gate to reach Grandma’s palace and the pocket dimension to move the loot.\"","\"How?\" Quylla asked.","\"You’ll see.\" Solus said with an impish smile.","Once they reached the Desert and Salaark prepared a space wide enough to contain eight Ishara corpses and seven sets of equipment in her palace, Solus emptied the pocket dimension before the Overlord.","At the same time, in the Mansion, Lith filled the now-empty dimensional storage with the second cargo that Solus took out in the Desert a second later.","\"Great Mother almighty!\" Friya said in awe. \"This is like conjuring a massive long-distance gate! By sharing the same pocket dimension and activating it in turns, there is no limit to the mass of inorganic matter you can transport. I envy you guys so much!\"","\"It’s called cheating.\" Solus chuckled. \"Deal with it.\"","\"I envy you too.\" Salaark frowned at the colossal pile of metal and bodies. \"Even I would need a squadron of Phoenixes or the help of another Guardian to bring so much stuff from the Kingdom to the Desert.","\"I’m so proud of you, Featherlings!\" The Overlord buried Solus’ head in her ample bosom with a hug and then did the same to Lith when he arrived.","\"Thanks, Grandma.\" He cleared his throat in embarrassment. \"Can you start with the equipment, please? The sooner I store the Orichalcum, the faster it evolves.\"","\"Sure thing.\" A snap of Salaark’s fingers and the tier one Creation Magic Spell, Dismantle, turned the equipment into a hill of enchanted metal and hardened shell plates.","\"What can you tell us about the corpses, Grandma?\" Solus asked. \"Do they have any value for research or as materials?\"","\"If you were an Ishara, maybe you could learn something. Since you are not, they are useless. As for the materials, flesh and organs are too squishy and frail to be preserved properly. Even worse, they have limited magical properties.","\"The real prize here is the Isharas’ chitinous shell. It’s harder than any Divine Beast’s bones and can be shaped however you like with Second Life. The Isharas’ lack of a skeleton and body fat makes their exoskeleton their only means of natural defense.","\"It is not only very tough, but it also offers a partial resistance to the elements.\"","\"Are you serious?\" Quylla was flabbergasted.","\"Of course.\" Salaark nodded. \"Look at this from the Ishara’s perspective. Once their shell is punctured, they have no defense. There’s nothing to stop or slow down a blade or spell that’s carving their insides.\"","\"I see.\" Quylla swallowed hard at the idea, glad to be a vertebrate.","\"Also, if I can offer you an unsolicited piece of advice, I think you got lucky here, Lith.\" The Overlord said.","\"Lucky how?\" He tilted his head in confusion. \"I just discovered I’ve got a bunch of psychos as neighbors in Distar, and they probably hate my guts now.\"","\"That’s all true, but are you really not seeing it?\" Salaark asked. \"What about you, Solus?\"","\"Seeing what?\" She looked around and noticed Quylla and Friya were just as stumped.","\"Fine. Consider this part of your birthday gift, Solus.\" Salaark conjured a hologram of an Ishara conjuring a spell in the space between his pincers and then shooting it in a compressed and amplified form. \"Seriously?\"","Everyone kept staring at the Overlord as she had gone insane.","\"Fine! I’ll dumb it down again.\" She grunted as she conjured a hologram of Thundercrash.","In the image, however, the tuning fork at the end of the railgun was replaced by the inner edges of an Ishara’s pincer.","\"You’re right!\" Lith’s eyes widened in understanding. \"The pincer is a natural focus for all kinds of magical energies. It should improve Thundercrash’s overall performance and shorten the charging time between shots.\"","\"Indeed.\" Solus nodded. \"Also, the biological component coming from a bright violet core means no impurities, and that Thundercrash can be stored in the Spark to be further refined.\"","\"Better late than never.\" Salaark sighed. \"Do you want me to butcher them for you?\"","\"Yes, please. And spare us the gory part, thank you.\" Lith nodded.","A wave of the Overlord’s hand removed every bit of flesh, blood, and organs from the corpses, giving the impression they were balloons and she had just deflated them. The black exoskeletons shone like polished stone, ready to be Forgemastered.","\"Out of curiosity, what will you do with the flesh of the Isharas?\" Quylla asked.","\"I didn’t lie when I told you the insides have no magical value. They have no use for my research.\" Salaark replied. \"Yet they will do wonders for my kitchens. Here in the Desert, we eat several species of insects and arachnids as you eat crustaceans.","\"Finding a scorpion that big is hard, but usually their meat is a rare delicacy.\"","\"Oh, gods!\" Friya turned green. \"Why did you ask, Quylla?\"","\"How can you do that?\" Quylla was flabbergasted. \"Aren’t Isharas also Divine Beasts just like you?\"","\"They sure are, and you can bet they’d eat my kind if given the chance.\" Salaark snorted. \"I don’t see why you act like that. All Divine Beasts gladly eat humans if they are so kind as to deliver themselves to the doorstep.\""]},{"number":4479,"title":"Chapter 4479 Semi Sentience (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Also, try a bite of Ishara meat buns before you judge me. I can assure you that not one of my subjects will turn this boon down, no matter their race.\"","\"I’m... I mean, sure.\" Lith nodded. \"Time sure flies when you have fun. Thanks for everything, Grandma. I prepared this for you, but I recommend consuming it at night to better appreciate it.\"","He handed her a Phoenix-sized molten chocolate cake with three cows’ worth of fresh cream, making her squirm with joy.","\"Thanks, Featherling. Much appreciated.\" Salaark stored the colossal dessert in her pocket dimension. \"See you tomorrow. It’s my turn with the kids.\"","***","After returning to the Vehren Mansion, Lith swapped the contents of the Crucibles and studied a new design for Thundercrash with Solus’ and Friya’s help. As for Tista, she now had a literal big problem.","\"Farm me sideways, where am I supposed to store all this stuff? I don’t have a farming pocket dimension!\" She groaned in frustration. \"I will need dozens of dimensional rings just for the metal, but there is no dimensional item with enough space to contain a single plate of the Isharas’ exoskeleton!\"","\"I hear you. It’s the reason all noble households and the Royals have a treasury.\" Quylla pointed out. \"Dimensional items are great, but they can be stolen after your death, and only one person can access them at any time.","\"Also, once you accumulate enough wealth and resources, no number of dimensional amulets is enough. The only solution is a treasury. The more you own, the bigger it must be.\"","\"Or a pocket dimension.\" Menadion said. \"That’s why I equipped my tower with one. The more powerful you are, the bigger the dimensional space, and a tower is the artifact-equivalent of a white core.","\"Its pocket dimension is the size of this Mansion. And I mean including the external walls, the park, and everything else.\"","\"How could I forget about you, Ripha?\" Tista said with the tone of a drowning woman seeing a lifeboat approaching. \"The only thing that surpasses your peerless beauty is the immense kindness of your heart.","\"Otherwise you wouldn’t need a chest so large to contain it.\"","\"Whoa, girl!\" The First Ruler of the Flames stepped back, her right hand raised. \"I can tell when someone is hitting on me and when they are just buttering me up. You belong to the second kind, and based on how desperate you sound, I wouldn’t be surprised if you shoved me in an oven with plenty of potatoes!\"","\"How can you say that, Ripha? I’m not buttering you up.\" Tista lied through her teeth. \"I was just about to ask you to craft a pocket dimension for me. I mean, I’m like a sister to Solus, which makes you like a second mother to me.","\"You wouldn’t say no to your step-daughter in her time of need, would you?\"","\"Riiiight.\" Menadion stretched the word to better spread sarcasm all over it. \"You are not buttering me up. You are just asking for one of the most precious, elusive, and sought-after artifacts on Mogar.\"","\"Exactly. A trifling matter for a Magus of your talent and a pillar of the Verhen family, Mommy.\" Tista nodded.","\"You know what? I’ll do it.\" Menadion replied snidely. \"Just bring me everything on this list, and I’ll whip you up a pocket dimension. If you want it crafted with modern magic, however, it will take me a few weeks.","\"I never had a reason to update the original design, but I can do it for you.\"","\"Thank you, thank you, thank-\" The joy died on Tista’s lips as she read an exhaustive list of some of the most precious, elusive, and sought-after magical ingredients on Mogar. \"Are you serious?\"","\"Why do you think omni pockets are so rare?\" Menadion scoffed. \"It’s not just a matter of finding someone with the right skill and knowledge. That’s just the final hurdle. First you have to collect a lot of priceless materials.","\"It took me about 200 years and Lochra’s and Yaga’s help to do it. Take your time. I’ll wait for you here.\"","\"You collected all this stuff?\" Tista went pale.","\"Actually, no. I could skip a few of them because the tower worked as an energy source. In your case, without a tower, I need something that can produce enough juice to remain connected with you at all times, no matter the distance.\"","\"What if I wanted a tower?\" Tista asked, aware she was likely digging herself an even deeper grave.","\"Then I’m going to need a bit more items.\" Menadion gave her a second list that Tista read, crumpled, and swallowed in fury.","\"It’s worse! So much worse!\" She whined.","\"And that’s why towers are even more precious, elusive, and sought-after than pocket dimensions.\" Menadion shrugged. \"Finding the necessary ingredients is torture, and if you don’t have a working blueprint or Creation Magic, even someone like Lochra would go broke in a few tries.","\"Even Guardians don’t craft their own mage towers because of this.\"","\"The irony.\" Tista slouched. \"I’m broke, yet I need a treasury.\"","\"Oh, you poor thing!\" Faluel Warped to the Mansion to take her share of the loot. \"You can donate everything to the poor, or maybe just entrust your cut to me. I already have a treasury, and storing a few tons of magical ingredients isn’t a big problem for me.\"","\"How could I forget about you, Master Faluel?\" Tista replied. \"You are like a star of hope that rises on the horizon to illuminate our darkest-\"","\"Yeah, and I heard what you said to Ripha earlier.\" The Hydra cut her short with a curt gesture. \"I’m not into women nor am I interested in flattery, so spare me the poetry.\"","\"And consider me offended, Tista!\" Menadion said in mock outrage. \"You dumped my large chest the moment Faluel offered you her secret vault.\"","Tista became beet red, while everyone else had a good laugh at her expense.","\"Jokes aside, I can use an extra set of hands and tails.\" Faluel said, wiping her tears of hilarity. \"Carrying all this stuff into my home will be a sweet pain in my even sweeter ass, but a pain nonetheless.\"","\"Worry not. I have the solution!\" Tista rushed into the tower, dragging Lith and Solus out to repeat the trick with their pocket dimension.","\"Well, if this isn’t gods-damn cheating!\" Faluel said as her and Tista’s share of the loot flew straight into the enchanted blast door of her treasury.","\"I thought that by now you would have gotten used to it.\" Lith said with a smug grin.","\"I am used to it, but that doesn’t mean I have to like it or not envy you.\" Faluel grunted. \"Is that it, Tista? You got nothing else on your name?\"","\"No.\" She sighed. \"My Orichalcum is already in the Crucible and Lith has taken my Adamant, so the Ishara corpses are all I have. I have no need for them now, and I don’t think I will in the near future either.\"","\"Can you put my share of the Orichalcum in the Crucible too, Lith?\" Faluel fluttered her eyelashes seductively. \"It shouldn’t take long to turn it into Adamant, and its value would be on another level.\""]},{"number":4480,"title":"Chapter 4480 Semi Sentience (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I can, but only after I finish upgrading Tista’s and my Orichalcum, since they’ll both end up in my pockets.\" Lith replied. \"Turning Adamant into Davross will take so long that giving you a hand with your Orichalcum is not a problem.\"","\"Thank you.\" It wasn’t what she had hoped for, but it was better than nothing. \"Before you go, do you have a minute?\"","\"For you, I have five.\" Lith smirked, receiving a smack on the shoulder. \"What’s the matter?\"","Faluel used a mind link to share every detail of her fight against the Isharas and Gungnir’s behavior.","\"I was surprised hearing it... Him talk, but after that day, he has remained completely silent, and it’s pissing me off.\" She said. \"Do you have any idea why he behaves like that?\"","\"As I told you the first time, I find it hard to believe the weapon Solus and I crafted for you is semi-sentient at all.\" Lith replied. \"Everything else is just absurd to me. My rule of thumb when I don’t understand something is to speak with an expert.\"","A flick of Lith’s fingers Warped everyone to the Mansion. He then asked Solus, Menadion, and the Ernas to join him. Another mind link shared Gungnir’s conundrum with them.","\"You’ve already Forgemastered a second semi-sentient weapon?\" Orion was flabbergasted. \"That’s an amazing feat for someone your age. I never made anything like that until I crafted War.\"","Ragnarök squeaked with joy hearing its old name and the pride its maker exuded when talking about it.","\"Well, good for you. I’ve never Forgemastered anything like that, Orion.\" Ripha studied the different weapons with her Forgemastering spells, trying to sort out their similarities and differences.","\"You didn’t?\" Much to everyone’s surprise, the question came from Jirni. \"The legendary First Ruler of the Flames never achieved a weapon of this quality?\"","\"No. Never.\" Menadion narrowed her eyes in annoyance. \"I can understand your pride in your husband’s skills, Jirni, but never question mine or my talent. I’m the first to admit I fall short in this aspect, but I think I know why this happened.\"","\"Which is?\" Lith asked.","\"Two reasons.\" Menadion replied. \"First, I never mastered Blade Magic myself. I knew it, understood it, and could even use it outside combat situations, but never at its full potential.","\"I never was a Blade Mage. I just knew enough to understand the phenomenon thoroughly and be able to reliably Forgemaster Blade Weapons for my clients. Which leads us to the second reason.","\"Blade Weapons were just another job. I put all my heart and soul into them, but I never gave them a purpose or poured more effort into them than my client’s reputation inspired me.","\"I suppose I unwittingly always held back a bit because I knew that someday those very weapons might be used against me. You guys, instead, have worked hard to master Blade Magic and can use it in actual combat.","\"You’ve ingrained it in your flesh and bones, and this makes your connection with your weapons much more intimate than I’ve ever allowed mine to be. Moreover, when you Forgemastered the semi-sentient weapons, they carried a great significance to you.\"","Menadion turned to examine them.","\"War was born to kill Phloria’s enemies. Grimlock was crafted to cut down all those who hurt Orion as Deirus and Jirni did.\" Everyone turned to look at Lady Ernas, but if those words hurt her, it didn’t show.","\"The conditions under which the rest of the semi-sentient weapons have been created are also similar. They all had a purpose and deep feelings behind them. Something I never did, not even while designing the Fury.","\"I didn’t want my descendants to fight. I wanted them to be happy and live the serene life I never had.\" Menadion said while looking at Solus.","\"This can’t be right.\" Orion’s voice expressed all the outrage he felt at such a theory. \"Why would I make a semi-sentient weapon for Lith, yet none of my daughters received one? My Little Flower’s Reaver was a masterpiece, but had no sentience.","\"The same happened for Bloodbind and Dreadnought. Are you telling me that I have deeper feelings for myself, Lith, and my wife than for my own children?\"","\"Quite the contrary, Orion.\" Menadion shook her head. \"It’s your love for them that clipped their weapons’ wings\"","\"I beg your pardon?\" Once again, Jirni chimed in unexpectedly.","’First, Menadion rubbed in my face how I hurt my husband, and now she’s implying that he loves me less than our daughters?’ She thought while keeping her face a stone mask.","\"You heard me.\" The First Ruler of the Flames nodded. \"When Orion Forgemastered the weapons for Phloria, Quylla, and Friya, you can bet his heart went to them. He poured his skill and soul into the metal, but gave them no purpose.","\"When he Forgemastered War, instead, he couldn’t give a damn about Lith. Orion put his mind, heart, and soul in every pulse of mana and strike of his hammer. He etched his fury not only in the metal, but also in the pseudo cores.","\"Orion’s entire being was channeled into the blade at the moment of War’s creation, and so it achieved semi-sentience. The same thing probably happened for the other weapons. Orion and Lith didn’t focus on the people they wanted to protect, but on those they wanted to hurt.","\"Defense is a passive thing, Jirni. It can’t do anything unless there is a threat, and a mind can’t be just turned on and off at will. Attack, instead, is active. It’s will, fire, and bloodthirst.","\"Even while at rest, your weapons think about how to use your and their powers. They revise the past fights, looking for any mistake either of you might have made. They plan ahead. They sharpen their edge in silence for the next kill.\"","At those words, everyone looked at their respective semi-sentient weapons, but they remained still. All but the Sage Staff which whistled awkwardly, trying to act natural and standing out like a sore thumb.","\"That’s why I’m not surprised Gungnir doesn’t speak outside of combat, and Skywarp and Grimlock have yet to speak at all. Gungnir was crafted with my and Lith’s methods, but it’s still young.","\"It needs all his effort to develop interest into something more than just fighting. Grimlock and Skywarp, instead, are just like War was. They were Forgemastered before your Awakening, Orion, and unlike War, they’ve seen a handful of fights.","\"In time, I’m sure they’ll talk, but do not expect them to make amiable conversations. At best they’ll exchange strategies with the other semi-sentient weapons and say a couple words to you if they believe it might help you.\"","\"It certainly makes sense.\" Jirni assembled her needles into the double-headed glaive Skywarp.","The weapon moved as an extension of her being, one attack flowing seamlessly into the next one. Yet the weapon didn’t say anything, and Jirni could only feel Skywarp’s energy remain placid like the surface of a lake.","\"I’ve been cooped up all this time. My weapon barely tasted any blood.\"","\"No offense, Ripha, but if I have to risk my life to get this jerk to open up, I’d rather he remain silent.\" Faluel said."]},{"number":4481,"title":"Chapter 4481 First of its Kind (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Still, thank you for your explanation.\" Faluel nodded goodbye and Warped away.","\"Is there any chance you can share your techniques with me, Master Menadion?\" Orion asked. \"I would love to reforge my daughters’ weapons with your help.\"","\"I’m sorry, but no.\" Menadion shook her head. \"Those techniques are meant solely for my heir.\"","’I bet that he believes Solus’ Staff and Gungnir are sentient because of my help, and in a way, Orion is right.’ She actually thought. ’The Ears greatly improved Solus’ and Lith’s craft, but what truly made the difference was the intent behind them.","’Lith worried about Solus while making the Staff, while Solus didn’t think at all. She put all of herself into it, which is probably the reason the Sage Staff came out so whimsical and silly.","’Gungnir, instead, was born from the desire to punish all those who threatened their family. It’s no wonder that glaive is obsessed with power and strength. To Gungnir, weakness means the death of the Verhens, which would negate its whole existence.’","\"It was worth a shot.\" Orion sighed as he gave her a deep bow. \"Thank you anyway, Master Menadion.\"","\"I wish I could help you, young man.\" She replied. \"But I don’t want to share my secrets with you more than I bet you want to share yours with me. And Lith, of course.\"","\"Guilty as charged.\" Orion raised his hands in surrender.","\"Wait. Doesn’t that mean that my new hammers might actually be semi-sentient, Daddy?\" Morok asked.","The mere thought of such a thing, and the Tyrant referring to Orion with such a moniker, made Lord Ernas want to puke blood.","\"I think so.\" Quylla said, delivering a second mortal blow to her father’s heart. \"Dad can’t stand you, so whatever feeling he had during the Forgemastering process, you can bet he focused it on the hammers. Your chances are pretty high, dear.\"","\"What about my crystal sword?\" Nalrond asked.","\"That’s a prototype.\" Friya replied. \"Let’s hope it’s just a weapon, because otherwise I would feel terrible abandoning it once you get something better.\"","\"Say something, dear. They-\" Orion turned to look at his wife, noticing her blank stare. \"It’s not what you think. I was still mad at you when I created Skywarp and-\"","\"And you had every reason to.\" Jirni dismissed the matter with a sweep of her hand. \"I hurt you, beloved. Deeply. I’m the one who should spend her days apologizing to you, but I know that words don’t mean much after what I did to you.","\"Only time can heal the wounds in your heart, and I’m grateful you gave me a second chance that I probably don’t deserve. In a way, your resentment was a blessing in disguise. Without it, Skywarp would be but a cold piece of metal.","\"Instead, it always reminds me of what I did and is a warning not to repeat my mistakes. I don’t blame you for the circumstances that led to Skywarp’s sentience. Only myself.\"","\"Then why that face?\" Orion asked.","\"Because Ripha just pointed out another thing I lack. Blade Magic.\" Jirni replied. \"Adding another item to my endless to-do list is the last thing I need, but I’ll have to find the time.","\"For someone as weak as me, it might make the difference between life and death.\"","\"I’ll teach you to the best of my abilities.\" Orion felt something tugging at his consciousness and took out his communication amulet. \"When our schedules align. Duty calls, dear. See you at lunch.\"","***","With Orion gone and Lith and Solus busy with their experiments, Jirni still had an ace up her sleeve.","\"Can you teach me?\" She asked Vastor on a secure back channel that the Master and Orion had created.","\"I can’t. I have my hands full of Ishara crap, if you catch my drift.\" Vastor snarled. \"But I can send you someone who can. Bytra knows Blade Magic, and so do Tezka and a few others of my hybrids.","\"Beware, though: you can’t learn someone else’s technique more than you can imitate the innate flow of their mana core. I had to sweat blood to find my own way to cast Blade Spells.\"","\"I’ll take what I can.\" Jirni didn’t miss the not-so-subtle message.","The Master kept growing stronger, and so did his forces.","\"Then I’ll send someone to you as soon as you get the Guardians’ promise not to kill, probe, or use my hybrids to track me down. I’m not that stupid, Jirni.\" He hung up the call and put the amulet back into his pocket dimension.","’Gods, I wonder how I could live without it for so long.’ Vastor smiled.","The Master lacked the means to Forgemaster an omni pocket, but also the need to.","The one he now possessed once belonged to the late Vareen the Plaguespreader. Vastor had hesitated for a long time before imprinting the ancient artifact, afraid that its dimensional aura might betray his identity as the Master.","Bytra had Forgemastered a special cloaking item for him and solved the issue. Now, unless someone used Invigoration on him, they wouldn’t notice the dimensional aura more than they could notice his black core.","’And the best part is that so few people can detect a pocket dimension that nobody ever found a way to hide their presence until Bytra and Tezka pooled her Forgemastering talent and his dimensional awareness.’ The Master thought.","’No one will suspect the pin on my shirt is a unique dimensional cloaking item because it’s the first of its kind. The only annoying part is that it must be constantly in direct contact with my skin.’","\"Tezka, do you mind teaching Jirni Ernas the basics of Blade Magic?\" He asked when the Suneater, Filia, and Frey entered his study.","Vastor observed the kids’ mana cores with Life Vision and noticed they had already turned orange.","\"As long as it’s just the basics, not at all. Besides, I bet our little archmages here can’t wait to test their new powers and knowledge in a battle to the ice cream with their Verhen friends.\" Tezka replied.","\"It would be amazing!\" Frey said. \"I love magic, but spending every day reading books and practicing breathing techniques is so boring.\"","The two Vastor children had dropped out of their schools to focus on their magical studies. The Master had claimed that Filia and Frey’s talent had bloomed late and needed proper nurturing, so no one dared oppose him.","Even for noble children, subjects like geography, history, and politics came after power and wisdom. Two more mages would increase House Vastor’s standing in the Royal Court and bring endless merits.","Also, it would more than justify an Archduke marrying a commoner.","***","Verhen Mansion, later on that same day.","\"I don’t really know how Jirni does it all. I need a real vacation or even better, a romantic date.\" Kamila sighed.","After spending her morning helping Jirni sift through the reports and the afternoon having many friendly magical challenges with Zinya, Kamila was exhausted. Her sister was much weaker and less skilled than her, but Zinya was more stubborn than a mule.","What she lacked in mana capacity and magical prowess, she more than made up for with pure will and fighting spirit."]},{"number":4482,"title":"Chapter 4482 First of its Kind (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Zinya managed to turn even a boring Accumulation session into a competition.","\"I have to admit that I’m a sheep to her wolf.\" Kamila sighed. \"I take magic one day at a time to learn how to take care of my children, whereas Zin practices magic as if she has to prove something to the rest of Mogar.\"","\"Sounds like those Snow Thrower magicos I worked with.\" Lith replied. \"Still, don’t worry too much. Everyone gets excited at first, but real discipline is hard to maintain when you have a busy life like you and Zin.\"","\"That’s so true.\" Kamila replied. \"If I were still working full time as a Constable instead of taking my maternity leave, I don’t think I’d have learned even one third of the spells I know, and my mana core would be yellow at best.","\"Once Zin has to breathe on for hours just to brighten a sliver of her core of a single shade, I doubt her enthusiasm will last long. Now, what were you saying about our date?\"","\"I’m way ahead of you.\" Lith replied. \"I’ve everything planned already, but there’s nothing I can do if you don’t let me know when you can take some time off from your work as vice-coordinator.","\"I can’t just kidnap you in the middle of a meeting and drop the children on Mom like a bad habit.\"","\"It would be so romantic, though.\" Kamila pictured herself being swept off her feet and whisked away to a nice restaurant, ending the evening in an intimate location covered in rose petals.","\"Right. Romantic.\" Lith snorted. \"I can almost picture myself barging inside Jirni’s office and carrying you away in the middle of a briefing while you’re instructing Royal Constables all over the Kingdom.","\"You’d become the butt of the jokes of your colleagues at best, and I’d throw hours of work and preparation in the gutter at best.\" Kamila swallowed hard as reality smashed through her idealized version of the events.","\"Gods, if you did something like that during a tactical briefing, the damage to the investigation would be incalculable.\" She said in horror.","\"And I’m not done yet.\" Lith tutted. \"At that point, I round up our children and throw them at Mom while they are still calling our names and begging us not to abandon them.\"","\"You monster!\" Kamila snarled at the mere thought.","\"Now answer me this. How romantic would you feel after I humiliated you in front of your subordinates and the last thing you heard were the desperate cries of our children?","\"How would you respond to my seduction attempts, knowing that Ral, Val, and Ely think we are gone forever?\" Lith asked.","\"I think I’d be too busy trying to kill you to listen to a word you say.\" Kamila said after taking off the rose-tinted glass of her consequences-free fantasy. \"After that, I’d run back home, reassure the kids that everything is alright, and try to salvage what I can of my work.\"","\"My point exactly.\" Lith nodded. \"Well, are you still interested in a spur-of-the-moment romantic trip?\"","\"Gods, no!\" She said. \"I’ll let you know as soon as Jirni can give me a few days off.\"","\"Good girl.\" Lith patted her head. \"See you later!\"","’I hate it when he treats me like that, and I hate it even more when he’s right!’ Kamila grunted.","***","Kamila had to wait until the Kingdom got the situation with the Ishara under control before she could apply for leave. With Jirni taking charge of the Ernas region, Kamila was the only one with the know-how to direct and coordinate the investigations in the rest of the Kingdom.","When she was finally granted a short vacation, Lith and Solus were already done upgrading Thundercrash and had even stored enough materials in the tower to conjure a Divine Beast-sized railgun from the Workshop if necessary.","Only replica ingredients would be used, and they would only keep physical form within the tower’s area of effect, but if anyone dared siege the Verhen Mansion, it would be more than enough to make the enemy a nasty surprise.","\"Mom, Dad, we’re about to leave. Is everything ready?\" Lith asked.","\"For the umpteenth time, yes!\" Raaz said in exasperation. \"We’ll be fine. We have half an army with us. Just go.\"","\"It’s still not too late, Tista.\" Menadion said.","\"Late for what?\" Tista asked.","\"To grow yourself a spine and ask me out.\" Menadion replied with a stern gaze while everyone else burst out laughing. \"We could go with them for a double date.\"","\"This is not funny, Ripha!\" Tista blushed up to her ears. \"Don’t you dare joke about this in front of Bodya. Even better, just drop it altogether!\"","\"What?\" Menadion clutched her chest in mock pain. \"All those beautiful things you said about my peerless beauty and my bosom, were they all an act to get yourself a pocket dimension?\"","\"No! I mean, yes!\" Tista wanted to die, but the rest of her family found her situation incredibly funny. \"I’m sorry. I let myself get carried away by Dragon Greed. Can we please forget about this? The joke has gotten old!\"","\"Then why am I laughing?\" Aran clenched his stomach, gasping for air.","\"That will always be funny, Auntie.\" Leria needed to cling to Abominus to keep standing.","\"I don’t get it.\" Falco said, and his two siblings shrugged with him. \"What part of this is funny, exactly?\"","\"You’ll understand when you grow up, little one.\" Leria patted his head just like Lith had done to Kamila, infuriating both her and Falco.","\"Enough is enough, guys.\" Lith raised his hands for silence, and the room quieted down. \"We all have Dragon blood in our veins, so I’d like to remind you that you too might struggle to control your Dragon Greed in the future.\"","\"Thanks, little brother.\" Tista sighed in relief.","\"So don’t be like Tista.\" Lith continued. \"Learn from her mistake and show her some compassion, or she’ll be entitled to mock you along with the rest of us when your turn comes.\"","\"I take that back!\" She snarled.","\"Also, before leaving, I’ve prepared a surprise for you.\" Lith activated the Mansion’s Warp Gate, ignoring his sister.","’If he called another band to throw one more parade to celebrate my alleged engagement with Ripha, I’m going to murder him!’ Tista thought.","Much to her relief, this time no musicians, bards, or jugglers came out of the dimensional corridor. It took her a handful of seconds to recognize the group of well-dressed people that were entering the Mansion.","The odd thing was that their clothes were fancy enough to be worthy of a gala, yet they lacked originality and looked the same. Moreover, those people looked familiar.","’Wait a minute, those are not gala clothes but work uniforms.’ Tista thought. ’Now I remember where I’ve seen these guys before. They all work at the Travelling Tavern!’","\"Where are my cuties?\" Dryna the Wyvern stepped through the Gate, confirming Tista’s suspicions.","She looked around the Mansion in a frenzy, clearly still under the effects of baby fever.","\"Here they are.\" Lith pushed the stroller toward her. \"Say hello to Auntie Dryna, kids.\"","\"Hi.\" Valeron and Elysia waved their tiny hands, making the Wyvern squeal with joy."]},{"number":4483,"title":"Chapter 4483 Different Kind of Fun (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Mama!\" Raldarak said, dealing a major blow to Dryna’s already fluttering heart.","\"Gods, you are so cute and handsome!\" The Wyvern lifted the baby boy and held him close to her chest. \"Of course, I can be your mom!\"","\"Mama?\" Raldarak asked in confusion.","\"Thanks, but he already has a mother.\" Kamila took her son back. \"More than one, actually, and way too many women already applied for the role. We don’t take any more candidates.\" She sighed.","\"What are you guys doing here?\" Tista asked.","\"I felt terrible knowing that while I am out there having fun, you’d be locked up here to ensure Jirni’s safety, so I hired Haug’s Travelling Tavern to keep you company while I’m away.\" Lith said.","\"Awakened detail service, good food, and house staff all at once. The full package.\"","\"Indeed.\" Parmegianno Haug entered the room, his face twisted into a surly grimace.","The owner of the Travelling Tavern looked the same as always. A man in his mid-thirties, about 1.8 meters (5’11\") tall, with brown hair, eyes, and a well-groomed beard streaked orange and yellow.","He had broad shoulders, but due to the loose white shirt, which along with the black pants, waistcoat, and bowtie that comprised his uniform, it was hard to tell whether he was thin or muscular.","Yet he didn’t sound the same. The chatty bartender with a perennial smile and a story to tell on the tip of his tongue had been replaced by a silent man who looked at Lith as if he were his jailer rather than a good client.","\"Why the long face?\" Tista asked.","\"Haven’t you heard?\" Dryna chuckled. \"Tyris’ mourning period is over, and the entire Awakened community is in an uproar.\"","\"Did Haug already ask Tyris out and she turned him down, or is he just tense at the idea of being rejected?\" Elina asked.","\"Please, as if I’d ever waste my time and energy in such a foolish endeavor.\" Haug snorted. \"Lady Tyris already has too many suitors, and if you ask me, none of them has a snowball’s chance in the sun.","\"She doesn’t have a type, but I bet that after someone noble and kind like Valeron the First, she’ll look for a bad boy like Lith.\"","\"I resent that.\" Lith grunted.","’I never cheated on anyone, nor did I play around with a woman’s feelings. How am I a-’","\"Really? Wasn’t it you who...\" Haug proceeded to list Lith’s confirmed kills, the crimes he had been accused of, and those he was suspected. \"You’re the classic dashing rogue type who does what he wants and gets away with it.\"","’Haug got a point.’ Solus chuckled. ’You are a bad boy, but only according to Mogar’s definition.’","\"This still doesn’t explain why you are in such a bad mood, Haug.\" Elina tilted her head.","\"Didn’t you hear Dryna?\" He sighed. \"Tyris’ mourning period is over. Her descendants, thousands of hungry and thirsty Griffons who until a while ago spent their days brooding, are partying day and night to celebrate the good news.","\"The entire Griffon bloodline is flooding bars and restaurants, leaving only when there is no more food to eat and alcohol to drink. Until your cruel son dragged me here, I was making more money in a single night than in a whole month!\"","\"Dragged?\" Elina echoed. \"You mean you don’t want to accept the job?\"","\"Of course I don’t!\" Haug snorted. \"The problem is that I ran out of Maekosh beer, and Oshek won’t sell me more unless I do Lith this favor. I can’t lose my only reliable supplier and golden goose!\"","\"Most Awakened don’t know the beer doesn’t come from Maekosh anymore and still pay the old price.\" Dryna explained.","\"That’s unscrupulous of you, Mr. Haug.\" Elina’s voice turned cold. \"You know what they say, what goes around comes around.\"","\"I know, hence why I’m here.\" He sighed.","\"See you later, Mom.\" Lith hugged his parents before leaving. \"I’ll come back to drop the kids with you once they are tuckered out.\"","The staff of the Travelling Tavern explored the Mansion and its external perimeter, setting up their own defenses and establishing guard shifts. They were all Awakened mages with plenty of experience dealing with dangerous customers.","Once Haug added the arrays of the Travelling Tavern to those of the Verhen Mansion, it became an impregnable fortress.","\"What is this place, mister?\" The bartender had just finished expanding his dimensional establishment in the center of the park when a small voice drew his attention.","\"This is my pride and joy, young man.\" He turned around and looked down to find a winged young boy with six eyes staring at him. \"Have you never seen a restaurant before?\"","Even with his sour mood, Haug would never be rude to a kid. Also, the way Garrik stared at his tavern in awe lifted the bartender’s mood more than any compliment Garrik could give him.","\"No, sir.\" Garrik shook his head. \"I’ve never been outside the Mansion. If I leave the mana geyser, my mom will get worried.\"","’This is why I’m here!’ Haug’s eyes went wide in understanding. ’This must be Morok’s little brother. The little fallen Fomor he always talks about. Garrik can’t go to a restaurant like a normal kid, so Lith brought my restaurant to him.","’He should have told me! I would have still said no until he blackmailed me, but at least I wouldn’t have acted like a jerk until now.’","\"I see.\" Haug nodded and smiled. \"Are you hungry, young man? Fancy something to eat?\"","\"Yes, please.\" Garrik tested the barstool before jumping on it, staring at everything with curiosity.","Haug prepared a milkshake for the boy, adding more ice cream and syrup than usual to make it extra sweet.","’The only good thing that came out of my deal with Lith is the recipe for his ice cream and those potato chips. I should make a killing with them.’ He thought.","\"This is delicious!\" Garrik said after taking a single slurp from a straw. \"Can I also have one for my mom, please?\"","\"Of course. Everything you want is on the house.\" Haug replied with a laugh, whipping out the second milkshake before the young boy was out of the door.","\"Come, Mom! Quick! You have to try it!\" Garrik returned a few seconds later, dragging Ryla with him. \"Mister Haug, this is my mother, Ryla. Mom, this is Mister Haug, the kind man offering us food.\"","\"Welcome to-\" When Haug’s eyes met the Fomor, he squeezed the glass so hard that it shattered, sending the milkshake flying across the tavern.","Ryla was a woman of striking beauty, over 2.3 meters (7’7\") tall, with light blue skin and waist-long hair of the six colors of the elements.","She wore only a loose toga that left her arms and back exposed, allowing her fluffy wings to move freely. If not for her six elemental eyes and the color of her skin, Haug would have easily mistaken her for a goddess descended among mortals.","\"Welcome to Haug’s Travelling Tavern. I’m sorry for the mess. Just give me a second.\" The bartender’s face turned into a professional mask as he filled the already-full glass with more milkshake."]},{"number":4484,"title":"Chapter 4484 Different Kind of Fun (Part 2)","paragraphs":["A snap of his fingers cleaned everything, and a wave of his hand invited his customers to sit.","\"Don’t worry, Mister Haug. Accidents happen.\" Ryla’s smile hit his heart with the intensity of a Silverwing’s Annihilation at point-blank. \"Thank you for your hospitality. I hope that Garrik didn’t bother you too much.\"","\"Not at all.\" Haug seemed calm and confident, but that was just his bartender routine. \"He’s a good kid, and all customers are welcome here.\"","He was actually sweating bullets.","\"You were right, baby. This is delicious.\" Ryla tucked her long hair behind her ear and sipped her drink, making Haug’s heart skip several beats. \"Can we have more?\"","\"Yes, but I recommend waiting until after lunch, or it will spoil your appetite.\" He replied.","\"Can we eat here, Mom?\" Garrik pulled at her dress, making it stick to her skin and emphasizing the gentle slopes of her chest. \"I’ve never been in a restaurant before.\"","\"Can we?\" She asked, and Haug needed sheer willpower to maintain eye contact.","\"Anytime you want.\" He gave them a deep bow to have respite from that torture. \"Is there anything else I can do for you?\"","\"Can you give me a tour of this place, mister?\" Garrik asked.","\"With pleasure.\" Haug walked in front of the Fomors, careful never to turn around for more than one second, and pointed out the various enchantments of the Tavern.","He even brought them to the kitchens, his hallowed grounds where no client had ever gone before. As soon as mother and son left the establishment, Haug sighed in relief and bolted out to look for a friendly ear.","\"Be honest with me, Vannir, do you believe in love at first sight?\" He asked with a quivering voice and a spirited gaze that unsettled the cook.","\"Look, Haug, we’ve known for years, so this pick-up line is even lamer than it usually is. I’m flattered by your feelings, but I don’t swing that way. I like women, as I thought you-\"","\"Not you, you moron!\" Haug snarled in outrage. \"How could I fall for an ugly mug like yours? That’s a face only a mother could love. You know what? Scratch that, I’ll go straight to the source!\"","He bolted away, leaving Vannir as flabbergasted as he was offended.","\"First, I’ve undergone body refining from a young age. I’m a handsome man by any standard, you old fart!\" The cook yelled to appease his wounded ego. \"Second, even if I liked men, I’m way out of your league!\"","\"There you are, Morok.\" Haug hadn’t listened to a word of Vannir’s rant, nor would he care about it if he did. \"Please, don’t take this the wrong way, but I need to ask. Is Ryla single and available?\"","\"Single she’s single, and she’s not seeing anyone either.\" The usually carefree Tyrant turned serious, but Haug didn’t notice. \"Why do you ask?\"","\"I’ll be honest with you.\" Haug sighed. \"I just met her, but I can’t stop thinking about her. I want to ask her out. With your permission, of course.\"","\"Let me be equally honest, Haug.\" Morok nodded. \"I like you, but Ryla is the mother of my little brother, and she’s family to me. I need to know of your intentions before giving you my answer.\"","\"My intentions?\" Haug asked in confusion. \"Isn’t that too much for a first date?\"","\"No.\" The Tyrant shook his head. \"You see, Ryla never had a date, and I don’t want you to take advantage of her naivety unknowingly.\"","\"She never dated?\" Haug was flabbergasted. \"What about Garrik?\"","\"Glemos, cursed be his name, did the bare minimum to breed with her, if you catch my drift.\" Morok replied.","\"Good gods!\" The bartender went pale, blood draining from all over his body.","\"Exactly.\" Morok nodded. \"She has that trauma to start with. Also, she never kissed anyone, let alone performed anything more intimate. The only things she knows about couples are what she sees us doing.\"","\"I’m sorry. I didn’t know. I’d never thought-\"","\"Calm down. I’m not saying you can’t ask her out.\" Morok raised his hand with his palm out, cutting Haug short. \"I’m not her jailer. Ryla is free to do what she wants. Yet I’d like you to think of me as her older brother.\"","The Tyrant’s eyes narrowed.","\"If you think to have your fun with her and then dump her, know that my hammers will have a completely different kind of fun with you. When I’m done, I’ll dump you in a ditch and pray the Great Mother someone kills you before you regain your consciousness. Did I make myself clear?\"","\"Crystal.\" The bartender swallowed hard, knowing the former Ranger’s reputation of being a man of his word.","\"If you still want to ask Ryla out, do it. Just remember that she can’t set foot outside a mana geyser without shortening her lifespan.\" Morok said. \"Her natural life force is still that of a fallen Balor, you know?\"","\"Yes, I remember what you told me about her and your wife’s research to cure Ryla and Garrik.\" Haug nodded.","\"Then we have nothing else to say.\" Morok walked away, leaving the bartender with his thoughts.","***","Griffon Kingdom, Remana Region, City of Deshia, at the same time.","Lith emerged from the Warp Gate of the local branch of the Association with Kamila at his side and the babies in the stroller before him.","Mages and clerks stood at attention, having a hard time believing the Supreme Magus of the Kingdom was there despite having read his identification rune in advance.","\"Yes, it’s a pleasure to meet you all. No, there is no ongoing crisis.\" Lith answered the mages’ questions before they could ask. \"Also, no. I don’t want to be disturbed. I’m on a family trip, so please turn down the invitations of every noble who learns of my presence in Deshia. Bye!\"","He walked out the door in long strides without waiting for a reply.","\"That was smooth.\" Kamila chuckled. \"Where are we, by the way?\"","\"Kami, kids, welcome to Deshia.\" Lith waved at the buildings around them. \"It’s a middle-sized city famous for its cooking tradition and surrounded by a lush forest filled with natural wonders.","\"There won’t be tourists until spring, so we should have the place all for ourselves. Before you ask, yes, there are a few museums, but I didn’t hire a guide this time. I’ll do the honors as usual.\"","His expression saddened at Elfiam’s memory, and Kamila remained silent to respect his feelings.","\"You have always been an amazing host. I’m sure this time will be no different.\" She said once he raised his eyes to look at her. \"Any particular reason you’ve chosen this city?\"","\"You’ll see.\" Lith stopped a stagecoach and told the driver to go to the Dryad’s Garden, one of the best hotels in Deshia.","\"Magus Verhen! I can’t believe you’re really here.\" Anxil, the concierge, quivered from toe to mustache in excitement. \"Welcome to our humble establishment. Miladies. Milords\"","He gave Kamila a deep bow and then another to the babies, who giggled at the unexpected treatment.","\"I’ve just come to check in, take our keys, and give the little imps a tour of the place. Is that a problem?\" Lith asked."]},{"number":4485,"title":"Chapter 4485 Somewhere to Belong (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Of course, not, Magus Verhen. Make yourself at home. We are at your service.\" The concierge pridefully gestured at the enchanted crystal chandeliers on the ceiling, the white, polished marble floor, and the refined tables and chairs of the Dryad’s Garden.","Every piece of furniture had been crafted by a skilled artisan from solid cherrywood and polished to the point it gleamed like a gemstone.","Anxil guided the Verhens to the reception desk for check-in and then to the restaurant area and the internal garden. The establishment owed its name to the vibrant flowers and colorful plants that decorated every corner and the hanging gardens on each of its five floors.","They were a feast for the guests’ eyes and noses. Delicate scents of the different flower species that bloomed and closed at different hours of the day wafted through the air.","\"Gods, this is beautiful!\" Kamila stared in amazement at the open aviaries filled with food that drew wildfowl from the local woods.","Winter was hard on animals and humans alike, and many birds came to the Dryad’s Garden for shelter, challenging the mysteries of the unknown yet friendly environment rather than starving or enduring long snowstorms.","After a while, most grew accustomed to humans and let them approach the aviaries. A few brave birds even flew onto the tables and chirruped in exchange for breadcrumbs.","\"Thanks.\" Anxil and Lith said in unison.","The concierge cowered under Lith’s glare and took a few steps back, giving the couple some privacy.","\"I remember how much you love flowers, Kami. You and Zin always planned to visit natural parks back when we lived in Belius. Since you never got the time for that because of your work and my messy life, I thought it was time to fulfill your wish.\"","\"I can’t believe you still remember that.\" Public displays of affection were frowned upon, but she kissed him anyway.","\"What can I say. The rumors about my Lich-like memory have been wildly exaggerated.\" Lith chuckled. \"Do you want to see our room next?\"","\"Depends. Is it romantic?\" She asked.","\"Yes. Why?\"","\"Because I don’t want these little imps to mess it up or to associate them with our... recreational activities.\" Kamila said, making the babies lower their gaze. \"Is there something else you want to show me here?\"","\"No.\" A snap of Lith’s fingers Warped them to the entrance, where the stagecoach waited for them. \"The city gates, please. East entrance for the Rozken Woods, thank you.\"","They could have flown to their destination, but Lith wanted Kamila to enjoy her stay and the sights the city offered. Not jump from one point to another to check something off their list of activities.","Once they reached the city gates, Lith paid the coachman and led his family into the woods. Everything was quiet and covered in snow, which made Rozken not so different from Trawn.","\"Fair warning, if someone is going to jump out of the trees, I’ll scream first and then fry their and your ass.\" Kamila said after they had walked deep enough in the woods not to see Deshia anymore.","\"Nothing of sorts.\" Lith opened the babies’ straps and set them free. \"Go and have some fun. You can shapeshift all you want. All of you.\"","Lith said while looking at Valeron the Second.","\"Only one thing. You’re the older brother, Val, so I’m entrusting Ral to you. Okay?\" He asked.","\"Okay.\" Valeron nodded with a smile as wide as Elysia’s frown was deep.","\"Ba!\" She grunted. \"Me sis! Wa mi bodder ’oo!\"","\"Indeed, but you are not big or strong enough to help Ral if he struggles.\" Lith said. \"Val can.\"","Elysia shapeshifted into her Tiamat form, snorting big puffs of black smoke in reply before taking off. Valeron and Raldarak shapeshifted as well, but the small Tiamat was afraid of leaving his parents’ side and refused to move.","\"Come on, Ral.\" Valeron caressed his younger brother’s muzzle, activating the Dragon Scales’ emotional link. \"Do you trust me?\"","Raldarak looked at Valeron and then at their parents, who nodded in approval. The baby boy tried to fly, but his movements were too awkward and his wings small.","\"You can do it.\" Valeron infused himself with a spark of Life Maelstrom, becoming strong enough to lift Raldarak off the ground.","The baby Tiamat flapped his wings in an attempt not to be a burden as his brother slowly rose into the air. Raldarak felt Valeron’s strength and trust through the Dragon Scales, and conquered his fears.","His instinct did the rest, triggering fire, air, and water fusion.","His wings now moved faster, and each flap was stronger and finely coordinated. Raldarak followed his brother’s lead as they slowly circled above their parents’ heads, and he didn’t even notice when Valeron let him go.","\"Gods, Ral! You did it! You’re flying on your own! This is your first flight!\" Kamila jumped with joy as she took countless pictures and a video with her amulet.","Raldarak looked up and noticed Valeron was still close, but wasn’t holding him. The baby Tiamat’s wings froze in fright, but before he could plunge like a brick, the small Bahamut caught him on the fly.","\"Great job, Val.\" Lith floated to caress his sons’ heads. \"Don’t be scared, Ral. You’ve done it once. You can do it again.\"","The baby Tiamat nodded and flapped his wings with renewed vigor and confidence. He wasn’t afraid of falling anymore. Even if that happened, his older brother would rescue him again.","\"Ba!\" Elysia sighed. \"Me ba. Ba sis.\"","\"Don’t beat yourself up, baby girl.\" Lith caressed her with the Dragon Scales. \"You’re a good sister. You’re just not perfect. Nobody is. Though if you learn from your mistakes, you’ll get better.\"","\"Dya!\" Elysia nodded and joined her brothers in a triangle formation with Raldarak on point, focusing more on having fun with the others than showing off her speed.","\"This is very cute, but I feel there’s something more to it.\" Kamila said while snapping more pictures.","\"I thought about this for a while.\" Lith sighed. \"Wherever we go, Val is the only one who can never be himself. He can’t shapeshift, breathe fire, or even show his powers to hide the fact that he is Thrud’s son.","\"It constantly reminds Val that he doesn’t carry our blood, Kami.\" Lith turned to look her in the eyes. \"It keeps him from taking what happened to his parents off his mind, and it’s robbing him of his childhood.","\"While Ely and Ral are carefree and tap into their powers because they can listen to the song of their life forces, Val is always worried about not blowing his cover, always thinking ahead. He’s me, Kami, and I don’t want this for him.","\"I want him to have a better childhood than mine. I want him to remember more than a list of chores when he recalls the time he spent with us. If I can’t do that, I’ll have failed as a father.\"","\"You are a great father, Lith.\" Kamila threaded her fingers into his, aware of how painful his life as Derek McCoy had been. \"I’m lucky to have you, and so are the kids. I don’t remember the last time I saw Val smile and laugh so much.\""]},{"number":4486,"title":"Chapter 4486 Somewhere to Belong (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The small Divine Beasts flew as fast as Raldarak could, taking sharp turns around the trees and chasing any birds or small critters unlucky enough to catch their attention.","\"He’s always so serious that I was starting to forget he’s actually a small child. You didn’t. You never stopped looking for a way to make him happy until you found it. I’m proud of you, Lith.","\"It takes a lot of strength to break the cycle, and even more to be the parent you never had. I don’t mind spending half of our date in the woods if it means making our little boy happy.\"","\"Thank you, Kami.\" Lith nodded.","The babies kept flying and chasing each other for a while, but they were still young and weak. Raldarak was the first to come down to his parents, huffing in exhaustion and sweating bullets as soon as he returned to his human form.","\"Da.\" He said, plopping in Lith’s arms. \"Da.\"","\"Da?\" Kamila echoed. \"Why didn’t he call you Dya? It’s perfectly normal for him not to be able to say dada yet.\"","\"Da means tired.\" Lith chuckled. \"Ral is telling us he wants to rest.\"","\"And why did he come to you?\" Kamila couldn’t help but feel jealous.","\"Because according to him, Mommy is a little slow on the uptake, whereas Daddy is quick to understand.\" He smirked.","\"And I suppose you didn’t bother explaining to Ral that Mommy has no fault for not having Dragon Scales, did you?\" She pouted.","\"No. It didn’t seem necessary.\" Lith’s answer made Kamila snort, but she remained calm for the babies. \"Come on, little fella, you need a bath.\"","A wave of Lith’s hand conjured the most pristine snow around them in a perfect floating sphere the size of a basin, which quickly melted into clear, steaming water. Raldarak struggled to keep his Voidwalker armor and avoid his bath.","Once Lith shoved him in the bubble, however, Raldarak giggled and happily splashed around. The water was warm, and the sticky, unpleasant feeling from the sweat was gone. Lith was washing Raldarak’s hair when he noticed Kamila staring at him with a fiery gaze.","\"What? Are you still angry because of the Dragon Scales thing?\" He asked.","\"No, it’s just that you look very hot right now.\" She replied, biting her lower lip.","\"Because I’m giving Ral a bath?\" Lith furrowed his brow.","\"Yes. You look like the kind of man I could give another child or ten.\" Kamila nodded, her voice sultry.","The couple hadn’t done more than hugs and soft kisses since the day Raldarak was born. Between Kamila’s magical practice and Lith’s Forgemastering experiments, they didn’t have much time together, and constantly changing Raldarak’s and Elyisa’s diapers at night killed their libido.","Right now, however, Lith could tell that his wife was about to reach the boiling point.","’I hate myself for this, but I can’t risk things going any further and the children remembering this in the future.’ Lith inwardly whined.","\"And you look like the mother I’d want for my children.\" He said to ensure Kamila understood he wasn’t rejecting her. \"About that, do you mind drying Ral off? I have to take care of another client.\"","Elysia had tried to keep up with Valeron, refusing to give up first, but the one-year and one-core-level difference was too much. She came down stumbling; her flight became more irregular as she got closer to Lith.","\"Mama!\" Raldarak happily said the moment Lith handed him to Kamila. \"Mama! Mama!\"","The disappointment she felt at the spoiled romantic mood popped like a balloon in front of her son’s happy smile as he begged her to hold him.","\"My sweet baby!\" She dabbed him with a warm cloth and peppered his head with kisses, returning his affection tenfold. \"Come here. Mommy loves you so much!\"","Raldarak giggled as Kamila cleaned his little feet and toes, falling asleep in her arms as soon as she put his enchanted clothes back on.","\"Tade.\" Elysia said. \"Bad.\"","\"Of course, a hot bath incoming for the little lady here.\" Lith said, using three eyes on Elysia and the other four to keep watch on Valeron.","The baby boy returned as soon as Elysia was done bathing. Flying alone was nice, but flying with his siblings was much better. Valeron was tired of being alone.","\"I’m sweaty.\" He tugged Lith’s arm. \"Bath?\"","Valeron didn’t know if he was too old to receive his siblings’ same treatment, so his little face lit up with joy when Lith said:","\"You bet.\" And prepared another for Valeron while Kamila dried Elysia off.","\"I’m hungry.\" Valeron didn’t splash, but he was no less happy than Raldarak, feeling like he finally belonged.","\"Me doo!\" Elysia raised her hand as if it was a quiz. \"Hungy!\"","\"In a second.\" Lith finished washing and drying Valeron before taking the food out of his pocket dimension.","Raldarak woke up immediately and cried, demanding his share.","\"Let’s feed the kids and then have our picnic.\" Kamila said with a radiant smile.","\"What picnic?\" Lith asked. \"Don’t tell me you prepared food for today.\"","\"No, but seeing how things are going, it seems the natural development of our date.\" She replied.","\"In spring, maybe.\" Lith shrugged. \"Not right now, though. The woods are too bare and silent.\"","\"What about the kids?\" She asked.","\"We leave them to Mom until the afternoon.\" Lith pointed at the snoring group of babies. \"I tired them out so that we have the rest of the morning for ourselves. They won’t even notice our absence for a few hours.\"","Kamila checked her clock and noticed that barely an hour and a half had passed since their arrival.","\"Gods, you’re an evil genius. That’s why I married you.\" She chuckled.","A quick Warp brought them back to the local branch of the Association, and from there the Gate took the babies back to the Mansion.","\"Have fun. I’ll contact you as soon as they wake up.\" Elina said with a smile while pushing the stroller with the babies away. \"Dear, when are we going to have a date as well?\"","\"Soon. I swear!\" Raaz gasped, knowing he was cornered.","\"What about now?\" Kamila asked.","\"Your beloved museums await us.\" Lith sighed.","\"What do you have against them?\" She chuckled.","\"They are boring, and you know it.\" Lith replied. \"Yet we didn’t come here to argue. We came to Deshia to have fun, and now it’s your turn.\"","He brought Kamila to the biggest museum in the city and used the time they had left before lunch to visit all the sites of historical relevance with her. Thanks to Soluspedia, Lith could explain every piece of art like a skilled tourist guide.","He always added his personal spin here and there, even at the cost of stretching the truth, to avoid sounding like a textbook and making the experience more enjoyable.","\"Thank you.\" Kamila said as they sat in the Dryad’s Garden restaurant after the tour. \"I know you have no interest in art, but I had lots of fun with you today.\"","They had both changed into more formal and elegant day clothes, but nothing too flashy. They looked like any other noble couple that was staying at the hotel."]},{"number":4487,"title":"Chapter 4487 Life Score (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"I’m glad to hear it.\" Lith gestured to one of the waiters, and he brought a large vase holding a composition of Moonroses.","They were flowers that grew in Verendi. Snow-white roses that had large, flat petals arranged in an almost perfect circle. They also matched Kamila’s moon pendant and had become her favorite flowers ever since Lith had gifted her the first bouquet of Moonroses.","\"Thank you! They are beautiful!\" She squealed in joy like a little girl, drawing the attention and envy of many noble dames who had never seen flowers like that.","\"Yeah, but I’m looking at someone much more beautiful right now.\" Lith said while staring Kamila in the eyes with an intensity that made her melt.","The meal was delicious, and Lith ordered only local specialties to immerse himself in Deshia’s tradition in a way he could enjoy and try new flavors. It turned out that the ancient Deshian’s love for spicy meat dishes matched Lith’s.","\"This is delicious.\" Lith nursed his red wine. \"Don’t you like it? You’re eating a bit faster than usual.\"","\"It’s really good.\" Kamila replied to reassure him. \"I’m in a bit of a hurry because I hope we can have a bit of time for ourselves before the kids wake up.\"","She gave him a flirty wink that made Lith reconsider ordering the dessert.","\"We’ll take it in our room.\" Lith’s husky voice was charged with expectation.","The couple had just closed the door and started kissing passionately when the communication amulets drew their consciousness.","\"It’s Elina!\" Kamila said. \"Answer it. Something might have happened.\"","\"I’m sorry to bother you.\" Elina sighed. \"The babies just woke up and want to see you at all costs. I tried to calm Ral down, but nothing worked.\"","\"Don’t worry, Mom.\" Lith sighed harder. \"We’ll be there in a minute.\"","\"Why not make it ten?\" Kamila wrapped her arms around his neck.","\"Really? Are you still in the mood knowing our kids are crying?\" Lith replied.","\"No.\" She admitted, lowering her eyes in shame. \"I just didn’t want you to-\"","\"And I appreciate that.\" Lith put his finger on her lips. \"We’ll make up for this tonight. Thank the gods Ral can already sleep the whole night and never wakes up when he’s tired.\"","When Lith and Kamila stepped through the Warp Gate in the Mansion, the children welcomed them as if they hadn’t seen their parents in weeks rather than the few minutes since they had woken up.","\"It’s alright, sweetie.\" Kamila gently caressed Raldarak to soothe his desperate cries. \"We’re here now. Everything is fine.\"","\"So’y!\" Elysia nodded, ashamed to have failed to placate her little brother. \"He dad.\"","\"She means sad.\" Lith translated for Kamila.","\"I noticed.\" She rocked the baby in her arms until he calmed down. \"What’s next? More woods?\"","\"Sort of.\" Lith led her to the keep of the Mansion, where the tower was hidden in plain sight. \"I’ll call you for the ride back home, Solus. Keep an eye on everyone for me.\"","\"I will.\" She said. \"Gods, I miss these little imps already.\"","\"I miss you too.\" Valeron hugged Solus, making her almost burst into tears.","\"Don’t worry, sweetie.\" She sniffled. \"I was joking. Don’t worry about me. Go and have fun.\"","Much to Kamila’s surprise and Raldarak’s wonder, the tower brought them to Mogar’s Garden. Lith checked the surroundings with the Watchtower, ensuring they were alone and nothing would threaten his family.","\"Not to complain, but why are we here again?\" Kamila said as the tower Warped back to the Mansion.","\"Ral has never been at the Garden of Mogar.\" Lith replied. \"Also, it’s filled with the luscious green you like so much, is warm and nice, and is the place where Val accepted his Camellia branch. This place is special for him and us.\"","Valeron became excited the moment he recognized the place. The Garden of Mogar was where he had officially become part of the Verhen family. Not because of a piece of paper or a silent agreement between adults, but because he wanted to.","He ran to the nearest bush of flowers, sniffing their petals and enjoying the good memories that the Garden evoked in him.","\"Don’t go too far away, Val.\" Kamila said while nodding at Lith with a smile. \"Stay where we can see you.\"","\"Yes, Mom!\" Valeron smiled back and gestured for Elysia and Raldarak to follow him.","The younger kids had to shapeshift into their Divine Beast forms; their stumpy human legs and weak bodies were unable to keep up with their older brother. Lith and Kamila took a stroll, following the kids at a relaxed pace.","Lith showed her all the exotic, beautiful flowers the Garden had to offer and warned her against the poisonous species and dangerous magical plants.","\"What about the kids? Isn’t this dangerous for them?\" Kamila asked.","\"They have Origin Flames.\" Lith shrugged. \"Also, they take after me and hate their greens.\"","\"Gods, that’s so true.\" Kamila chuckled. \"You should lead by example and eat more vegetables. Not now, of course.\"","\"Don’t push your luck, woman!\" Lith replied as if she had offended his entire bloodline, making her chuckle harder. \"I descend from noble Dragons, not fluffy rabbits!\"","Soon the kids got tired of walking and took to the skies. They explored the plants growing along the dome of the Garden and the ruins of Maergron’s lab under their parents’ strict supervision.","Then, Lith brought his family to a small, shallow stream of clear water surrounded by a large patch of silvery sand. It was akin to a small beach, and the water was so low it barely reached Raldarak’s waist.","The kids had fun playing in the water, building weird puppets in the sand with earth magic, and having mock battles with water magic.","\"Seriously, how did you know how to find so many family-friendly spots?\" Kamila asked as she let the gentle flow of water wash over her bare feet. \"I didn’t even notice one of these places the last time we came here.\"","\"I cheat.\" Lith conjured a hologram of the information the Watchtower had gathered. \"I studied the Garden beforehand and found the safest areas we could visit with the kids. I prepared this date for them as much as for us.\"","\"This is just amazing!\" Kamila replied, giving him a sweet kiss. \"You are amazing, Lith.\"","Valeron and Elysia played to their heart’s content, even tussling a bit in their Divine Beasts’ form. When Raldarak’s turn came, however, the small Tiamat had eyes so big and a smile so bright that when he opened his arms in a fighting stance, he seemed to be asking for a hug.","And that was exactly what Elysia did. She hugged her little brother, and when he tried to trip her down, she let him.","\"Yoo win. Yoo doo song.\" Even the idea of hurting Raldarak by mistake was too painful for her to bear.","Elysia’s wounded pride didn’t matter if it meant keeping her little brother safe.","\"Li! Li!\" Raldarak licked her snout, and Elysia started to cry. \"Li!\"","\"What’s happening? She can’t have gotten hurt so easily.\" Kamila turned around, noticing that Lith’s eyes were veiled with tears."]},{"number":4488,"title":"Chapter 4488 Life Score (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Ral just called her name.\" He replied, letting emotion transpire from his voice. \"Li is how he can say Ely at the moment. It’s his third word and the reason Ely is crying with joy.\"","\"Oh, gods, you should have told me sooner.\" Kamila tried to record the moment with her amulet, but she fumbled it and wept as silently as she could so she wouldn’t ruin it.","\"Don’t cry, Mom.\" Valeron didn’t understand what was happening, and seeing so many members of his family tearing up scared him.","\"It’s okay, baby.\" Kamila sniffled. \"I’m fine. I swear.\"","Yet Valeron could tell she wasn’t fine. Everybody seemed sad, and their eyes were moist.","\"Don’t cry. Please.\" Valeron felt something stirring inside of him, an intense desire to protect those around him.","His life force and mana core surged, his mind growing attuned to the Garden’s immense energy. It was a subtle feeling; the baby boy was too young and weak to manifest the full scope of his powers, but Lith felt it.","He called upon Solus, and the tower appeared in a nearby glade a split second later.","Valeron didn’t notice it. He was too focused on trying to make the pain and sadness of his loved ones go away. His fingers dug into the ground as he listened to the melody of the world energy around him and added a few notes of his own making.","Valeron was the son of Jormun, the Emerald Dragon, and Thrud, the Golden Griffon. The powers he inherited from his father allowed him to naturally understand and interact with all forms of life, while his mother’s Life Maelstrom was meant to nurture.","The young Bahamut answered the call of a dying seed, too weak to bloom on its own due to a congenital defect. The seed wanted to live, and Valeron needed help. The boy extended his aura, wrapping it around the seed’s life force to examine its symphony.","It was akin to a torn, crumpled musical score. The melody was punctuated with faded and missing notes, making it impossible for the seed to thrive even in the fertile soil of Mogar’s Garden.","The little Bahamut used his Emerald Dragon side to restore the faded notes and guess half the missing notes by studying the flow of the tunes preceding and following them.","The other half of the missing notes, however, was beyond even an Emerald Dragon. Yet not beyond a Bahamut.","Valeron the Second opened his life force to the dying seed and let them interact. New notes that perfectly suited the incomplete melodies came to his mind, and he engraved them in the Life Score.","The symphony of the seed’s life force was now complete, opening a path toward life in the dark corner where death awaited. Alas, one problem remained.","The seed was already withering after depleting the nutrients in its coat and couldn’t absorb more from its surroundings. Valeron injected a tiny spark of his Emerald Energy and another of Life Maelstrom into the seed.","Life nurtured life, and the silver lightning gave the dying seed the strength to sate its hunger. All that Lith and Kamila saw, however, was a seedling sprouting in the middle of a small pillar of light between Valeron’s hands.","The seedling grew at a speed visible to the naked eye, its stem stretching until it was centimeters away from the young boy’s face. A bud emerged from the stem and bloomed a heartbeat later into a beautiful flower like no other.","The stem had no thorns, and like its leaves, it shone with the vibrant emerald of a precious gemstone. It was crowned with a rose comprised of Indech-red petals alternating with silver ones that reflected the cave’s mystical lights like polished metal.","\"Don’t cry, Mom.\" Valeron dug out the flower along with enough soil to preserve its roots and offered it to Kamila with shuffling steps, trying not to stumble and fall. \"Please. Don’t be sad.\"","The young boy felt tired. More tired than after flying with his siblings in the morning, but something inside of him told him what he had done was worth the effort. That everything would be okay.","\"I’m not sad.\" Kamila sniffled. \"Not anymore. Thank you, sweetie. It’s a beautiful flower. What is it?\"","\"It’s for you.\" Valeron stared at her with his big round eyes in a silent plea to accept and like his gift.","\"I know that, silly boy.\" She chuckled, kissing his forehead before taking the soil and flower from his hands. \"I was asking you what its name is.\"","\"I don’t know.\" Valeron smiled. \"But it’s pretty, right?\"","\"The prettiest flower I’ve ever seen.\" Kamila gently caressed his hair. \"I’m so sorry, sweetie. I didn’t mean to make you worry.\"","\"It’s okay, Mom.\" Valeron saw her smile and sighed in relief.","He hugged Kamila tight and fell asleep with a peaceful expression on his face.","\"Wha!\" Elysia bolted to him as soon as the pretty lights stopped distracting her, quickly followed by Raldarak.","She sniffed her brother, relaxing as soon as she sensed that he was well and happy via the Dragon Scales. Raldarak squeaked loudly to wake Valeron, and when that failed, he joined him in their mother’s arms.","\"Okay, let’s stay calm.\" Kamila took deep breaths to keep her voice low and steady. \"What in the gods’ names just happened?\"","\"I have no idea, but it’s something related to Val’s bloodline.\" Lith replied. \"I called Solus here because between the Mana Injector, the Watchtower, and the Greenhouse, we should have a recording of what he did and how.","\"We need to know if it’s just some simple trick or something that might endanger his life if used on something bigger than a flower.\"","\"Good thinking.\" Kamila nodded. \"Unlike Ely and Ral, there’s nobody who can teach Val how to use his powers. He needs all the help we can give him.\"","\"Please, be okay. Please!\" Solus emerged from the tower and sprinted to reach Valeron.","She had checked the Infirmary’s readings thrice, and knew the little boy was fine, but her heart refused to believe it until her own Invigoration confirmed it.","\"Thank the gods Val’s okay.\" Solus sighed in relief.","\"Ack!\" Elysia dropped to the ground in a silly impression of a stroke to receive some attention as well.","The fact that she let herself fall slowly and kept an eye open to check her audience’s reaction ruined her performance.","\"I’m sorry, baby girl. Are you okay?\" Lith picked her up in mock worry.","\"Yah!\" Elysia sprang back to life, nodding excitedly.","\"Good girl.\" Lith ruffled her hair. \"What happened, Solus? What did Val just do?\"","\"Oh.\" It took her a couple of seconds to snap out of her worry and remember the reason she had rushed to the Garden of Mogar in the first place. \"You won’t believe it, guys.\"","\"What’s not to believe?\" Lith asked. \"Making a flower bloom is nothing much. I can do that as well. I’m asking you why he got so tired just from doing that.\"","\"I know, and you won’t believe my answer.\" Solus replied. \"Valeron didn’t make the flower bloom.\"","\"Are you sure about that?\" Kamila looked at the flower, and then at Solus as if she had gone insane. \"Seems bloomed to me.\""]},{"number":4489,"title":"Chapter 4489 A Small Miracle (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Yes, I know that is a flower in full bloom.\" Solus said. \"Yet as Lith said, there’s nothing amazing about that. What’s amazing is what Val did! That was just a rose like the thousand others in the Garden.","\"At least until Val altered its life force and shared a bit of his own with it.\" Then she noticed the confused expression on Lith’s and Kamila’s faces and rushed to add. \"Don’t you get it? The change is permanent.\"","\"You mean that Val used something akin to Body Sculpting to alter the flower’s colors permanently?\" Kamila asked.","\"No, I’m saying that Val created a new species of flowers!\" Solus replied. \"According to the tower, that flower is perfectly stable, and if we plant it in the Greenhouse or even at the farm, it will produce more that will look exactly like the one you hold in your hands, Kami!\"","\"Good gods!\" Lith rubbed his chin, narrowing his eyes in amazement.","\"I see that you two are really impressed, but I still don’t get it. What am I missing?\" Kamila turned from Lith to Solus in confusion.","\"This is huge, Kami.\" Lith pondered for a second, racking his brain for the most fitting example. \"Let’s say that you want to give wings to a cat. It’s a massive task that involves countless nerve endings and just as many potential issues.","\"The body needs to recognize the wings, and the brain needs to have a direct connection with them to exert fine control over the wings, but this is just the beginning. To keep things simple, let’s say that you’ve done a perfect job.","\"After countless hours of trial-and-error, Body Sculpting worked exactly as you intended. The cat can fly, and you’ve taken every precaution to avoid side effects to its metabolism or quality of life.","\"Even if you accomplished such an unimaginably difficult procedure, it wouldn’t guarantee that the cat’s offspring will be so lucky.","\"When you perform a change of that magnitude on someone’s life force, the only thing you can be sure of is that the mutation will be stable and functional only for the first subject, and only because you fine-tuned every single aspect of its life force.","\"Once the cat mates, however, the wings could make the pregnancy impossible to come to term or kill the mother altogether. Even if the kittens are born, they might be subject to severe mutations","\"The kittens might be born with atrophied wings or have no wings at all because the life force they inherited from the other parent perceives the alterations you made as unnatural and rejects them as the kittens develop in the womb.","\"What Valeron did wasn’t just graft wings onto a cat. He created a winged cat that can fly and whose descendants will inherit its wings and stable life force. In other words, Val just created a new form of life.","\"He didn’t do it in the safety of a lab or with any preparations, but in a few seconds and in front of our eyes.\"","\"Are you serious?\" Kamila stared at the flower in her hands, her eyes widening in awe.","\"He is.\" Solus nodded. \"If until a minute ago there were a million species of flowers, now there is a million plus one. The ramifications of what Val could do on more complex creatures are enormous.","\"And don’t get me started on what might happen if that flower evolves into a Dryad or another plant folk!\"","\"Good gods!\" Kamila stared at the nameless flower, almost expecting it could open a hidden mouth and bite her face off. \"What do we do?\"","\"The only thing we can.\" Lith took the flower from Kamila and handed it to Solus. \"Solus, please move the flower to the Greenhouse. I’m not letting Val’s gift to Kami die.\"","\"You don’t have to worry about that.\" Solus Blinked away, and when she returned, the flower was gone. \"The tower recorded everything about the flower’s development process and studied its properties.","\"According to the preliminary analysis, Val’s flower is just a flower. It requires no special conditions to grow. Just fertile soil, water, and plenty of sunlight. By the way, am I the only one who noticed?\"","\"Noticed what?\" Lith asked.","\"The flower is emerald like Val’s Emerald Dragon side, silver like his Griffon side, and red like... well, his human life force or Indech side, assuming he’ll develop it as he grows up. Isn’t it a weird coincidence?\"","\"The only coincidence is the flower being red in its natural state.\" Lith shook his head. \"The emerald comes from the life force Val shared with the flower, and the silver from the Life Maelstrom. Nothing more.\"","\"Yeah, right.\" Solus snorted. \"And instead of mixing together, those energies were so nice they split themselves and occupied different parts of the flower without producing a single smudge of color? It’s all too perfect to be a coincidence.\"","She conjured a hologram displaying how the silver petals showed no sign of red, just like the red petals showed no trace of silver or emerald.","\"She’s right.\" Kamila nodded. \"But what Lith says also makes sense. Val is just a baby and has no Indech side. That’s for sure.\"","\"Fine. We’ll settle this on another date. On a more pressing matter, do you have any ideas how to call it?\" Solus asked.","\"It’s not up to us.\" Kamila shook her head. \"Val should be the one to name his own creation. Speak of the little imp...\"","The young boy stirred with a big yawn. The tower and the ocean of world energy swirling across Mogar’s Garden had restored his strength after a short nap.","\"Mom?\" Valeron stared at Kamila in confusion until he remembered what had happened. \"Where is the flower?\"","He looked around, noticing his siblings snuggled up to him but finding no trace of his gift.","\"In the Greenhouse.\" Kamila activated the Warp Mirror and moved everyone inside the tower. \"There it is. See?\"","\"Yay!\" Valeron screamed with joy as he noticed Solus had made plenty of space around his flower so that more could grow.","He knelt and touched its stem, checking that the flower was okay and that he had made no mistake in fixing its life force.","\"Thank you for the beautiful gift, Val.\" Kamila sat next to him. \"I have only one question. How do we want to call it? Something so special can’t just be ’a flower’, no?\"","\"No!\" Elysia nodded.","\"Mama!\" Raldarak joined her.","Valeron thought long and hard about the issue, treating it like the most important decision of his two-year-long life.","\"Dad?\" Valeron asked.","’I would love to joke around and say that \"Dad\" sounds like a magnificent name for the flower, but Val might think I’m serious and name it after me. At that point, all the women in my family would be out for my blood.’ Lith inwardly sighed.","\"Yes, son?\" He actually said.","\"Is that real?\" Valeron pointed at the enchanted Camellia Kamila carried on her breast pocket. \"Does it exist?\"","\"No. I made that up.\" Lith replied. \"No such flower exists on Mogar.\"","\"Can I call it camellia, then? Mom’s flower?\" Valeron asked.","Kamila hiccupped, needing sheer willpower to keep herself together. She was one whimper away from a loud cry of joy."]},{"number":4490,"title":"Chapter 4490 A Small Miracle (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"You can.\" Lith caressed the young boy’s head. \"I think it’s a perfect name. Camellia, the mom’s flower.\"","\"Thank you, thank you, thank you.\" Kamila lifted Valeron in her arms and burst into tears. \"This is the best date ever. Thank you, Val. I love you so much.\"","\"Mom?\" Valeron looked at her in worry until he realized she wasn’t in pain, just happy. \"I love you too, Mom.\"","Solus burned with envy, but she could only swallow it up and smile.","\"Can we go out to play now?\" The baby boy asked, and his siblings cheered with approval.","\"Of course.\" Lith nodded. \"I’m sorry for bothering you, Solus, and thanks for coming so quickly. You can go back home now.\"","\"No problem.\" She sighed. \"Call me again when you need a ride back home. Bye.\"","The tower disappeared, leaving everyone standing on the soft grass that covered the Garden’s cave.","\"Is it me or was she a bit... hissy?\" Kamila asked as the children went back to playing in the stream.","\"How would you feel if Val made a flower for Solus and named it after her?\" Lith snorted.","\"I... \" The thought hit her like a sack of bricks falling from a skyscraper, and a burning envy rose from her gut. \"I would probably strangle her on the spot in a fit of rage. Poor Solus.\"","\"And poor Tyris.\" Lith said. \"And Grandma. They took care of Valeron long before we entered the picture, and you can bet they’ll be hissy too. Heck, if Thrud were alive, you’d just have made a mortal enemy.","\"I wouldn’t be surprised if she came back from the grave just to bite your feet in your sleep.\"","\"Don’t say that even as a joke!\" Kamila went pale. \"I never believed in ghosts, but after seeing your Demons, the idea isn’t so far-fetched anymore.\"","\"Okay, sorry.\" Lith raised his hands in apology. \"Bottom line, limit the gloating to a minimum. Many people are going to be angry at you for this.\"","\"Why me? I didn’t do anything!\" Kamila whined.","\"Do you expect them to take it on a baby? The baby they love and who just gifted something to a person he cares about?\" Lith asked.","\"No.\" Kamila groaned. \"I’m farmed. Thoroughly and completely farmed.\"","\"Let’s not get ahead of ourselves.\" Lith grabbed her by the waist and pulled her close. \"That’s the plan for the night. We still have the entire evening ahead of us.\"","He spoke with such a serious tone and intense stare that Kamila spouted gibberish in reply, turning red up to her ears.","***","The kids ran out of steam less than an hour later, just as Lith had predicted. Valeron was still tired from his uncanny endeavor and fell asleep after an abundant meal. Elysia let her competitive spirit get the better of her and tried to one-up her older brother.","She planted her small hands in the ground and poured out all the mana she could muster. She only obtained a few blades of lush grass, but she consumed all her stamina in the process.","As for Raldarak, he just ran, flew, and dug through the dirt like the excitable baby he was, tiring himself up quickly.","Lith had prepared a picnic for everyone, but it was way too early for dinner, and the babies snored as soon as the last drop of food entered their hungry mouths.","\"Time to bring them back home.\" Lith said. \"There’s no point bringing them with us. The kids will be much more comfortable in their crib than in the stroller, and no sudden noise will disturb them.","\"Moreover, we can have some time all to ourselves and start our real date.\"","\"Don’t say that.\" Kamila tugged Lith’s sleeve to draw his attention. \"There is no real date to start. This has always been our date, and so far, it’s been amazing. I’m not just talking about the camellia, even though, even in my wildest dreams, I never expected to have a real flower named after me.","\"I mean, what you did for Val is amazing. He spent the day like a normal kid. He had lots of fun and was free to express himself like Val and Ely always do. Even if no magical flower sprouted, it would have still been a small miracle.\"","\"So, you want to keep them with us for dinner and the rest of the night?\" Lith asked in confusion.","\"Heck, no!\" Kamila replied in horror. \"It’s been months since we... since you... you know. I need some us time. Badly.\"","She cleared her throat in embarrassment, turning to a shade of purple.","\"I couldn’t agree more.\" Lith sighed. \"Let’s go home. And remember, gloat with caution.\"","The tower reappeared a second later, and Solus welcomed them with a warm smile.","\"I hope you had fun.\" She said. \"Everyone is waiting for you.\"","\"Thanks- What do you mean, everyone?\" Kamila’s question received its answer when she walked out of the tower and into the Mansion.","A firing squad of murderous glares of varying intensity seemed to bore a hole in her head.","\"Congratulations.\" Tyris stepped forward first, her kind smile reaching nowhere near her cold eyes. \"The camellia is a beautiful flower. There is no woman on Mogar who wouldn’t kill to receive such honor.\"","\"Or at least a bit of gratitude.\" Salaark’s stern gaze softened at the sight of Valeron’s sleeping figure and hardened like steel when it shifted to Kamila. \"What can I say, some people have it all, Kami, and you are among them. Congratulations.\"","Elina, Rena, Quylla, Friya, and even Tista all gave Kamila their own insincere felicitations for Valeron’s display of filial love, hiding their envy beneath plastered smiles.","\"Thank you, but I really didn’t do anything to deserve such a wonderful gift.\" Kamila felt the heat rising and opted for a cautious approach.","’On that we can agree.’ More than one woman inwardly grunted.","\"I mean, it’s all thanks to Lith. He planned this wonderful date. Without him, Val would have never tapped into his Bahamut powers so easily.\" When that failed, she resorted to the last trick in the book.","Throwing her husband under the bus.","\"Ah.\" Elina said, her voice carrying the warmth of an ice age. \"That’s true. It’s just like the magical Camellia all over.\"","\"Mom!\" Lith felt the silent accusation in his mother’s voice along with the fiery gazes of the rest of the women in the room. \"How many times do I have to say that it was just a spur-of-the-moment thing?\"","\"I guess it’s my fault, baby.\" She sighed. \"I’m sorry that carrying you in my womb for nine months and taking care of you all my life wasn’t enough to inspire such wonderful thoughts in you.","\"At least Val loves you so much that he took you as his role model even when it comes to gifts.\"","\"You’re right, Elina.\" Salaark sighed even louder. \"Clearly, we have not done enough to deserve any gratitude or display of affection from Lith.\"","Rena, Tista, and Solus nodded at those words, expressing how sorry they were for being so inadequate in their respective roles.","’We’re going to talk about this later.’ Lith grunted via a mind link.","’I’m sorry! I got scared and panicked.’ Kamila whimpered in remorse."]},{"number":4491,"title":"Chapter 4491 Moment of Silence (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Don’t talk like that, Grandma.\" Lith replied. \"Val also named the camellia as mother’s flower, so it has to be intended as dedicated to all mothers. Especially Tyris, since it carries the silver of her eyes and she’s known as the Great Mother.\"","\"That’s true.\" The Guardian said, the icebergs in her eyes thawing.","She was unaware Lith had just drawn a target on her back, and now the rest of the women were glaring at her.","\"Oh, my. Look at the time.\" Lith said. \"We really have to go, or we won’t be able to visit even one museum. Bye!\"","A snap of his fingers Blinked him and Kamila before the Warp Gate, and from there they returned to Deshia.","\"That was brilliant.\" Kamila chuckled. \"Aren’t you worried they’ll realize your trick and make you pay for it later?\"","\"They were going to make me pay for it anyway.\" Lith shrugged. \"Also, I doubt their anger will last until tomorrow. Not with Val showing off his flower to them and probably saying something adorable that will melt their hearts.","\"Something like, ’It’s as beautiful as you, Grandma’.\"","\"That would indeed get at least three women off your back.\" Kamila smiled. \"What’s our destination?\"","\"We need to distance ourselves physically and mentally from the children, or we won’t be able to enjoy our night. We’ll start with an adult, not lewd snack.\" Lith replied, making her blush and many Association clerks snicker.","\"Did you have to say that out loud?\" She whimpered. \"They’ll think I’m some kind of pervert if you had to clarify the last point!\"","\"You are a pervert, and I love you for that.\" Lith shrugged. \"We both know what you would’ve thought without enough context.\"","He brought her to a nice tea house where they enjoyed hot and cold beverages and could talk about anything without the Guardians butchering their words. The cherrywood furniture gave the establishment warmth, while the many colorful paintings gave it a refined ambiance.","Lith ordered a strong tea for himself and a rose tea with plenty of pastries on the side for Kamila. The low murmur from the adjacent tables was silence compared to the constant squeals of the children during their friendly squabbles.","\"Gods, I didn’t know how much I needed this until this moment.\" Kamila leaned back and sighed in bliss. \"I can feel my ears healing. I can hear myself thinking.\"","\"I’m glad you like it.\" Lith nodded. \"Is there anything you want to talk about now that we don’t have naïve third wheels around?\"","\"Yes.\" She nodded, enjoying the silence for a few more seconds before speaking again. \"I want to apologize for panicking and throwing you under the carriage. It was cowardly of me.\"","\"Apology accepted.\" Lith replied. \"There are few things in this world as scary as my mother, and you got two of them glaring at you.\"","\"Also, how could you say that snack thing while we were still in the Association?\" She flushed at the memory. \"That was embarrassing!\"","\"That was just me being spontaneous, Kami.\" Lith replied. \"If I have to think before being playful and flirty and wait for the right moment, it would be a chore. I didn’t say anything inappropriate. I was just teasing my wife.","\"Are we just married, or are we still in love?\" His question hit her like a punch to the gut.","\"In love!\" She slammed her fist on the table, drawing attention to her. \"Forget that I asked, but please try being more mindful of where we are in the future.\"","After two cups of tea and a bit of chit-chat in the quiet of the tea house, Kamila was ready to face the bustling commercial districts of Deshia.","\"I had enough of art and culture for today. I’d rather do some shopping than visit another museum.\" She said.","Lith spent the whole time with the Eyes of Menadion on his nose, hoping to find a mystical tome or a lost artifact in the city’s small antique shops. Alas, life rarely is so easy.","At the end of the tour, Kamila had five new hairpins, three new sets of clothes, and three pairs of shoes to match with each outfit, while Lith was lighter by several coins.","\"Did I buy too much?\" She asked. \"It’s been too long since I last went on a shopping spree, and maybe I got carried away.\"","\"Don’t worry.\" Lith dismissed the issue with a shrug. \"It’s been months since the last time we went out, and even though my stinginess can lead you to believe otherwise, I’m rich. This much is nothing. Even for me.\"","\"I know.\" She giggled. \"I didn’t want you to think I’m taking you for granted.\"","\"If you really feel that way, we should buy you this, this, and this.\" Lith picked three skin-tight cocktail dresses with short skirts and ample cleavage.","\"Lith! I wouldn’t be caught dead wearing something like that in public!\" Kamila only had to look at the dresses to turn a deep shade of purple.","\"Who said anything about wearing them in public? I was thinking more about a private show.\" He replied.","\"Well, since it’s your money, sure.\" She replied with a flirty smile.","After the inevitable purchase and storing everything inside the pocket dimension, the couple took an aerial tour of Deshia. They visited bell towers, the spires of the tallest buildings, and admired the sunset from the city walls.","The crimson light of the dying sun painted the nearby forest red, making it look as if it were burning with a cold fire. They stayed there, hand in hand, until the stars became visible and the silver light of the crescent moon illuminated the night.","\"Did you really need silence so much?\" Lith asked.","\"Gods, yes.\" Kamila replied. \"I swear, if someone so much as asks me to pass them the salt at dinner, I’m going to shove it down their throat! Present excluded, of course.\"","The city guards didn’t know whether to feel included in the dinner invitation or offended for being blatantly ignored.","The couple had been sitting in a restricted area for quite some time, but shooing someone wearing the white and golden robe of the Supreme Magus was universally considered a major blunder.","Lith and Kamila returned to the Dryad’s Garden, and he was surprised by Kamila’s plan for the night. She insisted on going back to their suite and ordering room service for dinner.","\"Leave the cart outside the door after knocking, please.\" She told the concierge.","\"Do you already know what you want to eat, or would you like to carry a menu to your room, milady?\" Anxil asked.","\"I remember it from lunch.\" She proceeded to order a full-course meal for herself and Lith. \"Did I guess your order right, or do you want to change something?\"","\"I’m speechless.\" Lith replied. \"From appetizers to dessert, you didn’t make a single mistake.\"","He had booked the Royal Suite, and Kamila took a long appreciative look at the place before changing her clothes and freshening up.","There was a bedroom almost as big as the one they had in the Mansion, a spacious bath with a hot tub and shower, a luxurious dining room, and a hobby room with books, couches, and a pool table."]},{"number":4492,"title":"Chapter 4492 Moment of Silence (Part 2)","paragraphs":["A path of red rose petals led from the entrance to the bedroom, and the bouquet of Moonroses was the centerpiece on the dinner table.","\"I thought you liked the green.\" Lith said through the bathroom door. \"I booked this place because of that. I wanted to offer you a romantic dinner surrounded by birds, flowers, and non-toddlers.\"","\"Thanks, but we already did that for lunch.\" She replied. \"Now it’s my turn to make this date special.\"","She walked out of the bathroom wearing just enough makeup to emphasize her delicate features, a bit of eyeliner, and crimson-red lipstick. She also wore her \"lucky clothes\", a black pencil skirt and a light blue shirt.","\"Far from me to criticize your choice of clothing, but that lipstick doesn’t really go well with the rest.\" Lith frowned.","\"I know.\" She giggled shyly. \"Do you know what I’m wearing?\"","\"Yes, your ’lucky clothes’. You wore them on our first date, on the day of our marriage, and you wear them for our anniversaries.\" Lith replied. \"I never understood if they’re meant to remind me I’m lucky to have you, or that I’m about to get lucky.\"","\"Both.\" She smiled as she took his hand and placed it on her chest. \"Imprint me, please.\"","\"You’re a person, Kami. How am I supposed to imprint you?\" Lith asked.","\"Don’t be so literal.\" She chuckled. \"I’m talking about my clothes.\"","Lith recognized the Voidfeather armor Salaark had gifted Kamila, but contrary to his expectations, the armor accepted his imprint.","\"What’s the meaning of this?\" He asked.","\"I simply asked Grandma to help me surprise you.\" Kamila replied with a sultry smile. \"You can now access all the clothes stored in the Voidfeather armor and modify them as you please. Give it a try.\"","Lith didn’t make her say it twice. With one thought, the shirt now had a keyhole cleavage and the skirt became scandalously short, barely covering her thighs. Then it became a crop top with hot pants, and after that a skimpy bikini.","\"That’s the spirit, but you can dress me however you want.\" She leaned closer for a sweet kiss. \"I also stored those dresses you picked for me today, and you can modify them as well.\"","\"Great Mother almighty!\" Lith rediscovered religion as the lucky clothes turned into a halter-neck crimson cocktail dress that left Kamila’s back exposed down to her waist and had a deep neckline that reached her navel.","\"See? The lipstick matches my clothes now.\" She wrapped her arms around his neck and kissed him again.","\"You know me too well, woman.\" Lith needed sheer willpower to keep his hands on her back instead of tearing the revealing dress apart and Blinking to the bedroom. \"First my food and now this.\"","\"And the best part is that I’ll wear anything you want during our private dinner. Feel free to change my outfit anytime.\" Kamila said with a sensual voice that forced him to take a deep breath to keep his rationality from shattering.","\"How...\" Lith’s voice was dry and husky, like a man who had travelled a long time in a desert with little water. \"How did you manage to prepare all this if I mentioned the ’private show’ just a few hours ago and you never left my side?\"","\"Great minds think alike.\" Kamila blushed, flattered and excited by his reaction. \"This was my plan from the beginning. I didn’t expect you to buy me new dresses, but I had my Voidfeather armor a while ago.\"","\"I hope Grandma didn’t comment on your surprise.\" Lith was a bit embarrassed by Kamila talking with Salaark about their amorous plays.","\"Are you kidding?\" Kamila giggled at the memory. \"We have a secret wardrobe, but she has an entire secret tent. Of course, she commented, but not the way you think. She showed me her collection of special clothes and told me I could take anything I wanted.\"","\"An entire tent?\" Lith was flabbergasted. \"Grandma also stretches the space inside her palace with dimensional magic, doesn’t she?\"","\"Well, she’s lived for quite a bit, and she is a Forgemaster.\" Kamila shrugged. \"Unlike me, she can create any piece she can come up with without anyone’s help. Why are we talking about her, though? Are you already bored of this? Do you want to change my outfit?\"","\"Because I’m losing my mind and there’s still no trace of our dinner.\" Lith had to avert his gaze to keep his composure, making Kamila squeal in happiness. \"I’m not bored, and if I change your outfit one more time, I don’t know what I’ll do.\"","\"Thank you! That’s the best compliment you could give me!\" She tried to jump to his neck, but Lith stepped back.","\"For the love of the gods, woman! I’m barely holding on seeing you like that. There’s no way I can stay calm if I also feel you. Please, tell me something. Anything to distract me until the room service arrives.\"","\"Fine.\" Kamila pouted, half annoyed and half pleased by the unexpected turn of events. \"Know this. Grandma complimented me on my idea and asked my permission to make herself a dress like mine.\"","\"This is your original creation?\" Lith said in amazement. \"I-\"","\"Room service. Is anyone there?\" A cheery voice said through the door after knocking.","\"One moment.\" Lith went to the entrance, made sure it was impossible to see Kamila from there, and then opened the door just enough to let the food cart in. \"Thanks for the service. Now scram.\"","He pulled the cart in himself, without letting the valet take a single step inside the room. The young man had seen weirder things and the tip was generous, so he didn’t care.","Lith appreciated both the excellent quality of the food and the natural landscapes of his wife as they dined, but lost his train of thought from time to time when she leaned forward.","\"Finally! It’s time for the dessert!\" Lith sighed in relief, his massive headache still mounting.","\"Are you that fond of strawberry tart cake, or are you just happy we’re almost done eating?\" Kamila chuckled.","\"The latter.\" Lith nodded, his face fixed in a solemn expression of focus she recognized as his perverted face. \"I have no reason to hold back anymore.\"","A wave of his hand turned the deep V-neckline of her dress into a heart-shaped neckline that used Kamila’s full breasts as the upper left and right sides of the heart. It also exposed the red lingerie set she wore underneath and its see-through front-closure bra.","\"Hey, this was supposed to be a surprise for later. We’re not done eating yet.\" She giggled. \"Also, this is your idea of how to draw a heart?\"","\"The perfect heart.\" Lith nodded, standing up. \"Moreover, we are done here.\"","\"What about dessert?\" Kamila tilted her head.","\"This is a dessert. You’re my dessert. I can have both at the same time.\" Lith said, Blinking his wife and the plates to the bedroom.","***","Gorgon Empire, Drakeni Region, Outskirts of the city of Bornar, Night Court underground fortress, at the same time.","\"Are you sure this is a good idea?\" Tethre, the vampire in charge of the newly reestablished Night Court branch, asked. \"We invested a lot of time and resources to build Stonewall and our other ramparts.\""]},{"number":4493,"title":"Chapter 4493 Proof of Strength (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Moving so close to the surface so soon after recapturing Bornar from the Organization is reckless at best and stupid at worst.\" Tethre said.","\"What would have us do, Tethre?\" Cyrra Morghon, Banshee and current High General of the Night Court, scoffed. \"Spend months, if not years, in hiding and let our business and connections wither while we wait for the Incontinent King to make his move?","\"That man is a coward, and after his plans suffered so many setbacks, I wouldn’t be surprised if he never shows his face again.\" Her copper-red hair almost matched the intensity of her eyes as the power of undeath lit them from within like torches.","\"Indeed, but what was the point of the alliance with Verhen if we abandon our underground fortresses without even warning him? Why have Ruler Menadion adjust the arrays and defences of our strongholds to counter the Upyr’s powers just to abandon them?","\"Most importantly, my liege, what about me?\" Tethre’s voice quivered, and fear stole the allure from her fine features. \"I’m one of the members of the Night Courts who led the coup against Narchat.","\"I played a pivotal role in selling him out to the Mad Queen and his subsequent imprisonment. Why did you insist on making me come to Bornar? If the Dead King discovers I’m here, I’ll be his next target!\"","\"It’s true what they say, Tethre.\" Cyrra’s laughter was mirthless and cruel. \"Age alone brings no wisdom or courage. I wonder how you reached your position in the Night Court with such a weak heart and mushy brain.","\"The point of our deal with Vehren is being his allies, you dimwit, not his servants!\" The Banshee snarled, and the storm she carried within herself manifested in a gust of wind strong enough to force the vampire to step back.","\"We don’t have to ask his permission to do anything, let alone reestablish our centers of power and our connections with the black market! Ruler Menadion’s help was priceless in setting up our defense system.","\"She gave us the blueprints of her arrays, and we have deployed her improved creations here, and in all the branches of the Undead Courts we reconquered. Yet that doesn’t mean I’ll grant Verhen access and control to them.","\"Letting him set up the arrays to fuel his Omega Prime would be no different than living under his rule, knowing that he can kill us as soon as our interests no longer align. As for you, my dear Tethre...\" Cyrra’s rosy lips dripped sarcasm at those words.","\"You are bait. I won’t spend my eternal life in fear. I won’t hide and give up on everything I’ve built through the centuries just because of a little man like Narchat. This is my challenge to him!","\"If he really is worth more than the air he breathes, if he really thinks he has a chance of victory against my court, he’s free to come here and do his worst! We’ve proved our strength by defeating the Master’s Chosen.","\"We possess Ruler Menadion’s anti-Upyr spells. I’ve invested every coin I had left into this branch. If Narchat comes here, he will find me ready. Either he kills me, or I kill him; I’ll have my victory.","\"I, Cyrra Morghon, will have fought the Dead King’s army and proved the Night Court’s mettle. Even if we lose, we’ll force Narchat to reveal his cards. Whoever takes my place, if not even that Dawn fool of Bahz, will kill the Dead King.","\"I’ll be dead, sure, but my glory will be eternal, and the children of the Red Mother will rule the night again!\"","\"This is insane!\" Tethre snarled, her teeth turning into fangs and her fingers elongating into claws. \"Since when are we martyrs? I joined the Night Court to gain eternal life and unlimited power, not to be a hero!\"","\"A hero? Me?\" The Banshee’s amused laugh stopped the Vampire from jumping at her neck. \"I’m just like you, you fool! Tell me, how can you call forever hiding like a rat a life? What good are our powers if we can’t even enjoy the thrill of the hunt?","\"I’m not a martyr! I’m a predator, and I’d rather fight to the death to defend my hunting ground than go back to being a weak sheep afraid of her own shadow. I’m not that woman anymore, and I never will. What about you, Tethre?","\"Are you a daughter of Baba Yaga, returned from the grave to reclaim her life like me, or are you a scared little girl?\"","Those words hit the Vampire harder than any spell or blow ever could. The charisma they exuded and the shameful confession about Cyrra’s past shook Tethre to her core. The Banshee had become High General because the strength of her character matched that of her arm.","\"I’m a daughter of Baba Yaga.\" Her feral features regressed until she looked like a beautiful woman again. \"I fought that bastard once. I can do it again, my liege.\"","\"Well said, Major Tethre.\" Cyrra nodded as the Vampire bent the knee in submission. \"Now resume your station and don’t fret. I’m here to protect you, but make no mistake. I don’t care about you. I only care about what you stand for.","\"You are one of those who defied the Dead King first and lived. You are proof the Night Court can stand its ground against him. I’m going to protect the ideal you embody, but if you betray me or act like a coward, I’ll take you out myself.\"","\"I understand, my liege.\" Tethre nodded. \"I-\"","Alarms blared across the luxurious underground fortress, and all the mystical lights flashed red, alerting the undead that the perimeter had been breached.","\"You’ll contact our allies and then join me on the battlefield.\" A wave of Cyrra’s hand and her enchanted glaive, Blood Tear, flew into her palm. \"To arms!\"","Meanwhile, up in Bornar’s sky, a small contingent of Orpal’s Upyr army harried the city while the main force moved towards the Night Court’s branch. Finding it hadn’t been easy, but the result was worth the effort.","\"Those undead-brained idiots must have forgotten that I ruled over all the Courts and know how they handle their business.\" The laughter and the voice belonged to Orpal, but the body he inhabited wasn’t his own.","\"Those greedy morons always take the antique shipments to the local branch of a Court to look for something valuable or connected to their old life. All I had to do was find a few pieces of old junk and enchant them with a tracking spell.","\"Sure, all the branches of the Undead Courts are spatially sealed, but the external side of their old Gate Network is not. Once I found the hidden runes, it didn’t take much to identify the branch’s dimensional coordinate and, from there, its position.\"","\"It was a smart move.\" Jorl, the Storm Griffon, sat near the real Orpal in the fortress of Tle’ket. \"Still, I question its timing. Our forces are still growing, and the recruits don’t even come close to covering for our losses.\"","\"Winter is over, Jorl.\" Night spoke from Orpal’s right side of the face. \"We must fight with the army we have, not the one we want. Delaying our attack any longer would only prove our weakness.\""]},{"number":4494,"title":"Chapter 4494 Proof of Strength (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Now, instead, we’re about to make good on our promise. We are going to wipe out an entire branch of the Night Court. Their victory over the Master’s Organization will be further testament to our strength.","\"Young and ambitious Awakened from all over Mogar will come to us, looking for the invincible power of the Vurdalak. Our ranks will swell, and once we have an army of disciplined Upyrs, we’ll be unstoppable.\"","’I would agree on everything, if not for one crucial detail.’ Jorl thought, clutching his chest where the corrupted life force of the Vurdalak still tried to devour the Griffon side. ’Night’s grandiose plan requires an overwhelming victory, and we have yet to fight.","’If we lose, the number of new recruits will decrease even further, and our losses will be so great that we won’t be able to make a comeback anytime soon. The only silver lining in all this is that Orpal agreed not to send me to Bornar.","’He knows that if someone recognizes me, the Griffons will come running and his plan will fail. I doubt he and Night consider me more than a sacrificial pawn, but at least this proves they recognize my value as a general.’","Orpal had indeed kept Jorl by his side to employ the Griffon’s tactical acumen. Night was no strategist, and with their military strength at an all-time low, the Horseman couldn’t afford pointless deaths in her ranks.","\"Kill the humans and raze the city to the ground!\" Night yelled from her Chosen’s mouth. \"Leave nothing for those parasites to feed upon! Don’t chase them if they run. Let them live in poverty until they die of starvation.","\"Let their death be long and humiliating! Let everyone know that a swift demise is mercy to those who stand against the Dead King!\"","\"Hi, there!\" Cyrra’s Warp Steps appeared where Night could see it with Life Vision, but too far away to reach her before the Banshee stepped through the dimensional opening. \"Let me give your latest puppet a welcome gift!\"","Cyrra threw her glaive with all of her considerable strength. Blood Tear was true to its name, and the crimson aura surrounding the glaive as it bolted through the sky took the form of a drop, its power focused on the Adamant blade.","The Chosen raised his crystal spear to block it, but he was too slow. Blood Tear cut the Upyr asunder and performed a U-turn to return to its master.","\"Thank you. It was a lovely gift.\" Orpal laughed as black crystals knit the two halves of the clone together at a speed visible to the naked eye. \"Here’s mine!\"","A lunge of the crystal spear released a Wailing Wind the size of a pillar. Thorn was embedded at the core of the giant spear, and generated harrowing wails along with a blast of darkness, as if it carried the mournful souls of its victims.","Wailing Wind was too fast for Cyrra to dodge and too big to Blink away from it. She managed to avoid the brunt of the hit, but she was shot off the sky and crashed against the ground anyway.","\"I’m surprised you left the safety of your fortress to defend a bunch of mortals, undead rat.\" Orpal said. \"Don’t tell me you had a change of heart and discovered compassion.\"","\"That would require I had a heart to begin with.\" Cyrra’s Nightend armor had neutralized part of the darkness energy, and her blood core had already healed her wounds. \"I’m surprised you found someone stupid enough to become your Chosen.\"","\"You haven’t noticed yet?\" Orpal laughed as if he had just heard an amazing joke. \"I’m wearing an undead like you, whore. The first of many.\"","\"What?\" That piece of news took Cyrra by surprise, but didn’t slow her down.","She took to the sky again and charged at her enemy at the head of her lieutenants in a wedge formation.","\"Have you forgotten?\" Orpal’s smile went ear to ear. \"You undead are artificial. Not born, but created. I used Necromancy to raise the best specimens among you and had them accept my prism while they still considered me their father!","\"Sure, they start weak, but they become strong quickly if their maker is a Divine Beast and feeds them with plenty of his life force. Brilliant idea, isn’t it?\"","\"You degenerate scum!\" Cyrra’s face twisted in a disgusted grimace, and so did her allies’.","There were few things the Night Court wouldn’t do, but harming newborns was among them. Unless one was a White Lady, of course.","Just like babies, a newborn undead animated by Necromancy was a clean slate, with no memory or knowledge of their own. They depended on their maker for everything and trusted them blindly due to the spark of light magic they inherited.","\"Why so angry?\" Orpal laughed. \"It wasn’t I who told the world how to manufacture the different races of your kind. I just put to use what your precious Red Mother taught to us all. If you have a problem with it, take it to her!\"","At his signal, a 5-man squad of Upyrs moved to intercept the undead. They released the thick, sickly aura of Frost Soul and relied solely on their wings and air fusion to fly.","\"No mercy!\" Cyrra stopped in her tracks while the rest of her lieutenants threw themselves into the lion’s maw. \"Make those bastards regret the day they sided with Narchat!\"","\"How brave of you-\" Orpal’s mockery died on his fangs as the incoming undead released a brilliant red aura.","The six Blood Warlocks and Witches had taken their time absorbing as much world energy as they could, and released it in the form of six Blood Tides. The crimson domes expanded in every direction, overlapping until they fused into a massive sphere.","The violence of the impact blasted the Upyrs away and cleansed the air of the Frost Soul. On top of that, it left Bornar devoid of world energy, making elemental spells and bloodline abilities useless.","\"Second squad, attack!\" A cloud of Chiropterans swarmed the still-confused Upyr ranks, followed by other undead who didn’t need magic to fly.","Their claws cut deep into the depowered equipment of the Corrupted Divine Beasts, but the gap in mass and size left the Upyrs with little more than scratches. A few vampires tried to drink the Upyrs’ black blood to recover their strength, but it poisoned them.","The Vurdalak blood spread like cancer, robbing the vampires of their vigor and making them plummet until they purged it from their system.","\"Don’t drink their blood.\" A gasping vampire said amid barfs. \"Don’t feed on the Upyrs. Don’t touch them except for killing them. They are not undead or Abominations. They are a disease.\"","\"Damn! I was counting on sucking them dry.\" Cyrra cursed. \"Divine Beasts are supposed to be an acceptable meal for all undead races. Change of plans! Retreat! All forces, retreat to the first line of defenses!\"","\"What about the humans?\" A Dread Knight asked. \"There is no Bornar without them, and without a city, there’s no point having a branch here.\"","\"That’s none of our business.\" The High General replied. \"We held the Upyrs back long enough. Let those bleeding hearts of the Dawn Court take care of the rest.\""]},{"number":4495,"title":"Chapter 4495 Knight in Shining Armor (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Cyrra was still talking in her amulet when Erslan Bhaz, Blood Warlock and current king of the Dawn Court, entered the fray accompanied by his own forces.","One of the advantages of the old Warp Gates was that no dimensional sealing magic could keep them closed. The High General and the Dawn King had set up direct connections between their respective bases exactly for a moment like that.","Bhaz charged the Chiropterans of the Dawn Court with crimson bolts of Blood Maelstrom, increasing their physical and magical prowess tenfold. A second bolt spread as a thin mist, supercharging the Chiropterans’ equipment upon their passage.","\"What?\" Orpal snarled in outrage, and Life Vision revealed to him that the undead now far exceeded the power of a bright violet core. \"Blood Maelstrom is nothing but a cheap imitation of the real deal. My deal!\"","Silver lightning sparked from the red fragments of Dusk’s crystal in Tle’ket and instantly moved to Night’s prism in the Chosen’s chest. From there, they struck the nearest Upyrs, tipping the scales of the fight.","Yet there were many Blood Warlocks and only one Vurdalak. The prism in the Chosen’s chest could transmit the Life Maelstrom, but not produce it. Every spark of power Orpal consumed came from his own reserves.","\"How can you be this strong?\" He snarled","\"Who knows?\" Bhaz smirked as he cut through the Upyrs’ flesh with astounding ease.","He had shrouded himself with the Blood Magic spell, Murder Shroud.","The mana and life force formed an exoskeleton around him that supported his every move.","It granted the Blood Warlock the strength and mass of a much bigger creature, and was further boosted by the effects of the Blood Maelstrom cursing through his body.","\"There!\" Jorl’s keen eyes spotted the missing piece of the puzzle. \"Many of those undead wear a weird metal collar on their neck, just like Verhen’s allies in Jiera. The Tuners!\"","\"Harmonizers!\" Orpal snorted. \"But you’re right. Somehow Leech and his leech friends have perfected Thrud’s design for undead. It doesn’t matter. I still get to test my newest weapon.\"","The Vurdalak focused in Jiera, and the Chosen responded in Garlen. The fake Vurdalak swung his spear through the air, tracing several strings of black runes that blotted out the stars for those looking at them from below.","\"Fool!\" Bhaz roared as his Dread Knights drove the Upyrs away from the ground with their lightning-fast charges. \"You think we didn’t prepare for your Blade Spell? You’ll never cast it in time?\"","\"Are you sure about that?\" Orpal had performed three swings before a pillar of silvery light erupted from his spear.","The Blade Tier Spell, Nascent Sprout, contained only a fraction of Shattered Moon, but it was much faster to cast and still carried enough power to vaporize the 5-man squad of Chiropteran charging at Orpal.","The Blade Spell merely coated the Wailing Wind released by the Thorn spear, allowing Orpal to save a lot of time by not giving Nascent Sprout shape or will.","\"It’s too soon to be surprised!\" The Vurdalak smirked. \"Upyrs, bring down the hammer!\"","The backline of Corrupted Divine Beasts conjured the tier five War Mage spells, Raging Sun and Night Storm, to conjure the Source Magic spell, Shadow Meteor.","Earth magic carved giant rocks filled to the brim with darkness magic out of the ground. The fire element turned stone into magma, and the air element lifted them and gave them speed.","The barrage of Source Spells forced the combined forces of the Undead Courts to retreat and turned the outskirts of Bornar into a molten crater exuding noxious gas. Living beings would have become incapable of breathing, no matter their race.","The spell sealed the Awakened’s breathing techniques and poisoned them, yet it had no such effect on the undead.","\"My King, the treacherous Night Court is retreating.\" Anghor, the Draugr, said. \"If we leave, Bornar will be defenseless, and countless humans will die.\"","\"How many Upyrs are left?\" Bhaz broke a small ampule containing a preserved piece of flesh that he drained of life force to regain a bit of his strength.","\"Four. We managed to kill only one in the initial charge.\" Anghor was a mountain of a man, his face covered in a thick beard.","Yet even the cruel light of undeath animating his eyes couldn’t hide his embarrassment for failing his mission.","\"Too many. Wings and hooves.\" Bhaz said, conjuring two wings of blood to take flight despite the lack of world energy.","\"Wings and hooves!\" Anghor roared, his voice reverberating across the city without the need for an amplification spell.","The sound faded after a few city blocks, but undead had the keen senses of predators, and in the silence of the night, they could hear Anghor’s orders from kilometers away.","Bhaz and all the undead who could fly bolted upward and aimed their most destructive spells at the Upyrs’ wings. The rest of the Dawn Court had to escape the range of the lingering effects of Blood Tide before they could join their king.","The Corrupted Divine Beasts were caught by surprise and their wings shredded. They could have still conjured a Spirit flying spell, but the ensuing barrage of fire and darkness disrupted their focus.","They fell to the ground like living meteors, relaxing their legs in preparation for the impact. It was then they heard the hooves.","Dread Knights appeared on the horizon. Their steeds moved at full gallop and became faster by the second. The Windwalker bloodline ability of the undead horses condensed the air in front of the Dread Knights’ spear tips in a spiral pattern.","It created a slipstream effect in front of the horses and accumulated destructive power as they moved. Windwalker allowed a Dread Knight to accelerate without end as long as they kept moving, reaching speeds that even Awakened couldn’t follow.","The steeds stepped on the guards’ booths outside of the city and used them to reach the top of the city walls with one step. From there, they jumped ahead and landed on the nearest roof, barely producing a noise on impact.","The Dread Knights arrived as graceful as butterflies and as fast as lightning. They moved from roof to roof until they charged at the still-falling Upyrs, piercing through them thanks to the kinetic energy they had accumulated.","Each one of them opened a hole the size of a double door, a small wound for a creature the size of a Divine Beast. Moreover, the plant folk’s regenerative abilities would close such wounds in a matter of seconds.","Dozens of Dread Knights, however, carried enough power to blow even a violet-cored Upyr to pieces and destroy the plant folk’s Roots in a single charge.","\"Retreat!\" Anghor yelled with a savage smirk, seeing that only one Corrupted Divine Beast had survived the onslaught. \"Retreat and regroup to rally point one! Leave the last vermin to the humans!\"","\"Don’t let them escape!\" Orpal’s clone snarled. \"The humans are not our opponents. Bring me those Harmonizers!\"","The Dead King hadn’t missed that no mystical collar was left behind. If its wearer died, the closest undead would pick it up and put it on, becoming the new leader of their unit."]},{"number":4496,"title":"Chapter 4496 Knight in Shining Armor (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Brilliant.\" Jorl pondered. \"The undead could have all worn a Harmonizer, but that would have also meant they could be more easily stolen or lost in the chaos of battle. Those artifacts must hold an important secret if the Undead Courts put so much thought into protecting them.\"","\"Of course they do, you foolish sparrow!\" Night snarled. \"Those are not regular Harmonizers. They carry the mark of my mother’s workings. She must have found a way to further her children’s evolution potential like Glemos did for the Balors.\"","\"So what? They are useless away from a mana geyser.\" The Storm Griffon shrugged.","’Undead are supposed to be an evolutionary dead branch, and Vurdalaks are part Vampire.’ Orpal said via a mind link to keep the conversation secret from the rest of his underlings. ’It means Upyrs might be a dead branch as well.","’Though if those Harmonizers work on a Vampire, they should work on me as well. If I can find a path toward evolution, then I, you, and all my loyal followers would enjoy the bloodline abilities of my human, Dragon, and Phoenix aspects.’","The Dead King hated to admit the possibility he might be a flawed being instead of the supreme existence he claimed, yet he had no other choice. He needed Jorl’s help to succeed, and the Griffon couldn’t plan their way to success if he wasn’t aware of Orpal’s real goal.","’We’ll take a few, then.’ Jorl replied, secretly hoping the Harmonizer might hold the secret to restore his original life force.","\"You’ll pay for this, Bhaz!\" The Chosen roared with Orpal’s voice. \"Take this!\"","What energy was left of Nascent Sprout answered its master’s call and returned to the crystal spear. Night and Orpal added new rune sequences to the Blade Spell and infused it with more mana, turning it into Death Seedling.","The new Blade Spell was carried by a fresh Wailing Wind and possessed a destructive power several times greater. It struck the backline of the retreating Dread Knight, causing a shockwave so powerful that many of them were sent flying despite dodging the actual blast.","\"My King!\" Anghor cried for Bhaz to retreat. \"He’s slaughtering us!\"","\"A few lives are a price worth paying to expose the Dead King’s new strength.\" The Dawn King replied. \"Rescue the wounded, but don’t stop! Retreat!\"","He was the first to follow his own orders, Blood Blinking to the ground and rescuing two injured Dread Knights before it was too late. Death Seedling vaporized the undead steeds, but they were also part of the Dread Knight.","With time and nourishment, they would return, whereas the death of a Dread Knight would have been an unacceptable loss.","The members of the Dawn Court ran for their undeath as the Upyrs gained more ground. As soon as the world energy filled the air again, the Corrupted Divine Beasts’ size and mass gave them an overwhelming advantage over their puny enemies.","Even the most powerful undead like the Grendels could only defend and run.","\"This makes no sense.\" Jorl said as the enemy’s retreat devolved into a rout. \"Those are not cowardly humans, but ancient undead. Then why are they scrambling like that? Where is the discipline? Why aren’t they assuming a defensive formation? Unless...\"","His bird eyes widened in understanding.","\"Order all the troops to stop! It’s a trap!\" He clenched Orpal’s shoulder.","Truth dawned before the charging Upyrs, in the literal sense of the word.","As the first wave of soldiers of the Undead Courts retreated, the second wave advanced. It was an orderly line of knights in armor of the purest Adamant that reflected the faintest starlight, making them visible from a great distance.","\"Not them!\" Orpal cursed. \"Not now!\"","\"Dawnbringers!\" A tenor voice rose to cover the din of battle. \"Show the traitor child of the Red Mother and her offspring what true darkness looks like!\"","The silvery knights raised their arms in unison, and the light from the moon and the stars disappeared. Each Dawnbringer projected an expanding dome of darkness from their body that no sight could penetrate.","Life and Fire Vision were as useless as the night vision each Upyr gained upon turning into a Corrupted Divine Beast. Light was gone, and with it anything their eyes could perceive.","\"Dodge!\" Orpal yelled. \"Throw yourself on the ground! Now!\"","\"Light the way!\" Erril Song, commander of the Dawnbringers, said.","The accumulated light element erupted from the silvery knights’ hands in the form of hyper-focused laser beams. Each blast lasted the blink of an eye, but moved just as fast.","The first row of Upyrs plunged from the sky with large, fuming holes all over their bodies.","Their flesh, bones, and organs had been vaporized on impact. Healing those wounds required vast amounts of nutrients. Without them, what the Upyr regained in mobility, they would lose in vigor.","\"Hold the line!\" Erril yelled. \"Let them come to their death!\"","Light coated the armor and weapons of the Dawnbringers, forming a thick, incandescent layer that boosted both their offense and defense.","Dawnbringers were the undead species Baba Yaga had created as a prototype for her first Horseman, the Bright Day. They could absorb sunlight, becoming temporarily immune to it, but the darkness that accompanied them made it impossible to hide their presence.","The Dawnbringers were no Light Masters and couldn’t conjure constructs, but they could coat their equipment with light element and use it as a scaffold for high-density heat rays.","Unlike Nightwalkers and Blood Warlocks, Dawnbringers needed a special kind of armor and weapon to tap into their full potential, and only the Bright Day and Baba Yaga had known how to craft them for a long time.","Dawn had passed down the secret to the Dawnbringers before abandoning her court almost a millennium ago, hoping to set her honor guard free as her siblings had done before her.","Yet her gesture and parting words had only strengthened the Dawnbringers’ oath of loyalty, and they had refused to take part in any activity of the Undead Courts, waiting for their liege to return.","\"They are impressive.\" Zepho Acala said while staring at the line of Dawnbringers cutting the darkness of the night asunder through the surveillance mirror.","\"They are also the origin of the expression ’knight in shining armor’, my love.\" Dawn said with pride. \"I can’t believe those fools waited for me for all this time. They haven’t seen me since before the founding of the Griffon Kingdom, yet I only needed to say the word to let them come out of their isolation.\"","\"I’m sure the promise of upgraded equipment and a few Light Mastery lessons sweetened the deal.\" Baba Yaga grunted.","\"It was the least I could do, Mom.\" Dawn replied. \"They are risking their lives for me. For us.\"","\"About that, why aren’t we out there to help them?\" The traitorous Ranger asked.","\"Because that’s not Orpal. Just a clone.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"There’s nothing to gain from this and a lot to lose. Don’t reveal your best cards until the moment comes. Let the Undead Courts play their role.","\"If you keep rescuing them, you’ll shatter their pride, and Orpal will ignore them. He must think of them as a threat if we want him to spread his forces thin and leave himself vulnerable. Also, you’d ruin my trap.\""]},{"number":4497,"title":"Chapter 4497 Corrupted Energy (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Are the Dawnbringers something you created after studying evolved humans like the Balors?\" Baba Yaga refused to elaborate on her plan further, so Acala changed the topic.","\"Don’t be silly, son.\" The Mother said with a warm smile. \"Balors were incomplete beings, and I only want the best for my children. All my prototype undead and my Horsemen are based on what I know best. Myself.","\"Nightwalkers and Dawnbringers embody the Odi’s natural mastery over darkness and light that evolution magnifies at every step of the way. Creating the Blood Witches was much harder, but I’d say the result was worth the effort. Look.\"","Bhaz and the Blood Witches from both the Night and Dawn Courts released bolts of crimson lightning that turned the line of Dawnbringers into a massive Wall of Light.","\"Hold!\" Erril repeated, his aura and his comrades’ growing by the second as the tidal wave of Upyrs crashed down on them.","The Corrupted Divine Beast hit the Wall of Light with their full might, but the Dawnbringers pushed them back. The Upyrs snarled in pain, their bodies sizzling from the contact with the incandescent construct.","They waited for the second wave of Corrupted Divine Beasts to reach their position and launched a joint attack to bring the Wall of Light down.","\"Hold!\" Erril kept his eyes fixed on the incoming colossi, focusing his powers to the extreme until the Upyrs were upon his soldiers. \"Now!\"","The Dawnbringers jumped back and released part of the accumulated light element from their feet into a jet of fire that propelled them at blinding speed.","\"What?\" The Upyrs’ weapons, claws, and extra limbs hit only air, leaving them full of openings and offering a clear line of fire to the undead.","A barrage of tier five elemental spells shot down the Corrupted Divine Beasts from the sky. They crashed to the ground where the undead swarmed them like a school of piranhas and tore them apart.","\"Those spells are much stronger than normal.\" Jorl pondered. \"The Wall of Light was a diversion to hide the presence of a mana geyser. All this was a set-up to lure your Upyrs to a location where the Harmonizers can express their full power.\"","\"I noticed.\" Orpal grunted as his clone approached the front lines and spotted the raging stream of world energy coming from the ground below the undead’s rally point. \"Take one Harmonizer and leave.","\"I repeat, take at least one Harmonizer and leave. I won’t fight an unfavorable battle, but I won’t leave empty-handed. For power!\"","\"For power!\" The Upyr chanted as one, calling upon the only thing they truly believed in.","The Vurdalak clone recalled Death Seedling as well and added more runes and mana, bringing it one step closer to her full-powered Blade Spell, Shattered Moon. The silver light of Blooming Night had just left the crystal spear’s tip when a red wave crushed it.","\"Not so fast, you bitch.\" Vladion Dragonborn, the First Vampire, held his Primordial Thirst blade while it still exuded a crimson aura. \"It’s not fair for us old coots to interfere in a squabble between children, Night.\"","\"Vladion? What are you doing here?\" The Horseman snarled, trying to buy time to finish conjuring at least another Nascent Sprout.","\"I live here. The Gorgon Empire is my home.\" He replied. \"Also, I’ve been waiting for this moment ever since I almost died at the hands of your Chosen. Let’s see how strong you are when I have more than a bunch of rags on me!\"","Vladion charged forward, but had to stop when the clone conjured Orpal’s bloodline ability, King’s Wraith. It mixed the accumulated darkness element stored inside Night’s prism with the Vurdalak’s life force, generating a vortex of dark fog the size of a tornado.","The abundant darkness element in the air during the night further reinforced the bloodline ability, forcing Vladion to halt so as not to lose most of his strength before delivering the first blow.","’Red Mother almighty!’ He thought. ’I can’t believe that half-baked Blade Spell neutralized my full-powered Bloodbreak. Life Maelstrom gives him too much of an advantage, but I can’t let him notice.’","While Orpal focused on the Firstborn Vampire, afraid more Firstborns of Baba Yaga might enter the fray, Jorl took command of the army.","\"Don’t forget your training.\" He said. \"Harmonizers are just another piece of equipment.\"","The Upyrs obeyed as one, igniting the blue flame that orbited over their heads. Frost Soul spread like a disease, infecting the world energy of the geyser and making it visible to the naked eye.","A thick, sickly fog enveloped the undead, turning them into ice sculptures by freezing the world energy they drew into their bodies to conjure their spells and bloodline abilities.","\"Cold and shock!\" Cyrra snarled, and her soldiers obeyed.","Wendigos unleashed their bloodline ability, Chilling Wail, before the Frost Soul reached them. The eternal winter trapped in their flesh clashed against the corrupted water element, freezing it solid.","The ice propagated across the blue mist and went all the way back to its source. The Upyrs became covered in a thick layer of snow that didn’t hurt them much but sealed Frost Soul inside their bodies.","\"I knew it!\" Baba Yaga clenched her fist. \"Wendigos can’t conjure the Jerak Cursed Element, but once they wear the Harmonizer, the boost in their powers can still neutralize Orpal’s unique water element.\"","\"What do you mean, Mom?\" Dawn asked.","\"The Dead King’s powers don’t tap into the natural components of the world energy like spells and bloodline abilities do.\" The Mother explained. \"They corrupt and twist what’s in the world energy similarly to Forbidden Magic.","\"It gives Orpal’s bloodline abilities great power, but it also makes them unstable, and the world energy rejects them. My Wendigos and Jerak tip the scales further, allowing the world energy to purge itself of the corruption.\"","\"So, it’s not the Wendigos. Mogar itself is fighting the Upyrs.\" Acala said.","\"That’s a dramatic way to put it, but yes.\" Baba Yaga shrugged. \"Always remember, if Mogar chose to fight, this battle would have ended before it started.\"","At the same time, the Banshees of the Night Court released their sonic screech, Shattered Soul. The bodies of the frozen Upyrs cracked while the rest of them fell to their knees, holding their bleeding ears.","Amid the chaos of battle, a Corrupted Divine Beast pushed his comrades aside and slammed his mace in the middle of the Banshees’ formation. The Thunder Soul it carried killed one undead and sent the other members of her unit flying.","\"Finally! A chance to overcome the limits of the Vurdalak bloodline!\" Colurra, the Treant-Upyr, shrank to humanoid size and wore the Harmonizer of his victim. \"Yes. Yes!\"","His life force restructured itself thanks to the pressure of the world energy released by the mana geyser and the powerful enchantments Baba Yaga had imbued in the Harmonizer.","\"What are you doing, you traitor?\" Orpal snarled. \"That’s my prize! Bring it to me, now!\"","The Treant felt his power swell and his body change as it approached the next evolutionary step. So great was his ecstasy that he didn’t notice how, among those changes, there was also a direct connection between the Harmonizer and his brain."]},{"number":4498,"title":"Chapter 4498 Corrupted Energy (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"I got him!\" Baba Yaga extended her consciousness, reading the Upyr’s mind like an open book. \"Show me where you little critters hide. Share with me Orpal’s plans. Tell me how I can destroy him once and for all!\"","Alas, the open book still had a will of its own, and the Mother struggled to suppress Colurra’s thirst for power and dreams of glory. His delusions of grandeur kept flashing before her eyes, eclipsing the information that truly mattered.","\"Orpal is in Jiera, as I suspected.\" Baba Yaga said, recognizing the familiar environment. \"Verendi is too unstable and populous to hide for as long as he did. Yet I need a location. Show me where he hides. Is that the Vepta Region?\"","As the Harmonizer’s spells suppressed the willpower of the Treant and froze his life force to ease Baba Yaga’s way into his mind, something went wrong. The Upyr side felt his prey relax and grow weak until the gates to Colurra’s essence were unguarded and open.","The silver flame burning over the Treant-Upyr’s head shone bright as the Vurdalak blood ravaged the Fae’s life force, devouring it with ravenous hunger. The same spell that suppressed Colurra’s mind also opened the path to his core.","Colurra screamed in agony and terror, the Harmonizer no longer able to suppress his survival instinct as Orpal’s blood ate the Fae alive. The change happened at mind-link speed, the long and painstaking preparations of the Upyr side at every moment of Colurra’s weakness finally paying off.","\"What’s going on? Go back! I need to be sure that’s the city of Tle’ket!\" Baba Yaga poured her mana and will into the Harmonizer, but it found nothing to hold onto. The Upyr-Treant was gone, and a Vurdalak stood in his place.","\"There’s something wrong with the Harmonizers.\" A cold shiver ran down Jorl’s spine, knowing he was one step away from sharing Colurra’s fate. \"To all troops, disengage and retreat! Cover each other’s backs and return to base.\"","\"Leech!\" Colurra sensed the intrusion in his mind and rejected it, snapping the Harmonizer in half with a single twist of his hands. \"I’m coming for you, Leech. But first...\"","The Undead Courts’ members raised their guards and the Dawnbringers prepared to unleash their incandescent blades upon the newborn monstrosity when it bolted away. The Vurdalak flew at breakneck speed toward Vladion, but his bloodlust wasn’t aimed at the vampire.","\"What the?\" The clone and the Firstborn thought in unison when Colurra struck at the Chosen with all his newfound malice and power.","The former Treant entered the King’s Wraith, yet suffered no wound. The darkness element inflicted no harm to him, and when the clone tried to strike Colurra down with his crystal spear, Thorn remained silent.","The two Vurdalaks bolted away in a growling mass of claws, teeth, and anger under the stupefied gazes of their enemies and allies.","\"What in the Red Mother’s name is happening?\" Vladion, Cyrra, Bhaz, and the rest of the undead said as one.","They had prepared many more traps and battle formations, but they were all based on the assumption the fight would take place over the mana geyser. The Upyrs’ units left in a hurry, scattering in every direction with Spirit Blinks.","The undead could chase after them, but at the cost of their teamwork and leaving their base exposed to whatever treachery the Dead King might have prepared.","\"Die!\" Colurra the Vurdalak shattered the clone’s crystal spear with a blow of his Thunder Soul-infused mace. \"Die, you impostor! Like there can be only one sun and one king, there can only be one Orpal!\"","The fury and savagery of the former Treant shocked the Dead King, but it was nothing compared to his surprise when the silvery flame above his head finally flared up.","’I tried activating my light element bloodline ability countless times, yet I always failed. Why now, and why do I feel so hungry?’ Orpal asked.","Something inside him opened. It didn’t appear or break. It had always been there, but until that moment, it had no reason to manifest itself.","’Of course!’ The Dead King solved the mystery of his silver flame and his Vurdalak nature that had tormented him for so long.","As his clone slowly crumbled under the frenzied attacks of the newborn creature and deep, mirror wounds opened all over his body, Orpal used his link with his Chosen to open a series of Warping Arrays to its position with Moonlight.","He only took Jorl with him, to have at least one person witness his success. In the blink of an eye, the two Corrupted Divine Beasts arrived close enough to Colurra and the Chosen to Warp them before the Dead King.","The frenzied creature hadn’t ceased his attack for a second, and the Chosen was covered in grievous defensive wounds. Feeling that the prism was about to shatter, the Dead King rushed to rescue his clone.","’It’s not that these injuries hinder me so much that I can’t afford to lose an undead I nurtured for so long.’ Orpal thought. ’Creating an undead with Necromancy is easy, but developing their blood cores takes a lot of time!’","\"We finally meet, impostor!\" Colurra roared, releasing a violet aura and injecting his mace with more Thunder Souls. \"Die!\"","\"Please, tell me that I don’t sound like that.\" Orpal snorted as he readied for the challenge.","\"I’m sorry, but that’s you down to a t.\" Jorl replied. \"Do you need a hand?\"","\"Stay out of this.\" The Dead King infused himself with a jolt of silver lightning and intercepted the mace with his open hand.","The Treant wore good Adamant equipment he had received from his bloodline after Awakening, whereas Orpal only had his black crystal armor. The mace shattered it and the hand it covered despite the Life Maelstrom empowering them, but Orpal didn’t care.","He didn’t feel pain, and Moonlight healed his hand at a speed visible to the naked eye. More importantly, he had Colurra exactly where he wanted him. At the perfect distance for a burst of Origin Flames.","The Dead King tapped into Dusk’s crystal again and released a jet stream of violet flames that he boosted with a spark of silver lightning. Colurra couldn’t dodge at point-blank range, and there was no defense against the roaring of mystical fire.","The newborn Vurdalak screamed in pain, and the Dead King exploited Colurra’s agony to rip the mace out of his hands. The weapon altered its shape and size to fit its new owner, and its enchantments answered his touch.","’I was right! Just like Thorn refused to kill Colurra because it mistook him for me, I can use his mace. He’s not just become a Vurdalak; he’s become a copy of me with my same energy signature!’ Orpal thought.","Joy didn’t stay his hand, quite the contrary. He struck at the pretender with savage fury, aiming only for vitals. Whenever Colurra tried to defend himself or chant a spell, another burst of Origin Flames disrupted his focus.","Colurra still possessed most of his regenerative abilities, but they weren’t as effective as those of his former Treant life force. Moreover, with nothing from which to draw sustenance, every healed wound further drained his vitality."]},{"number":4499,"title":"Chapter 4499 Blade at the Neck (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"You were right about one thing, traitor.\" The Dead King lifted the ruins that Colurra’s body had become with one hand, holding him by the neck. \"Like there can be only one sun and one king, there can only be one Orpal!\"","He called upon the silver fire that blazed above his head and activated his newfound bloodline ability, Feast Soul. Orpal’s silver flame released a beam of energy that its twin orbiting Colurra’s head answered in kind.","The two pillars of silvery energy battled for dominance for a few seconds before the strong flame empowered by Life Maelstrom overtook the weak, dwindling fire connected to Colurra’s life force.","Orpal’s Feast Soul burned at its victim from the inside out and stole everything that the former Treant was. The transformation from Upyr into Vurdalak had turned Colurra into a nigh-identical clone of Orpal, and their life forces were a perfect match.","Mana, strength, and vitality moved from the loser to the winner like spoils of a blazing war. When the process ended, Colurra was dead, and his corpse resembled a dried-up mummy.","Orpal, instead, was bigger, stronger, and his insatiable hunger for power tormented him a tiny bit less.","\"I knew it!\" He laughed in a frenzy. \"I knew my powers couldn’t amount to so little! I’m part vampire, after all, and I need to feed to increase my strength. My problem was that no one in this world is a meal worthy of me.","\"According to Night, I have even absorbed one of Colurra’s mana organs. I can now manipulate plant life to some extent! I might not have exterminated those parasites of the Undead Courts, but this is still a great victory.","\"It’s thanks to them and their ploy to probe my minions’ minds that I finally uncovered what might be the strongest among my bloodline abilities!\"","’Yeah, too bad that the mana organ looks nothing like the one Colurra possessed.’ Night said via their mind link. ’The transformation mutated and corrupted the Treant, and what you inherited from him is the result of that corruption.","’This will take some time and lots of experiments to understand if your new power is better, equal, or worse than the original.’","’It’s more than I had until a second ago, so it’s plenty enough.’ Orpal replied.","\"One mana organ from each of my meals. The Vurdalak truly is the king of the undead and the most perfect Divine Beast.\" He actually said. \"And this is just the beginning.\"","Orpal turned to Jorl, looking at him with a hungry spark in his eyes.","The Storm Griffon wielded his maces and infused himself with Life Maelstrom, preparing for the fight.","’He has Moonlight, but I won’t get down on my knees and beg for mercy. I-’","\"What are you doing?\" Orpal asked in honest confusion. \"I’m not going to eat you. I already have Life Maelstrom.\"","\"Yeah, but you lack my Light Raider, Focus Point, and physical might, to name a few.\" Jorl replied. \"Those might come in handy.\"","\"I won’t deny I gave it a thought, but it’s a dumb move, and you and I know it, Jorl.\" Orpal shrugged. \"I would lose your strategic mind, your charisma in handling our troops, and your invaluable knowledge.","\"And for what? A gamble that might as well give me one of your bloodline abilities I don’t need. Do you think me stupid enough to risk a certainty for a possibility?\"","\"No.\" Jorl replied, putting his Dusk Wraith maces away.","’Also, he doesn’t know I’ve started turning into a Vurdalak, and even if he did, he can’t eat me unless I complete the transformation. Being a Upyr is my best insurance that Orpal won’t get funny thoughts about me.’","\"How much did you change after feeding?\" He asked.","In the future, the Storm Griffon might have to defend from Feast Soul or maybe even use it himself. It was one of those cases where knowledge was literal power.","\"My mana core progressed a bit, I gained a mana organ, and I feel completely refreshed.\" Orpal sounded disappointed. \"My mass didn’t increase, though, and whatever knowledge Colurra had is lost.","\"The worst part is that the energy assimilation is nowhere near 1:1. There is a lot of waste. Still, it saved me hours, if not days of Accumulation. The day I reach the violet, and then the bright violet is not as distant as I thought.\"","\"What are we going to say to our soldiers? They will question Colurra’s disappearance.\" Jormun pointed out.","\"We’ll tell them the truth.\" Orpal grinned ear to ear. \"He had gone insane, and we had to put him down. After all, only a madman can think he can defeat me.\"","The maniacal laughter that followed only reinforced Jorl’s belief that Colurra hadn’t gone insane. He had simply fallen victim to the madness that plagued the Vurdalak bloodline.","He had no idea how right he was, yet he should have.","As Orpal enjoyed his victory, the first activation of Feast Soul triggered a resonance effect in those who carried the Vurdalak blood. All of them, even those who hadn’t yet developed a light affinity, had the silver blaze appear over their heads.","It burned bright for a few seconds before reverting to its neutral state. The Upyrs considered it a blessing and rejoiced no less than the Dead King. No one suspected it was both a curse and the warning sign that the Upyrs had become each other’s predator and prey.","***","When Baba Yaga reached Tle’ket in Jiera, she didn’t find anything. Orpal and his army of Upyrs had long since left after stripping and storing away everything precious and useful.","He had issued the evacuation order as soon as the Harmonizer had struck Colurra, and his preparations paid off. Night knew her mother’s methods well enough to suspect the secret of the undead Harmonizers and warn Orpal.","It was just a guess, but the Horseman of Night preferred to err on the side of caution since Baba Yaga could easily kill her and slaughter the Upyr army if she found them.","The Upyrs returning from the Gorgon Empire followed the established protocol, scattering into small groups and Warping to different locations before moving on to the meeting points.","There, they would find coded instructions leading to a destination where they would be examined and scanned before being brought to the new fortress.","It took hours to complete the move, but as soon as it was done and the defensive arrays reestablished, Jorl could finally leave Orpal’s side.","The Black Throne waited for him on a nearby mana geyser in the Maneka Region. The equipment he had crafted for Jorl contained a tracker that allowed the cursed tower to know the Storm Griffon’s position at all times.","The cursed tower had relocated minutes after the Dead King, keeping the distance with his disciple unchanged.","The news that Jorl brought worried the Black Throne more than even such an ancient being would expect.","\"Interesting.\" The cursed tower examined the memories that Jorl had shared with him very carefully, studying Feast Soul’s effects frame by frame. \"It seems that my theory was right. Orpal’s vampire side is more than dominant.\""]},{"number":4500,"title":"Chapter 4500 Blade at the Neck (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"When Night fused his life forces, she did such a poor job that she also turned the human and Dragon aspects into undead. It’s no wonder Orpal lost most of his original bloodline abilities.","\"Undeath kills the body, and only a few mana organs survive the transformation. When you face the Dead King, apprentice, you must consider him the fusion of a vampire, an undead Dragon, and a non-evolved human.\"","\"Good to know. Too bad it doesn’t change the fact that Orpal is now stronger, has a new ability, new equipment, and we finally know what happens when an Upyr turns into a Vurdalak.\" Jorl paced the throne room, trying to calm his nerves.","\"I don’t know what to do. Heck, I don’t even know what to say. Should I warn Akhton and my loyalists, or should I keep this to myself? Orpal wants to keep Feast Soul secret for obvious reasons, but I agree with him.","\"If I told the truth to my troops, they’d likely run for their lives. All I can offer them is a maybe, whereas Orpal is a concrete threat. Being close to him is no different from having a blade at your neck for an Upyr.\"","\"You’re lucky, apprentice.\" The Black Throne’s voice was raspy yet full of confidence and determination. \"I know what to do and say. Reveal the secret of Feast Soul only to Akhton and Uragar.","\"The Bastet is a precious ally, and Orpal might deem the chance of acquiring his Mana Body worth killing Akhton. The Dead King already has your Life Maelstrom and doesn’t know if one mana organ is enough to use Light Raider or Focus Point.","\"Those are complex bloodline abilities, and killing you to obtain an incomplete power would be foolish. Mana Body, however, only requires one mana organ, and I’m sure Night knows it.","\"If Orpal’s gamble pays off, he’d get one step closer to obtaining all the bloodline abilities of the six original Guardians. At that point, he only has to consume Erion and pray his luck holds.\"","\"Good gods!\" Jorl rubbed his beak with his clawed hand, realizing the truth in the Black Throne’s words.","\"As for Uragar, he won’t get scared. Even if Orpal feeds on the Book of Knowledge’s host, he can get another, and Feast Soul can’t rob a cursed object of its enchantments. Conversely, Uragar can feed on Orpal and steal his bloodline abilities.","\"The Book of Knowledge has everything to gain from our war against Orpal. He won’t leave your side. Not until he’s built himself the most powerful host he can.\"","\"Our war?\" Jorl echoed.","\"Yes, apprentice. Our war.\" The Black Throne nodded. \"As I said, I know what we have to do. First, set aside any plans about killing Orpal. Those have to wait. Our top priority is capturing Dawn.","\"Once she is in our hands, we’ll cure ourselves of our respective afflictions. With your body purged from the Vurdalak blight and my Battle Form, we will have everything we need to kill the Dead King.\"","\"How can I believe you?\" Jorl snorted. \"What if after you get what you want, you drop me like a bad habit? That’s what I’d do in your shoes. You are powerful, but so is Orpal. Also, a battle between towers can’t be easy.\"","\"I don’t believe you would do that, apprentice.\" The Black Throne extended a tendril of Spirit Magic to pat Jorl’s shoulder. \"You’re scared now, but as soon as you calm down, you’ll understand I’m telling the truth.","\"I’m no hero, apprentice. I don’t fight for justice. Yet I didn’t live thousands of years just to leave Mogar in the hands of a madman. Orpal has the means to become a threat to the balance and to me.","\"If I let him grow his powers, when we meet in the future, it will be on his terms, and by then I might not be able to defeat him. That’s unacceptable!\" The floor and walls of the tower trembled. \"I’m the master of my own destiny.","\"Mogar is my house! I won’t let that little rabid bastard make a mess of my lawn! Orpal has to die, apprentice, and mark my words, he will.\"","***","Lith was at the Verhen Mansion when Baba Yaga visited him to report her failure. She showed him the fight for Bornar from the beginning and multiple angles, hoping he might spot something she had missed or maybe something she could improve.","\"Those Dawnbringers look powerful.\" Lith narrowed his eyes. \"We’re lucky they don’t obey the Undead Courts. That said, your plan was perfect, Yaga. There’s nothing I, or anyone else for that matter, would have done better.\"","\"Thanks.\" She sighed. \"Yet there’s something nagging at the back of my head. The way the Upyr turned into a Vurdalak caught me by surprise, but the way he spoke and acted shocked me. That Treant turned into a perfect copy of Orpal in a heartbeat.","\"It must mean something, and I can feel it in my blood it’s nothing good.\"","\"We’ll worry about that when the moment comes.\" Lith sighed. \"There are too many possible explanations for that, and we have nothing to work on. Meat skewers?\"","\"Yes, thanks.\" Baba Yaga took a bite of the food, and her mood instantly improved. \"This is Zima’s Firghi pork! It’s as rare as delicious. Where did you get it?\"","\"Haug.\" Lith jabbed his thumb at the Travelling Tavern in the park. \"Feel free to eat and drink to your content. My treat.\"","Meanwhile, inside the establishment, Parmegianno Haug didn’t know what to do or say either. He had been at the Verhen Mansion for days now, but had never made a move on Ryla.","’The situation is too messy, and that poor kid and his mother don’t need more chaos in their lives.’ He inwardly sighed, trying to forget his crush and the romantic dreams it stirred in his heart.","Alas, he had no way to succeed. Garrik had become a regular guest at the Tavern, and enjoyed spending hours on end with the chatty bartender. Unlike Lith, Haug had an endless repertoire of funny and amazing stories that didn’t involve fights to the death.","Haug also spiced things up by using the arrays of his Tavern to conjure holograms of the events as he described them, giving a face and voice to his characters. The bartender had been to every continent, and many of his stories took place in exotic countries.","Garrik gaped in awe at the different races Haug had encountered and the weird clothes they wore. The young Fomor had stars in his eyes whenever the bartender had the restaurant shapeshift to suit the different cultures on Mogar, and squealed with joy when Haug served him local dishes at the end of each story.","\"Thank you, Mister Haug!\" Garrik said while savoring a bowl of noodles covered in black bean sauce and seasoned with many unknown spices. \"I can’t step away from Uncle Lith’s house, but you always bring a new piece of Mogar to me.","\"After listening to your stories, I feel like I’ve been there with you.\"","\"Don’t mention it, young man, and you can drop the mister.\" Haug tutted while refilling Garrik’s glass of water."]}]);
